window.ZGCLAB_DETAILS["news-35"]=[{"id":"news-1277","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"与伊朗有关联的黑客声称入侵FBI局长帕特尔个人邮箱","title_en":"Iran-linked hackers breach Kash Patel's personal email | The Jerusalem Post","summary_cn":"与伊朗有关联的黑客组织Handala Hack Team于3月27日声称已访问FBI局长卡什·帕特尔的个人电子邮箱，并在网上发布其照片和文件。FBI证实帕特尔的邮箱遭到针对性攻击，发言人称已采取必要缓解措施，涉及数据属历史性质且不含政府信息。Handala被西方研究人员视为伊朗政府网络情报单位使用的多个身份之一。黑客发布了300多封邮件样本，路透社无法独立核实其真实性。","summary_en":"Iran-linked hacker group Handala Hack Team claimed on March 27 to have accessed FBI Director Kash Patel's personal email inbox, publishing photographs and documents online. The FBI confirmed Patel's emails were targeted, with a spokesman saying necessary mitigation steps were taken and the data was historical with no government information. Handala is considered by Western researchers to be one of several personas used by Iranian government cyberintelligence units. The hackers published over 300 emails that Reuters could not independently authenticate.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:36:13.769899+00:00","url":"https://www.jpost.com/international/article-891432","content":"Jerusalem Post/World NewsIran-linked hackers claim breach of FBI director's personal email, DOJ official confirms break-inA Justice Department official confirmed to Reuters that Patel's emails were compromised but did not go into detail. Follow us on GoogleFBI Director Kash Patel testifies before the Senate Appropriations Committee hearing on President Trump's proposed budget request for the Federal Bureau of Investigation, on Capitol Hill in Washington, DC, US, May 8, 2025.(photo credit: REUTERS/KEVIN LAMARQUE)ByREUTERSMARCH 27, 2026 17:36Updated: MARCH 27, 2026 21:33Iran-linked hackers on Friday claimed they had accessed FBI Director Kash Patel's personal email inbox, publishing photographs of the director and other documents to the internet.On their website, the hacker group Handala Hack Team said Patel \"will now find his name among the list of successfully hacked victims.\" The hackers published a series of personal photographs of Patel sniffing and smoking cigars, riding in an antique convertible, and making a face while taking a picture of himself in the mirror with a large bottle of rum.The FBI confirmed that Patel's emails had been targeted. In a statement, bureau spokesman Ben Williamson said, \"We have taken all necessary steps to mitigate potential risks associated with this activity,\" and that the data involved was \"historical in nature and involves no government information.\"Handala tied to Iranian government cyberintelligence units Handala, which calls itself a group of pro-Palestinian vigilante hackers, is considered by Western researchers to be one of several personas used by Iranian government cyberintelligence units. Handala recently claimed the hack of Michigan-based medical devices and services provider Stryker on March 11, claiming to have deleted a massive trove of company data.The website used by the Handala Hack Team, an Iran-linked hacker group which has claimed credit for the breach of FBI Director Kash Patel’s personal email, is shown on a screen in Washington DC, US, March 27, 2026. (credit: REUTERS/Raphael Satter)Alongside the photographs of Patel, the hackers published a sample of more than 300 emails, which appear to show a mix of personal and work correspondence dating between 2010 and 2019.Reuters was not able to independently authenticate the Patel messages, but the personal Gmail address that Handala claims to have broken into matches the address linked to Patel in previous data breaches preserved by the dark web intelligence firm District 4 Labs. Alphabet-owned Google, which runs Gmail, did not immediately respond to a request for comment.See more onIran|United States|FBI|cybersecurity|hack|Kash Patel|HandalaFollow us on GoogleRelated ArticlesUS gives UN time to end supporting Somalia peacekeepersZelensky launches Carpathian Eight security blocRussia begins three-day Duma electionSpanish police launch op. to clear Ceuta migrants off beachCar bomb kills at least 16 in PakistanIran war, Houthi advance test Trump’s peacemaker claimsPro-Israel former US senator Jon Kyl dies at 84","content_cn":"《耶路撒冷邮报》/世界新闻\n与伊朗有关联的黑客称入侵FBI局长个人邮箱，司法部官员确认遭入侵\n一名司法部官员向路透社证实，帕特尔的电子邮件遭到入侵，但未详述。关注我们的 Google\n2025年5月8日，美国华盛顿特区国会山，联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔在参议院拨款委员会就特朗普总统为联邦调查局提出的预算请求举行的听证会上作证。（图片来源：路透社/KEVIN LAMARQUE）\n作者：路透社\n2026年3月27日 17:36\n更新：2026年3月27日 21:33\n与伊朗有关联的黑客周五称，他们已进入联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔的个人电子邮箱收件箱，并在网上发布了这位局长的照片及其他文件。\n黑客组织 Handala Hack Team 在其网站上称，帕特尔“现在会发现自己的名字出现在已成功被黑客入侵的受害者名单中”。黑客发布了一系列帕特尔的私人照片，其中包括他闻雪茄和抽雪茄、驾驶一辆古董敞篷车，以及手持一大瓶朗姆酒对着镜子自拍时做鬼脸。\n联邦调查局确认帕特尔的电子邮件曾成为攻击目标。该局发言人本·威廉姆森在一份声明中表示：“我们已采取一切必要措施，以减轻与此活动有关的潜在风险。”他还称，所涉数据“具有历史性质，且不涉及任何政府信息”。\n\nHandala 与伊朗政府网络情报部门有关联\nHandala 自称是一个亲巴勒斯坦义警黑客组织，西方研究人员认为它是伊朗政府网络情报部门使用的数个身份之一。Handala 最近声称于3月11日入侵了总部位于密歇根州的医疗设备及服务供应商 Stryker，并称已删除了海量公司数据。\n2026年3月27日，美国华盛顿特区，一块屏幕上显示与伊朗有关联的黑客组织 Handala Hack Team 所使用的网站；该组织声称对入侵联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔的个人电子邮箱负责。（图片来源：路透社/Raphael Satter）\n除帕特尔的照片外，黑客还发布了300多封电子邮件的样本，内容似乎混合了2010年至2019年间的个人及工作往来信件。\n路透社无法独立验证这些帕特尔邮件，但 Handala 称其入侵的个人 Gmail 地址，与暗网情报公司 District 4 Labs 保存的先前数据泄露记录中关联帕特尔的地址一致。运营 Gmail 的 Alphabet 旗下 Google 未立即回应置评请求。\n查看更多：伊朗｜美国｜联邦调查局｜网络安全｜黑客入侵｜卡什·帕特尔｜Handala\n关注我们的 Google\n相关文章\n美国给予联合国时间结束对索马里维和人员的支持\n泽连斯基启动喀尔巴阡八国安全集团\n俄罗斯开始为期三天的国家杜马选举\n西班牙警方展开行动，将休达海滩上的移民清离\n巴基斯坦汽车炸弹袭击至少造成16人死亡\n伊朗战争与胡塞武装推进考验特朗普的和平缔造者主张\n亲以色列的美国前参议员乔恩·凯尔去世，享年84岁","publish_source":"jpost.com","publish_time":"2026-03-27T17:36:33+00:00"}},{"id":"news-546","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国官员称FBI局长卡什·帕特尔将于10月访问莫斯科","title_en":"US FBI Director Kash Patel to visit Moscow in October, US official says | The Jerusalem Post","summary_cn":"据Politico援引一名美国官员及知情人士报道，美国联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔计划于今年访问俄罗斯，预计10月中旬访问莫斯科和圣彼得堡，东道主可能是俄罗斯联邦安全局。帕特尔的讨论议程及会晤对象尚不清楚。白宫发言人让Politico向FBI寻求置评，FBI和司法部发言人均未回应。报道还提及帕特尔曾否认俄罗斯干预美国大选，并曾于2024年收受与克里姆林宫有关联电影公司2.5万美元。","summary_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel is planning to visit Russia this year, Politico reported, citing an unnamed US official and a person familiar with the situation. Patel is scheduled to visit Moscow in mid-October and also St. Petersburg, with his host likely the Russian secret service, the FSB. His agenda and meeting details remain unclear. White House spokespeople referred Politico to the FBI, while FBI and Justice Department spokespeople did not respond. The report also noted Patel has denied Russian election interference and was previously paid $25,000 by a Kremlin-linked film company in 2024.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:24:07.771146+00:00","url":"https://www.jpost.com/international/article-903156","content":"Jerusalem Post/World NewsFBI Director Kash Patel to visit Russia later this year, US official says - reportPolitico cited a US official saying Patel is scheduled to visit Moscow and St. Petersburg in mid-October. The official also said Patel's host is likely the Russian secret service.Follow us on GoogleFBI Director Kash Patel attends the signing of an executive order by U.S. President Donald Trump on a deal that would divest TikTok's U.S. operations from ByteDance from its Chinese owner ByteDance, at the White House in Washington, D.C., U.S.(photo credit: REUTERS/KEVIN LAMARQUE/FILE PHOTO)ByTZVI JASPERJULY 21, 2026 11:21FBI Director Kash Patel is planning on visiting Russia at some point this year, Politico reported on Monday, citing an unnamed US official and a person familiar with the situation.According to the US official, Patel is scheduled to visit Moscow in mid-October and also visit St. Petersburg. The official also told Politico that Patel's host is likely to be the Russian secret service, commonly known by the acronym FSB.Patel's agenda for discussion remains unclear, as do the details on who he will be meeting with. White House spokespeople referred Politico to the FBI for comment, while spokespeople for the FBI and Justice Department did not respond.Patel has spent years as FBI director denying claims of Russian interference in the United States election process, particularly in US President Donald Trump's first election in 2016.Politico reported that Patel had previously been paid $25,000 dollars by a film company linked to the Kremlin in 2024, after participating in a documentary series entitled All the President’s Men: The Conspiracy Against Trump.Patel accused of excessive drinkingPatel has also faced criticism over his alleged episodes of excessive drinking, which resulted in his grilling by Democratic lawmakers during a hearing before a Senate budget panel in May.During the panel, lawmakers questioned Patel about a report in the Atlantic magazine that detailed instances of \"conspicuous inebriation and unexplained absences\" during his tenure that had alarmed officials at the FBI and the Justice Department.Patel has sued the Atlantic and its reporter over the article, accusing them of defamation. The magazine has said it stands behind its reporting.Reuters contributed to this report.See more onRussia|Vladimir Putin|moscow|Donald Trump|FBI|Russia-US|Kash PatelFollow us on GoogleRelated ArticlesFrance allows Netanyahu overflight despite ICC warrantTrump-Xi meeting spotlights tests of UN's powerMahmoud Abbas denounces settlement expansion in West BankVance linked to article at center of White House press banKremlin brands EU asset transfer ‘theft’Russia invites Kim Jong Un to visit Moscow Denmark warns of Russian hybrid escalation","content_cn":"《耶路撒冷邮报》/世界新闻\n\nFBI局长卡什·帕特尔将于今年晚些时候访问俄罗斯，美国官员称——报道\n\nPolitico援引一名美国官员的话称，帕特尔计划于10月中旬访问莫斯科和圣彼得堡。该官员还表示，帕特尔的接待方可能是俄罗斯情报部门。\n\n在美国华盛顿特区白宫，美国总统唐纳德·特朗普签署一项行政命令，推动将TikTok在美国的业务从其中国所有者字节跳动剥离的交易时，FBI局长卡什·帕特尔出席签署仪式。（图片来源：路透社/凯文·拉马克/资料照片）\n\n作者：TZVI JASPER\n2026年7月21日 11:21\n\nPolitico周一援引一名未具名美国官员和一名知情人士的话报道，FBI局长卡什·帕特尔计划在今年某个时候访问俄罗斯。\n\n据这名美国官员称，帕特尔计划于10月中旬访问莫斯科，并前往圣彼得堡。该官员还告诉Politico，帕特尔的接待方可能是俄罗斯情报部门，即通常以缩写FSB为人所知的机构。\n\n帕特尔的讨论议程仍不清楚，他将与谁会面等细节也不得而知。白宫发言人让Politico向FBI置评，而FBI和司法部发言人均未回应。\n\n帕特尔担任FBI局长多年来一直否认俄罗斯干预美国选举进程的说法，尤其是否认俄罗斯干预美国总统唐纳德·特朗普于2016年首次参选时的选举。\n\nPolitico报道，帕特尔此前曾于2024年从一家与克里姆林宫有关联的电影公司获得25,000美元，此前他参与了一部名为《总统身边的人：针对特朗普的阴谋》的纪录片系列。\n\n帕特尔被指控酗酒过度\n\n帕特尔还因涉嫌多次过量饮酒而受到批评；5月，在参议院预算委员会举行听证会期间，他受到民主党议员的严厉质询。\n\n在委员会会议上，议员们就《大西洋月刊》一篇报道向帕特尔提问。该报道详细描述了他任职期间“明显醉酒和无法解释的缺席”情况，这些情况曾令FBI和司法部官员感到担忧。\n\n帕特尔已就该文章起诉《大西洋月刊》及其记者，指控其诽谤。该杂志表示坚持其报道。\n\n路透社为本报道提供素材。\n\n查看更多：俄罗斯｜弗拉基米尔·普京｜莫斯科｜唐纳德·特朗普｜FBI｜俄美关系｜卡什·帕特尔\n\n在Google上关注我们\n\n相关文章\n法国允许内塔尼亚胡飞越领空，尽管其面临国际刑事法院逮捕令\n特朗普与习近平会晤凸显对联合国权力的考验\n马哈茂德·阿巴斯谴责约旦河西岸定居点扩张\n万斯与白宫新闻禁令核心文章有关联\n克里姆林宫称欧盟资产转移为“盗窃”\n俄罗斯邀请金正恩访问莫斯科\n丹麦警告俄罗斯混合升级行动","publish_source":"jpost.com","publish_time":"2026-07-21T11:21:16+00:00"}},{"id":"news-940","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"威斯康星州州长埃弗斯称已为FBI任何选举调查做好准备","title_en":"Gov. Tony Evers says Wisconsin is prepared for any FBI election probe","summary_cn":"《密尔沃基哨兵报》报道，威斯康星州州长托尼·埃弗斯表示，他未获悉FBI在该州就2020年总统选举展开“大范围”调查，但已制定应对措施。此前该报披露FBI探员询问了州选举委员会副行政官罗伯特·基霍，并寻求约谈参与密尔沃基2020年选举工作的人员。报道称调查目的和范围尚不明确，FBI发言人多次拒绝置评。文章还提到佐治亚州富尔顿县选票被查封及亚利桑那州马里科帕县收到大陪审团传票等类似联邦行动。","summary_en":"The Milwaukee Journal Sentinel reported that Wisconsin Gov. Tony Evers said he has not been made aware of any widespread FBI effort to probe the 2020 presidential election in the state, but that measures are in place to respond. The comments followed reporting that FBI agents questioned Wisconsin Elections Commission deputy administrator Robert Kehoe and sought interviews with people who helped administer Milwaukee's 2020 election. The purpose and scope of the questioning remain unclear, and an FBI spokeswoman declined to comment. The article also notes similar federal actions in Fulton County, Georgia, and Maricopa County, Arizona.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T10:47:32.330151+00:00","url":"https://www.jsonline.com/story/news/politics/2026/05/18/gov-tony-evers-says-wisconsin-is-prepared-for-any-fbi-election-probe/90132492007","content":"POLITICSGov. Tony Evers says Wisconsin is prepared for any FBI election probe Molly BeckMilwaukee Journal SentinelUpdated May 18, 2026, 9:49 a.m. CTThe FBI has questioned Wisconsin election officials about the 2020 presidential election.Wisconsin Gov. Tony Evers stated he is not aware of a widespread FBI effort but has measures in place to respond.The purpose and scope of the FBI's questions remain unclear.Similar federal actions regarding the 2020 election have occurred in Georgia and Arizona.MADISON - Wisconsin Gov. Tony Evers says he has not been made aware of any \"widespread\" Federal Bureau of Investigation effort to probe the 2020 presidential election in this battleground state but has measures in place to respond if one materializes.Evers made the comments days after the Milwaukee Journal Sentinel first reported FBI agents had questioned a top state election official and have sought interviews with people who helped administer Milwaukee's 2020 election.It's so far unclear what the goals are of the questions.A spokeswoman for the FBI has repeatedly declined to answer questions about the probe's scope and purpose. But sources told the Journal Sentinel the FBI's interview with Wisconsin Elections Commission deputy administrator Robert Kehoe focused on how elections work in Wisconsin and debunking conspiracy theories about the 2020 election in the state.\"No, I'm not,\" Evers told WISN 12 News political reporter Matt Smith when asked if Evers was aware of \"widespread FBI activity here in the state.\"\"I haven't heard it, but we are adequately prepared and I won't tell you what pieces are in place but we're prepared to make sure that our elections happen safely,\" Evers said about November's elections.\"We have plans to, if they show up, we will be there to make sure that they are asking for what they have access to but also making sure that they're not doing what they shouldn't do,\" he said.The Wisconsin probe comes after federal officials in January seized hundreds of boxes of ballots related to the 2020 election in Fulton County, Georgia, and after the FBI issued a grand jury subpoena in March for voting information in Maricopa County, Arizona.Georgia, Arizona and Wisconsin have all been central to Trump's false claims that he won the 2020 election. Trump has insisted, without evidence, that former President Joe Biden didn’t win in Wisconsin that year.More: Trump re-ups myth about Wisconsin voter numbers. Here are the factsA recount in two Wisconsin counties that Trump's campaign paid for, court rulings, a state audit and a conservative review have confirmed that Trump lost. Biden defeated Trump in Wisconsin by about 21,000 votes.Officials in Wisconsin – and especially Milwaukee – have been bracing for an investigation.If federal officials advance an investigation of the 2020 election in Milwaukee, it's possible that poll books and nearly 180,000 absentee ballots with attached ID numbers could be turned over to investigators. Since state law requires absentee ballots counted at a central counting facility to include poll list numbers, the data could be matched with poll book information to identify voters.Ballots from the 2020 election typically would have been destroyed by now. But Milwaukee's 2020 ballots still exist, partly because of a lawsuit filed against the city by a New London man who has sued state and local election officials over the 2020 election and related issues.Sources told the Journal Sentinel earlier this month no ballots have been seized by the FBI.Agents sought to question one of Milwaukee County's top election officials about the 2020 presidential election at her home last week. Evers said the agents' decision to visit her home was \"bizarre.\"Molly Beck can be reached at molly.beck@jrn.com.Featured Weekly Ad","content_cn":"政治\n托尼·埃弗斯州长称威斯康星州已准备应对任何 FBI 选举调查\nMolly Beck\n《密尔沃基哨兵日报》\n更新于2026年5月18日，中部时间上午9:49\nFBI 已就2020年总统选举询问威斯康星州选举官员。\n威斯康星州州长托尼·埃弗斯表示，他不知道 FBI 是否在开展大范围行动，但已采取措施应对。\nFBI 提问的目的和范围仍不明确。\n类似的联邦行动也曾在佐治亚州和亚利桑那州针对2020年选举展开。\n麦迪逊——威斯康星州州长托尼·埃弗斯表示，他没有被告知联邦调查局（FBI）在这个摇摆州对2020年总统选举展开任何“广泛”调查，但如果调查出现，他已采取措施应对。\n埃弗斯发表上述言论前几天，《密尔沃基哨兵日报》首次报道，FBI 特工已询问该州一名高级选举官员，并寻求采访协助管理密尔沃基市2020年选举的人员。\n目前尚不清楚这些问题的目标是什么。\nFBI 女发言人多次拒绝回答有关调查范围和目的的问题。但消息人士告诉《哨兵日报》，FBI 对威斯康星州选举委员会副行政长官罗伯特·基奥的采访，重点是威斯康星州选举如何运作，以及揭穿有关该州2020年选举的阴谋论。\n当 WISN 12 新闻政治记者马特·史密斯问埃弗斯是否知道“FBI 在本州开展广泛活动”时，埃弗斯回答：“不，我不知道。”\n埃弗斯谈到11月的选举时说：“我没有听说过，但我们已经做好充分准备。我不会告诉你具体有哪些安排，但我们已准备好确保选举安全进行。”\n他说：“如果他们出现，我们有计划应对；我们会确保他们只询问自己有权获取的信息，同时也确保他们不做不该做的事。”\n威斯康星州的调查发生在联邦官员今年1月没收佐治亚州富尔顿县数百箱与2020年选举有关的选票之后，也发生在 FBI 今年3月向亚利桑那州马里科帕县发出大陪审团传票、要求提供投票信息之后。\n佐治亚州、亚利桑那州和威斯康星州一直是特朗普虚假声称自己赢得2020年选举的核心地区。特朗普毫无证据地坚持认为，前总统乔·拜登当年没有赢得威斯康星州。\n更多：特朗普再次炒作威斯康星州选民人数的神话。事实如下\n特朗普竞选团队出资的威斯康星州两个县重新计票、法院裁决、州审计以及保守派审查均已确认特朗普落败。拜登在威斯康星州以约2.1万票击败特朗普。\n威斯康星州，尤其是密尔沃基的官员，一直在为调查做准备。\n如果联邦官员推进对密尔沃基2020年选举的调查，投票名册以及近18万张附有身份编号的缺席选票可能会被移交给调查人员。由于州法律要求，在中央计票设施统计的缺席选票必须包含投票名单编号，这些数据可以与投票名册信息匹配，以识别选民。\n2020年选举的选票通常到现在早已被销毁。但密尔沃基2020年的选票仍然存在，部分原因是一名来自新伦敦的男子对该市提起诉讼；此人还因2020年选举及相关问题起诉州和地方选举官员。\n消息人士本月早些时候告诉《哨兵日报》，目前没有选票被 FBI 扣押。\n上周，特工前往密尔沃基县一名高级选举官员的住所，试图就2020年总统选举向她提问。埃弗斯称，特工决定上门拜访她“很古怪”。\n可通过 molly.beck@jrn.com 联系 Molly Beck。\n每周精选广告","publish_source":"jsonline.com","publish_time":"2026-05-18T10:04:38+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3568","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国国土安全部称美加边境寻求庇护者与律师会面时间因新安全政策而缩短","title_en":"US Homeland Security says asylum seekers at Canada border have less time with lawyers as part of new security policies - JURIST - News","summary_cn":"美国国土安全部向CBS新闻提供内部文件，披露美加边境两项政策调整：寻求庇护者与律师会面的最短时间从24小时缩短至4小时，且须提前备好文件以供筛查是否适用2002年《安全第三国协议》。DHS表示此举可在不影响非公民获得完整公正庇护程序的前提下简化边境流程，两项变化于2024年8月14日生效，但DHS尚未公布内部文件或发布官方声明。","summary_en":"The US Department of Homeland Security shared internal documents with CBS News revealing two changes to Canada-US border policy: the minimum time asylum seekers have with lawyers drops from 24 to 4 hours, and migrants must have documents ready for screening under the 2002 Safe Third Country Agreement. DHS said the changes streamline the border process without affecting access to a full and fair asylum procedure. Both took effect August 14, 2024, though DHS has not published the documents or an official statement.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:36:20.573811+00:00","url":"https://www.jurist.org/news/2024/08/us-homeland-security-says-asylum-migrants-at-canada-border-have-less-time-with-lawyers-as-part-of-new-security-policies","content":"NewsMakaristos, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons\nUS Homeland Security says asylum seekers at Canada border have less time with lawyers as part of new security policies\nDrew Meetze | U. Ottawa Faculty of Law, CA\nAugust 14, 2024 03:15:30 pm\nThe US Department of Homeland Security (DHS) shared internal documents with CBS News on Tuesday concerning two incoming changes to border policies for the Canada-US border, which will aim to expedite the processing time on migrants’ applications for border officials. These changes include decreasing the time migrants are allowed with their lawyers from a minimum of 24 hours to a minimum of 4 hours. Migrants will now also be required to have their official documents ready for screening to see if they are subject to the 2002 Safe Third Country Agreement (STCA) between Canada and the US. Before this update, migrants who were exempt from the STCA’s application could delay their screening to collect their supporting documents. The STCA allows Canada and the US to share the responsibility of processing refugee applications. According to the STCA, whichever country an applicant arrives in first is the country in which the applicant must apply for refugee status. In 2023, the STCA was updated to expand its effect to include migrants who enter the countries at any border entry, unofficial or official. This expansion targeted irregular border crossings Canada began to experience upon the closure of an official entry point, Roxham Road in Quebec. The Supreme Court of Canada (SCC) revisited the constitutionality of the STCA in a 2023 decision where the plaintiff refugee applicants argued their rights protected by the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms had been violated, particularly when one of the plaintiffs was subject to the STCA, returned to the US and detained. The SCC held the plaintiffs’ section 7 Charter rights had not been violated, but remitted the section 15 claim to the Federal Court. In regards to these incoming policy changes, DHS explained: DHS carefully reviewed its implementation of the Safe Third Country Agreement with Canada and concluded that it could streamline that process at the border without impacting noncitizens’ ability to have access to a full and fair procedure for determining a claim to asylum or equivalent temporary protection. DHS has confirmed these two policy changes will begin effect on August 14, 2024. DHS has yet to publish the internal documents or release any official statement on its website.","content_cn":"NewsMakaristos，公共领域，来自维基共享资源\n美国国土安全部称，作为新安全政策的一部分，加拿大边境的寻求庇护者与律师相处的时间减少\nDrew Meetze｜加拿大渥太华大学法学院\n2024年8月14日下午03:15:30\n美国国土安全部（DHS）周二向CBS新闻分享了有关加美边境政策即将发生的两项变化的内部文件，这些变化旨在加快边境官员处理移民申请的时间。这些变化包括将移民获准与律师相处的时间从至少24小时缩短至至少4小时。移民现在还必须准备好官方文件，以便接受审查，确定他们是否受2002年加拿大与美国签署的《安全第三国协定》（STCA）约束。在此次更新之前，免于适用STCA的移民可以推迟审查，以收集证明文件。STCA允许加拿大和美国分担处理难民申请的责任。根据STCA，申请人首先抵达哪个国家，就必须在哪个国家申请难民身份。2023年，STCA进行了更新，将其适用范围扩大到在任何边境入口（无论是非官方还是官方）进入两国的移民。这一扩展针对的是加拿大在魁北克省一个官方入境点罗克瑟姆路关闭后开始出现的非正常越境。加拿大最高法院（SCC）在2023年的一项判决中重新审视了STCA的合宪性，原告难民申请人主张，他们受《加拿大权利与自由宪章》保护的权利遭到侵犯，尤其是在其中一名原告受STCA约束、被遣返回美国并遭拘留的情况下。SCC裁定，原告依据《宪章》第7条享有的权利没有受到侵犯，但将依据第15条提出的主张发回联邦法院审理。关于这些即将实施的政策变化，DHS解释道：\nDHS仔细审查了其与加拿大实施《安全第三国协定》的方式，并得出结论认为，可以在不影响非公民获得完整、公平程序以确定其庇护申请或同等临时保护资格的能力的情况下，在边境简化这一流程。\nDHS已确认，这两项政策变化将于2024年8月14日开始生效。DHS尚未公布这些内部文件，也未在其网站上发布任何官方声明。","publish_source":"jurist.org","publish_time":"2024-08-14T19:15:30-04:00"}},{"id":"news-3185","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国国土安全部长称关塔那摩湾被拘留移民将获得正当程序","title_en":"US Homeland Security Secretary says migrants detained in Guantanamo Bay will receive due process - JURIST - News","summary_cn":"美国国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆在接受NBC新闻采访时表示，联邦政府将对所有被转移至古巴关塔那摩湾的移民遵循正当程序。她称关塔那摩湾用于关押“最恶劣的”人员，并否认计划无限期拘留。此前特朗普签署行政令，要求关塔那摩湾移民行动中心达到满负荷，古巴官员对此计划反应强烈。","summary_en":"US Department of Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem said in an NBC News interview that the federal government will follow due process for all migrants transferred to Guantanamo Bay, Cuba. She said the facility is for the \"worst of the worst\" and denied plans for indefinite detention. The comments followed President Trump's executive order authorizing the Guantanamo Bay Migrant Operations Center to reach full capacity, which drew harsh criticism from Cuban officials.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:09:03.372584+00:00","url":"https://www.jurist.org/news/2025/02/us-homeland-security-secretary-says-migrants-detained-in-guantanamo-bay-will-receive-due-process","content":"NewsDigital scan of postcard, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons\n(1948)\nUS Homeland Security Secretary says migrants detained in Guantanamo Bay will receive due process\nSean Beeghly | U. Pittsburgh School of Law, US\nFebruary 3, 2025 08:00:56 pm\nUS Department of Homeland Security (DHS) Secretary Kristi Noem stated in an interview Sunday with NBC News that the federal government will follow due process for all migrants transferred to Guantanamo Bay, Cuba.The comment followed a question by NBC’s “Meet the Press” host, Kristen Welker, about whether migrants will have due process rights and access to attorneys as they would in the US. Noem stated, “Due process will be followed.” She said that the facilities located at the naval base had a long history of housing “illegal immigrants,” and had the capacity to handle these issues.Welker also expressed concerns that officials could hold migrants at the facility indefinitely. As of January, 15 detainees from the War on Terror remain in detention, some for over 20 years. Noem stated that indefinite detention was “not the plan.” She elaborated that DHS was working with Congress to develop immigration laws to lay out deportation processes and timelines.When asked if officials would eventually hold “women, children, and families” at the base, Noem stated that Guantanamo Bay was for the “worst of the worst.” Furthermore, she noted that the federal government may utilize other facilities for non-dangerous migrants.President Trump signed an executive order last week authorizing the Guantanamo Bay Migrant Operations Center to reach full capacity. Trump stated in a briefing that the detention facility contains “30,000 beds,” and will “double” US holding capacity.Reaction from Cuban officials to the plan was harsh. Cuban President Miguel Diaz-Canel described the US plan on X as an “act of brutality,” and stated that the detention facility was known for “torture and illegal detention.”","content_cn":"新闻\n明信片扫描图，公有领域，来自 Wikimedia Commons\n（1948年）\n美国国土安全部长称，被拘留在关塔那摩湾的移民将获得正当程序\nSean Beeghly｜美国匹兹堡大学法学院\n2025年2月3日晚上08:00:56\n美国国土安全部（DHS）部长克里斯蒂·诺姆周日接受 NBC 新闻采访时表示，联邦政府将对所有被转移到古巴关塔那摩湾的移民遵循正当程序。\n此前，NBC《新闻会客厅》主持人克里斯汀·韦尔克询问，这些移民是否会像在美国一样享有正当程序权利并获得律师帮助。诺姆表示：“将遵循正当程序。”她说，海军基地内的设施有长期收容“非法移民”的历史，并且有能力处理这些问题。\n韦尔克还表达了官员可能无限期将移民关押在该设施的担忧。截至1月，仍有15名反恐战争期间的被拘留者被关押，其中一些人已超过20年。诺姆表示，无限期拘留“不是计划”。她进一步解释说，国土安全部正与国会合作制定移民法，以明确遣返程序和时间表。\n当被问及官员最终是否会在基地关押“妇女、儿童和家庭”时，诺姆表示，关塔那摩湾是关押“最危险的人”。此外，她指出，联邦政府可能会利用其他设施安置不具危险性的移民。\n特朗普总统上周签署行政命令，授权关塔那摩湾移民运营中心达到满负荷。特朗普在一次简报会上表示，该拘留设施拥有“3万张床位”，并将使美国的收容能力“翻倍”。\n古巴官员对这一计划的反应十分强烈。古巴总统米格尔·迪亚斯-卡内尔在 X 上称美国计划是“野蛮行径”，并表示该拘留设施以“酷刑和非法拘禁”闻名。","publish_source":"jurist.org","publish_time":"2025-02-04T01:00:56-05:00"}},{"id":"news-3034","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"特朗普政府证实裁撤国土安全部监督办公室","title_en":"Trump administration confirms Department of Homeland Security oversight office cuts - JURIST - News","summary_cn":"美国国土安全部发言人特里西娅·麦克劳克林证实，该部监督办公室遭到裁撤，包括公民权利与公民自由办公室及移民拘留监察员办公室。麦克劳克林称这些办公室妨碍移民执法、浪费纳税人资金。这是继2月裁员后国土安全部遭受的第二轮裁员。民主党议员此前致信部长诺姆，强调这些办公室的重要职能。","summary_en":"US Department of Homeland Security spokesperson Tricia McLaughlin confirmed cuts to DHS oversight offices, including the Office for Civil Rights and Civil Liberties and the Office of the Immigration Detention Ombudsman. McLaughlin said the offices obstructed immigration enforcement and misused taxpayer funds. It is the second round of firings to hit DHS after a February wave of layoffs. Democratic lawmakers had written to Secretary Kristi Noem stressing the offices' essential functions.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:57:27.239060+00:00","url":"https://www.jurist.org/news/2025/03/trump-administration-confirms-department-of-homeland-security-oversight-office-cuts","content":"News© WikiMedia (US Department of Homeland Security (DHS))\nTrump administration confirms Department of Homeland Security oversight office cuts\nSean Nolan | Southwestern Law School, US\nMarch 23, 2025 07:58:30 pm\nUS Department of Homeland Security (DHS) spokesperson Tricia McLaughlin on Friday confirmed cuts to DHS oversight offices, including the Office for Civil Rights and Civil Liberties and the Office of the Immigration Detention Ombudsman, in the newest round of government layoffs under the Trump administration.In text messages confirming the cuts to Bloomberg News, McLaughlin excoriated the department’s affected sectors: “These offices have obstructed immigration enforcement by adding bureaucratic hurdles and undermining DHS’s mission.”“Rather than supporting law enforcement efforts, they often function as internal adversaries that slow down operations,” McLaughlin continued.McLaughlin accused the affected offices of “misusing taxpayer funds” and contributing to illegal immigration. In addition to the aforementioned offices, the Office of the Citizenship and Immigration Services Ombudsman was also targeted in the cuts.Together these offices served oversight roles in the DHS by investigating rights violations, public complaints, and ensuring the DHS followed proper procedures and protocols.This is the second round of firings to hit the DHS after a February wave of layoffs targeted other areas of the department including cybersecurity, technology, disaster response, and science. Democrat lawmakers authored a letter to the Secretary of the Department of Homeland Security Kristi Noem before news of the latest cuts came out highlighting the essential functions of affected offices in the department:From the establishment of DHS, Congress’s intent was clear–given the Department’s impacts on the lives of everyone in the United States, including DHS’s own employees, it is essential that there be an Office responsible for oversight of how DHS’s work impacted civil rights and civil liberties, starting with policy development and continuing through implementation and oversight.The Department of Homeland Security was created shortly after the 9/11 attacks by the Homeland Security Act of 2002. It has expanded from further congressional action over the last 20 years and is now the third largest Presidential Cabinet Department. Areas under its control include the Office of Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE), the Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA), the Transportation Security Administration (TSA), the Coast Guard and the Secret Service.","content_cn":"新闻© 维基媒体（美国国土安全部（DHS））\n特朗普政府确认削减国土安全部监督办公室\nSean Nolan | 美国西南法学院\n2025年3月23日晚上07:58:30\n美国国土安全部（DHS）发言人特里西娅·麦克劳克林周五确认，DHS正在削减包括民权与公民自由办公室以及移民拘留监察员办公室在内的监督办公室，这是特朗普政府最新一轮政府裁员的一部分。在通过短信向彭博新闻社确认这些裁员时，麦克劳克林严厉批评了该部门受影响的部门：“这些办公室通过增加官僚障碍、削弱DHS的使命，阻碍了移民执法。”麦克劳克林继续说道：“它们非但没有支持执法工作，反而常常充当内部对手，拖慢行动。”麦克劳克林指责受影响的办公室“滥用纳税人资金”，并助长非法移民。除上述办公室外，公民身份与移民服务监察员办公室也成为此次裁员的目标。这些办公室共同在DHS中承担监督职能，包括调查权利侵犯和公众投诉，并确保DHS遵循适当的程序和规程。这是继2月份裁员潮之后，DHS遭遇的第二轮解雇；此前的裁员针对该部门的其他领域，包括网络安全、技术、灾害响应和科学。在最新一轮裁员消息传出前，民主党议员曾致信国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆，强调受影响办公室在该部门中的重要职能：自DHS成立以来，国会的意图就很明确——鉴于该部门对美国每个人（包括DHS自身雇员）生活的影响，必须设立一个负责监督DHS工作如何影响民权和公民自由的办公室，从政策制定开始，并贯穿实施和监督全过程。国土安全部是在“9·11”袭击后不久依据《2002年国土安全法》成立的。在过去20年中，随着国会进一步采取行动，该部门不断扩张，如今已成为总统内阁中规模第三大的部门。其管辖领域包括移民与海关执法局（ICE）、联邦紧急事务管理局（FEMA）、运输安全管理局（TSA）、海岸警卫队和特勤局。","publish_source":"jurist.org","publish_time":"2025-03-23T23:58:30-04:00"}},{"id":"news-2962","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国联邦法官叫停国土安全部未经正当程序将非公民遣送至外国的行动","title_en":"US federal judge halts Homeland Security efforts to remove non-citizens to foreign countries without due process - JURIST - News","summary_cn":"马萨诸塞州联邦法官布赖恩·墨菲批准初步禁令，阻止特朗普政府实施国土安全部允许将数百名移民快速遣送至非其本国的政策。墨菲认定原告在实体上可能胜诉，并批准面临遣返令的非美国公民获得集体诉讼资格。国土安全部辩称非公民可申请重开移民程序，但法官认为该救济在法律上不充分且操作上不可行。","summary_en":"A federal judge in Massachusetts, Brian Murphy, granted a preliminary injunction barring the Trump administration from implementing a Department of Homeland Security policy allowing rapid deportation of hundreds of migrants to countries other than their own without due process. Murphy found the plaintiffs likely to succeed on the merits and granted class-action status to non-citizens facing removal orders. DHS argued non-citizens could move to reopen proceedings, but the judge called that remedy legally insufficient and logistically impossible.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:50:59.880348+00:00","url":"https://www.jurist.org/news/2025/04/us-judge-puts-homeland-security-efforts-to-remove-non-citizens-on-hold","content":"NewsU.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons\nUS federal judge halts Homeland Security efforts to remove non-citizens to foreign countries without due process\nEmily Corio | U. Dayton School of Law, US\nApril 20, 2025 02:45:23 pm\nA federal judge in Massachusetts on Friday barred the Trump administration from implementing a Department of Homeland Security (DHS) policy allowing the rapid deportation of hundreds of migrants to countries other than their own without due process.US District Court Judge Brian Murphy granted the plaintiffs’ request for a preliminary injunction on the DHS policy. The injunction effectively halts the DHS from implementing the policy until the legal claims play out in court.In granting the injunction, Murphy found that the plaintiffs showed a likelihood of success on the merits, a possibility of irreparable harm if the injunction is not granted, a balance of hardships that favored the plaintiff, and that the injunction is in the public interest. “Plaintiffs are simply asking to be told they are going to be deported to a new country before they are taken to such a country, and be given an opportunity to explain why such a deportation will likely result in their persecution, torture, and/or death,” Murphy wrote.The order also grants class-action status to non-US citizens who are facing removal orders and may be sent to a country not designated in their initial immigration proceedings. The order cites hundreds of potential class members. The court explained, “What Plaintiffs challenge is Defendants’ authority to effectively depart from the removal orders by designating new countries for removal outside of the immigration proceedings and, in doing so, circumvent Plaintiffs’ due-process rights…”DHS argues that the non-citizens can file motions to reopen their immigration proceedings, but Murphy wrote in his order that this presents a “legally insufficient and logistically impossible” remedy and that the government’s “obligations under Convention Against Torture (CAT) and the Due Process Clause require more.”Immigrants may seek refuge in the US from violence in their home countries. In immigration removal proceedings, they can make a case not to be returned to their home country due to fear of being persecuted, tortured, or killed if they are returned, or perhaps to a neighboring country.DHS issued a directive in February to Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) to review cases with removal orders to determine whether these non-citizens could be sent to other countries. The DHS guidance announced in March permits sending non-citizens to countries where officials have “provided diplomatic assurances that aliens removed from the United States will not be persecuted or tortured…and if the Department of State believes those assurances to be credible, the alien may be removed without the need for further procedures.”Prior to the order Friday, Murphy had issued a temporary restraining order against DHS in the same case.","content_cn":"新闻\n美国移民与海关执法局，美国政府公共领域作品，经维基共享资源发布\n美国联邦法官叫停国土安全部未经正当程序将非公民遣送至外国的行动\nEmily Corio | 美国代顿大学法学院\n2025年4月20日 下午02:45:23\n马萨诸塞州一名联邦法官周五禁止特朗普政府实施国土安全部（DHS）的一项政策。该政策允许在未经正当程序的情况下，将数百名移民迅速驱逐到并非其本国的其他国家。\n美国地区法院法官Brian Murphy批准了原告针对DHS该政策提出的初步禁令请求。该禁令实际上暂停DHS实施这项政策，直至法院审理完相关法律主张。\nMurphy在批准禁令时认定，原告证明了其诉求在实体问题上胜诉的可能性、若不颁发禁令可能遭受不可弥补损害的可能性、对原告有利的困难平衡，以及禁令符合公共利益。“原告只是要求，在他们被带往一个新国家之前，先被告知他们将被驱逐到该国，并获得机会解释为什么这种驱逐很可能导致他们遭受迫害、酷刑和/或死亡，”Murphy写道。\n该命令还赋予集体诉讼地位，覆盖面临遣送令、且可能被送往其最初移民程序中未指定国家的非美国公民。命令提到，潜在集体成员有数百人。法院解释说：“原告所质疑的是，被告是否有权在移民程序之外指定新的遣送国家，从而实质性偏离遣送令，并在此过程中规避原告的正当程序权利……”\nDHS辩称，非公民可以提出动议，要求重新启动其移民程序；但Murphy在命令中写道，这是一种“法律上不足且在后勤上不可能”的救济，而且政府“根据《禁止酷刑公约》（CAT）和正当程序条款承担的义务要求更多”。\n移民可能因本国的暴力而寻求在美国避难。在移民遣送程序中，他们可以提出理由，说明由于担心被迫害、遭受酷刑或被杀害，若被遣返回本国，或许被遣往邻国，他们不应被送回。\nDHS于2月向移民与海关执法局（ICE）发布指令，要求审查已有遣送令的案件，以确定这些非公民是否可以被送往其他国家。DHS在3月发布的指导意见允许将非公民送往这样的国家：当地官员“已提供外交保证，保证从美国遣返的外国人不会遭受迫害或酷刑……如果国务院认为这些保证可信，该外国人即可被遣返，无需进一步程序”。\n在周五的命令之前，Murphy已在同一案件中对DHS发布临时限制令。","publish_source":"jurist.org","publish_time":"2025-04-20T18:45:23-04:00"}},{"id":"news-2268","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"前FBI局长对妨碍司法和虚假陈述指控作无罪抗辩","title_en":"Former FBI director pleads not guilty to obstruction of justice and false statement charges - JURIST - News","summary_cn":"前FBI局长詹姆斯·科米周三对美国司法部指控其在国会听证中作虚假陈述的罪名作无罪抗辩。起诉涉及科米2020年的陈述，他曾在2017年告诉国会未授权与特朗普政府相关调查有关的泄密。科米在社交媒体视频中坚称自己无罪，称对司法部感到心碎但相信联邦司法系统。审判定于1月5日进行，其团队计划以报复性和选择性起诉等理由提出动议。","summary_en":"Former FBI Director James Comey pleaded not guilty on Wednesday to US Department of Justice charges accusing him of lying during a congressional hearing. The indictment concerns statements Comey made in 2020; he told Congress in 2017 that he did not authorize leaks related to investigations of the first Trump administration. In an Instagram video, Comey maintained his innocence, saying his heart is broken for the DOJ but he has confidence in the federal judiciary. Trial is set for January 5, and his team plans motions challenging the case as vindictive and selective prosecution.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:03:17.022839+00:00","url":"https://www.jurist.org/news/2025/10/former-fbi-director-pleas-not-guilty-to-obstruction-of-justice-and-false-statement-charges","content":"NewsFederal Bureau of Investigation (FBI), Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons\nFormer FBI director pleads not guilty to obstruction of justice and false statement charges\nMorgan Polen | U. Pittsburgh School of Law, US\nOctober 9, 2025 08:02:48 pm\nFormer FBI director James Comey on Wednesday pleaded not guilty to US Department of Justice charges accusing him of lying during a congressional hearing.The indictment concerns statements that Comey made in 2020. Comey told Congress in 2017 that he did not authorize leaks related to various investigations of the first Trump administration and other matters. At the hearing in question, on September 30, 2020, he defended his position, stating: “I can only speak to my testimony. I stand by the testimony you summarized that I gave in May of 2017.”In a recent video posted to Instagram, Comey maintained his innocence:My family and I have known for years that there are costs to standing up to Donald Trump. But we couldn’t imagine ourselves living any other way. We will not live on our knees, and you shouldn’t either… Fear is the tool of a tyrant, but I’m not afraid, and I hope you’re not either… My heart is broken for the Department of Justice, but I have great confidence in the federal judicial system, and I’m innocent, so let’s have a trial.Comey, the primary individual responsible for investigating Trump’s campaign-links to Russia, was indicted in September. Charges against him came days after Trump urged Attorney General Pam Bondi on social media to pursue legal action against him and other political rivals:Pam: I have reviewed over 30 statements and posts saying that, essentially, “same old story as last time, all talk, no action. Nothing is being done. What about Comey, Adam “Shifty” Schiff, Leticia [James]??? They’re all guilty as hell, but nothing is going to be done”…  JUSTICE MUST BE SERVED, NOW!!!Comey had served in the Justice Department since the George W. Bush administration, and was fired as FBI director by Trump in 2017. Trump has continued to target Comey since he helped spark Robert Mueller’s investigation into Russian interference in the 2016 election.Trial has been set for January 5. Comey’s team has said it plans on filing motions to challenge the case as a vindictive and selective prosecution as well as the appointment of Lindsey Halligan, Trump’s former personal attorney, as US attorney for the Eastern District of Virginia, where the case was brought.","content_cn":"新闻\n联邦调查局（FBI），公共领域，经维基共享资源提供\n\n前联邦调查局局长被控妨碍司法和作虚假陈述，拒不认罪\n\nMorgan Polen｜美国匹兹堡大学法学院\n2025年10月9日晚上08:02:48\n\n前联邦调查局局长詹姆斯·科米周三对美国司法部指控其在国会听证会上撒谎的罪名表示不认罪。起诉书涉及科米在2020年作出的陈述。科米在2017年告诉国会，他没有授权泄露与特朗普第一届政府的各种调查及其他事项有关的信息。在相关听证会上，即2020年9月30日，他为自己的立场辩护，称：“我只能谈我的证词。我坚持你们总结的、我在2017年5月作出的证词。”\n\n科米最近在Instagram发布的一段视频中坚持自己的清白：\n\n多年来，我和我的家人都知道，站出来反对唐纳德·特朗普是要付出代价的。但我们无法想象自己以其他方式生活。我们不会跪着活着，你们也不应该……恐惧是暴君的工具，但我不害怕，我希望你们也不害怕……我为司法部感到心碎，但我对联邦司法系统有很大信心，而且我是无辜的，所以让我们进行审判吧。\n\n科米是负责调查特朗普竞选团队与俄罗斯关系的主要人士，于9月被起诉。特朗普敦促司法部长帕姆·邦迪在社交媒体上对科米及其他政治对手采取法律行动，几天后，对科米的指控便提出了：\n\n帕姆：我审阅了30多条声明和帖子，它们基本上都在说：“和上次一样的老故事，只说不做。什么都没做。科米、亚当‘狡猾’·希夫、莱蒂西亚［詹姆斯］呢？他们全都罪大恶极，但什么都不会发生”……现在必须伸张正义！！！\n\n科米自乔治·W·布什政府时期起便在司法部任职，2017年被特朗普解雇联邦调查局局长职务。自科米帮助促成罗伯特·穆勒对俄罗斯干预2016年选举的调查以来，特朗普一直在针对他。\n\n审判已定于1月5日举行。科米的团队表示，计划提交动议，质疑此案属于报复性和选择性起诉，并质疑林赛·霍利根的任命；霍利根曾是特朗普的私人律师，现任弗吉尼亚东区美国检察官，而案件正是在该地区提起的。","publish_source":"jurist.org","publish_time":"2025-10-10T00:02:48-04:00"}},{"id":"news-2286","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"非营利组织起诉FBI和司法部隐瞒霍曼贿赂案视频","title_en":"Nonprofit sues FBI and DOJ for withholding video in Homan bribery case - JURIST - News","summary_cn":"非营利组织Democracy Forward周一起诉美国司法部和FBI，指其在涉及前ICE代理局长、现白宫“边境沙皇”汤姆·霍曼的涉嫌贿赂案中未公布关键录像。霍曼被指于2024年9月从FBI卧底探员处收受装有5万美元现金的袋子。尽管国会多次要求、媒体广泛报道，DOJ和FBI仍未公布录像，并于9月20日称未发现可信的犯罪证据后结案。诉讼依据《信息自由法》要求加快处理并公布非豁免部分。","summary_en":"Nonprofit Democracy Forward sued the US Department of Justice and FBI on Monday for failing to release key video recordings in an alleged bribery case involving former ICE director and current White House \"Border Czar\" Tom Homan. Homan allegedly accepted a bag with $50,000 in cash from undercover FBI agents in September 2024. Despite congressional requests and media coverage, the DOJ and FBI have not released the video and closed the investigation on September 20, saying they found no credible evidence of criminal wrongdoing. The suit cites FOIA and seeks expedited release of non-exempt portions.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:03:24.509862+00:00","url":"https://www.jurist.org/news/2025/10/nonprofit-sues-fbi-and-doj-for-withholding-video-in-alleged-bribery-case","content":"NewsU.S. Customs and Border Protection, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons\nPhotographer: Donna Burton\nNonprofit sues FBI and DOJ for withholding video in Homan bribery case\nSofia Jenkins | U. Pittsburgh School of Law, US\nOctober 7, 2025 08:36:24 pm\nNonprofit organization Democracy Forward sued the US Department of Justice (DOJ) and FBI on Monday after the agency failed to release key video recordings in an alleged bribery scheme case involving former Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) director Tom Homan.Homan, currently Trump’s White House “Border Czar,” became the subject of a federal bribery investigation after he allegedly accepted a bag filled with $50,000 in cash from undercover FBI agents in September 2024. Agents reportedly posed as business executives and gave Homan the money after he offered to help them win government contracts in the second Trump administration.Despite multiple requests from congressional representatives, extensive media coverage, and possible information leaks to news outlets, the DOJ and FBI have not released a video recording showing Homan accepting the cash. On September 20, the FBI and DOJ issued a statement saying they “found no credible evidence of any criminal wrongdoing” and have subsequently closed the investigation. The lawsuit argued that if the DOJ and FBI withhold such information, it runs afoul of the Freedom of Information Act (FOIA), which provides US citizens the right to request access to records from any US agency. Federal agencies must disclose any information requested under FOIA unless it falls within one of nine exemption categories.Democracy Forward is a nonprofit organization based in Washington, D.C. the aims to promote government transparency and inform the public on government action. The organization requests relief in the form of an order requiring the DOJ and FBI to grant expedited processing and promptly release the non-exempt portions of the recording.","content_cn":"新闻 美国海关与边境保护局，公有领域，经由维基共享资源\n摄影师：Donna Burton\n非营利组织起诉 FBI 和 DOJ，称其在霍曼贿赂案中扣留视频\nSofia Jenkins | 美国匹兹堡大学法学院\n2025 年 10 月 7 日 08:36:24 pm\n非营利组织 Democracy Forward 周一起诉美国司法部（DOJ）和联邦调查局（FBI），原因是该机构未能公布一宗涉嫌贿赂案中的关键视频录像，该案涉及前美国移民及海关执法局（ICE）局长 Tom Homan。Homan 现任特朗普白宫“边境沙皇”，据称他于 2024 年 9 月从卧底 FBI 特工手中收下一袋装有 50,000 美元现金后，成为联邦贿赂调查的对象。据报道，这些特工冒充企业高管，在 Homan 提出帮助他们在第二届特朗普政府中赢得政府合同后将钱交给了他。尽管国会代表多次提出请求、媒体进行了广泛报道，并且可能存在向新闻媒体泄露信息的情况，DOJ 和 FBI 尚未公布显示 Homan 收下现金的视频录像。9 月 20 日，FBI 和 DOJ 发表声明称，他们“未发现任何可信的犯罪不当行为证据”，并随后结束了调查。\n诉讼称，如果 DOJ 和 FBI 扣留此类信息，就违反了《信息自由法》（FOIA）；该法赋予美国公民请求查阅任何美国机构记录的权利。除非请求的信息属于九类豁免类别之一，否则联邦机构必须披露根据 FOIA 请求的任何信息。\nDemocracy Forward 是一家总部位于华盛顿哥伦比亚特区的非营利组织，旨在促进政府透明度，并让公众了解政府行动。该组织请求法院作出救济命令，要求 DOJ 和 FBI 给予加急处理，并迅速公开录像中不受豁免的部分。","publish_source":"jurist.org","publish_time":"2025-10-08T00:36:24-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1901","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI宣布加强对明尼苏达州公共援助项目欺诈的应对","title_en":"FBI announces increased response to fraud in Minnesota public support programs - JURIST - News","summary_cn":"FBI局长卡什·帕特尔宣布，将向明尼苏达州派遣大量调查人员和资源，继续调查一起涉及新冠疫情期间盗窃联邦儿童食品援助的巨额欺诈案。该案已导致78项起诉和57项定罪，涉案金额据称可能高达10亿美元。明尼苏达州州长沃尔兹回应称对此负责并将修复问题。案件涉及索马里裔美国人，具有政治影响。","summary_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel announced that the agency will send a large number of investigators and resources to Minnesota to continue investigating a multi-million dollar fraud scheme involving the theft of federal food aid from children during the COVID-19 pandemic. The case has led to 78 indictments and 57 convictions, with as much as $1 billion of taxpayer money possibly fraudulently taken. Minnesota Governor Tim Walz responded that he is accountable and will fix the issue. The case involves Somali-Americans and has political implications.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:36:33.644577+00:00","url":"https://www.jurist.org/news/2025/12/fbi-announces-increased-response-to-fraud-in-minnesota-public-support-programs","content":"NewsThe White House, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons\nFBI announces increased response to fraud in Minnesota public support programs\nBrendan Hickey | Vermont Law & Graduate School, US\nDecember 29, 2025 07:19:33 pm\nFBI Director Kash Patel announced Sunday that the agency will send a large number of investigators and resources to Minnesota to continue investigating a multi-million dollar fraud scheme that is said to have involved theft of federal food aid from children during the COVID-19 pandemic.According to Patel, the investigation has so far…exposed sham vendors, shell companies, and large-scale money laundering tied to the Feeding Our Future network. The case led to 78 indictments and 57 convictions… others were charged for attempting to bribe a juror… Those responsible pleaded guilty and were sentenced, including a 10-year prison term and nearly $48 million in restitution in related cases.The New York Times late last month reported that federal prosecutors say that as much as $1 billion of taxpayer money may have been fraudulently taken. Minnesota Governor Tim Walz responded to the news of possible fraud within Minnesota’s Housing Stabilization Services and Autism Service Center programs, saying:This [was] on my watch.  I am accountable for this, and more importantly, I am the one that will fix it… Whoever is in charge. Unlike the president, I’m governor now [and] whether these programs happen before we got here or afterwards, it doesn’t matter. We’re here now. We’re the ones fixing it. You have my guarantee on this, that I certainly will have this thing fixed.When announcing the new investigation last week, US Attorney Joe Thompson listed 14 state programs currently under investigation. Walz responded to the alleged widespread fraud, calling it “problematic” and claiming many programs “providing incredible services” are now “at a disadvantage because” of fraudulent actors.The situation has political implications and connections to President Donald Trump’s strong stance on immigration. Many defendants charged in the investigation are Somali-Americans. Trump has said that he does not want Somalis in the US. He has also called Minnesota a “hub of fraudulent money laundering activity.”Minnesota has the nation’s largest Somali population, about 84,000 people living mostly in the Minneapolis-Saint Paul area.","content_cn":"新闻\n白宫，公共领域，来自维基共享资源\n\nFBI宣布加大对明尼苏达州公共援助项目欺诈的应对力度\n\nBrendan Hickey｜美国佛蒙特州法律与研究生院\n2025年12月29日晚上7:19:33\n\nFBI局长Kash Patel周日宣布，该机构将向明尼苏达州派遣大量调查人员和资源，继续调查一项数百万美元的欺诈计划。据称，该计划涉及在新冠疫情期间盗取联邦政府为儿童提供的食品援助。\n\nPatel表示，调查迄今已揭露与“为我们的未来供餐”网络有关的虚假供应商、空壳公司和大规模洗钱活动。该案件导致78项起诉和57项定罪……另有一些人因试图贿赂陪审员而被起诉……相关责任人认罪并被判刑，其中相关案件包括10年监禁和近4800万美元的赔偿。\n\n《纽约时报》上月底报道，联邦检察官表示，纳税人的资金可能有多达10亿美元被欺诈性挪用。明尼苏达州州长Tim Walz针对明尼苏达州住房稳定服务项目和自闭症服务中心项目中可能存在欺诈的消息作出回应，他说：\n\n“这件事发生在我的任期内。我对此负责，更重要的是，我将解决它……无论谁负责。和总统不同，我现在是州长，[无论]这些项目是在我们到任之前还是之后发生的，这都不重要。我们现在就在这里。是我们在解决问题。我向你保证，我一定会把这件事解决好。”\n\n上周宣布展开新调查时，美国检察官Joe Thompson列出了目前正在调查的14个州项目。Walz回应所谓的广泛欺诈，称其“令人担忧”，并表示许多“提供令人难以置信服务”的项目如今“因为”欺诈行为而“处于不利地位”。\n\n这一局势具有政治影响，也与总统Donald Trump对移民问题的强硬立场有关。调查中被起诉的许多被告是索马里裔美国人。Trump曾表示，他不希望索马里人在美国。他还称明尼苏达州是“欺诈性洗钱活动的中心”。\n\n明尼苏达州拥有全美最大的索马里裔人口，约有8.4万人，主要居住在明尼阿波利斯—圣保罗地区。","publish_source":"jurist.org","publish_time":"2025-12-30T00:19:33-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1862","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI在ICE枪杀明尼苏达州女子后接管调查","title_en":"FBI 'takes over' investigation following ICE shooting of Minnesota woman - JURIST - News","summary_cn":"美国移民和海关执法局（ICE）特工在明尼阿波利斯开枪打死一名37岁美国公民女子。FBI随后接管调查，并告知明尼苏达州警方不会提供案件材料。明尼苏达州州长沃尔兹对调查公正性表示担忧。联邦官员称枪击是自卫行为，但明尼阿波利斯市长等人士提出质疑。事件引发对ICE执法策略的争议。","summary_en":"A US Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) agent fatally shot a 37-year-old US citizen woman in Minneapolis. The FBI subsequently took over the investigation and told Minnesota state police it would not grant access to case materials. Minnesota Governor Tim Walz expressed concern about a fair outcome. Federal officials claimed the shooting was self-defense, but Minneapolis Mayor Jacob Frey and others challenged this. The incident raised concerns about ICE tactics.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:34:01.849481+00:00","url":"https://www.jurist.org/news/2026/01/fbi-takes-over-investigation-following-ice-shooting-of-minnesota-woman","content":"NewsFBI, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons\nFBI ‘takes over’ investigation following ICE shooting of Minnesota woman\nAdamo Marinelli | U. Ottawa Faculty of Law, CA\nJanuary 8, 2026 08:04:50 pm\nA US Customs and Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) agent fatally shot a Minneapolis woman on Wednesday during continuing agency operations in the city.The next day, CNN reported that Minnesota officials told the news outlet that “the feds have blocked them from investigating the fatal ICE shooting” of Renee Nicole Good, 37-year-old mother and US citizen. The FBI and state law enforcement originally agreed to work together on the case. However, Minnesota state police said in a statement on Thursday that the FBI told the state that it would not grant access to any case materials moving forward.Minnesota Governor Tim Walz expressed concern and doubt about a fair outcome to the shooting investigation, following the FBI’s complete takeover of the case.The FBI’s website clarifies that “the FBI does not supervise or take over [state or local law enforcement agencies’] investigations,” and states that federal and state law enforcement often work together. However, the Supremacy Clause of the Constitution grants federal law power over state law when the two conflict. The FBI may exercise sole jurisdiction over investigations involving federal crimes, such as domestic terrorism—overriding conflicting state or local actions in the process.Federal officials claim the shooting was an act of self-defense. Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem described the incident as “an act of domestic terrorism” against ICE agents by a woman who “attempted to run them over and rammed them with her vehicle.” Vice President JD Vance made statements claiming that Good’s death was “a tragedy of her own making.”Other prominent figures have challenged officers’ claims of self defense. Numerous rights groups have raised concerns about ICE’s tactics during immigration raids.“They are already trying to spin this as an [act] of self defense. Having seen the video myself, I want to tell everybody directly, that is bullshit,” Minneapolis Mayor Jacob Frey said in a press conference. Frey expressed his frustration over the roughly 2,000 federal officers deployed in Minneapolis and St. Paul as part of the administration’s latest surge in immigration enforcement in the city, stating:They are not here to cause safety in this city. What they are doing is not to provide safety in America. What they are doing is causing chaos and distrust… They’re ripping families apart. They’re sowing chaos on our streets and in this case quite literally killing people.","content_cn":"NewsFBI，公共领域，经维基共享资源提供\nFBI“接管”明尼苏达州女子遭ICE枪击事件的调查\nAdamo Marinelli｜加拿大渥太华大学法学院\n2026年1月8日晚上8:04:50\n周三，美国海关与移民执法局（ICE）一名特工在该机构继续于明尼阿波利斯开展行动期间，开枪打死了一名女子。次日，CNN报道称，明尼苏达州官员告诉该媒体，“联邦人员阻止他们调查ICE致命枪击案”，死者是37岁的美国公民、母亲Renee Nicole Good。FBI和州执法部门最初同意共同处理此案。然而，明尼苏达州警察周四在一份声明中表示，FBI告知该州，今后不会允许其查阅任何案件材料。FBI完全接管案件后，明尼苏达州州长Tim Walz对枪击调查能否得到公正结果表示担忧和怀疑。FBI网站澄清称，“FBI不会监督或接管[州或地方执法机构的]调查”，并表示联邦和州执法部门经常合作。然而，宪法的至上条款规定，当联邦法律与州法律发生冲突时，联邦法律优先。FBI可以对涉及联邦犯罪的调查行使单独管辖权，例如国内恐怖主义，并在此过程中推翻相冲突的州或地方行动。联邦官员声称，这起枪击是自卫行为。国土安全部长Kristi Noem将此事件描述为一名女子针对ICE特工实施的“国内恐怖主义行为”，称她“试图驾车撞倒他们，并用车辆冲撞他们”。副总统JD Vance发表声明称，Good的死亡是“她自己造成的悲剧”。其他知名人士对官员关于自卫的说法提出质疑。众多权利团体对ICE在移民突袭行动中的策略表示担忧。明尼阿波利斯市长Jacob Frey在新闻发布会上说：“他们已经试图把这说成是[一种]自卫行为。我亲眼看过视频，我想直接告诉所有人，那是胡扯。”Frey对政府在明尼阿波利斯和圣保罗部署约2,000名联邦官员、作为该市最新一轮移民执法行动的一部分表示沮丧，并说：他们不是来确保这座城市安全的。他们所做的不是为美国提供安全。他们正在制造混乱和不信任……他们拆散家庭。在我们的街道上播撒混乱，而在这起案件中，他们简直杀了人。","publish_source":"jurist.org","publish_time":"2026-01-09T01:04:50-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1686","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国联邦上诉法院裁定国土安全部不得终止委内瑞拉和海地移民的保护","title_en":"US federal appeals court rules DHS cannot end protections for Venezuela and Haiti immigrants - JURIST - News","summary_cn":"美国第九巡回上诉法院裁定，国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆终止委内瑞拉人和海地人临时保护身份的行为违法。法院认为，8 USC §1254a赋予部长指定、延长和终止TPS的权力，但未授权其撤销现有指定。法院指出诺姆的非法行为对数十万依赖TPS的委内瑞拉人和海地人造成了实际而重大的后果。","summary_en":"The US Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit ruled that Department of Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem acted illegally when she ended Temporary Protected Status for Venezuelans and Haitians. The court held that 8 USC §1254a gives the secretary authority to designate, extend and terminate TPS but no authority to vacate an existing designation. The court said Noem's unlawful actions had real and significant consequences for hundreds of thousands of Venezuelans and Haitians relying on TPS.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:39:48.627760+00:00","url":"https://www.jurist.org/news/2026/01/us-federal-appeals-court-rules-dhs-cannot-end-protections-for-venezuela-and-haiti-immigrants","content":"NewsJoe Gratz, CC0, via Wikimedia Commons\nUS federal appeals court rules DHS cannot end protections for Venezuela and Haiti immigrants\nBrendan Hickey | Vermont Law & Graduate School, US\nJanuary 30, 2026 07:46:57 am\nThe US Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit ruled Wednesday that Department of Homeland Security (DHS) Secretary Kristi Noem acted illegally when she ended Temporary Protected Status (TPS) for Venezuelans and Haitians, effective on April 7, 2025.Noem’s order in April would have vacated a designation for Venezuelans that was set to expire on October 2, 2026. The court held that 8 USC §1254a, which created the TPS program, gives the secretary of DHS the authority to designate countries for TPS and to extend and terminate that status. However, the statute gives the secretary no authority to vacate an existing TPS designation. The court wrote: “The Secretary attempted to exercise powers Congress simply did not provide under the statute.”TPS can only be designated for periods of six, 12, or 18 months at a time, though it can be extended for the same periods.The court ruled similarly on Noem’s partial vacatur of TPS for Haitians, adding that §1254a includes procedural safeguards to ensure predictability and stability for citizens of other countries while in the US under TPS status. The justices stated:The Secretary’s unlawful actions have had real and significant consequences for the hundreds of thousands of Venezuelans and Haitians in the United States who rely on TPS. The record is replete with examples of hard-working, contributing members of society … who have been deported or detained after losing their TPS. Other TPS beneficiaries have lost their jobs (or) homes.The court further emphasized that, as a result of Noem’s actions, hundreds of thousands of individuals have been left “in a constant state of fear that they will be deported, detained, separated from their families, and returned to a country in which they were subjected to violence or any other number of harms.A federal judge in Washington is expected to rule soon on the termination of TPS for Haiti, pending a separate suit. The country’s TPS designation will end on February 3.Noem’s order in April has led to a long procedural history over the last nine months. The US Supreme Court allowed Noem’s order to stand in May. The US District Court for the Northern District of California halted the revocation of TPS and deportation of 5,000 Venezuelans in June. The US Court of Appeals for the Fifth Circuit ruled that the 1798 Alien Enemies Act could not be used to deport Venezuelans, and the US District Court for the Northern District of California ruled again that DHS could not remove TPS protections from Venezuelans and Haitians. Donald Trump’s administration appealed again and, on October 3, the Supreme Court ordered the immediate termination of TPS status for Venezuelans.","content_cn":"新闻\nJoe Gratz，CC0，经维基共享资源提供\n美国联邦上诉法院裁定，国土安全部不能终止委内瑞拉和海地移民的保护\nBrendan Hickey｜美国佛蒙特法律与研究生院\n2026年1月30日上午07:46:57\n美国第九巡回上诉法院周三裁定，国土安全部（DHS）部长克里斯蒂·诺姆在终止委内瑞拉人和海地人的临时保护身份（TPS）时违法，该终止决定于2025年4月7日生效。诺姆4月的命令本会撤销对委内瑞拉的指定，而该指定原定于2026年10月2日到期。法院认定，创设TPS项目的《美国法典》第8编第1254a条赋予DHS部长指定TPS国家以及延长和终止该身份的权力。然而，该法没有赋予部长撤销现有TPS指定的权力。法院写道：“部长试图行使国会在该法中根本未赋予的权力。”TPS一次只能指定6个月、12个月或18个月，但可以按相同期限延长。法院对诺姆部分撤销海地TPS的做法作出了类似裁定，并补充说，第1254a条包含程序保障措施，以确保其他国家公民在美国以TPS身份居留期间获得可预测性和稳定性。大法官们表示：部长的违法行为已经对依赖TPS的数十万名在美委内瑞拉人和海地人造成真实且重大后果。记录中充满了勤劳、有贡献的社会成员……他们在失去TPS后被驱逐或拘留。其他TPS受益人失去了工作（或）住房。法院进一步强调，由于诺姆的行为，数十万人一直“处于持续恐惧之中，担心自己会被驱逐、拘留、与家人分离，并被送回曾遭受暴力或其他种种伤害的国家”。华盛顿的一名联邦法官预计很快将就海地TPS的终止作出裁决，目前该问题正等待另一宗诉讼处理。该国的TPS指定将于2月3日结束。诺姆4月的命令在过去九个月引发了漫长的程序历程。美国最高法院在5月允许诺姆的命令继续有效。加州北区联邦地区法院6月叫停撤销TPS以及驱逐5,000名委内瑞拉人。美国第五巡回上诉法院裁定，1798年的《外侨敌人法》不能用于驱逐委内瑞拉人；加州北区联邦地区法院再次裁定，DHS不能取消对委内瑞拉人和海地人的TPS保护。唐纳德·特朗普政府再次提起上诉，10月3日，最高法院下令立即终止委内瑞拉人的TPS身份。","publish_source":"jurist.org","publish_time":"2026-01-30T12:46:57-05:00"}},{"id":"news-468","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"联邦法官以缺乏管辖权为由驳回FBI局长卡什·帕特尔的诽谤诉讼","title_en":"Kash Patel Defamation Lawsuit Dismissed Over Jurisdiction","summary_cn":"JURIST报道，美国内华达州联邦地区法院首席法官安德鲁·戈登以缺乏属人管辖权为由，驳回FBI局长卡什·帕特尔及其基金会针对加州博主吉姆·斯图尔特森的诽谤诉讼，并撤销此前25万美元的缺席判决。法官强调裁决未认定相关言论真假，仅认定博主与内华达州缺乏最低联系。帕特尔此前还针对《大西洋月刊》提起2.5亿美元诽谤诉讼。","summary_en":"JURIST reports that Chief US District Judge Andrew Gordon of Nevada dismissed FBI Director Kash Patel's defamation suit against California blogger Jim Stewartson for lack of personal jurisdiction, and vacated a prior $250,000 default judgment as void. The judge stressed the ruling did not resolve whether the statements were true or protected opinion, only that the blogger lacked minimum contacts with Nevada. Patel is also pursuing a separate $250 million defamation suit against The Atlantic.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:17:48.374178+00:00","url":"https://www.jurist.org/news/2026/07/federal-judge-dismisses-fbi-director-kash-patels-defamation-suit-against-blogger-for-lack-of-jurisdiction","content":"News\nFederal judge dismisses FBI Director Kash Patel’s defamation suit against blogger for lack of jurisdiction\nZachary Fedyk | U. Pittsburgh School of Law, US\nJuly 30, 2026 10:48:24 pm\nA US federal judge in Nevada on Thursday dismissed a defamation lawsuit brought by FBI Director Kash Patel and his nonprofit foundation against a California blogger on July 25.Chief US District Judge Andrew P. Gordon of the District of Nevada granted blogger Jim Stewartson’s motion to dismiss under Federal Rule of Civil Procedure 12(b)(2) for a lack of personal jurisdiction. He also vacated the $250,000 default judgment entered in Patel’s favor last year as void under Rule 60(b).(4).Gordon stressed the limits of his decision stating that it does not resolve whether Stewartson’s statements—which included calling Patel a “Kremlin asset” and “guilty of sedition”—were true, false, or protected opinion. It holds only that Stewartson lacked the minimum contacts with Nevada required for the court to hear the case. Gordon applied the “effects test” from the US Supreme Court’s Calder v. Jones, as well as the Ninth Circuit’s minimum-contacts framework. He found that Stewartson, posting from California, had not expressly aimed his conduct at Nevada. The blogger’s statements, the judge wrote, were directed at “the American body politic writ large” and not towards a Nevada audience. Stewartson tagging Patel, a Nevada resident, online did not create the necessary connection. He distinguished Calder, where California had been the “focal point” of both the story and the harm.Patel, a longtime ally of President Donald Trump, was confirmed to lead the FBI in 2025. He filed the suit back in June 2023, before his appointment. The complaint sought $10 million on claims of defamation, injurious falsehood, and business disparagement over a series of online posts. These included statements that Patel had “attempted to overthrow the government,” “planned” the January 6 Capitol attack, and was a “blatantly incompetent chud”, which refers to a pejorative for figures on the political right.Stewartson did not initially respond, and Gordon entered a default judgment on August 5, 2025. He awarded Patel $200,000 and the Kash Foundation $50,000—far less than the $10 million sought. In September, Stewartson moved to vacate the judgment and dismiss the case, arguing that he was never properly served, that Nevada lacked jurisdiction, and that the claims were barred by the First Amendment.Although he ruled for Stewartson, Gordon criticized the blogger’s conduct. He wrote that Stewartson appeared to know about the suit, may have tried to avoid service, and had “wasted the plaintiffs and the court’s time.” The judge said he would have required Stewartson to pay Patel’s attorney’s fees had he possessed the discretion to do so, but concluded that a judgment void for a lack of jurisdiction left him with no such power. Stewartson celebrated the ruling on X, noting that Gordon had cited some of his cruder language in a footnote.The dismissal comes as Patel pursues a separate $250 million defamation suit against The Atlantic over an April article describing his alleged drinking. The magazine has moved to dismiss the case. The New York Times reported in June that Patel has filed six defamation suits over the last seven years.","content_cn":"新闻\n联邦法官因缺乏管辖权驳回联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔针对博主提起的诽谤诉讼\n扎卡里·费迪克｜美国匹兹堡大学法学院\n2026年7月30日晚上10:48:24\n美国内华达州一名联邦法官于周四驳回了联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔及其非营利基金会于7月25日针对一名加州博主提起的诽谤诉讼。\n内华达区首席美国地区法官安德鲁·P·戈登依据《联邦民事诉讼规则》第12(b)(2)条，以缺乏对人管辖权为由，准许博主吉姆·斯图尔特森提出的驳回动议。他还依据第60(b)(4)条撤销了去年作出的、判给帕特尔25万美元的缺席判决，认定该判决无效。\n戈登强调其裁决的限度，称该裁决并未判定斯图尔特森的言论——包括称帕特尔为“克里姆林宫资产”和“犯有煽动罪”——是真实、虚假，还是受保护的意见。裁决仅认为，斯图尔特森与内华达州之间缺乏法院审理此案所需的最低联系。戈登适用了美国最高法院在《考尔德诉琼斯案》中确立的“效果测试”，以及第九巡回上诉法院的最低联系框架。他认定，斯图尔特森从加州发帖，并未明确将其行为指向内华达州。法官写道，这名博主的言论针对的是“广义上的美国政治共同体”，而非内华达州受众。斯图尔特森在网上标记身为内华达州居民的帕特尔，并未建立必要的联系。他将本案与《考尔德案》区分开来，后案中，加州是报道和损害的“焦点”。\n帕特尔是唐纳德·特朗普总统的长期盟友，于2025年获确认领导联邦调查局。他在2023年6月，即获任命前，提起本案。诉状针对一系列网络帖子，以诽谤、恶意虚假陈述和商业诋毁为由索赔1000万美元。这些帖子包括称帕特尔“试图推翻政府”、“策划”了1月6日国会大厦袭击事件，以及是一个“明显无能的chud”；该词是对政治右翼人物的贬义称呼。\n斯图尔特森起初未作回应，戈登于2025年8月5日作出缺席判决。他判给帕特尔20万美元，并判给卡什基金会5万美元——远低于所主张的1000万美元。9月，斯图尔特森申请撤销判决并驳回案件，主张其从未被适当送达，内华达州没有管辖权，且这些主张受《第一修正案》禁止。\n尽管裁定支持斯图尔特森，戈登仍批评了这名博主的行为。他写道，斯图尔特森似乎知道这起诉讼，可能曾试图逃避送达，并且“浪费了原告和法院的时间”。法官称，若他拥有这样做的裁量权，本会要求斯图尔特森支付帕特尔的律师费，但他认定，因缺乏管辖权而无效的判决使其不具备这种权力。斯图尔特森在X上庆祝该裁决，并指出戈登在脚注中引用了他的一些更粗俗的措辞。\n此次驳回之际，帕特尔正就《大西洋月刊》4月一篇描述其涉嫌饮酒的文章，另行向该刊提起2.5亿美元诽谤诉讼。该杂志已申请驳回该案。《纽约时报》6月报道称，帕特尔在过去七年中已提起六起诽谤诉讼。","publish_source":"jurist.org","publish_time":"2026-07-31T02:48:24-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1261","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"马林部长如何改革国土安全部","title_en":"How Secretary Mullin Can Reform DHS","summary_cn":"文章讨论美国国土安全部新任部长Markwayne Mullin面临的改革任务。作者指出，前部长Kristi Noem任内存在放弃第四修正案搜查令要求、缩短ICE培训、阻碍监察长办公室调查等问题。文章提出四项建议：恢复监察长办公室独立性、支持举报人、恢复并加强ICE培训课程、停止无司法搜查令的入户搜查，并呼吁国会提供支持。","summary_en":"The article discusses reform tasks facing new U.S. Department of Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin. The authors note that under former Secretary Kristi Noem, DHS abandoned Fourth Amendment warrant requirements, cut ICE training, and blocked the Inspector General's investigations. They offer four recommendations: restore OIG independence, support whistleblowers, restore and strengthen ICE training, and stop warrantless home searches, while urging congressional support.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:08:03.001812+00:00","url":"https://www.justsecurity.org/135134/secretary-mullin-reform-dhs","content":"How Secretary Mullin Can Reform DHSBy Mark Zaid and Andrew P. BakajPublished on March 30, 2026Note: The authors are co-founder and chief legal counsel, respectively, at WhistleblowerAid.org, which provides pro bono representation to public interest whistleblowers. They represented the whistleblower whose complaint led to President Trump’s first-term impeachment.\nPresident Donald Trump’s choice to replace Kristi Noem at the Department of Homeland Security (DHS), Markwayne Mullin, the former junior senator from Oklahoma, was quickly confirmed by the Senate. He now leads a powerful institution in desperate need of reform.\nIn a normal administration, it would not be hard for Mullin to outperform Noem’s dismal tenure as DHS Secretary. After all, it was under Noem’s leadership that the Department unconstitutionally abandoned centuries-long Fourth Amendment precedent, authorizing searches of homes without judicial warrants. It was also under her leadership that Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) drastically reduced its training requirements in order to meet unrealistic recruitment quotas, and sent unprepared ICE officers to conduct unprecedented—and violent—operations throughout the country.\nThe above revelations came to light thanks to brave whistleblowers who sought and received assistance from WhistleblowerAid.org to responsibly and lawfully speak out on illegal—and frankly, terrifying—acts and directives occurring at DHS. But Noem’s legacy will not just be about the countless acts of wrongdoing under her leadership; it will also center around the institutional changes she made at DHS that make uncovering and correcting that wrongdoing much more difficult.\nJust before Noem’s firing, Joseph Cuffari, the Trump-appointed DHS Inspector General (IG) from the first administration, cited 11 instances in which the Department blocked his office from accessing records and information it needed to pursue its inquiries. Cuffari described the Department’s refusal to cooperate in criminal investigations with national security implications as being “particularly egregious.”\nCuffari’s revelations led to bipartisan calls for Noem to correct the Department’s course. Senator Thom Tillis (R-NC) grew incensed while questioning Noem at a committee hearing in early March. Senator Tammy Duckworth (D-IL) was likewise outraged several weeks earlier when she revealed that the DHS General Counsel had effectively threatened Cuffari with repeated “reminders” that then Secretary Noem was authorized to kill supposedly independent IG investigations.\nEnter Secretary Mullin.\nIf Mullin is serious about doing his job well, then he should consider the following list of suggestions—a “to-do” list—based on information provided to the public by our clients:\n1. Restore full independence and autonomy to the DHS Office of the Inspector General (OIG). Under Noem, the OIG was blocked from doing its job 11 times. And so, logically, the first and most important thing that Mullin can do is to let the OIG do its job and conduct independent oversight of the Department.\n2. Listen to and support whistleblowers. Creating a culture where misconduct can easily be reported will help reduce the wrongdoing that has been plaguing DHS in the public image. If Mullin takes whistleblowers seriously, then he will listen to their concerns and address the problems they expose.\n3. Restore and perhaps enhance the previous training curriculum for ICE cadets. According to our client, ICE whistleblower Ryan Schwank, ICE cut its training regimen for new recruits from the previously required 72 days to just 42 days, excising key parts of the curriculum focusing on firearms training, use of force, and ICE agents’ legal authority under the U.S. Constitution. At a minimum, the previous training requirements should be restored. But Mullin should also direct an audit of the training regimen, particularly given that the murders of Renee Good and Alex Pretti in Minneapolis were committed by officers who had passed the full 72-day training curriculum. Mullin can learn important lessons from a ruling earlier this month by Judge Gary R. Brown, a Trump appointee, who found “systemic” problems in ICE officers’ training and knowledge of the law.\n4. Stop the searching of homes with no judicial warrant. The memo directing ICE agents to search homes with only an administrative warrant flies in the face of the Fourth Amendment, which protects Americans “against unreasonable searches and seizures.” Mullin should immediately issue a memo affirming that ICE officers will need a judicial warrant—signed by an independent Article III judge—to enter people’s homes without consent.\nIdeally, Mullin should also ask Congress for support that extends beyond his duties as DHS Secretary – namely, to reverse the at-will designation of federal employees and create additional routes to Congress for members of the U.S. Intelligence Community.\nAt his confirmation hearing, Mullin said, “I will do everything required of me by law.” Perhaps Mullin meant that he will do the bare minimum. From a more optimistic perspective, he may have been tacitly acknowledging that DHS has departed from the law and therefore needs change. An even more optimistic reading of Mullin’s words is that he was inviting Congress to amend the law where it needs amending.\nIf the previous four steps are completed successfully, Mullin could help turn DHS—currently the poster child for the urgency of reform—into an example that other departments can and should follow.\nIs Mullin—or anyone who would be in his position for that matter—going to accomplish everything on this to-do list? No. In fact, it is unfortunately doubtful he will check off any one item fully. But he must try his hardest to do so.\nNoem failed spectacularly in executing her duties, and no one should be bullish about Mullin’s chances. After all, the Trump administration is waging a relentless campaign to slash and neuter accountability mechanisms and gaslight truth-tellers who put their careers and even their lives at risk to report wrongdoing.\nAmericans cannot and should not accept this as the new normal. Citizens and politicians must summon the strength to support whistleblowers and work toward accountability. That also means giving Mullin an opportunity to do the right thing and return DHS, at least in part, to a functioning and law-abiding professional organization.\nFEATURED IMAGE: The U.S. Department of Homeland Security emblem on the U.S.Immigration and Customs Enforcement building as seen on January 07, 2026 in Washington, DC. (Photo by Heather Diehl/Getty Images)Share\nFollow us on BlueSky\nFollow us on Twitter\nFollow us on Linkedin\nFollow us on Threads\nFollow us on Facebook\nPrint this page\nCopy this page URL to your clipboard\nURL copied to clipboard.\nFiled Under4th Amendment, Accountability, Confirmation Hearing, Congress, Department of Homeland Security (DHS), General Warrants, Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE), Law enforcement, Office of the Inspector General (OIG), Transparency, Trump administration second term, United States (US), WhistleblowingAbout the AuthorsMark ZaidMark Zaid is a Founding Legal Partner of Whistleblower Aid, which provides pro bono representation to public interest whistleblowers.\nAndrew P. BakajAndrew P. Bakaj is Chief Legal Counsel at Whistleblower Aid, which provides pro bono representation to public interest whistleblowers.\nSend A Letter To The EditorRead Next:Guantanamo Dispatch: Prosecutors Turn to Remote Testimony For First-Ever Capital Trial at Guantanamo\nSep. 24, 2026\nCarol Rosenberg\nFirst, Do No Harm: Four Questions Government Reformers Must Ask to Avoid Counterproductive Changes\nSep. 24, 2026\nMartha Roberts\nThe Supreme Court’s Open-Weight AI Regulation Gauntlet\nSep. 24, 2026\nJack Thorlin\nLitigation Tracker: Legal Challenges to Trump Administration Actions\nSep. 24, 2026\nJust Security\n12323Featured Articles:Guantanamo Dispatch: Prosecutors Turn to Remote Testimony For First-Ever Capital Trial at Guantanamo\nSep. 24, 2026\nCarol Rosenberg\nThe Supreme Court’s Open-Weight AI Regulation Gauntlet\nSep. 24, 2026\nJack Thorlin\nExpert Backgrounder: Weapons in Space Under International Law\nSep. 23, 2026\nMichael Schmitt\nWith Muse, Meta Could Have the Power to Decide What Matters in Your Life\nSep. 23, 2026\nMariana Olaizola Rosenblat","content_cn":"穆林部长如何改革国土安全部\n作者：马克·扎伊德和安德鲁·P·巴卡杰\n发表于2026年3月30日\n注：两位作者分别是 WhistleblowerAid.org 的联合创始人和首席法律顾问。该组织为公益举报人提供无偿代理服务。他们曾代理过一名举报人，该举报人的投诉促成了特朗普总统第一任期内的首次弹劾。\n\n总统唐纳德·特朗普选择前俄克拉何马州初级参议员马克韦恩·穆林接替国土安全部（DHS）的克里斯蒂·诺姆后，穆林很快获得参议院确认。他现在领导着这个亟须改革的强大机构。\n\n在一个正常的政府中，穆林要做得比诺姆在国土安全部长任上的惨淡表现更好，并不困难。毕竟，正是在诺姆的领导下，该部门违宪地抛弃了延续数百年的第四修正案判例先例，授权在没有司法令状的情况下搜查住宅。同样是在她的领导下，移民与海关执法局（ICE）为达到不切实际的招募配额而大幅降低培训要求，并派遣未经充分准备的 ICE 官员在全国各地开展前所未有且暴力的行动。\n\n上述披露之所以能够曝光，要归功于勇敢的举报人。他们寻求并获得了 WhistleblowerAid.org 的协助，以负责任且合法地揭露发生在国土安全部的非法——坦率地说，令人恐惧的——行为和指令。但诺姆留下的遗产不会只是她领导期间无数不当行为的总和；还将包括她在国土安全部实施的制度性变化，而这些变化使揭露和纠正不当行为变得更加困难。\n\n就在诺姆被解职前，特朗普第一届政府任命的国土安全部监察长（IG）约瑟夫·卡法里指出了11起该部门阻止其办公室获取开展调查所需记录和信息的事件。卡法里称，该部门拒绝配合涉及国家安全的刑事调查，“尤其恶劣”。\n\n卡法里的披露引发了两党要求诺姆纠正该部门方向的呼声。3月初的一次委员会听证会上，参议员汤姆·蒂利斯（共和党，北卡罗来纳州）在质询诺姆时怒不可遏。几周前，当参议员塔米·达克沃思（民主党，伊利诺伊州）披露国土安全部总法律顾问实际上曾以反复“提醒”的方式威胁卡法里，称当时的部长诺姆有权终止所谓独立的监察长调查时，她同样感到震怒。\n\n穆林部长登场。\n\n如果穆林认真想把工作做好，那么他应当考虑以下建议清单——一份“待办事项”清单——这些建议基于我们的客户向公众提供的信息：\n\n1. 恢复国土安全部监察长办公室（OIG）的完全独立性和自主权。在诺姆任内，OIG 有11次被阻止履行职责。因此，穆林能够做的第一件、也是最重要的事情，合乎逻辑地就是让 OIG 履行职责，对该部门开展独立监督。\n\n2. 倾听并支持举报人。营造一种能够轻松报告不当行为的文化，将有助于减少一直损害国土安全部公众形象的不当行为。如果穆林认真对待举报人，那么他就会倾听他们的担忧，并处理他们所揭露的问题。\n\n3. 恢复并或许加强 ICE 学员此前的培训课程。根据我们的客户、ICE 举报人所提供的信息，\nRyan Schwank，ICE将新招募人员的培训期限从此前要求的72天缩短至仅42天，删去了课程中有关枪械训练、武力使用以及ICE特工依据美国宪法所拥有的法律权限等关键部分。至少，应恢复此前的培训要求。但穆林还应指示对培训制度进行审计，尤其是考虑到明尼阿波利斯市发生的蕾妮·古德和亚历克斯·普雷蒂谋杀案，是由通过完整72天培训课程的警员实施的。穆林可以从本月早些时候加里·R·布朗法官（特朗普任命的法官）作出的一项裁决中吸取重要教训；布朗法官认定，ICE警员的培训和法律知识存在“系统性”问题。\n4. 停止在没有司法搜查令的情况下搜查住宅。那份指示ICE特工仅凭行政搜查令搜查住宅的备忘录，公然违背了《第四修正案》；该修正案保护美国人“不受不合理的搜查和扣押”。穆林应立即发布备忘录，确认ICE警员未经同意进入他人住宅时，必须取得司法搜查令——并由一名独立的第三条法官签署。\n理想情况下，穆林还应请求国会提供超出其国土安全部长职责范围的支持——即撤销联邦雇员的任意雇佣身份，并为美国情报界成员创建更多通往国会的途径。\n在确认听证会上，穆林说：“我将依法履行对我提出的一切要求。”也许穆林的意思是，他只会做到最低限度。从更乐观的角度看，他可能是在含蓄地承认，国土安全部已经偏离法律，因此需要改变。对穆林这番话更为乐观的解读是，他是在邀请国会修改那些需要修订的法律。\n如果前四项措施能够成功完成，穆林或许可以帮助把国土安全部——目前改革紧迫性的典型代表——变成其他部门能够且应当效仿的榜样。\n穆林——或者任何处于他这一职位的人——会完成这份待办清单上的所有事项吗？不会。事实上，很遗憾，他很可能无法完整完成其中任何一项。但他必须竭尽全力去做。\n诺姆在履行职责方面惨败，没有人应该对穆林的机会过于乐观。毕竟，特朗普政府正在发动一场无休止的运动，削减并削弱问责机制，对那些冒着职业生涯甚至生命危险举报不当行为、揭露真相的人进行煤气灯操纵。\n美国人不能也不应接受这成为新常态。公民和政治家必须鼓起力量支持举报人，并努力实现问责。这也意味着，应给穆林一个做正确事情的机会，至少在一定程度上让国土安全部恢复为一个正常运作、遵守法律的专业组织。\n特色图片：2026年1月7日，在华盛顿特区看到的美国国土安全部徽章，位于美国移民与海关执法局大楼上。（Heather Diehl/Getty Images 摄）分享\n在BlueSky上关注我们\n在Twitter上关注我们\n在Linkedin上关注我们\n在Threads上关注我们\n在Facebook上关注我们\n打印此页面\n将此页面网址复制到剪贴板\n网址已复制到剪贴板。\n归档于第4修正案、问责、确认听证会、国会、国土安全部（DHS）、一般搜查令、移民与海关执法局（ICE）、法律\n执法、监察长办公室（OIG）、透明度、特朗普政府第二任期、美国（US）、举报\n关于作者\n马克·扎伊德\n马克·扎伊德是举报人援助组织的创始法律合伙人，该组织为公共利益举报人提供无偿代理。\n安德鲁·P·巴凯\n安德鲁·P·巴凯是举报人援助组织的首席法律顾问，该组织为公共利益举报人提供无偿代理。\n致编辑的一封信\n接下来阅读：关塔那摩动态：检察官转向远程证词，进行关塔那摩首次死刑审判\n2026年9月24日\n卡罗尔·罗森伯格\n首先，不要造成伤害：政府改革者为避免适得其反的改变必须提出的四个问题\n2026年9月24日\n玛莎·罗伯茨\n最高法院的开放权重人工智能监管挑战\n2026年9月24日\n杰克·索林\n诉讼追踪：针对特朗普政府行动的法律挑战\n2026年9月24日\nJust Security\n12323\n精选文章：关塔那摩动态：检察官转向远程证词，进行关塔那摩首次死刑审判\n2026年9月24日\n卡罗尔·罗森伯格\n最高法院的开放权重人工智能监管挑战\n2026年9月24日\n杰克·索林\n专家背景资料：国际法下的太空武器\n2026年9月23日\n迈克尔·施米特\n借助Muse，Meta或许拥有决定你生活中何为重要之事的权力\n2026年9月23日\n玛丽安娜·奥莱佐拉·罗森布拉特","publish_source":"justsecurity.org","publish_time":"2026-03-30T12:50:56+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2338","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI：一名女子在取下脚踝监视器后被通缉","title_en":"FBI: Woman wanted after removing ankle monitor","summary_cn":"FBI正在寻求公众帮助寻找与阿肯色州有关的通缉女子拉蒂莎·塔玛拉·拉克。她因取下脚踝监视器并未能出席关于涉嫌违反审前释放条件的保释撤销听证会而被通缉。拉克于2022年8月被控共谋银行欺诈和电汇欺诈，2025年8月29日联邦逮捕令发出。她与阿肯色州小石城、得克萨斯州休斯顿和加利福尼亚州旧金山有联系。","summary_en":"The FBI is seeking public help to find wanted woman Latisha Tamara Lak, tied to Arkansas. She is wanted for removing her ankle monitor and failing to appear for a bond revocation hearing regarding alleged violations of her pretrial release. Lak was charged with conspiracy to commit bank fraud and wire fraud in August 2022, and a federal arrest warrant was issued on August 29, 2025. She has ties to Little Rock, Arkansas; Houston, Texas; and San Francisco, California.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:15:14.121711+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2025/09/27/fbi-woman-wanted-after-removing-ankle-monitor","content":"FBI: Woman wanted after removing ankle monitorThe Federal Bureau of Investigation needs your help in finding a wanted woman tied to Arkansas.By K8 NewsdeskPublished: Sep. 26, 2025 at 9:25 PM CDT|Updated: Sep. 26, 2025 at 10:15 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) - The Federal Bureau of Investigation needs your help in finding a wanted woman tied to Arkansas. According to the FBI news release, Latisha Tamara Lak is wanted for removing her ankle monitor and failing to appear for a “bond revocation hearing regarding alleged violations of her pretrial release.”The Federal Bureau of Investigation needs your help in finding a wanted woman tied to Arkansas.(Federal Bureau of Investigation)Lak was charged with conspiracy to commit bank fraud and wire fraud in August 2022 in Arkansas. Lak has been on supervised release pending trial.On August 29, 2025, a federal arrest warrant was issued for Lak in the United States District Court for the Eastern District of Arkansas, Little Rock, Arkansas, after she was charged with Failure to Appear, the news release said. She has ties to Little Rock, Arkansas; Houston, Texas; and San Francisco, California.Please contact the FBI’s toll-free tipline at 1-800-CALL-FBI (1-800-225-5324).For more information, click here.To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2025 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI：一名移除脚踝监控器的女子被通缉\n联邦调查局需要您的帮助，以寻找一名与阿肯色州有关的在逃女子。\nK8新闻编辑部\n发表于：2025年9月26日中部夏令时间晚上9:25|更新于：2025年9月26日中部夏令时间晚上10:15\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——联邦调查局需要您的帮助，以寻找一名与阿肯色州有关的在逃女子。\n根据FBI新闻稿，拉蒂莎·塔玛拉·拉克因移除脚踝监控器，并未出席“有关其涉嫌违反审前释放规定的保释撤销听证会”而被通缉。\n联邦调查局需要您的帮助，以寻找一名与阿肯色州有关的在逃女子。（联邦调查局）\n2022年8月，拉克在阿肯色州被控合谋实施银行欺诈和电信欺诈。拉克在候审期间一直处于监督释放状态。\n新闻稿称，2025年8月29日，在她被控未出庭后，美国阿肯色东区联邦地区法院（阿肯色州小石城）对拉克签发了联邦逮捕令。她与阿肯色州小石城、得克萨斯州休斯敦和加利福尼亚州旧金山有关联。\n请拨打FBI免费举报热线1-800-CALL-FBI（1-800-225-5324）。\n如需更多信息，请点击此处。\n如要报告错字或更正，请点击此处。\n版权所有2025 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2025-09-27T02:25:53.503000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1677","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学就“仇恨与不当行为”报道发表声明","title_en":"Arkansas State University releases statement amid reports of “hateful and inappropriate behavior”","summary_cn":"KAIT报道，阿肯色州立大学校长托德·希尔兹就校园内“仇恨和不当行为”的报道发表声明。希尔兹表示，校方已收到相关报告，正由有关部门严肃调查，并强调此类行为在阿肯色州立大学没有立足之地，不符合学校的价值观和学术共同体标准。他呼吁知情者举报，同时表示学校致力于营造安全的学习环境。声明未具体说明正在调查的事件内容。","summary_en":"KAIT reports that Arkansas State University Chancellor Todd Shields issued a statement following reports of 'hateful and inappropriate behavior' on campus. Shields said the incidents are being taken very seriously and are under investigation by the appropriate offices, adding that such behavior has no place at Arkansas State and is inconsistent with institutional values. He urged anyone who witnessed or experienced inappropriate behavior to report it and said the university is committed to a safe learning environment. The statement did not specify the incidents under investigation.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T17:14:25.388498+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/02/02/arkansas-state-university-releases-statement-amid-reports-hateful-inappropriate-behavior/","content":"Arkansas State University releases statement amid reports of “hateful and inappropriate behavior”By K8 NewsdeskPublished: Feb. 1, 2026 at 10:56 PM CST|Updated: Feb. 1, 2026 at 10:57 PM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) - Arkansas State University Chancellor Todd Shields has released a statement following reports of “deeply inappropriate behavior” on campus.In the statement, the chancellor acknowledged the school has received reports of “hateful and inappropriate behavior.”“These incidents are being taken very seriously, and investigations are underway by the appropriate offices,” he said in the statement. “Let me be clear: this type of behavior has no place at Arkansas State. It is not consistent with our institutional values and the standards we uphold as an academic community.”Shields said the university was committed to fostering a safe learning environment.“While we honor each person’s individual beliefs and values, we also expect all members of our community to act with integrity and accountability in both their words and their actions,” he said.He urged anyone who has witnessed or experienced inappropriate behavior to report it.The statement did not specify what incidents were under investigation.Chancellor Shields’ complete statement is available on the university’s website.To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学就“充满仇恨且不当的行为”报道发布声明\n作者：K8 新闻编辑部\n发布时间：2026年2月1日美国中部标准时间晚上10:56｜更新时间：2026年2月1日美国中部标准时间晚上10:57\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上添加为首选来源\n\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——阿肯色州立大学校长托德·希尔兹在校园内出现“极其不当行为”的报道后发布了一份声明。\n\n声明中，校长承认学校已收到有关“充满仇恨且不当的行为”的报告。\n\n“这些事件正受到非常严肃的对待，相关办公室正在展开调查，”他在声明中说。“我要明确表示：这类行为在阿肯色州立大学没有立足之地。它不符合我们的机构价值观，也不符合我们作为学术共同体所坚持的标准。”\n\n希尔兹表示，大学致力于营造安全的学习环境。\n\n“在尊重每个人个人信仰和价值观的同时，我们也期待社区所有成员在言语和行动中都秉持正直并承担责任，”他说。\n\n他敦促任何目睹或经历过不当行为的人进行举报。\n\n该声明未具体说明正在调查哪些事件。\n\n希尔兹校长的完整声明可在该大学网站上查阅。\n\n如需报告错别字或更正，请点击此处。\n\n版权所有 2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-02-02T04:56:13.750000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1672","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学学生就网上流传的种族主义指控表达担忧","title_en":"Arkansas State University students share concerns about alleged racism reports surfacing online","summary_cn":"KAIT报道，阿肯色州立大学因网上流传的两起种族主义和不当行为报告引发学生不满。一起指控称一名宿舍助理使用种族歧视用语，另一起照片显示一名兄弟会学生背上写有种族歧视用语和纳粹标志。校长希尔兹此前发表声明称正在调查“仇恨和严重不当行为”。受访学生表示愤怒和失望，要求涉事兄弟会及宿舍助理受到停学或开除等处分。声明未指明具体调查哪起事件。","summary_en":"KAIT reports that racism allegations are roiling Arkansas State University after two separate reports of racism and inappropriate behavior circulated online. One report alleges a resident assistant used a racial slur; another showed a fraternity student with a racial slur and swastika written on their back. Chancellor Todd Shields had said the university is investigating 'hateful and deeply inappropriate behavior.' Students interviewed expressed anger and disappointment and called for the fraternity and the RA to face suspension or expulsion. The statement did not specify which incidents are being examined.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T17:14:10.946715+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/02/03/arkansas-state-university-students-share-concerns-about-alleged-racism-reports-surfacing-online/","content":"Arkansas State University students share concerns about alleged racism reports surfacing onlineBy Jake TesterPublished: Feb. 2, 2026 at 6:00 PM CST|Updated: Feb. 2, 2026 at 6:16 PM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) - Racism allegations are rocking Arkansas State University as students speak out after two separate reports of racism and inappropriate behavior circulated online.Arkansas State University Chancellor Todd Shields released a statement Sunday saying the university is investigating “hateful and deeply inappropriate behavior,” and that “this type of behavior has no place at Arkansas State.”One report alleges a resident assistant used a racial slur.Another showed a picture of a student at a fraternity with a racial slur and swastika written on their back.“I felt mad, I feel disappointed, I feel upset. Like, I have so many emotions,” said Andrea Arenales, a student.“Never did I think I would see that written on someone’s back or anything like that, and then the fact that it was posted,” said SaKamryn Furlow, a student.“I just feel really disappointed. We are all grown adults, like, why are we doing this at our certain age, writing hateful things?” Arenales said.Students are now pushing for action against those involved.“I would like that chapter to be like gone,” said Furlow. “Gone or like suspended,” said Ashley Ortiz, another student.“Yes, suspended; they deserve some sort of punishment,” said Furlow.Regarding the RA incident, students called for consequences.“Also, with the RA, like getting suspended or expelled,” said Arenales. “Yeah, he does not deserve his position,” said Furlow. “He doesn’t deserve it because he’s working with a bunch of minorities,” said Arenales.The chancellor’s statement confirmed investigations were underway but did not specify which incidents are being examined.Read the full statement.To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学学生分享对网上出现的涉嫌种族主义报告的担忧\n作者：Jake Tester\n发布时间：2026年2月2日 中部标准时间下午6:00 | 更新：2026年2月2日 中部标准时间下午6:16\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上添加为首选来源\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——随着两份关于种族主义和不当行为的独立报告在网上流传，学生发声后，阿肯色州立大学正因种族主义指控而震动。\n阿肯色州立大学校长 Todd Shields 周日发表声明称，该校正在调查“仇恨且极其不当的行为”，并表示“这种行为在阿肯色州立大学没有立足之地”。\n一份报告指称，一名住校助理使用了种族侮辱性词语。\n另一份报告展示了一张照片：一名学生在兄弟会中，其背上写有种族侮辱性词语和纳粹标志。\n“我感到愤怒、失望和难过。我有太多情绪了，”学生 Andrea Arenales 说。\n“我从没想过会看到有人背上写着那种东西之类的，然后更别提它还被发布出来，”学生 SaKamryn Furlow 说。\n“我真的很失望。我们都是成年人了，为什么在这个年纪还要做这种事，写下仇恨的东西？”Arenales 说。\n学生们现在要求对涉事者采取行动。\n“我希望那个分会消失，”Furlow 说。“消失，或者被停牌，”另一名学生 Ashley Ortiz 说。\n“是的，被停牌；他们应该受到某种惩罚，”Furlow 说。\n关于住校助理事件，学生们要求追究责任。\n“还有住校助理，也应该被停职或开除，”Arenales 说。“是的，他不配拥有这个职位，”Furlow 说。“他不配，因为他面对的是一群少数族裔学生，”Arenales 说。\n校长的声明确认调查正在进行，但未具体说明正在调查哪些事件。\n阅读完整声明。\n如需报告错别字或更正，请点击此处。\n版权所有 2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-02-03T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1654","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学创下入学人数纪录","title_en":"Arkansas State University sets enrollment record","summary_cn":"KAIT报道，阿肯色州立大学宣布2026年春季学期注册学生达16145人，创历史新高，较去年春季增长6.4%，为连续第五个破纪录学期。校内注册人数增长8.4%至8141人，在线注册人数也创纪录达8004人，增长4.5%。校长托德·希尔兹表示，连续五个破纪录学期并非偶然，反映了教职员工在学术、可负担性和学生成功方面的投入，以及阿肯色州和中南部家庭对学校的信任。","summary_en":"KAIT reports that Arkansas State University announced record enrollment of 16,145 students for the 2026 spring semester, a 6.4% increase over last spring and the fifth consecutive record-breaking semester. On-campus enrollment rose 8.4% to 8,141 students, while online enrollment set a record of 8,004 students, up 4.5%. Chancellor Todd Shields said five consecutive record-breaking semesters don't happen by chance and reflect intentional investments by faculty and staff in academics, affordability and student success, as well as the trust placed in A-State by Arkansas and Mid-South families.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-24T17:11:42.443654+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/02/04/arkansas-state-university-sets-enrollment-record/","content":"Arkansas State University sets enrollment recordBy K8 NewsdeskPublished: Feb. 4, 2026 at 2:08 PM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) - More students are enrolled at Arkansas State University than at any time in its history.The university announced Wednesday that 16,145 students enrolled for the 2026 spring semester. That’s a 6.4% increase over last spring’s enrollment and fifth consecutive record-breaking semester for the university.“Five consecutive record-breaking semesters don’t happen by chance,” said Chancellor Todd Shields. “They reflect intentional investments by dedicated faculty and staff in academics, affordability and student success, and the trust Arkansas and Mid-South families place in what we are building at A-State.”On-campus enrollment saw an 8.4% increase from last year to 8,141 students. Online enrollment also set a new record with 8,004 students, a 4.5% increase.Read the full report.Three A-State Pack Leaders smile and pose with a “Found My Place in the Pack” sign.(Arkansas State University)To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学创下招生纪录\n作者：K8新闻编辑部\n发布时间：2026年2月4日，美国中部标准时间下午2:08\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——阿肯色州立大学的在校学生人数达到建校以来最高水平。\n该大学周三宣布，2026年春季学期共有16,145名学生入学。这比去年春季的招生人数增长6.4%，也是该大学连续第五个创纪录的学期。\n校长托德·希尔兹表示：“连续五个学期打破纪录并非偶然。这反映了敬业的教职员工在学术、可负担性和学生成功方面的有意投入，以及阿肯色州和中南部地区家庭对我们在A-State所建设事业的信任。”\n校内招生人数较去年增长8.4%，达到8,141人。在线招生也创下新纪录，达到8,004人，增长4.5%。\n阅读完整报道。\n三名A-State Pack Leaders面带笑容，手持写有“我在这个团队中找到了自己的位置”的标语牌合影。\n（阿肯色州立大学）\n如需报告错别字或更正，请点击此处。\n版权所有 © 2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-02-04T20:08:41.016000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1645","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学纽波特分校获资助新建护理设施","title_en":"Arkansas State University Newport secures funding for new nursing facility","summary_cn":"阿肯色州立大学纽波特分校经三年半筹款，已从阿肯色州立大学系统、地方捐赠者及联邦和州政府获得资金，将新建健康科学中心，使护理及相关医疗专业招生规模翻倍。临时校长艾克·惠勒表示，现有护理课程所在的校园最老建筑已逾50年，新设施将配备模拟教室等先进设备，目标今年破土动工，并期望五年内改善本地区及邻近各州整体健康水平。","summary_en":"Arkansas State University Newport has secured funding after three and a half years of fundraising from the Arkansas State University System, local donors, and federal and state sources to build a new Center for Health Sciences that will double the number of nursing and healthcare students it trains. Interim Chancellor Ike Wheeler said the current nursing program occupies the campus's oldest building, over 50 years old, and the new state-of-the-art facility will include simulation rooms. He aims to break ground this year and hopes to improve regional health within five years.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T17:10:35.857883+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/02/06/arkansas-state-university-newport-secures-funding-new-nursing-facility/","content":"Arkansas State University Newport secures funding for new nursing facilityBy Jake TesterPublished: Feb. 5, 2026 at 6:40 PM CST|Updated: Feb. 5, 2026 at 10:16 PM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleNEWPORT, Ark. (KAIT) -Arkansas is facing a critical nursing shortage, but Arkansas State University Newport is taking action. The school has secured funding for a new state-of-the-art facility called the Center for Health Sciences that will double the number of nurses they train.“It’s going to have amazing results, not just for the students in the area today, but for generations to come,” said Ike Wheeler, interim chancellor of ASU Newport.A decade-long vision is becoming reality at Arkansas State University Newport. The school is now just steps away from breaking ground on a new facility designed to transform its nursing program.After three and a half years of fundraising efforts, the university has assembled support from the Arkansas State University System, local donors, and both federal and state funding.For Wheeler, this project represents more than just a building. It’s the answer to a critical workforce need across the state.“This facility will allow us to not only serve students, but to double the number of students that we serve in our nursing healthcare professions,” Wheeler said.The new building comes at the right time. The current nursing program operates out of the oldest building on campus at over 50 years old.“The building that these courses are being offered now is the oldest building on campus. It’s been a great building and it’s done great stuff, but it’s had its challenges. This will be state of the art, this will be simulation rooms, these will be things that make our graduates even more successful,” Wheeler said.This vision extends beyond Newport. Wheeler sees this investment improving healthcare across the region and beyond.“It is my goal 5 years down the road that we have programs that are full of students, and that we have programs that are turning out young women and men that are well trained, as well as, seeing the overall health of the region improve, not just Newport, not just Arkansas, but the contiguous states,” Wheeler said.While there are still procedural hurdles to clear through the school board, Wheeler is optimistic. His goal is to break ground this year, turning this long-awaited dream into tangible progress.To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学纽波特分校获得新护理设施资金\n作者：Jake Tester\n发布时间：2026年2月5日中部标准时间下午6:40 | 更新：2026年2月5日中部标准时间晚上10:16\n分享\n将我们添加到Google\n在Google中添加为首选来源\n阿肯色州纽波特（KAIT）——阿肯色州正面临严重的护理人员短缺，但阿肯色州立大学纽波特分校正在采取行动。该校已为一座名为健康科学中心的全新先进设施获得资金，该设施将使他们培养的护士数量增加一倍。\n“这将带来惊人的成果，不仅惠及今天当地的学生，也惠及未来几代人，”阿肯色州立大学纽波特分校临时校长Ike Wheeler说。\n阿肯色州立大学纽波特分校长达十年的愿景正在成为现实。该校距离为一座旨在改变其护理项目的新设施奠基已近在咫尺。\n经过三年半的筹款工作，该大学已获得阿肯色州立大学系统、当地捐赠者以及联邦和州两级资金的支持。\n对Wheeler来说，这个项目不仅仅是一栋建筑。它是解决全州关键劳动力需求的答案。\n“这座设施不仅能让我们服务学生，还能让我们将护理和医疗专业服务的学生人数增加一倍，”Wheeler说。\n新大楼来得正是时候。目前的护理项目在校园最古老的建筑内运行，该建筑已有50多年历史。\n“目前开设这些课程的建筑是校园里最古老的建筑。它一直是一栋很棒的建筑，也发挥了很大作用，但也面临一些挑战。这将是一座最先进的设施，将配备模拟室，这些设施会让我们的毕业生取得更大成功，”Wheeler说。\n这一愿景超越了纽波特。Wheeler认为，这项投资将改善整个地区乃至更广范围的医疗服务。\n“我的目标是，五年后，我们的项目里坐满学生，并且我们培养出训练有素的年轻男女，同时看到整个地区的健康状况得到改善，不仅是纽波特，不仅是阿肯色州，还包括邻近各州，”Wheeler说。\n尽管仍需通过校董会完成程序性障碍，Wheeler对此持乐观态度。他的目标是在今年奠基，将这一等待已久的梦想转化为切实进展。\n如需报告错别字或更正，请点击此处。\n版权所有2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-02-06T00:40:06.995000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1429","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学设立阅读障碍研究实验室","title_en":"Arkansas State University establishes dyslexia research lab","summary_cn":"阿肯色州立大学传播障碍系成立ALLIANCE实验室，帮助有学习困难的儿童，由临床服务主任阿里安·佩特领导，是该校二十年来服务东北阿肯色阅读困难学生工作的延伸。实验室与计算机科学系等跨学科合作开展三项研究，将读写科学与技术创新结合，用于阅读障碍的早期识别和干预。阅读障碍影响15%至20%人口，干预在幼儿园和一年级最有效。实验室同时为言语语言病理学研究生提供培训。","summary_en":"Arkansas State University's Department of Communication Disorders has established the ALLIANCE Lab to assist children with learning difficulties, led by Arianne Pait, director of clinical services. It evolves a two-decade commitment to struggling readers in Northeast Arkansas. The lab collaborates across disciplines, including computer science, on three research projects integrating literacy science with technology for earlier dyslexia identification and intervention. Dyslexia affects 15-20% of the population, and intervention is most effective in kindergarten and first grade. The lab also trains speech-language pathology graduate students.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T17:06:28.408661+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/03/09/arkansas-state-university-establishes-dyslexia-research-lab/","content":"Arkansas State University establishes dyslexia research labArkansas State University’s Department of Communication Disorders has established an ALLIANCE Lab to assist children with learning difficulties.By K8 NewsdeskPublished: Mar. 9, 2026 at 5:34 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT/Edited News Release) - Arkansas State University’s Department of Communication Disorders has established an ALLIANCE (Applied Literacy Learning through Innovation, Collaboration and Evidence) Lab to assist children with learning difficulties.The lab, led by Arianne Pait, director of clinical services in communication disorders, represents the evolution of a two-decade commitment to serving struggling readers in Northeast Arkansas. This also expands research using technology to improve early intervention.“This marks an expansion into cutting-edge research using technology to improve early identification and intervention for dyslexia,” said Pait, who also works as an assistant professor of communication disorders at A-State.First started in 2004 with a service-learning partnership with Brookland Public School District, ALLIANCE Lab has created opportunities for students in the communication disorders graduate program. Students have worked to provide evidence-based literacy interventions to assist school-age children with reading difficulties.“As the demand for services grew throughout the region, we moved the program to the A-State Speech and Hearing Center, allowing greater access for underserved K-12 students across Northeast Arkansas,” added Pait.The formal establishment of the ALLIANCE Lab provides infrastructure for enhanced research collaboration and expanded student mentorship opportunities.“What began more than 20 years ago has grown into a comprehensive program that serves students throughout our region,” Pait continued. “The ALLIANCE Lab allows us to formalize our research efforts, collaborate with experts across disciplines, and develop innovative tools that can identify and support struggling readers earlier and more effectively than ever before.”Dyslexia affects 15-20% of the population. Despite its prevalence, dyslexia is often not identified until third grade or later. Intervention is most effective when provided in kindergarten and first grade, before reading difficulties compound and negatively impact learning across all academic areas.Members of the ALLIANCE Lab, including Dr. Jake Qualls, associate professor of bioinformatics in the Department of Computer Science, are collaborating in three research projects that integrate literacy science with technological innovation. “These projects represent exactly what the ALLIANCE acronym stands for,” Pait explained. “We are taking applied research questions that matter for real children in real classrooms, using innovative technology to solve practical problems, collaborating across disciplines to combine expertise in literacy and computer science, and ensuring everything we do is grounded in evidence. This is research with immediate impact potential.” The ALLIANCE Lab’s research agenda extends beyond current projects to encompass broader questions about literacy development, dyslexia identification, and effective intervention.The lab also serves as a critical training site for graduate students in speech-language pathology, preparing future clinicians to assess and treat literacy disorders.For more information about the ALLIANCE Lab for Dyslexia Research and Literacy Innovation, to inquire about clinical services, to explore research collaboration opportunities, or to learn about student mentorship possibilities, one may contact Arianne Pait at apait@AState.edu. Subscribe to the K8 News YouTube channel.To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学成立阅读障碍研究实验室\n阿肯色州立大学传播障碍系成立了ALLIANCE实验室，以帮助有学习困难的儿童。\n作者：K8 Newsdesk\n发布时间：2026年3月9日美国中部夏令时间下午5:34\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n将我们添加为Google首选来源\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT/编辑新闻稿）——阿肯色州立大学传播障碍系成立了ALLIANCE（通过创新、协作和证据开展应用读写学习）实验室，以帮助有学习困难的儿童。\n\n该实验室由传播障碍临床服务主任Arianne Pait领导，体现了二十年来致力于服务阿肯色州东北部阅读困难者的演进。此举还扩大了利用技术改善早期干预的研究。\n\n“这标志着我们拓展至利用技术改善阅读障碍早期识别和干预的前沿研究，”Pait说。她同时担任阿肯色州立大学传播障碍学助理教授。\n\nALLIANCE实验室最初于2004年通过与Brookland公立学区的服务学习合作关系启动，为传播障碍研究生项目的学生创造了机会。学生们一直致力于提供循证读写干预，以帮助有阅读困难的学龄儿童。\n\nPait补充说：“随着整个地区对服务的需求增长，我们将该项目迁至阿肯色州立大学言语与听力中心，使阿肯色州东北部服务不足的K-12学生能够获得更广泛的服务。”\n\nALLIANCE实验室的正式成立为加强研究合作和扩大学生导师指导机会提供了基础设施。\n\nPait继续说：“20多年前开始的工作，已发展为服务我们地区各地学生的综合项目。ALLIANCE实验室使我们能够将研究工作正式化，与跨学科专家协作，并开发创新工具，以比以往更早、更有效地识别和支持阅读困难者。”\n\n阅读障碍影响15–20%的人口。尽管其很常见，阅读障碍通常要到三年级或更晚才被识别。若在幼儿园和一年级提供干预，在阅读困难累积并对所有学科领域的学习造成负面影响之前，干预效果最为显著。\n\nALLIANCE实验室成员，包括计算机科学系生物信息学副教授Jake Qualls博士，正在合作开展三个将读写科学与技术创新结合的研究项目。Pait解释道：“这些项目正体现了ALLIANCE这一首字母缩略词的含义。我们围绕真实教室中真实儿童所面临的重要应用研究问题，利用创新技术解决实际问题，开展跨学科合作以结合读写与计算机科学方面的专长，并确保我们所做的一切均以证据为基础。这是具有即时影响潜力的研究。”ALLIANCE实验室的研究议程不止于当前项目，还涵盖关于读写发展、阅读障碍识别和有效干预的更广泛问题。\n\n该实验室还是言语语言病理学研究生的重要培训场所，为未来临床医生评估和治疗读写障碍做好准备。\n\n如需了解更多关于阅读障碍研究与读写创新ALLIANCE实验室的信息、咨询临床服务、探索研究合作机会，或了解学生导师指导的可能性，可通过apait@AState.edu联系Arianne Pait。订阅K8 News YouTube频道。\n\n如需报告错字或要求更正，请点击此处。\n\n版权所有©2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-03-09T22:34:35.980000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1265","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学博物馆举办“透过孩子的眼睛”艺术展","title_en":"Arkansas State University Museum opens ‘Through a Child’s Eyes’ art display","summary_cn":"阿肯色州立大学博物馆于周六开放“透过孩子的眼睛”艺术展，展出东北阿肯色州幼儿园至八年级学生的200多件作品，由教师提交并分年级评选。博物馆策展人吉尔·卡里表示，最佳展品出自一名五岁幼儿园儿童，十分罕见。家长带孩子前来观展拍照。卡里引用毕加索的话称每个孩子都是艺术家，展览将持续整个四月。","summary_en":"The Arkansas State University Museum opened its \"Through a Child's Eyes\" art display on Saturday, featuring more than 200 pieces by pre-K through eighth grade students from around Northeast Arkansas, submitted by teachers and judged by grade. Curator Jill Kary said the best-in-show piece was created by a 5-year-old kindergartner, which is rare. Parents and children came to view the art and take pictures. Kary cited Picasso's words that every child is an artist. The display will remain up for the month of April.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-24T17:02:13.329111+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/03/28/arkansas-state-university-museum-opens-through-childs-eyes-art-display/","content":"Arkansas State University Museum opens ‘Through a Child’s Eyes’ art displayBy Bryant KwileckiPublished: Mar. 28, 2026 at 5:02 PM CDT|Updated: Mar. 28, 2026 at 6:22 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) - The Arkansas State University Museum opened its “Through a Child’s Eyes” art display on Saturday.The display features art from pre-K through eighth grade students from around Northeast Arkansas. Teachers submitted the art pieces to the museum. The art pieces are judged and each grade gets a winner.More than 200 art pieces are on display. Parents with their children came to see the art and take pictures.The best in show piece was created by a 5-year-old kindergartner, which is rare to see, said Jill Kary, curator of the Arkansas State University Museum.“We love meeting these little artists and they have been proudly showing us their art, and they have just standing beside them, having their pictures made,” Kary said. “Every child is a winner and like Picasso said, ‘Every child is an artist.’”Kary said the display is a beautiful way to see a child’s imagination.“We’re looking at their imaginations and it so much to look and what you’re seeing is a representation of everything that’s in their mind and that’s what makes it so popular,” Kary said.The display will be up for the month of April.To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学博物馆举办“透过儿童的眼睛”艺术展\n作者：Bryant Kwilecki\n发布时间：2026年3月28日下午5:02（美国中部夏令时）｜更新时间：2026年3月28日下午6:22（美国中部夏令时）\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上将其添加为首选来源\n\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——阿肯色州立大学博物馆周六开设了“透过儿童的眼睛”艺术展。\n\n展览展出来自阿肯色州东北部各地学前班至八年级学生的艺术作品。教师将作品提交给博物馆参展。作品将接受评审，每个年级都会选出一名获胜者。\n\n展出的艺术作品超过200件。家长带着孩子前来观看作品并拍照。\n\n博物馆馆长 Jill Kary 表示，最佳展品由一名5岁的幼儿园学生创作，这很罕见。\n\nKary 说：“我们喜欢见到这些小艺术家，他们骄傲地向我们展示自己的作品，就站在作品旁边拍照。每个孩子都是赢家，正如毕加索所说，‘每个孩子都是艺术家。’”\n\nKary 表示，这个展览是了解儿童想象力的美好方式。\n\nKary 说：“我们在看他们的想象力，有这么多值得看的东西；你看到的是他们脑海中一切事物的呈现，这正是它如此受欢迎的原因。”\n\n展览将持续整个4月。\n\n如需报告错别字或更正，请点击此处。\n版权所有 © 2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-03-28T22:02:42.115000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1254","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学卡塔尔校区转为远程教学","title_en":"Arkansas State University-Qatar campus shifts to remote learning","summary_cn":"随着中东紧张局势升级，阿肯色州立大学位于多哈的卡塔尔校区转为线上授课。校方周一宣布，其全球研究学院校区立即生效远程教学，直至另行通知。校方要求学生定期查看学校邮箱，并准备在线参加所有课程，同时表示学生安全仍是首要任务。","summary_en":"As tensions rise in the Middle East, Arkansas State University's Qatar campus in Doha is shifting to online-only classes. The university announced Monday that remote learning is in effect at its Global Studies Institute campus, effective immediately and continuing until further notice. Students are asked to check their university email regularly and be prepared to attend all sessions online. The university said student safety remains its top priority.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-24T17:01:03.998827+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/03/30/arkansas-state-university-qatar-campus-shifts-remote-learning/","content":"Arkansas State University-Qatar campus shifts to remote learningBy K8 NewsdeskPublished: Mar. 30, 2026 at 5:45 PM CDT|Updated: Mar. 30, 2026 at 6:14 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleDOHA, Qatar (KAIT) - As tensions rise in the Middle East, Arkansas State University’s Qatar campus is shifting to online-only classes.The university announced Monday that remote learning is in effect at its Global Studies Institute campus in Doha. The change is effective immediately and will continue until further notice.Students are being asked to check their university email regularly and to be prepared to attend all sessions online. The university said student safety remains its top priority.To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学卡塔尔校区转为远程教学\n作者：K8新闻编辑部\n发布时间：2026年3月30日，美国中部夏令时间下午5:45｜更新：2026年3月30日，美国中部夏令时间下午6:14\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n卡塔尔多哈（KAIT）——随着中东紧张局势升温，阿肯色州立大学卡塔尔校区正转为仅在线授课。\n该大学周一宣布，其位于多哈的全球研究学院校区已实施远程教学。这一调整立即生效，并将持续至另行通知。\n校方要求学生定期查看大学电子邮件，并做好在线参加所有课程的准备。大学表示，学生安全仍是其首要任务。\n如需报告错别字或更正，请点击此处。\n版权所有 © 2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-03-30T22:45:47.184000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1111","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学枪击事件正在调查中，多人受伤","title_en":"Shooting under investigation at Arkansas State University, multiple injured","summary_cn":"阿肯色州立大学琼斯伯勒校区4月26日凌晨发生枪击，造成四人受伤，其中三人为该校学生。校方称接到枪击报警后，一名学生在现场接受治疗，另三人送医，伤势多为轻微且情况稳定。警方报告列出两名嫌疑人，未公布姓名。校董事会主席表示该活动未经学校批准，案件已移交阿肯色州警方，校方也将审查事件经过。","summary_en":"A shooting at Arkansas State University in Jonesboro early on April 26 left four people injured, including three A-State students. One student was treated at the scene and three others were taken to hospitals with mostly minor, stable conditions. A university police report listed two suspects without releasing names. The Board of Trustees chair said the gathering was not university-sanctioned, and the investigation was turned over to Arkansas State Police while the university reviews the circumstances.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:52:48.023327+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/04/26/shooting-under-investigation-arkansas-state-university-multiple-injured/","content":"Shooting under investigation at Arkansas State University, multiple injuredAn overnight shooting at Arkansas State University in Jonesboro left four people injured.By K8 NewsdeskPublished: Apr. 26, 2026 at 2:15 AM CDT|Updated: Apr. 27, 2026 at 4:05 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) - A shooting at Arkansas State University in Jonesboro left four people injured.In a Sunday statement, the university said a 911 call was received just after midnight April 26 regarding shots fired in the area.Four people were injured, including three A-State students. One student was treated at the scene, and three other people were taken to local hospitals with mostly minor conditions and are currently stable.According to the University Police Department’s initial incident report, a 19-year-old woman suffered a gunshot wound to the right leg. Another 19-year-old woman suffered a minor injury to her leg and abdomen, believed to be from shrapnel. The other victims suffered minor scrapes and cuts.There were two suspects listed in the UPD report, including a 19-year-old man, but no names or identifying information was provided.Robert Rudolph Jr., chair of the ASU Board of Trustees, released the following statement Monday in response to the incident:“We want to acknowledge there was a shooting incident Saturday night at a social gathering on the Arkansas State campus which was not sanctioned by the university. Our thoughts are with the four individuals who were injured, and we’re grateful there were no serious injuries. We’re thankful to our campus police and other local law enforcement who responded and now have turned over the investigation to the Arkansas State Police. A-State will also review all the circumstances of the event. Campus alert systems kept students informed, and we are committed to doing everything possible to keep our campuses safe.”Robert Rudolph Jr.Todd Clark, the university’s chief marketing and communications officer, said a gathering was underway at Unity Park at the time of the shooting. An email alert later notified the campus community of an “active shooter” incident.Clark later said there was no active threat and that the shooting was isolated to Unity Park.K8 News was previously told by Arkansas State Police two students were injured during the incident. The university has since confirmed three students were injured.The university also provided a message to the public:“We are grateful that no lives were lost in this incident. Our thoughts are with those who were injured and their families.Our strength as a university lies in our close-knit campus and the way we care for one another. We encourage everyone to stay connected and support each other in the days ahead.\"Arkansas State UniversityA-State encouraged students to contact the University Counseling Center if they need support.The shooting remains under investigation. The university asks anyone with information to call Arkansas State Police at 870-935-7303.To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学枪击事件正在调查，多人受伤\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒的阿肯色州立大学发生凌晨枪击事件，造成4人受伤。\n作者：K8新闻编辑部 发布：2026年4月26日凌晨2:15 CDT｜更新：2026年4月27日下午4:05 CDT 分享 在Google上添加我们 在Google上设为首选来源\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——琼斯伯勒阿肯色州立大学发生的一起枪击事件造成4人受伤。\n该大学在周日的一份声明中表示，4月26日刚过午夜时，接到一通有关该地区发生枪击的911电话。\n4人受伤，其中包括3名阿肯色州立大学学生。一名学生在现场接受治疗，另有3人被送往当地医院，伤势大多较轻，目前情况稳定。\n根据大学警察部门的初步事件报告，一名19岁女子右腿中枪。另一名19岁女子腿部和腹部受到轻伤，据信是弹片所致。其他受害者遭受轻微擦伤和割伤。\n大学警察部门报告中列出两名嫌疑人，其中包括一名19岁男子，但未提供姓名或身份信息。\n阿肯色州立大学董事会主席小罗伯特·鲁道夫周一就该事件发表如下声明：\n“我们想确认，周六晚间在阿肯色州立大学校园内一次未获校方批准的社交聚会上发生了枪击事件。我们牵挂4名受伤人员，并庆幸没有发生严重伤害。我们感谢作出响应的校园警察和其他地方执法部门，他们现已将调查移交给阿肯色州警察。阿肯色州立大学也将审查此次事件的所有情况。校园警报系统让学生及时了解情况，我们致力于竭尽所能保障校园安全。”\n小罗伯特·鲁道夫\n该大学首席营销与传播官托德·克拉克表示，枪击发生时，Unity Park正在举行聚会。随后的一封电子邮件警报通知校园社区发生了“活跃枪手”事件。\n克拉克后来表示，不存在持续威胁，枪击事件仅限于Unity Park。\nK8新闻此前获阿肯色州警察告知，事件中有两名学生受伤。该大学此后确认有3名学生受伤。\n该大学还向公众发布了一则消息：\n“我们庆幸此次事件没有人员丧生。我们牵挂受伤人员及其家属。\n我们作为一所大学的力量，源于紧密团结的校园以及彼此关怀的方式。我们鼓励大家在未来几天保持联系、相互支持。”\n阿肯色州立大学\n阿肯色州立大学鼓励需要支持的学生联系大学咨询中心。\n枪击事件仍在调查中。该大学请任何掌握信息的人致电阿肯色州警察，电话：870-935-7303。\n如需报告错别字或更正，请点击此处。\n版权所有 © 2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-04-26T07:15:21.501000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1093","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学披露未经登记的活动导致校园枪击","title_en":"Arkansas State University reveals unregistered event led to campus shooting","summary_cn":"阿肯色州立大学官员表示，4月27日披露琼斯伯勒校区Unity Park一场未经学校登记的聚会引发枪击，造成四人受伤，其中一名学生脚踝中弹。校方称第三方因场地临时取消而将活动移至Unity Park，违反学校政策，且警方到场时被参与者误导以为活动已登记。枪击后学校通过RAVE系统发布警报，但部分短信未发出，校方随后通过邮件和门户补充通知。案件已由阿肯色州警方接手，校方也将自行调查。","summary_en":"Arkansas State University officials said an unregistered gathering at Unity Park led to an early Sunday shooting that injured four people, including a student shot in the ankle. A third party moved the event to Unity Park after a last-minute venue cancellation, violating university policy, and police were misled that it was registered. After shots were fired, the university used its RAVE alert system, but some text messages failed to send, prompting duplicate emails and other notifications. Arkansas State Police took over the investigation, and the university will conduct its own review.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:49:33.794220+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/04/27/arkansas-state-university-reveals-unregistered-event-led-campus-shooting/","content":"Arkansas State University reveals unregistered event led to campus shootingBy Alejandra HernándezPublished: Apr. 27, 2026 at 6:01 PM CDT|Updated: Apr. 27, 2026 at 6:51 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) - Arkansas State University officials said an unregistered gathering at Unity Park led to a shooting early Sunday that injured four people, including one student who was shot in the ankle.The university said the event was not school sanctioned. A third party had a last-minute cancellation at its venue and decided to move the party to Unity Park, which was not in compliance with university policy.Todd Clark, chief marketing and communications officer at Arkansas State University, said police were misled about the event.“Two police officers on campus noticed the event taking place. When they approached the event, they were assured by event participants that the event was registered,” Clark said.The university requires events to be registered with Student Affairs, which shares location, date and time with the university. Events after 10 p.m. are allowed and the university advises organizers on security, noise control, controlled access, and maximum crowd capacity. Despite not being registered, officers were notified and sent to the gathering. The university said the officers were misled and told the event was organized.“And because of the amount of people that were there and the same organization of the event, they had reason to believe that they were being truthful,” Clark said.Once shots rang out after midnight, the university used its RAVE active messaging system to send a campus alert, but not everyone received an alert.“It was determined after the initial alert went out that the text message did not fire,” Clark said. “Dispatch tried to remedy and send it again, which is why we got duplicate emails and duplicate desk notifications.”As information and misinformation started circulating online and the university became aware of the alert malfunction, Clark said the university took other methods to inform parents and students.“We also decided to send out a post on the parent Facebook group,” Clark said. “And then we also pushed out an alert through our PAC portal, which would have spawned a push notification on cell phones and another campus email.”Arkansas State Police have taken over the shooting investigation, but Clark said the university will also conduct its own investigation into the matter to make sure another incident does not happen on campus.“We’ll look at what went right, what went wrong, to make sure that the policies and procedures we have in place are effective and working as they are intended,” Clark said.He said the university tried to contact the students who were injured and have spoken to one of them. He said all three are now back on campus.Arkansas State Police have not released information on any possible suspect or suspects. To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学披露，未登记活动导致校园枪击案\n作者：Alejandra Hernández\n发表于：2026年4月27日中部夏令时间下午6:01\n更新于：2026年4月27日中部夏令时间下午6:51\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上添加为首选来源\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——阿肯色州立大学官员表示，Unity Park 一场未登记的聚会导致周日凌晨发生枪击，造成4人受伤，其中包括一名脚踝中弹的学生。\n\n该大学表示，这场活动未经学校批准。一个第三方场地临时取消了活动，随后决定将聚会转移到 Unity Park，但这不符合大学政策。\n\n阿肯色州立大学首席营销与传播官 Todd Clark 表示，警方被误导了。\n\n“校园里的两名警察注意到活动正在举行。当他们接近活动现场时，活动参与者向他们保证活动已经登记，”Clark 说。\n\n该大学要求活动向学生事务部门登记，由该部门向大学提供活动地点、日期和时间。晚上10点后的活动可以获准举行，大学会就安保、噪音控制、出入口管控以及最大容纳人数向组织者提供指导。尽管活动没有登记，警方仍收到通知并被派往聚会现场。大学表示，警员被误导，被告知该活动已经组织妥当。\n\nClark 说：“由于现场人数众多，而且活动组织方式看起来也很正规，他们有理由相信对方说的是真话。”\n\n午夜过后枪声响起，大学使用 RAVE 主动消息系统发送校园警报，但并非所有人都收到警报。\n\nClark 说：“初次警报发出后，我们发现短信并未发送成功。调度部门试图补救并再次发送，这就是为什么我们收到了重复的电子邮件和重复的桌面通知。”\n\n随着信息和错误信息开始在网上传播，且大学意识到警报发生故障，Clark 表示，大学采取了其他方式通知家长和学生。\n\nClark 说：“我们还决定在家长 Facebook 群组发布一则消息。随后，我们也通过 PAC 门户推送了一条警报，这本应在手机上触发推送通知，并再发送一封校园电子邮件。”\n\n阿肯色州警方已经接手枪击案调查，但 Clark 表示，大学也将对此事展开自己的调查，以确保校园内不再发生类似事件。\n\nClark 说：“我们会查看哪些地方做对了、哪些地方出了问题，以确保现有的政策和程序有效，并按预期运行。”\n\n他说，大学试图联系受伤学生，并已与其中一人通话。他说，三人目前都已返回校园。\n\n阿肯色州警方尚未公布任何可能的嫌疑人信息。\n\n如需报告错字或更正，请点击此处。\n\n版权所有 2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-04-27T23:01:43.890000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1092","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学枪击事件：治疗师呼吁家庭关注创伤迹象","title_en":"Arkansas State University shooting: Therapist urges families to watch for trauma signs","summary_cn":"在阿肯色州立大学周末枪击造成四人受伤、其中三人为学生后，圣伯纳德医疗中心治疗师乔丹·泰勒提醒家长和同学关注创伤反应。她表示，紧急警报可能已触发学生的“战斗、逃跑或僵住”反应，接下来几天应注意退缩、噩梦、反复回想、注意力难以集中等迹象。她建议限制事后媒体接触，主动询问并再次询问对方状况，为需要帮助者提供安全空间。受伤的三名学生均已接受治疗并返回校园。","summary_en":"After a weekend shooting at Arkansas State University injured four people, three of them students, St. Bernards therapist Jordan Taylor urged families to watch for trauma signs. She said emergency alerts can trigger fight, flight, or freeze responses, and people should watch for withdrawal, nightmares, reliving the event, racing thoughts, and trouble concentrating. She recommended limiting media exposure, checking in and asking again, and offering a safe space. All three injured students were treated and are back on campus.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:49:07.036705+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/04/28/arkansas-state-university-shooting-therapist-urges-families-watch-trauma-signs/","content":"Arkansas State University shooting: Therapist urges families to watch for trauma signsSt. Bernards therapist Jordan Taylor says for many students and parents, that fear response had already taken hold.(kait)By Jake TesterPublished: Apr. 27, 2026 at 7:27 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) - A weekend shooting at Arkansas State University left four people hurt, three of them students. Shots rang out at Unity Park early Sunday morning. For many, the fear didn’t end when the gunfire stopped.Arkansas State University sent an emergency alert warning of an active shooter. While they later confirmed there was no ongoing threat, St. Bernards therapist Jordan Taylor says for many students and parents, that fear response had already taken hold.“Immediately we’re getting probably some type of notification of the event, and it kind of startles that fight, flight, or freeze response in our brain,” Taylor said. “So, you may literally freeze, kind of not knowing what to do.”Taylor says over the next few days, it’s important to watch for signs that someone is struggling more than they let on.“Withdrawing from people, withdrawing from social settings, maybe having some type of nightmares, reliving the event over and over again in your head, racing thoughts, not being able to concentrate on things around you, or again, in general, withdrawing from classes and things like that,” Taylor said.She says knowing the signs is only half of it. Knowing how to start that talk is just as important.“Whenever asked those questions, it kind of prompts them and it’s a little bit easier for them to open up about,” Taylor said. “So whenever doing that, if they want to get professional help or if they want to just talk about it, being that safe space for them to do that.”Taylor also urges students and parents to be careful with social media after something like this.“My first recommendation would be maybe to just limit media exposure for some time after the event,” Taylor said. “A lot of information is going to come in at once, and that can be very overwhelming.”She says don’t wait for someone to come to you. Whether you’re a parent, a roommate, or a friend, check in, ask how they’re doing, and then ask again. Sometimes that second question is what opens the door.“As a parent, you know, seeing that, knowing that your child’s on campus, you can kind of have some of those same responses and wanting to be there for your child immediately,” Taylor said.All three students who were hurt were treated and are back on campus. Both Arkansas State and outside services like St. Bernards have counseling services available.To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学枪击案：治疗师敦促家庭留意创伤迹象\n圣伯纳兹治疗师Jordan Taylor表示，对许多学生和家长而言，这种恐惧反应已经出现。\n（KAIT）\n作者：Jake Tester\n发布于：2026年4月27日美国中部夏令时间晚上7:27\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n将其添加为Google首选来源\n\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——阿肯色州立大学上周末发生的一起枪击事件造成4人受伤，其中3人为学生。周日凌晨，Unity Park响起枪声。对许多人而言，枪声停止后，恐惧并未结束。\n\n阿肯色州立大学发出紧急警报，警告有活跃枪手。尽管该校后来确认不存在持续威胁，圣伯纳兹治疗师Jordan Taylor表示，对许多学生和家长而言，这种恐惧反应已经出现。\n\nTaylor说：“我们很可能会立刻收到有关这起事件的某种通知，这会惊动大脑中的战斗、逃跑或僵住反应。因此，你可能真的会僵住，不知道该怎么办。”\n\nTaylor表示，未来几天，重要的是留意某人是否比其表现出来的更难以应对。\n\nTaylor说：“疏远他人，退出社交场合，也许会做噩梦，在脑海中反复重历该事件，思绪飞快，无法专注于周围的事物，或者总体而言退出课程及诸如此类的活动。”\n\n她说，了解这些迹象只是一半；知道如何开始这场谈话同样重要。\n\nTaylor说：“提出这些问题时，会促使他们开口，也会让他们更容易敞开心扉谈论这件事。因此，在这样做时，无论他们想寻求专业帮助，还是只想谈谈，都要为他们提供一个可以这样做的安全空间。”\n\nTaylor还敦促学生和家长在发生此类事件后谨慎使用社交媒体。\n\nTaylor说：“我的首要建议是，事件发生后的一段时间内，或许应限制媒体接触。大量信息会同时涌入，这可能会令人不堪重负。”\n\n她说，不要等别人来找你。无论你是家长、室友还是朋友，都应关心一下，问问他们怎么样，然后再问一次。有时第二个问题正是打开话匣子的关键。\n\nTaylor说：“作为父母，看到那种情况，知道自己的孩子在校园里，你也可能会有同样的一些反应，并想立刻陪在孩子身边。”\n\n3名受伤学生均已接受治疗并返回校园。阿肯色州立大学及圣伯纳兹等外部机构均提供心理咨询服务。\n\n如需报告错字或更正，请点击此处。\n\n版权所有2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-04-28T00:27:59.903000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-991","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学预计本周末举行校史最大规模毕业典礼","title_en":"Arkansas State University expects largest commencement in school history this weekend","summary_cn":"阿肯色州立大学预计本周末在第一国民银行竞技场举行校史最大规模毕业典礼，将授予超过2500个学位，近1700名学生登台。校方提醒红狼大道及校园周边交通拥堵，建议提前到场，所有停车场开放且抬杆，但不要停在草地或Embassy Suites。每场仪式提前90分钟开门，实施透明包政策。由于多所地区高中也在此举行毕业典礼，相关提示同样适用。","summary_en":"Arkansas State University expects its largest commencement in school history this weekend at First National Bank Arena, awarding just over 2,500 degrees with nearly 1,700 students walking. Officials warned of heavy traffic on Red Wolf Boulevard and across campus, urged early arrival, and said all lots will be open with gates raised, but parking on grass or at Embassy Suites is prohibited. Doors open 90 minutes before each ceremony, and a clear-bag policy will be in effect. Many area high schools also graduate there, so the tips apply to them too.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:43:01.448752+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/05/07/arkansas-state-university-expects-largest-commencement-school-history-this-weekend/","content":"Arkansas State University expects largest commencement in school history this weekendBy Jake TesterPublished: May 7, 2026 at 4:50 PM CDT|Updated: May 7, 2026 at 6:20 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) -Arkansas State University is expecting its largest commencement in school history this weekend at First National Bank Arena, and officials are warning attendees to prepare for heavy traffic and crowded parking.Just over 2,500 degrees will be awarded, and nearly 1,700 students will walk the stage.Chief Marketing and Communications Officer Todd Clark said the weekend will be a celebration.“This weekend will be a huge celebration of life-changing degrees being conferred on our graduates,” Clark said. “It’s life-changing for the students, but also their families. It changes the entire trajectory of their lives.”Heavy traffic is expected on Red Wolf Boulevard and across campus.Officials are asking drivers to watch for pedestrians and take it slow in the parking lots.“We will have all of the lots open. Parking gates will be raised,” Clark said. “We just ask that people don’t park on grass, and don’t park at the Embassy Suites, because that’s reserved for hotel guests.”Doors open 90 minutes before each ceremony. A clear-bag policy will be in effect.Clark said, once graduates from the earlier colleges finish crossing the stage, seats will start opening up around the arena within 20 to 30 minutes.Graduating nursing student Jamyra Nelson said she is telling her family to arrive early.“I’ve told them multiple times come at like 12:30. I’m graduating at 2:00, get here super, super early so you can get in a good seat where you can see me,” Nelson said. “As a graduate, I am going to be here as soon as the doors open.”Graduating student Emily Reaves said she sent a message to her education major classmates.“I sent a message out to our little big group of all of our education majors, y’all need to get here early; and everyone’s stressing out now,” Reaves said.A majority of area high schools also hold their graduations at First National Bank Arena, meaning these tips apply to them as well.“It’s such an amazing thing that a majority of our regional high schools graduate in this building,” Clark said. “I think it’s a great introduction to the campus. We’re happy to host families and make sure that everyone has room to watch their graduates.”To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学预计本周末将举行校史上规模最大的毕业典礼\n作者：Jake Tester\n发布于：2026年5月7日中部夏令时间下午4:50｜更新于：2026年5月7日中部夏令时间下午6:20\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上将其添加为首选来源\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——阿肯色州立大学预计本周末将在第一国民银行体育馆举行校史上规模最大的毕业典礼，校方官员警告与会者要为交通拥堵和停车场拥挤做好准备。\n\n将授予2,500多个学位，近1,700名学生将登台。\n\n首席营销与传播官Todd Clark表示，本周末将是一场庆祝活动。\n\n“本周末将是庆祝向毕业生授予改变人生的学位的一场盛大活动，”Clark说，“这会改变学生的人生，也会改变他们家庭的人生。它会改变他们整个人生的发展轨迹。”\n\n预计红狼大道和整个校园将出现严重交通拥堵。\n\n官员要求驾驶员留意行人，并在停车场内缓慢行驶。\n\n“我们将开放所有停车场。停车闸门将抬起，”Clark说，“我们只要求大家不要停在草地上，也不要停在Embassy Suites，因为那里是为酒店客人预留的。”\n\n每场典礼开始前90分钟开门。将实施透明袋政策。\n\nClark表示，较早学院的毕业生完成登台后，体育馆内将在20至30分钟内陆续腾出座位。\n\n即将毕业的护理专业学生Jamyra Nelson说，她正告诉家人提前到达。\n\n“我已经多次告诉他们，大约12:30来。我2:00毕业，一定要非常、非常早到，这样你们就能坐到一个能看见我的好位置，”Nelson说，“作为毕业生，我会在开门后立刻到这里。”\n\n即将毕业的学生Emily Reaves说，她向教育专业的同学们发了一条消息。\n\n“我给我们所有教育专业学生的大群发了一条消息：你们得早点到；现在大家都在焦虑，”Reaves说。\n\n该地区大多数高中也在第一国民银行体育馆举行毕业典礼，因此这些建议同样适用于他们。\n\n“我们地区大多数高中在这栋建筑里毕业是一件非常棒的事，”Clark说，“我认为这是了解校园的绝佳开端。我们很高兴接待家庭，并确保每个人都有空间观看他们的毕业生。”\n\n如要报告错字或更正，请点击此处。\n\n版权所有2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-05-07T21:50:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-974","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学开始修复校园钟楼和时钟","title_en":"Arkansas State University begins restoring campus bell tower and clock","summary_cn":"阿肯色州立大学启动校园钟楼与时钟修复工程，起重机已进场。因时钟电机驱动故障、钟声停摆近一年，项目筹备近一年，内容包括更换新钟针、中央驱动装置及重新调校钟琴。项目负责人肖恩·布鲁尔表示，校园社区将乐见其恢复运转。施工预计本周末前完成。","summary_en":"Arkansas State University has begun restoring its campus bell tower and clock, with a crane set up on site. The project, nearly a year in the making after the clock's motor drive failed and the bells stopped working, includes new clock hands, a new center drive and a retuned carillon. Project manager Shawn Brewer said the campus community will enjoy seeing it running again. Construction is expected to wrap up by the end of the week.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:40:01.831807+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/05/11/arkansas-state-university-begins-restoring-campus-bell-tower-clock/","content":"Arkansas State University begins restoring campus bell tower and clockBy Jake TesterPublished: May 11, 2026 at 5:13 PM CDT|Updated: May 11, 2026 at 5:47 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) - A crane has been set up on Arkansas State University’s campus as crews work to restore the university’s bell tower and clock.The project has been in the works for nearly a year, after the clock’s motor drive failed and the bells stopped working.New clock hands, a new center drive, and a retuned carillon are all part of the upgrade.Shawn Brewer, project manager with the plan, design, and construction office, said the campus community will enjoy the restoration.“A lot of people that look up there and can see that it’s been almost eight o’clock for about a year now, because the motor of the clock hands has went out, the bells have quit working,” Brewer said. “So, just to get everything refurbished, renewed and back up and running, I think the campus community will enjoy it.”Construction is expected to wrap up by the end of the week.To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学开始修复校园钟楼和时钟\n作者：Jake Tester\n发布时间：2026年5月11日美国中部夏令时间下午5:13｜更新时间：2026年5月11日美国中部夏令时间下午5:47\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上添加为首选来源\n\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——阿肯色州立大学校园内已架设起一台起重机，工作人员正着手修复该大学的钟楼和时钟。\n\n在时钟的电机驱动器发生故障、钟声停止后，该项目已筹备近一年。\n\n新的时钟指针、新的中心驱动装置以及重新调音的钟琴均是此次升级的一部分。\n\n规划、设计与建设办公室的项目经理肖恩·布鲁尔表示，校园社区将会享受这次修复成果。\n\n“许多人抬头一看，会发现大约一年来一直快到八点钟，因为时钟指针的电机坏了，钟也不响了，”布鲁尔说，“所以，把一切翻新、更新并恢复运行，我认为校园社区会很高兴。”\n\n施工预计将在本周末前完成。\n\n如需报告错别字或更正，请点击此处。\n\n版权所有 2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-05-11T22:13:29.239000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-897","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"托德·希尔兹被任命为阿肯色州立大学系统新任校长","title_en":"Todd Shields named as new Arkansas State University System President","summary_cn":"阿肯色州立大学系统董事会宣布，托德·希尔兹博士将于7月1日起出任该系统新任校长，董事会在5月26日的特别会议上一致通过任命。希尔兹表示感激信任，并对在琼斯伯勒建立的关系心怀感恩。他于2022年成为该校第四位获任命的校长、第14位领导人。董事会还投票任命卡尔文·怀特博士自7月1日起担任阿肯色州立大学临时校长兼教务长。","summary_en":"The Arkansas State University System Board of Trustees announced that Dr. Todd Shields will serve as the new president of the ASU System beginning July 1, unanimously approving the appointment at a special meeting on May 26. Shields expressed gratitude for the trust and for relationships built in Jonesboro. He became the fourth appointed chancellor and 14th leader of Arkansas State University in 2022. The board also named Dr. Calvin White interim chancellor and provost at Arkansas State starting July 1.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:34:58.143209+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/05/26/todd-shields-named-new-arkansas-state-university-system-president/","content":"Todd Shields named as new Arkansas State University System PresidentBy K8 NewsdeskPublished: May 26, 2026 at 4:21 PM CDT|Updated: May 26, 2026 at 5:55 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) - The Arkansas State University System Board of Trustees announced that Dr. Todd Shields would serve as the new President of the ASU System, beginning July 1. In a special called meeting on May 26, the board unanimously voted the appointment. “I am grateful for their trust, their leadership and their steadfast commitment to expanding educational opportunity across our state and beyond,” Shields said. “While I am excited about this new opportunity to serve, my heart is filled with gratitude for the relationships that my wife Karen and I have built in Jonesboro.Shields became the fourth appointed chancellor and 14th to lead Arkansas State University in 2022. Prior to Shield’s appointment, the system board appointed Dr. Robin Myers to serve as interim system president in 2024. In a special called meeting, the board also voted to name Dr. Calvin White executive vice chancellor and provost at Arkansas State as interim chancellor on July 1. To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"Todd Shields 被任命为阿肯色州立大学系统新任校长\n作者：K8 新闻编辑部\n发布时间：2026年5月26日下午4:21（美国中部夏令时）｜更新时间：2026年5月26日下午5:55（美国中部夏令时）\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上将其添加为首选来源\n\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——阿肯色州立大学系统董事会宣布，Todd Shields 博士将自7月1日起担任阿肯色州立大学系统新任校长。在5月26日举行的一次特别会议上，董事会一致投票批准了这项任命。\n\nShields 表示：“我感谢他们的信任、领导力，以及他们始终坚定地致力于扩大本州乃至更广范围的教育机会。尽管我对获得这个新的服务机会感到兴奋，但我内心充满感激，因为我的妻子 Karen 和我已在琼斯伯勒建立了深厚的人际关系。”\n\nShields 于2022年成为阿肯色州立大学第四位获任命的校长，也是领导该校的第14人。在 Shields 获任命之前，系统董事会于2024年任命 Robin Myers 博士担任系统临时校长。在同一次特别会议上，董事会还投票任命阿肯色州立大学执行副校长兼教务长 Calvin White 博士自7月1日起担任临时校长。\n\n如需报告错别字或更正，请点击此处。\n版权所有 © 2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-05-26T21:21:35.151000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-699","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"GOJO为阿肯色州立大学乘客增设红狼二号线","title_en":"GOJO adding Red Wolf Two route for Arkansas State University riders","summary_cn":"琼斯伯勒市交通部门GOJO与阿肯色州立大学合作，将于今年秋季推出名为“红狼二号线”的新线路，服务A-State学生，从学生会出发，途经附近学生公寓、阿吉路和校友中心，并由市内已有电车运营。GOJO市场总监瑞安·布拉舍表示，电车环校既有趣又为不愿开车者提供免费交通。A-State学生、教职员工免费乘车，非校内居民单程票价1.25美元。","summary_en":"GOJO, the city of Jonesboro's transportation arm, is expanding its service to Arkansas State University through a partnership with the university. The new Red Wolf Two route launches this fall for A-State students, running from the Student Union to nearby student apartments, Aggie Road and the Alumni Center, served by an existing trolley. GOJO marketing director Ryan Brasher said the trolleys are fun and provide free transportation for those who prefer not to drive. Transit is free for A-State students, faculty and staff; unaffiliated riders pay $1.25 per one-way trip.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:27:56.211366+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/06/24/gojo-adding-red-wolf-two-route-arkansas-state-university-riders/","content":"GOJO adding Red Wolf Two route for Arkansas State University ridersBy Josh DrollPublished: Jun. 23, 2026 at 8:38 PM CDT|Updated: Jun. 23, 2026 at 10:32 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) - GOJO, the transportation arm of the city of Jonesboro, is expanding upon its existing service to Arkansas State University through a partnership with the university.The new route, called Red Wolf Two, is launching this fall for A-State students. It will run from the Student Union to nearby student apartments, Aggie Road, and the Alumni Center.The route also will be served by one of the trolleys already seen on city streets.Ryan Brasher, marketing director for GOJO, said having the trolleys out accomplishes two goals.“The trolleys that loop around campus are super cool and fun, so everyone loves riding those,” said Brasher. “But it is that free transportation for anyone who might not want to drive.”Transit is free for all A-State students, faculty, and staff, regardless of whether school is in session.Brasher said the new route is part of GOJO’s continuing effort to expand service.He does admit that goal will take some more time, though.“The end goal for GOJO is to continue to be able to provide reliable transportation to all parts of Jonesboro,” Brasher said. “That does take a while.”Residents who are not affiliated with the university can still ride all routes for $1.25 per one-way trip.To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"GOJO 为阿肯色州立大学乘客新增 Red Wolf Two 路线\n作者：Josh Droll\n发布时间：2026年6月23日中部夏令时间晚上8:38|更新时间：2026年6月23日中部夏令时间晚上10:32\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上添加为首选来源\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——琼斯伯勒市的交通部门 GOJO 正通过与该大学合作，扩大其现有的阿肯色州立大学服务。\n这条名为 Red Wolf Two 的新路线将于今年秋季面向 A-State 学生开通。路线将从学生会出发，经过附近的学生公寓、Aggie Road 和校友中心。\n该路线还将由一辆已经在城市街道上运行的电车提供服务。\nGOJO 市场总监 Ryan Brasher 表示，投入这些电车可以实现两个目标。\nBrasher 说：“环绕校园运行的电车非常酷、非常有趣，所以大家都喜欢乘坐。但它也为那些可能不想开车的人提供了免费交通。”\n无论是否在上课期间，所有 A-State 学生、教职员工均可免费乘坐。\nBrasher 表示，这条新路线是 GOJO 持续扩大服务努力的一部分。\n不过，他承认实现这一目标还需要一些时间。\nBrasher 说：“GOJO 的最终目标是继续为琼斯伯勒各个地区提供可靠的交通服务。这确实需要一段时间。”\n与该大学无关联的居民仍可乘坐所有路线，单程票价为1.25美元。\n如要报告拼写错误或更正，请点击此处。\n版权所有 2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-06-24T01:38:25.995000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-591","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学即将建成该州首所兽医学院","title_en":"Arkansas State University set to complete first veterinary school in state","summary_cn":"阿肯色州立大学本周将完成耗资3320万美元的兽医学院建设，这将是阿肯色州首所兽医学院。这座5.6万平方英尺的建筑预计今年秋季迎来120名学生。项目自2024年启动，2025年3月破土动工。A-State兽医学院院长海蒂·班斯博士表示，该学院将惠及社区，并让阿肯色州学生能够留在本州接受教育，此前他们不得不前往外州就读。","summary_en":"Arkansas State University is scheduled to finish construction this week on its $33.2 million veterinary school, the first in the state of Arkansas. The 56,000-square-foot building is expected to welcome 120 students this fall. The project has been underway since 2024 and broke ground in March 2025. Dr. Heidi Banse, dean of the A-State Veterinary School of Medicine, said the school will benefit the community and allow Arkansas students to remain in-state for their education, as previously they had to go out of state.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:25:39.063712+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/07/15/arkansas-state-university-set-complete-first-veterinary-school-state/","content":"Arkansas State University set to complete first veterinary school in stateBy K8 NewsdeskPublished: Jul. 15, 2026 at 6:44 PM CDT|Updated: Jul. 15, 2026 at 6:46 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) - Arkansas State University is scheduled to finish construction on its $33.2 million veterinary school this week. The school will be the first veterinary school in the state of Arkansas.The 56,000-square-foot building is expected to welcome 120 students this fall. The project has been underway since 2024 and broke ground in March 2025.Dr. Heidi Banse, dean of the A-State Veterinary School of Medicine, said the school will benefit the community and allow Arkansas students to remain in-state for their education.“Prior to this, all Arkansas students had to go out-of-state for their education,” Banse said. “The state of Arkansas did fund students to go out at an out-of-state rate, but still, they had to leave and didn’t always come back to serve their community.”To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学即将建成该州首所兽医学院 作者：K8 新闻编辑部 发布：2026 年 7 月 15 日中部夏令时间下午 6:44｜更新：2026 年 7 月 15 日中部夏令时间下午 6:46 分享 在 Google 上添加我们 将其设为 Google 首选来源。阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——阿肯色州立大学计划于本周完成其耗资 3320 万美元的兽医学院建设。该学院将成为阿肯色州首所兽医学院。这座面积为 56,000 平方英尺的建筑预计将在今年秋季迎来 120 名学生。该项目自 2024 年启动，并于 2025 年 3 月破土动工。阿肯色州立大学兽医学院院长 Heidi Banse 博士表示，该学院将使社区受益，并让阿肯色州学生能够留在本州接受教育。“在此之前，所有阿肯色州学生都必须出州接受教育，”Banse 说。“阿肯色州确实按州外费率资助学生外出就学，但他们仍然必须离开，而且并不总会回来服务自己的社区。”如需报告错字或申请更正，请点击此处。版权所有 © 2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-07-15T23:44:07.295000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-411","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学为首届兽医学院举行白袍典礼","title_en":"Arkansas State University holds white coat ceremony for inaugural veterinary class","summary_cn":"阿肯色州立大学8月7日为兽医学院首届120名学生举行白袍典礼，标志着这些学生今秋开始兽医教育的重要里程碑。典礼上，学院院长Heide Bansee、阿肯色州兽医协会主席Sarah Shedenhelm及临时教务长Will McLean等致辞。来自Paragould的学生Katie Kasserman表示，她选择留在东北阿肯色州就近求学，并认为作为首届学生有引领后来者的意义。","summary_en":"Arkansas State University held a white coat ceremony Friday for the inaugural class of 120 students at its College of Veterinary Medicine, marking the first milestone as they begin veterinary education this fall. Speakers included Dean Heide Bansee, Arkansas Veterinary Medical Association President Sarah Shedenhelm and Interim Provost Will McLean. Paragould native Katie Kasserman said she chose to stay close to home in Northeast Arkansas and felt meaningful being part of the inaugural class leading the way for future students.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:18:52.988265+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/08/08/arkansas-state-university-holds-white-coat-ceremony-inaugural-veterinary-class/","content":"Arkansas State University holds white coat ceremony for inaugural veterinary classArkansas State University held a white coat ceremony Friday for the inaugural class of its College of Veterinary Medicine.By Alejandra HernándezPublished: Aug. 8, 2026 at 4:18 PM CDT|Updated: Aug. 8, 2026 at 6:27 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) - Arkansas State University held a white coat ceremony Friday for the inaugural class of its College of Veterinary Medicine, marking the first milestone for 120 students beginning their veterinary education this fall.Students put on their white coats for the first time during the ceremony. Speakers included Dr. Heide Bansee, dean of the college, Dr. Sarah Shedenhelm, president of the Arkansas Veterinary Medical Association, and Dr. Will McLean, Interim Provost and Executive Vice Chancellor of Arkansas State University. Among those in attendance was Katie Kasserman, a Paragould native who said she considered other veterinary schools before the college finished construction. She chose to stay close to home.“Obviously, as Arkansas State opened, it was so exciting. Because I was so excited I got to stay in Northeast Arkansas when I got the acceptance and stay close to family and give back to the same community that I grew up in,” Kasserman said.Kasserman said being part of the inaugural class was meaningful. “I know that me and also a bunch of other of my classmates, we feel like we’re leading the way with all the classes that will come after us. It a big thing to go through, but I know we’re all excited and going to do our best.” Kasserman said. Kasserman also said a tour of the facility ahead of the ceremony left an impression.“Yesterday we actually got to go on a tour of the whole facility and I was just like, my jaw was dropped. It was beautiful. It was top notch. I mean, I’m just so excited to get to learn there,” she said.To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学为首届兽医班举行白大褂仪式\n阿肯色州立大学周五为其兽医学院首届学生举行了白大褂仪式。\n作者：Alejandra Hernández\n发布时间：2026年8月8日中部夏令时间下午4:18｜更新时间：2026年8月8日中部夏令时间下午6:27\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上将其添加为首选来源\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——阿肯色州立大学周五为其兽医学院首届学生举行白大褂仪式，标志着120名今年秋季开始兽医学教育的学生迈出的第一个里程碑。\n学生们在仪式上首次穿上白大褂。发言者包括该学院院长 Heide Bansee 博士、阿肯色州兽医协会会长 Sarah Shedenhelm 博士，以及阿肯色州立大学临时教务长兼常务副校长 Will McLean 博士。出席者中有帕拉古尔德本地人 Katie Kasserman；她说，在该学院建成前，她曾考虑过其他兽医学院。她选择留在离家近的地方。\nKasserman说：“显然，随着阿肯色州立大学开办，这实在令人兴奋。当我收到录取通知时，我非常激动，因为我可以留在阿肯色州东北部，离家人近一些，并回馈养育我的同一个社区。”\nKasserman说，成为首届学生的一员意义非凡。Kasserman说：“我知道，我和我的许多同学都觉得，我们正在为以后所有的班级开路。这是一件大事，但我知道我们都很兴奋，并且会尽最大努力。”Kasserman还说，仪式前对设施的参观给她留下了深刻印象。\n她说：“昨天我们实际上参观了整个设施，我当时简直目瞪口呆。它非常漂亮，属于顶级水平。我非常期待能在那里学习。”\n如需报告错别字或更正，请点击此处。\n版权所有 2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-08-08T21:18:32.723000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-391","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学开设该州首所公立兽医学院","title_en":"Arkansas State University opens state’s first public veterinary school","summary_cn":"阿肯色州立大学8月11日正式开设该州首所也是唯一一所公立兽医学院，并举行剪彩仪式，州长Sarah Huckabee Sanders等出席。学院首届2030届120名学生于次日开课。新设施耗资3320万美元、占地5.6万平方英尺，已获全面认证，配备实验室和先进技术，教职员工从两年前的2人增至19人。学院侧重大型和小型动物，尤其关注农村和农业牲畜需求。","summary_en":"Arkansas State University officially opened the state's first and only public veterinary school Tuesday with a ribbon-cutting attended by Gov. Sarah Huckabee Sanders. Classes for the inaugural Class of 2030, 120 students, begin Wednesday. The $33.2 million, 56,000-square-foot facility is fully accredited and features laboratories and state-of-the-art technology, with 19 faculty and staff versus two two years ago. The school focuses on large and small animals, emphasizing rural and agricultural livestock needs.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:17:17.766559+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/08/11/arkansas-state-university-opens-states-first-public-veterinary-school/","content":"Arkansas State University opens state’s first public veterinary schoolArkansas State University officially opened the state’s first and only public veterinary school Tuesday.By Josh DrollPublished: Aug. 11, 2026 at 5:48 PM CDT|Updated: Aug. 11, 2026 at 5:51 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) - Arkansas State University officially opened the state’s first and only public veterinary school Tuesday, with a ribbon cutting ceremony drawing attendees from across Arkansas, including Gov. Sarah Huckabee Sanders.Classes begin Wednesday for the inaugural class of 2030, with 120 students.The new school makes Arkansas State the only public university in the state with a veterinary school, and one of only a handful of universities in the nation with both a medical school and a veterinary school on the same campus.The $33.2 million, 56,000-square-foot facility is fully accredited and features in-house laboratories, dedicated classroom and study spaces, and what the university describes as state-of-the-art technology.The program is staffed by 19 faculty and staff members — a stark contrast from two years ago, when Heidi Banse, the vet school’s dean, said the staff was just two.The new school will focus on both large and small animals, with a primary emphasis on rural and agricultural livestock — a need the university says is critical in a state with more than 12,500 farms.Interim Chancellor Calvin White Jr. said the university prioritized getting the program right from the start.“We understood that we had one chance to get this right,” White said.White acknowledged skepticism surrounding a first-year program and said the school was built to address it directly.“We know that there’s a lot of skepticism around ‘first.’ And so, what we wanted to guarantee mom and dad and any student who chose to come here, is that they were going to get a world-class education,” White said.White also framed the school as a statewide resource.“Although Arkansas State — our name is on it — but this college belongs to the people and the state of Arkansas,” White said.Sanders said during her remarks that the school addresses a longstanding challenge of Arkansas veterinary students leaving the state for veterinary training and not returning.“In years past, we would have seen those same students going off to Louisiana or Oklahoma and just hoping that they came back home when they finished. That doesn’t have to happen anymore,” Sanders said.Among the class of 2030 is Katie Kasserman, a Paragould native and the first student admitted to the program. Kasserman said she plans to work with both large and small animals.“Getting the opportunity to come to school here at Arkansas State is really amazing because I get to stay close to home while also getting my higher education and getting to eventually serve the community that I was raised in,” Kasserman said.The college’s first class of veterinary students, including Kasserman, start classes Wednesday.To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学开设该州首所公立兽医学院\n阿肯色州立大学周二正式开设了该州第一所、也是唯一一所公立兽医学院。\n\n作者：Josh Droll\n发布：2026年8月11日中部时间下午5:48｜更新：2026年8月11日中部时间下午5:51\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——阿肯色州立大学周二正式开设了该州第一所、也是唯一一所公立兽医学院。剪彩仪式吸引了来自阿肯色州各地的参加者，其中包括州长莎拉·赫卡比·桑德斯。\n\n首届2030届学生将于周三开始上课，共有120名学生。\n\n这所新学院使阿肯色州立大学成为该州唯一一所设有兽医学院的公立大学，也是全美少数在同一校园内同时设有医学院和兽医学院的大学之一。\n\n这座耗资3320万美元、面积5.6万平方英尺的设施已获得全面认证，配备校内实验室、专用教室和学习空间，以及该大学所称的尖端技术。\n\n该项目由19名教职员工负责运营——与两年前形成鲜明对比，当时兽医学院院长海蒂·班斯表示，教职员工只有两人。\n\n新学院将同时关注大型动物和小型动物，重点培养农村和农业牲畜领域的人才。该大学表示，在拥有超过1.25万座农场的阿肯色州，这是至关重要的需求。\n\n临时校长小卡尔文·怀特表示，学校从一开始就优先确保项目办得正确。\n\n“我们明白，只有一次机会把这件事做好，”怀特说。\n\n怀特承认，人们对一个首年项目存在怀疑，并表示学校的建设就是为了直接回应这种怀疑。\n\n“我们知道，人们对‘第一’有很多怀疑。因此，我们想向选择来这里的每一位父母和学生保证，他们将接受世界一流的教育，”怀特说。\n\n怀特还将该学院定位为全州的资源。\n\n“虽然名字上有阿肯色州立大学，但这所学院属于阿肯色州的人民和整个州，”怀特说。\n\n桑德斯在讲话中表示，这所学院解决了一个长期存在的问题：阿肯色州兽医学生离开本州接受兽医培训后不再回来。\n\n“过去，我们会看到这些学生前往路易斯安那州或俄克拉何马州，只能希望他们完成学业后回到家乡。现在不必再这样了，”桑德斯说。\n\n2030届学生中有来自帕拉古尔德的凯蒂·卡瑟曼，她是该项目录取的第一名学生。卡瑟曼表示，她计划同时从事大型动物和小型动物诊疗工作。\n\n“有机会在阿肯色州立大学这里上学真的很棒，因为我既可以离家近，又能接受高等教育，最终还能服务于我成长的社区，”卡瑟曼说。\n\n该学院首届兽医学生，包括卡瑟曼，将于周三开始上课。\n\n如需报告错别字或更正，请点击此处。\n版权所有2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-08-11T22:48:23.569000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-383","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学以“团队协作”保障新生搬入安全","title_en":"‘Teamwork’ key to Arkansas State University for keeping new students safe for move-in","summary_cn":"在持续高温天气下，阿肯色州立大学联合琼斯伯勒市及校内多方力量，为周末返校搬入的学生提供安全保障。圣伯纳德医院捐赠瓶装水，第一国民银行提供冷藏箱，应急管理专员里德建议提前两天补水并定时休息。琼斯伯勒消防局、阿肯色州警、Medic One等随时待命，校园内设有红色标记的紧急求助信标。2026年秋季课程将于8月19日开始。","summary_en":"With dangerous heat persisting, Arkansas State University is working with city and campus partners to keep students safe during weekend move-in. St. Bernards donated water bottles and First National Bank provided coolers. Emergency management specialist Wyatt Reed advised hydrating two days in advance and taking frequent breaks. The Jonesboro Fire Department, Arkansas State Police and Medic One are on standby, and campus emergency beacons are available. Fall 2026 classes begin Aug. 19.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-18T12:48:11.520406+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/08/12/teamwork-key-arkansas-state-university-keeping-new-students-safe-move-in","content":"‘Teamwork’ key to Arkansas State University for keeping new students safe for move-inWith dangerous heat sticking around, Arkansas State University is working alongside multiple city and campus entities as students are set to move back to campusBy Josh DrollPublished: Aug. 12, 2026 at 6:20 PM CDT|Updated: Aug. 12, 2026 at 6:38 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) - With dangerous heat sticking around, Arkansas State University is working alongside multiple city and campus entities as students are set to move back to campus this weekend.Highs are expected to stay in the triple digits for the weekend, and the university said it has already received some support from its partners.St. Bernards has provided water bottles, which will be spread throughout campus during move-in and stored in coolers provided by First National Bank.“So, we’ll be able to ice those down and then have them at our different housing locations across campus, so that our members can stop, take a break, get a cold bottle of water, and hopefully stay safe from the heat,” Wyatt Reed, emergency management specialist, said.Reed said he manages any disaster or emergency that could affect campus, and that includes dangerous heat waves like the one he’s facing now.He said everyone who plans to be on campus that day can take simple steps before they even set foot on campus to prevent overheating.“Take time to hydrate early,” Reid said. “Good hydration starts two days in advance. So don’t wait to move-in day to start drinking water. Be doing that early, preparing yourself, because it is going to be a strenuous activity on your body.”On top of pre-hydrating, Reed said taking frequent breaks during move-in is also vital, since moving objects — especially up and down flights of stairs — can be a difficult task on its own.“Sometimes just making sure that you put yourself on a schedule with that,” Reed said. “Rather than letting yourself get to the point where you start experiencing symptoms, it’s the best proactive measure that you can take.”Jaiden Forte, an incoming freshman at Arkansas State, moved in early and said he knows firsthand that this heat is serious.“I ain’t going to lie, it’s beaming out here,” Forte said. “Wear sunscreen. Make sure y’all drink water four hours before y’all try to come out here and move in this heat. It’s going to make y’all realize.”And if the worst happens and someone experiences a heat-related illness, Reed said the community is on standby, including the Jonesboro Fire Department, Arkansas State Police, Medic One, and more.Additionally, campus has emergency beacons — marked with red paints and blue lights — that anybody can use to get in contact with campus dispatch.Reed said that teamwork is what will keep everyone safe as he looks forward to another new year on campus.“When we can do that ... all working together, we can help keep our campus safe and make things run as smoothly as possible,” Reed said.Fall 2026 classes begin Wednesday, Aug. 19.For more information on the safety regulations in place at Arkansas State, visit their website.To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"“团队合作”是阿肯色州立大学保障新生搬迁安全的关键\n随着危险高温天气持续，阿肯色州立大学正与多个城市及校园机构合作，学生们准备在本周末搬回校园\n作者：Josh Droll\n发布：2026年8月12日 CDT下午6:20｜更新：2026年8月12日 CDT下午6:38\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上添加为首选来源\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——随着危险高温天气持续，阿肯色州立大学正与多个城市及校园机构合作，学生们准备在本周末搬回校园。\n预计周末最高气温将持续达到三位数，该大学表示已经获得合作伙伴的一些支持。\n圣伯纳德医院提供了瓶装水，这些水将在搬入期间分发到校园各处，并存放在第一国民银行提供的冷藏箱中。\n“这样，我们就能把水冰镇，然后放在校园各处不同的住宿地点，让我们的成员可以停下来休息，拿一瓶冰凉的水，希望能在高温下保持安全。”应急管理专家怀亚特·里德说。\n里德说，他负责管理任何可能影响校园的灾害或紧急情况，其中包括他现在面对的这种危险热浪。\n他说，计划当天到校园的每个人，甚至在踏入校园之前，都可以采取一些简单措施来防止过热。\n“要尽早补水，”里德说。“良好的水分补充要提前两天开始。所以不要等到搬入当天才开始喝水。要尽早进行，为自己做好准备，因为这会给你的身体带来剧烈活动。”\n除了提前补水，里德还说，在搬入期间频繁休息也至关重要，因为搬运物品——尤其是上下楼梯——本身就是一项困难的任务。\n“有时，只要确保你为此制定一个时间安排就行，”里德说。“与其等到自己开始出现症状，采取主动预防措施是你能做的最好办法。”\n阿肯色州立大学新生贾登·福特提前搬入，他说自己亲身体会到这种高温有多严重。\n“我不骗你们，外面热得灼人，”福特说。“涂防晒霜。确保在你们准备出来、在这种高温下搬东西前四个小时喝水。这会让你们明白的。”\n如果最坏的情况发生，有人出现与高温有关的疾病，里德说社区已经待命，其中包括琼斯伯勒消防部门、阿肯色州警察、Medic One 等。\n此外，校园内设有紧急信标——标有红漆和蓝灯——任何人都可以使用它们联系校园调度中心。\n里德说，正是团队合作将保障每个人的安全，而他也期待校园迎来又一个新学年。\n“当我们能够做到这一点……大家共同努力时，我们就能帮助维护校园安全，并让事情尽可能顺利地进行，”里德说。\n2026年秋季课程将于8月19日星期三开始。\n有关阿肯色州立大学现行安全规定的更多信息，请访问其网站。\n如需报告错别字或更正，请点击此处。\n版权所有 2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-08-12T23:20:39.037000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-342","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学开学","title_en":"Classes begin at Arkansas State University","summary_cn":"阿肯色州立大学8月19日开学，数千名学生返回琼斯伯勒校区。大三学生Lauren Rodgers表示，朋友们重返校园让她对新学期充满期待，但也对新课程和教授感到紧张；大三学生Emma Everett则对开学感到兴奋。秋季学期官方注册人数尚未公布，该校此前春季学期注册人数超过1.6万人，创下纪录，同比增长6.4%。","summary_en":"Classes began Wednesday at Arkansas State University as thousands of students returned to the Jonesboro campus. Junior Lauren Rodgers said having friends back on campus made her excited for the semester, though she was nervous about new classes and professors, while junior Emma Everett said she was excited to start. Official fall enrollment numbers have not been released; the university is coming off a record spring semester with more than 16,000 students, a 6.4% increase over last spring.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:14:27.148131+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/08/19/classes-begin-arkansas-state-university/","content":"Classes begin at Arkansas State UniversitySummer break is over for thousands of students at Arkansas State University, as classes start Wednesday.By Talecia ClarkPublished: Aug. 19, 2026 at 4:38 PM CDT|Updated: Aug. 19, 2026 at 5:41 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) - Summer break is over for thousands of students at Arkansas State University, as classes start Wednesday.Students packed the Jonesboro campus Wednesday morning for the start of the new school year. From the first day of college for freshmen to the last first day of college for seniors, the day was a big moment for many on campus.Junior Lauren Rodgers said her friends play a huge part in her excitement for the semester.“I’m really excited for the first day of class because all my friends are back on campus together, but I am nervous because I always just get nervous for my new classes and like meeting my new professors, kind of catching the drift of how they’ll be all semester, but overall I would say I’m more just excited to be back with all my friends and have all the fun events on campus,” Rodgers said.Junior Emma Everett said she couldn’t wait to get started.“I’m so excited to be here today, see all my new friends and get into classes and just have a great day,” Everett said.Official enrollment numbers for the fall semester have not yet been released. The university is coming off a record-breaking spring semester, with more than 16,000 students enrolled. That is a 6.4% increase compared to last spring.To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学开课\n阿肯色州立大学数千名学生的暑假已经结束，课程于周三开始。\n作者：Talecia Clark\n发布：2026年8月19日中部夏令时间下午4:38｜更新：2026年8月19日中部夏令时间下午5:41\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n将其添加为 Google 首选来源\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——阿肯色州立大学数千名学生的暑假已经结束，课程于周三开始。\n周三上午，学生们涌入琼斯伯勒校区，迎接新学年的开始。从新生的大学第一天到高年级学生的最后一个大学开学第一天，这一天对校园里的许多人而言都是重要时刻。\n大三学生 Lauren Rodgers 表示，朋友是她对本学期感到兴奋的重要原因。\n“我真的很期待开学第一天，因为我所有朋友都一起回到校园了，但我也很紧张，因为我总会对新课程感到紧张，比如认识新教授，慢慢了解他们整个学期会是什么样，不过总体来说，我更是为能回到朋友们身边、参加校园里所有有趣的活动而感到兴奋。”Rodgers 说。\n大三学生 Emma Everett 表示，她迫不及待想要开始。\n“我今天非常兴奋能来到这里，见到所有新朋友，去上课，然后度过美好的一天。”Everett 说。\n秋季学期的官方招生人数尚未公布。该大学刚刚结束创纪录的春季学期，注册学生超过16,000人，较去年春季增长6.4%。\n如需报告错别字或提出更正，请点击此处。\n版权所有 2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-08-19T21:38:22.546000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-258","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学秋季入学创纪录，接近1.9万名学生","title_en":"Arkansas State University sets fall enrollment record, approaching 19,000 students","summary_cn":"阿肯色州立大学2026年秋季学期入学人数达18775人，较2025年秋季的17926人增长4.7%，为连续第六次创下秋季或春季学期纪录。增长主要来自州内新生增加、留存率提升及研究生项目扩张。新生2247人，其中阿肯色州居民1851人，占逾82%；校内住宿入住率达99.8%。研究生入学5743人，含兽医学院首届120名学生。自2022年秋季以来总入学人数增长逾33%。","summary_en":"Arkansas State University set another fall enrollment record with 18,775 students for fall 2026, up 4.7% from 17,926 in fall 2025, marking its sixth consecutive record fall or spring semester. Growth was driven by more in-state freshmen, improved retention and expanding graduate programs. There were 2,247 freshmen, including a record 1,851 Arkansans (over 82%). Campus housing reached 99.8% capacity. Graduate enrollment hit 5,743, including the inaugural 120-student veterinary class. Total enrollment is up over 33% since fall 2022.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-18T12:39:29.314180+00:00","url":"https://www.kait8.com/2026/09/03/arkansas-state-university-sets-fall-enrollment-record-approaching-19000-students","content":"Arkansas State University sets fall enrollment record, approaching 19,000 studentsBy K8 NewsdeskPublished: Sep. 3, 2026 at 12:58 PM CDT|Updated: Sep. 3, 2026 at 6:50 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT) - Arkansas State University has set another fall enrollment record, reaching 18,775 students for the fall 2026 semester.The university announced Thursday that overall enrollment increased by 4.7% from the previous record of 17,926 students in fall 2025. This marks A-State’s sixth consecutive record-breaking fall or spring semester.School officials attributed the growth to an increase in in-state freshmen, improved student retention rates, and rising enrollment in graduate programs.“Arkansas State is increasingly becoming a university of choice for students from across our state, region and beyond,” Interim Chancellor Dr. Calvin White Jr. said. “This growth underscores the opportunities we are creating, the investments we are making in our students and programs, and the work of our faculty and staff to make this campus a place where students want to learn, live and build their futures.”In-State Freshmen Lead GrowthThe university welcomed 2,247 freshmen this fall, including 2,045 domestic first-year students at the Jonesboro campus. That represents a 5.9% increase over fall 2025.Arkansas residents continue to make up the overwhelming majority of the incoming class. A record 1,851 Arkansans enrolled this fall, accounting for more than 82% of all freshmen.Student Retention Rates RiseA-State is also retaining more of its current students. A total of 7,138 undergraduate students returned to the Jonesboro campus this fall, compared with 6,623 last year—an increase of 7.8%.“Growth gives us an opportunity to serve more students, but it also reinforces the importance of student success and making sure all students know they matter here,” said Dr. Nikesha Nesbitt, dean of University College. “We want students to build relationships, find support when they need it, feel inspired to succeed, and ultimately leave A-State with a degree in hand.”Campus Housing Nears CapacityDemand for the traditional on-campus college experience also reached historic highs. A record 1,576 freshmen are living on campus this semester, pushing university residence halls to 99.8% capacity.A-State officials said they have intentionally prioritized campus housing for first-year students to help them adjust to college life.“One of the most important things we can do for new students is help them find their place at A-State,” Vice Chancellor for Student Affairs Dr. Martha Spack said. “Living on campus surrounds them with opportunities to meet people, get involved and become part of the Red Wolves community from the moment they arrive.”Graduate and Professional Programs ExpandA-State’s graduate programs experienced some of the university’s strongest growth. Graduate enrollment reached 5,743 students, including 1,904 new graduate students—a 21.5% increase from last year’s 1,567 new graduate students.The growth includes the inaugural 120-student class of the College of Veterinary Medicine, which is Arkansas’ first veterinary school.“There is a clear message from this year’s enrollment data: Arkansas State is becoming a destination of choice for students seeking advanced expertise and lasting career value,” Interim Provost Dr. Will McLean said. “Sustained growth in our research enterprise and our graduate and professional programs confirms that A-State has established itself as a comprehensive university.”Long-Term Enrollment SurgeStudents are also taking more coursework, with total credit hours reaching a record 170,003, up 5% from last fall.Since fall 2022, when the university enrolled 14,109 students, total enrollment has increased by more than 33%. A-State has established a new overall enrollment record in each fall semester since.To report a typo or correction, please click here.Copyright 2026 KAIT. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学秋季招生创纪录，学生人数接近19,000人\nK8新闻台\n发布时间：2026年9月3日，中部夏令时间12:58\n更新时间：2026年9月3日，中部夏令时间18:50\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT）——阿肯色州立大学再次创下秋季招生纪录，2026年秋季学期达到18,775名学生。\n\n该校周四宣布，总招生人数较2025年秋季17,926人的上一纪录增长4.7%。这标志着A-State连续第六个秋季或春季学期创下纪录。\n\n校方将增长归因于州内新生人数增加、学生留校率提高以及研究生项目招生上升。\n\n临时校长小卡尔文·怀特博士说：“阿肯色州立大学正日益成为来自全州、本地区及更广泛地区学生的首选大学。这一增长凸显了我们正在创造的机会、对学生和项目的投入，以及教职员工为把校园建设成学生愿意学习、生活并建立未来的地方所付出的努力。”\n\n州内新生引领增长\n\n该校今年秋季迎来2,247名新生，其中包括琼斯伯勒校区的2,045名国内一年级学生，较2025年秋季增长5.9%。\n\n阿肯色州居民仍占新生群体的绝大多数。今年秋季共有创纪录的1,851名阿肯色州居民入学，占全部新生的82%以上。\n\n学生留校率上升\n\nA-State还留住了更多在校生。今年秋季共有7,138名本科生返回琼斯伯勒校区，而去年为6,623名，增长7.8%。\n\n大学学院院长尼凯莎·内斯比特博士说：“增长让我们有机会服务更多学生，但也进一步凸显学生成功的重要性，并确保所有学生都知道自己在这里受到重视。我们希望学生建立关系，在需要时获得支持，受到成功的激励，并最终手持学位离开A-State。”\n\n校园住宿接近满员\n\n对传统校园大学体验的需求也达到历史新高。本学期共有创纪录的1,576名新生住在校内，使大学宿舍达到99.8%的入住率。\n\nA-State官员表示，他们有意优先为一年级学生提供校园住宿，帮助他们适应大学生活。\n\n学生事务副校长玛莎·斯派克博士说：“我们能为新生做的最重要事情之一，就是帮助他们在A-State找到自己的位置。住在校园里，他们从抵达那一刻起就有机会结识他人、参与活动并成为红狼社区的一员。”\n\n研究生和专业项目扩展\n\nA-State的研究生项目实现了全校最强劲的增长之一。研究生招生达到5,743人，其中包括1,904名新研究生，较去年1,567名新研究生增长21.5%。\n\n这项增长包括兽医学院首届120人班级；该学院是阿肯色州第一所兽医学校。\n\n临时教务长威尔·麦克莱恩博士说：“今年的招生数据传达出一个明确信息：对于寻求高阶专业知识和持久职业价值的学生而言，阿肯色州立大学正成为首选目的地。研究事业以及研究生和专业项目的持续增长证实，A-State已经确立了综合性大学的地位。”\n\n长期招生激增\n\n学生修读的课程也更多了，总学分达到创纪录的170,003，比去年秋季增长5%。\n\n自2022年秋季招生14,109人以来，总招生人数已增长逾33%。此后，A-State在每个秋季学期都创下新的总招生纪录。\n\n如需报告拼写错误或更正，请点击此处。\n\n版权所有 2026 KAIT。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kait8.com","publish_time":"2026-09-03T17:58:03.500000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1627","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI芬太尼调查在纳奇托什教区起诉5人","title_en":"5 indicted in FBI fentanyl investigation in Natchitoches Parish","summary_cn":"纳奇托什教区警长办公室宣布，一项为期一年的联邦芬太尼调查取得结果，五人被起诉。被告来自纳奇托什和拉皮兹教区，面临共谋分销芬太尼、持有意图分销芬太尼等指控。调查由FBI、FBI安全街道工作组及多个地方执法机构合作进行。警长表示将继续合作打击毒品贩运。","summary_en":"The Natchitoches Parish Sheriff's Office announced the resolution of a year-long federal investigation into fentanyl distribution, with five people indicted. The defendants from Natchitoches and Rapides Parishes face charges including conspiracy to distribute fentanyl and possession with intent to distribute fentanyl. The investigation involved the FBI, FBI Safe Streets Task Force, and multiple local law enforcement agencies. The sheriff stated that the partnership will continue to combat drug trafficking.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:24:43.224564+00:00","url":"https://www.kalb.com/2026/02/11/5-indicted-fbi-fentanyl-investigation-natchitoches-parish","content":"5 indicted in FBI fentanyl investigation in Natchitoches Parish(Source: FBI)By KALB Digital TeamPublished: Feb. 10, 2026 at 9:30 PM CST|Updated: Feb. 10, 2026 at 10:02 PM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleNATCHITOCHES PARISH, La. (KALB) - On Tuesday, February 10, Natchitoches Parish Sheriff’s Office announced the resolution of a year-long federal investigation into the spread of fentanyl in Natchitoches Parish.According to NPSO, the Western District Court of Louisiana has indicted five people from Natchitoches and Rapides Parishes on multiple drug offenses. Per court documents, the indictment was received by the Alexandria Division on December 3, 2025. All defendants are presumed innocent until proven guilty in a court of law. The following people were indicted with multiple offenses related to the sale of drugs:Edward “Pooh” Paige of NatchitochesConspiracy to Distribute FentanylDistribution of FentanylDonovan “NuFive” Solitaire of NatchezConspiracy to Distribute FentanylPossession with Intent to Distribute FentanylMaintaining a Drug PremisesRaven Gray of NatchezMaintaining a Drug PremisesKendrick Moses of AlexandriaConspiracy to Distribute FentanylPossession with Intent to Distribute FentanylQuenderrick “Bing” Williams of ColfaxConspiracy to Distribute FentanylA copy of the indictment is provided below: Western District Of Louisiana Indictment 120325 by jkinder The operation was specifically targeting gang violence and the distribution of fentanyl within Natchitoches Parish. The following agencies were involved with the investigation, per NPSO: Federal Bureau of Investigations (FBI)FBI Safe Streets Task ForceNatchitoches Parish Sheriff’s Office Drug Enforcement Unit (NPSO DEU)Natchitoches Police DepartmentRapides Parish Sheriff’s OfficeLouisiana State PoliceThough this investigation has concluded, officials said the partnership between the FBI and local law enforcement will continue, “in hopes of further curbing violence and drug trafficking throughout the region.”Natchitoches Parish Sheriff Steven Wright released the following statement alongside Tuesday’s announcement:“I would like to extend my sincere appreciation to the U.S. Attorney’s Office, Western District of Louisiana, the Federal Bureau of Investigation, Louisiana State Police, Rapides Parish Sheriff’s Office, and the Natchitoches Parish Sheriff’s Office Drug Enforcement Unit for their outstanding work and dedication in the recent federal indictments involving individuals trafficking the illegal and extremely dangerous narcotic fentanyl in Natchitoches Parish.This successful investigation and prosecution are the result of strong partnerships, tireless efforts, and a shared commitment to protecting our community. Fentanyl continues to pose a serious threat to public safety, and these actions send a clear message that drug trafficking and related criminal activity will not be tolerated in our parish.We remain committed to working alongside our federal, state, and local partners to combat illegal drugs and keep our citizens safe. I am proud of the professionalism and dedication demonstrated by everyone involved in this operation.”Natchitoches Parish Sheriff Stuart WrightClick here to report a typo. Please provide the title of the article in your email.Copyright 2026 KALB. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"纳奇托什堂区联邦调查局芬太尼调查中5人被起诉\n（来源：FBI）\n作者：KALB数字团队\n发布时间：2026年2月10日晚上9:30（中部标准时间）｜更新时间：2026年2月10日晚上10:02（中部标准时间）\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上将其添加为首选来源\n\n路易斯安那州纳奇托什堂区（KALB）——2月10日，星期二，纳奇托什堂区治安官办公室宣布，一项历时一年的联邦调查已告破，该调查针对芬太尼在纳奇托什堂区的扩散。\n\n据NPSO称，路易斯安那州西区法院以多项毒品罪名起诉了5名来自纳奇托什堂区和拉皮兹堂区的人员。根据法庭文件，该起诉书于2025年12月3日由亚历山德里亚分部接收。在法庭上被证明有罪之前，所有被告均被推定无罪。以下人员因多项与贩卖毒品有关的罪名被起诉：\n\n来自纳奇托什的爱德华·“Pooh”·佩奇\n共谋分销芬太尼\n分销芬太尼\n\n来自纳奇兹的多诺万·“NuFive”·索利泰尔\n共谋分销芬太尼\n意图分销芬太尼而持有芬太尼\n维持毒品场所\n\n来自纳奇兹的拉文·格雷\n维持毒品场所\n\n来自亚历山德里亚的肯德里克·摩西\n共谋分销芬太尼\n意图分销芬太尼而持有芬太尼\n\n来自科尔法克斯的昆德里克·“Bing”·威廉姆斯\n共谋分销芬太尼\n\n下方提供起诉书副本：\njkinder 发布的《路易斯安那州西区起诉书 120325》\n\n据NPSO称，此次行动专门针对纳奇托什堂区内的帮派暴力和芬太尼分销。参与调查的机构包括：\n联邦调查局（FBI）\nFBI安全街道特别工作组\n纳奇托什堂区治安官办公室缉毒组（NPSO DEU）\n纳奇托什警察局\n拉皮兹堂区治安官办公室\n路易斯安那州警察\n\n尽管该调查已经结束，官员表示，FBI与地方执法部门之间的合作关系将继续，“希望进一步遏制整个地区的暴力和毒品贩运。”\n\n纳奇托什堂区治安官史蒂文·赖特在周二的公告中发表了以下声明：\n\n“我谨向路易斯安那州西区联邦检察官办公室、联邦调查局、路易斯安那州警察、拉皮兹堂区治安官办公室，以及纳奇托什堂区治安官办公室缉毒组致以诚挚感谢，感谢他们在近期涉及于纳奇托什堂区贩运非法且极其危险的麻醉品芬太尼的人员的联邦起诉案中所做出的出色工作和奉献。\n\n此次成功的调查和起诉，是强有力的伙伴关系、不懈努力以及保护我们社区这一共同承诺的结果。芬太尼仍然对公共安全构成严重威胁，这些行动传递了明确的信息：本堂区绝不容忍毒品贩运及相关犯罪活动。\n\n我们仍致力于与联邦、州和地方合作伙伴并肩合作，打击非法毒品，保障居民安全。我为所有参与此次行动人员所展现的专业精神和奉献精神感到自豪。”\n\n纳奇托什堂区治安官斯图尔特·赖特\n\n点击此处报告错别字。请在电子邮件中提供文章标题。\n版权所有 © 2026 KALB。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kalb.com","publish_time":"2026-02-11T03:30:46.426000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-761","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI查封13个网站，官员称其被中国用于针对并招募美国工作人员","title_en":"FBI seizes 13 websites that officials say were used by China to target and recruit US workers","summary_cn":"美国司法部表示，FBI查封了13个网站，官员称这些网站是中国针对可接触机密或敏感政府信息的美国工作人员行动的一部分。这些网站冒充咨询公司，发布面向现任及前任安全许可持有者的虚假招聘信息，利用伪造或窃取身份及AI生成照片制造合法假象，并通过加密货币和在线支付系统隐藏真实身份。FBI称信息来自主动报告可疑互动的目标人员，并认为还有其他类似网站。中国驻华盛顿大使馆称相关指控“纯属捏造”。","summary_en":"The Justice Department said the FBI seized 13 websites that officials say were part of a Chinese effort to target American workers with access to classified or sensitive government information. The sites posed as consulting companies advertising sham jobs for current and former security clearance holders, using fraudulent or stolen identities and AI-generated photos for legitimacy, and hiding operators' identities via cryptocurrency and online payments. The FBI said tips came from targets who reported suspicious interactions and believes other similar sites exist. China's embassy in Washington called the allegations \"entirely fabricated.\"","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:21:47.990182+00:00","url":"https://www.kalb.com/2026/06/11/fbi-seizes-13-websites-that-officials-say-were-used-by-china-target-recruit-us-workers","content":"FBI seizes 13 websites that officials say were used by China to target and recruit US workersFILE - The seal of the Federal Bureau of Investigation is displayed at its headquarters in Washington, Nov. 18, 2024. (AP Photo/Jose Luis Magana, File)(Jose Luis Magana | AP)By The Associated Press and ERIC TUCKER Published: Jun. 11, 2026 at 3:34 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleWASHINGTON (AP) — The FBI has seized more than a dozen websites that officials say were part of a Chinese effort to target American workers who have access to classified or sensitive government information, the Justice Department said Wednesday.The 13 websites purported to be affiliated with consulting companies that advertised job openings for current and former holders of security clearances. But the companies were all fakes and the job postings were a sham, officials said.The internet domain seizure is part of a broader effort by Western law enforcement and intelligence agencies to sound the alarm about alleged Chinese government plots to recruit workers who can be duped into disclosing sensitive information.Last week, for instance, the English-speaking Five Eyes intelligence-sharing alliance — Australia, Canada, New Zealand, the U.K. and the U.S. — issued a bulletin warning that China is targeting personnel from those countries on job websites to get access to classified or sensitive information.The bulletin said spies for Chinese military intelligence have been posing as workers acting on behalf of private businesses or think tanks, advertising for bogus jobs such as foreign policy or defense analysts and pressuring candidates to provide “non-public” information.According to an FBI affidavit filed in connection with the website seizure, the fake websites relied on fraudulent or stolen identities and AI-generated photographs to give them the appearance of legitimacy, and advertised generic “consulting” jobs geared toward current or former U.S. government employees.“These websites are often linked or referenced within the entities’ job postings on LinkedIn and other hiring platforms,” the affidavit said.Applicants and recruits were offered money for reports related to their work and for sensitive information, the Justice Department said. The operators of the plot, who officials allege to be tied to Chinese intelligence services, used cryptocurrency and online payment systems to hide their real identities, officials said.Law enforcement officials identified the websites through information from targets who came forward to report what they believed to be suspicious interactions.“A lot of this information came from doing interviews, interviews with people who came forward that something didn’t seem right,” Dan Wierzbicki, the special agent in charge of the counterintelligence and cyber division of the FBI’s Washington field office, said in an interview.“They provided information and said, ‘Hey, this is kind of weird, we’re kind of getting paid by a cryptocurrency or an online payment system that’s not typical,’” he added.He said the FBI believes there are other websites serving a similar purpose and is seeking the public’s help in identifying them.A spokesperson for the Chinese embassy in Washington called allegations of Chinese espionage “entirely fabricated” and “malicious slander.”___Associated Press writer Didi Tang in Washington contributed to this report.Copyright 2026 The Associated Press. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI查封13个网站，官员称这些网站被中国用来针对并招募美国工作人员\n文件照片——2024年11月18日，在华盛顿，联邦调查局总部展示联邦调查局印章。（美联社照片/何塞·路易斯·马加纳，文件）（Jose Luis Magana | AP）\n美联社和埃里克·塔克报道 发布于：2026年6月11日下午3:34（中部夏令时间）\n分享\n将我们添加到Google\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n\n华盛顿（美联社）——美国司法部周三表示，联邦调查局查封了十多个网站，官员称这些网站是中国方面行动的一部分，目标是接触那些能够获取政府机密或敏感信息的美国工作人员。\n\n官员称，这13个网站声称隶属于提供职位招聘的咨询公司，招聘对象是现任和前任持有安全许可的人员。但这些公司全是假的，招聘信息也是骗局。\n\n此次互联网域名查封是西方执法和情报机构更广泛行动的一部分，旨在敲响警钟，警告所谓中国政府策划招募那些可能被诱骗泄露敏感信息的工作人员的阴谋。\n\n例如，上周，由澳大利亚、加拿大、新西兰、英国和美国组成、以英语为工作语言的“五眼”情报共享联盟发布公告，警告中国正通过招聘网站针对这些国家的人员，以获取机密或敏感信息。\n\n公告称，中国军事情报部门的间谍冒充代表私营企业或智库行事的工作人员，发布所谓外交政策或国防分析师等虚假职位，并施压候选人提供“非公开”信息。\n\n根据联邦调查局就查封网站提交的一份宣誓书，这些假网站利用欺诈或盗用的身份以及人工智能生成的照片，使其看起来合法可信，并发布面向现任或前任美国政府雇员的普通“咨询”职位。\n\n宣誓书称：“这些网站经常在LinkedIn及其他招聘平台上相关实体的招聘信息中被链接或引用。”\n\n司法部表示，申请人和被招募人员会因提供与其工作有关的报告以及敏感信息而获得报酬。官员称，据指与中国情报机构有关联的阴谋操作者利用加密货币和在线支付系统掩盖真实身份。\n\n执法官员通过一些目标对象提供的信息发现了这些网站。这些目标对象主动报告了他们认为可疑的互动。\n\n联邦调查局华盛顿外勤办公室反情报与网络部门负责人丹·维尔兹比茨基在采访中说：“很多信息来自访谈，来自那些主动联系我们、觉得有些不对劲的人。”\n\n他补充说：“他们提供了信息并说，‘嘿，这有点奇怪，我们似乎通过加密货币或在线支付系统获得报酬，这并不常见。’”\n\n他说，联邦调查局相信还有其他网站发挥类似作用，并寻求公众帮助识别这些网站。\n\n中国驻华盛顿大使馆发言人称有关中国从事间谍活动的指控“完全捏造”且是“恶意诽谤”。\n\n___\n\n美联社记者迪迪·唐在华盛顿对本报道亦有贡献。\n\n版权所有 2026 美联社。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kalb.com","publish_time":"2026-06-11T20:34:37.605000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-810","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI警告世界杯期间无人机规则：违规最高罚款10万美元并监禁一年","title_en":"FBI warns of this World Cup rule. Break it and risk a $100K fine and a year in prison","summary_cn":"FBI堪萨斯城分局警告无人机操作者，在世界杯相关活动期间飞入受限空域属联邦犯罪。违规可能面临最高10万美元罚款、最长一年监禁及无人机被扣押。FBI表示将与联邦航空管理局合作，使用联邦授权的反无人机能力探测、追踪和评估未经授权的无人机活动，并建议操作者起飞前通过B4UFLY等FAA认可工具查询现行飞行限制。","summary_en":"FBI Kansas City warned drone operators that flying in restricted airspace during World Cup-related events is a federal crime, with penalties of up to $100,000 in fines, up to one year in prison and seizure of the drone. The agency said it works with the FAA and uses federally authorized counter-drone capabilities to detect, track and assess unauthorized drone activity, urging operators to check active flight restrictions before flying using FAA-approved tools such as the B4UFLY app.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:23:50.796424+00:00","url":"https://www.kansascity.com/news/local/article316023469.html","content":"Local\nFBI warns of this World Cup rule. Break it and risk a $100K fine and a year in prison\nBy Ben Wheeler\nUpdated June 5, 2026 5:25 PM\nConstruction crews prepare the FIFA Fan Festival site during a media walkthrough at the National WWI Museum and Memorial on Wednesday, May 27, 2026, in Kansas City.\nEmily Curiel\necuriel@kcstar.com\nKey TakeawaysAI-generated summary reviewed by our newsroom.Read our AI Policy.FBI Kansas City warns flying drones in World Cup restricted airspace is a federal crime.Violations can carry up to $100,000 in fines and up to one year in prison.The FBI and FAA will detect, track, seize drones and enforce airspace rules.The Federal Bureau of Investigation is warning drone operators that flying in restricted airspace during World Cup-related events in Kansas City will be a federal crime, as officials prepare for increased security around stadiums, fan festivals and other venues.FBI Kansas City urged the public to avoid flying drones in areas that will be designated as Temporary Flight Restrictions during the tournament, the agency said in a press release on Thursday.“As teams from around the world convene in and around Kansas City for FIFA World Cup Matches, the United States Government will establish Temporary Flight Restrictions around the World Cup Stadiums, Fan Festivals and other events,” Chris Ormerod, FBI Kansas City special agent in charge, said in a release.“Flying a drone in these areas is strictly prohibited. Flying in a restricted zone isn’t just dangerous, it’s a federal crime,” he said.The release said violations of restricted airspace can carry penalties including up to $100,000 in fines, up to one year in prison and seizure of the drone. Officials emphasized that Temporary Flight Restrictions are used to protect fans, players and critical infrastructure from both accidents and potential security threats.The agency said it works with the Federal Aviation Administration to enforce the restrictions and uses federally authorized counter-drone capabilities to detect, track and assess unauthorized drone activity.Officials from both agencies are expected to be deployed during World Cup events to monitor airspace around venues, the release said.“The FBI is legally authorized to use counter-UAS capabilities to detect, assess, and mitigate unauthorized drone activity within restricted airspace, while preserving evidence for potential enforcement action,” officials said.Officials urged drone operators to check for active flight restrictions before any flight using FAA-approved tools such as the B4UFLY app and other airspace awareness services.This story was originally published June 5, 2026 at 2:38 PM.\nRelated Stories from Kansas City Star\nLocal\nKCPD to receive $17M for World Cup overtime with federal grant\nJune 4, 2026 6:18 PM\nLocal\nDEA eyes potential drug trafficking risks tied to World Cup in Kansas City\nJune 4, 2026 5:27 PM\nBen Wheeler\nThe Kansas City Star\nBen Wheeler is the Law Enforcement Watchdog Reporter for The Star. He joined The Star after spending the last five years of his career in Memphis, Tennessee where he worked as an investigative reporter focused on law enforcement accountability reporting, covering everything from budgets to Tyre Nichols death at the hands of police officers and the subsequent Department of Justice pattern or practice investigation.","content_cn":"本地\nFBI警告世界杯这项规定。违反规定将面临10万美元罚款和一年监禁的风险\n\n作者：Ben Wheeler\n更新于2026年6月5日下午5:25\n\n2026年5月27日星期三，媒体参观期间，施工人员在国家第一次世界大战博物馆和纪念馆为国际足联球迷节场地做准备，地点在堪萨斯城。\n\nEmily Curiel\necuriel@kcstar.com\n\n要点\n由人工智能生成的摘要，已由本报编辑部审核。阅读我们的人工智能政策。\n\n堪萨斯城FBI警告，在世界杯受限空域飞行无人机属于联邦犯罪。\n违规行为可能处以最高10万美元罚款和最高一年监禁。\nFBI和联邦航空管理局将探测、跟踪、扣押无人机并执行空域规定。\n\n随着官员为体育场、球迷节和其他场馆加强安保，联邦调查局正在警告无人机操作员，在堪萨斯城与世界杯有关的活动期间，于受限空域飞行将构成联邦犯罪。\n\n该机构在周四的新闻稿中说，堪萨斯城FBI敦促公众避免在比赛期间被指定为临时飞行限制区的区域飞行无人机。\n\n堪萨斯城FBI负责特工长Chris Ormerod在新闻稿中说：“当来自世界各地的球队齐聚堪萨斯城及周边地区参加国际足联世界杯比赛时，美国政府将在世界杯体育场、球迷节和其他活动周围设立临时飞行限制区。”\n\n他说：“在这些区域飞行无人机是严格禁止的。在受限区域飞行不仅危险，而且是联邦犯罪。”\n\n新闻稿称，违反受限空域规定可能受到包括最高10万美元罚款、最高一年监禁以及无人机被扣押在内的处罚。官员强调，设立临时飞行限制区是为了保护球迷、球员和关键基础设施，防范事故及潜在安全威胁。\n\n该机构表示，它与联邦航空管理局合作执行限制规定，并使用联邦授权的反无人机能力，探测、跟踪和评估未经授权的无人机活动。\n\n新闻稿称，世界杯活动期间，两家机构的官员预计将被部署到现场，监控场馆周围的空域。\n\n官员说：“FBI依法获授权使用反无人机系统能力，在受限空域内探测、评估并缓解未经授权的无人机活动，同时保存证据，以便采取可能的执法行动。”\n\n官员敦促无人机操作员在任何飞行前，使用FAA批准的工具（如B4UFLY应用程序）及其他空域态势感知服务，检查当前是否存在有效的飞行限制。\n\n本文最初发表于2026年6月5日下午2:38。\n\n堪萨斯城星报相关新闻\n\n本地\nKCPD将获联邦拨款，为世界杯加班支付1700万美元\n2026年6月4日下午6:18\n\n本地\nDEA关注与堪萨斯城世界杯相关的潜在毒品贩运风险\n2026年6月4日下午5:27\n\nBen Wheeler\n堪萨斯城星报\n\nBen Wheeler是《星报》的执法监督记者。他加入《星报》前，曾在田纳西州孟菲斯工作五年，担任调查记者，专注于执法问责报道，报道内容从预算到Tyre Nichols被警察杀害，以及随后司法部展开的模式或惯例调查等。","publish_source":"kansascity.com","publish_time":"2026-06-05T17:25:04-05:00"}},{"id":"news-2887","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI希望在堪萨斯城增设岗位以打击中西部“暴力犯罪激增”","title_en":"FBI wants more jobs in KC to target ‘explosion of violent crime’ in Midwest","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局局长Kash Patel向国会作证称，FBI计划将约1000个岗位从华盛顿特区迁往各地外勤办公室，其中约33个岗位可能迁至堪萨斯城外勤办公室，另有少量迁往斯普林菲尔德、托皮卡、威奇托和杰斐逊城。Patel表示此举旨在应对中西部暴力犯罪激增，岗位分配依据各地人均暴力犯罪比例，并强调将与州和地方执法部门合作。","summary_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel testified to Congress that the bureau plans to relocate about 1,000 positions from Washington, D.C., to field offices nationwide, including roughly 33 positions to the Kansas City field office and a few others to Springfield, Topeka, Wichita and Jefferson City. Patel said the move aims to address an explosion of violent crime in the Midwest, with locations chosen based on per capita violent crime rates, and stressed partnership with state and local law enforcement.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:13:54.274198+00:00","url":"https://www.kansascity.com/news/local/crime/article306234631.html","content":"Crime\nFBI wants more jobs in KC to target ‘explosion of violent crime’ in Midwest\nBy Robert A. Cronkleton\nMay 12, 2025 3:28 PM\nThe Federal Bureau of Investigation is eyeing the possible relocation of about three dozen positions to Missouri as it looks to move more than 1,000 jobs out of Washington, D.C., into field offices across the country, FBI Director Kash Patel testified to Congress last week.Patel said the move would help address an “explosion of violent crime” in the Midwest.In all, the FBI might move approximately 33 positions to the Kansas City field office, two to Springfield and one each to Topeka, Wichita and Jefferson City, Patel said during a U.S. House appropriations subcommittee hearing Wednesday concerning his agency’s fiscal year 2026 budget request.A spokesman for the FBI’s field office in Kansas City referred questions about the possible additional staffing to Patel’s testimony.U.S. Rep. Mark Alford, a Missouri Republican, asked Patel why they were needed in Kansas City. Patel responded that the move is to address violent crime in the Midwest and the locations were chosen based on proportion of violent crime per capita in those regions.“I don’t want to say Kansas City has an explosion itself, but Kansas City covers down a large area in Missouri and surrounding states that have an explosion of violent crime, and that’s why we’re sending them there,” Patel said.During the U.S. Appropriations subcommittee hearing on Thursday, Patel said the way they set out on deciding where to move the positions was not done by “throwing darts on a map.” He said the FBI identified violent crime hot beds across America and then apportioned the FBI employees where the need is the greatest.U.S. Sen. Jerry Moran, a Kansas Republican, asked whether there will be an increase FBI participation in partnerships with local law enforcement as a result of the relocating positions to field offices.Patel said it will be up to special agents in charge of the field offices to determine where the employees are embedded.“A big part of the process is . . . commitment to state and local authorities that we’re not just sending a federal agent to do work alone, we’re sending them to do it with you,” Patel said.\nRelated Stories from Kansas City Star\nLocal\nYoung rider without helmet thrown from minibike in crash in KC’s Northland\nMay 12, 2025 8:10 AM\nCrime\nGoose on the loose: Gosling flees from Lenexa police during rescue\nMay 9, 2025 1:08 PM\nRobert A. Cronkleton\nThe Kansas City Star\n816-234-4261\nRobert A. Cronkleton is a breaking news reporter for The Kansas City Star, covering crime, courts, transportation, weather and climate. He’s been at The Star for 36 years. His skills include multimedia and data reporting and video and audio editing.\nSupport my work with a digital subscription","content_cn":"犯罪\n联邦调查局希望在堪萨斯城增加岗位，以打击中西部“暴力犯罪爆炸式增长”\n作者：罗伯特·A·克朗克尔顿\n2025年5月12日下午3:28\n联邦调查局正考虑将大约三十个职位迁往密苏里州。该机构计划把1000多个岗位从华盛顿特区调往全国各地的外地办事处，联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔上周在国会作证时表示。帕特尔说，此举将有助于应对中西部“暴力犯罪爆炸式增长”的问题。\n帕特尔在周三举行的美国众议院拨款小组委员会听证会上谈及该机构2026财年预算申请时表示，联邦调查局可能会将约33个职位调往堪萨斯城办事处，两个调往斯普林菲尔德，托皮卡、威奇托和杰斐逊城各调一个。堪萨斯城外地办事处的一名发言人将有关可能增加人员配置的问题转交给帕特尔在听证会上的证词。\n密苏里州共和党籍联邦众议员马克·奥尔福德询问帕特尔，为什么堪萨斯城需要这些岗位。帕特尔回答说，此举是为了应对中西部的暴力犯罪，这些地点是根据相关地区人均暴力犯罪比例选定的。\n帕特尔说：“我不想说堪萨斯城本身发生了爆炸式增长，但堪萨斯城覆盖了密苏里州及周边各州的一大片区域，而这些地方的暴力犯罪出现爆炸式增长，这就是我们把他们派往那里的原因。”\n在周四举行的美国拨款小组委员会听证会上，帕特尔说，他们决定将这些岗位调往何处的方式并不是“向地图上投飞镖”。他说，联邦调查局确定了全美暴力犯罪热点，然后根据需求最迫切的地方分配联邦调查局雇员。\n堪萨斯州共和党籍联邦参议员杰里·莫兰询问，随着这些岗位迁往外地办事处，联邦调查局与当地执法部门开展合作的参与度是否会增加。\n帕特尔说，将由各外地办事处负责的特别探员决定这些雇员被派驻在哪里。\n帕特尔说：“这一过程的重要部分是……向州和地方当局作出承诺：我们不是只派一名联邦探员单独开展工作，而是派他们与你们一起工作。”\n\n《堪萨斯城星报》相关新闻\n本地\n堪萨斯城北区一名未戴头盔的年轻骑手在小型摩托车事故中被甩出\n2025年5月12日上午8:10\n犯罪\n大雁逃跑：小雁获救期间从莱内克萨警方手中逃脱\n2025年5月9日下午1:08\n罗伯特·A·克朗克尔顿\n《堪萨斯城星报》\n816-234-4261\n罗伯特·A·克朗克尔顿是《堪萨斯城星报》的突发新闻记者，报道犯罪、法院、交通、天气和气候。他在《星报》工作了36年。他的技能包括多媒体和数据报道，以及视频和音频编辑。\n通过数字订阅支持我的工作","publish_source":"kansascity.com","publish_time":"2025-05-12T15:28:26-05:00"}},{"id":"news-2502","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"安德鲁·贝利是谁？认识这位加入特朗普FBI团队的密苏里州总检察长","title_en":"Who is Andrew Bailey? Meet the Missouri AG who’s joining Trump’s FBI team","summary_cn":"文章介绍密苏里州总检察长Andrew Bailey将辞去现职，出任美国联邦调查局联合副局长。贝利现年44岁，退伍军人，2022年底被任命为总检察长，2024年赢得完整任期。他以针对拜登政府及特朗普政治对手的多起诉讼闻名。作为FBI联合副局长，他将与现任副局长Dan Bongino共事，向局长Kash Patel汇报，该任命无需参议院确认。","summary_en":"The article profiles Missouri Attorney General Andrew Bailey, who will resign to become co-deputy director of the FBI. Bailey, 44, an Army veteran, was appointed attorney general in late 2022 and won a full term in 2024. He gained prominence for lawsuits against the Biden administration and Trump's political opponents. As FBI co-deputy director, he will work alongside current deputy director Dan Bongino under Director Kash Patel; the appointment does not require Senate confirmation.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:08:03.180205+00:00","url":"https://www.kansascity.com/news/politics-government/article311760282.html","content":"Government & Politics\nWho is Andrew Bailey? Meet the Missouri AG who’s joining Trump’s FBI team\nBy Matthew Kelly\nAugust 19, 2025 1:00 PM\nSpringfield News-Leader file photo\nLess than three years ago, Andrew Bailey was a political novice. Now, the Missouri attorney general plans to resign his position and join the Trump administration as co-deputy director of the Federal Bureau of Investigation.Bailey’s Monday announcement makes him the latest in a string of Missouri Republican attorneys general to parlay their role as the state’s top lawyer into a high-profile job in the federal government. His two most recent predecessors, Eric Schmitt and Josh Hawley, were both elected to the U.S. Senate.Early careerBailey, a 44-year-old Army veteran from Rhineland, had never held an elected office before former Gov. Mike Parson selected him in late 2022 to replace the outgoing Schmitt.Before his appointment, Bailey served as Parson’s general counsel, rising from the deputy role he was hired for in 2019. Prior to that, he was the general counsel for the Missouri Department of Corrections.Bailey handily defeated Democrat Elad Gross in 2024 to win a four-year term, capturing nearly 60% of the vote.Despite his low profile entering office, Bailey made a name for himself by unleashing a torrent of attention-grabbing lawsuits challenging the Biden administration on everything from access to abortion medication to whether the president has the authority to forgive student loan debt.When Trump took over as president, Bailey shifted gears, leveraging his legal firepower to attack Trump’s political enemies and support his agenda. In February, his office sued Starbucks, alleging that the coffee giant discriminated against white men in its hiring process.Notable casesBailey also drew sharp criticism from criminal justice activists for using the power of his office to fight claims of innocence made by incarcerated people in the Missouri prison system he used to represent.Last year, Bailey’s office argued that Sandra “Sandy” Hemme, a wrongfully imprisoned woman, should not be released from prison. Bailey’s office also attempted to block death row inmate Marcellus “Khaliifah” Williams from arguing his innocence claim in court before his execution.Bailey’s also took the unprecedented step in 2023 of seeking to overturn the conviction of Eric DeValkenaere, Kansas City’s first police officer to be found guilty in the killing of a Black man. Those efforts proved unsuccessful, but Parson commuted DeValkenaere’s sentence last December.Bailey’s Missouri replacementAs co-deputy director of the FBI, Bailey will work alongside current deputy director Dan Bongino, serving as second-in-command to FBI Director Kash Patel under U.S. Attorney General Pam Bondi. Bailey’s appointment, which will be effective after he resigns as AG on Sept. 8, does not require Senate confirmation.On Tuesday, Gov. Mike Kehoe picked Catherine Hanaway, a former federal prosecutor and Missouri House speaker, to replace Bailey. She will be the first woman to serve as Missouri attorney general, which is widely viewed as the second most powerful state-level position.\nRelated Stories from Kansas City Star\nGovernment & Politics\nMissouri governor picks state’s first woman attorney general to replace Bailey\nAugust 19, 2025 10:18 AM\nGovernment & Politics\nMissouri Attorney General Andrew Bailey is resigning to join Trump administration\nAugust 18, 2025 5:59 PM\nMatthew Kelly\nThe Kansas City Star\n316-268-6203\nMatthew Kelly is The Kansas City Star’s Kansas State Government reporter. He previously covered local government for The Wichita Eagle. Kelly holds a political science degree from Wichita State University.","content_cn":"政府与政治\n安德鲁·贝利是谁？认识这位将加入特朗普 FBI 团队的密苏里州总检察长\n作者：Matthew Kelly\n2025年8月19日 下午1:00\n《斯普林菲尔德新闻领袖报》资料照片\n不到三年前，安德鲁·贝利还是一名政治新人。如今，这位密苏里州总检察长计划辞职，作为联邦调查局共同副局长加入特朗普政府。贝利周一的宣布使他成为一连串密苏里州共和党总检察长中的最新一位：他们将州最高法律官员这一职务转化为联邦政府中的高知名度职位。他最近两位前任埃里克·施密特和乔什·霍利均当选为美国参议员。\n早期职业生涯\n来自莱茵兰、现年44岁的陆军退伍军人贝利，在前州长迈克·帕森于2022年底选中他接替即将离任的施密特之前，从未担任过民选公职。\n获任前，贝利担任帕森的总法律顾问，由他2019年受聘的副职晋升而来。在此之前，他担任密苏里州惩教署总法律顾问。\n贝利在2024年以明显优势击败民主党人埃拉德·格罗斯，赢得四年任期，获得近60%的选票。\n尽管就职时知名度不高，贝利却通过发起一连串引人注目的诉讼而声名鹊起，挑战拜登政府在从堕胎药物获取到总统是否有权免除学生贷款债务等各类问题上的做法。\n特朗普就任总统后，贝利转变策略，运用其法律力量攻击特朗普的政治对手并支持其议程。2月，他的办公室起诉星巴克，指控这家咖啡巨头在招聘过程中歧视白人男性。\n重要案件\n贝利还因利用其办公室权力反对他曾代表的密苏里州监狱系统中被监禁者提出的无罪主张，受到刑事司法活动人士的严厉批评。\n去年，贝利的办公室主张，一名被错误监禁的女性桑德拉·“桑迪”·赫姆不应获释出狱。贝利的办公室还试图阻止死囚马塞勒斯·“哈利法”·威廉姆斯在被处决前在法庭上陈述其无罪主张。\n2023年，贝利还采取了前所未有的行动，寻求推翻埃里克·德瓦尔肯纳雷的定罪；德瓦尔肯纳雷是堪萨斯城首位因杀害一名黑人男子而被判有罪的警察。这些努力未能成功，但帕森于去年12月减刑了德瓦尔肯纳雷的刑期。\n贝利在密苏里州的继任者\n作为 FBI 共同副局长，贝利将与现任副局长丹·邦吉诺共事，在美国司法部长帕姆·邦迪领导下担任 FBI 局长卡什·帕特尔的副手。贝利的任命将在他于9月8日辞去总检察长职务后生效，无需参议院确认。\n周二，州长迈克·基霍选择前联邦检察官、密苏里州众议院议长凯瑟琳·哈纳韦接替贝利。她将成为首位担任密苏里州总检察长的女性；该职位被广泛视为州一级第二有权力的职位。\n《堪萨斯城星报》相关报道\n政府与政治\n密苏里州州长选择该州首位女性总检察长接替贝利\n2025年8月19日 上午10:18\n政府与政治\n密苏里州总检察长安德鲁·贝利辞职加入特朗普政府\n2025年8月18日 下午5:59\nMatthew Kelly\n《堪萨斯城星报》\n316-268-6203\nMatthew Kelly是《堪萨斯城星报》驻堪萨斯州政府记者。他此前为《威奇托鹰报》报道地方政府新闻。Kelly拥有威奇托州立大学政治学学位。","publish_source":"kansascity.com","publish_time":"2025-08-19T13:00:46-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1513","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"堪萨斯城官员回应FBI调查报道：称其“恶劣”","title_en":"Kansas City official responds to report of FBI investigation: ‘Egregious’","summary_cn":"堪萨斯城副市长临时议长瑞安娜·帕克斯-肖回应福克斯4台匿名消息源报道称其与丈夫、市公共工程主任迈克尔·肖正接受FBI调查。她表示未接到联邦调查人员联系，但未直接否认调查存在，并称将请求进行伦理调查。市长卢卡斯办公室称已知悉相关报道，但未提供更多信息。报道称该调查可能影响2027年市长竞选。","summary_en":"Kansas City Mayor Pro-Tem Ryana Parks-Shaw responded to a FOX 4 report, based on anonymous sources, that she and her husband, Public Works Director Michael Shaw, are under FBI investigation. She said she has not been contacted by federal investigators but stopped short of denying an investigation exists, and said she would request an ethics inquiry. Mayor Quinton Lucas's office acknowledged awareness of the report but offered no further details. The probe could affect the 2027 mayoral race.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:21:11.653523+00:00","url":"https://www.kansascity.com/news/politics-government/article314855892.html","content":"Government & Politics\nKansas City official responds to report of FBI investigation: ‘Egregious’\nBy Kacen Bayless\nFebruary 26, 2026 6:06 PM\nKansas City Mayor Pro-Tem Ryana Parks-Shaw on Thursday addressed a report that she and her husband, a city director, were under investigation by the Federal Bureau of Investigation.\nKacen Bayless\nkbayless@kcstar.com\nKansas City Mayor Pro-Tem Ryana Parks-Shaw on Thursday blasted a report that she and her husband, a city director, were under investigation by the Federal Bureau of Investigation.Parks-Shaw, speaking inside the Kansas City Council chambers at City Hall, said she has not been contacted by federal investigators, but stopped short of directly refuting the existence of an investigation.“Yesterday, I was made aware of recent headlines containing egregious and misleading accusations designed to generate attention rather than inform the public,” she said. “I have not been contacted by any federal officials regarding any investigation. Should I be contacted, I will cooperate fully.”Parks-Shaw’s comments came a day after FOX 4 reported through anonymous sources that the FBI was investigating Parks-Shaw and her husband, Michael Shaw, the city’s public works director. The report was short on specifics about the investigation, but said the FBI asked sources about Parks-Shaw and her husband using their authority for their own gain.The allegations come as Parks-Shaw has launched a campaign for mayor in 2027, potentially upending the mayoral race. The existence of an FBI investigation also reverberated through City Hall on Thursday and Parks-Shaw called it the “elephant in the room.”A spokesperson for Kansas City Mayor Quinton Lucas, in a statement on Thursday, acknowledged that he was aware of the media report but did not provide additional information.“The Mayor’s Office is aware of the reports regarding an ongoing federal investigation,” said spokesperson Megan Strickland. “We remain focused on delivering for Kansas City residents and remain committed to transparency in city government.”While addressing her colleagues on Thursday, Parks-Shaw added that she would request her own ethics investigation to learn more information. It was not immediately clear what the focus of her ethics investigation would be.\nRelated Stories from Kansas City Star\nGovernment & Politics\nPort KC wants more power — and armed police force. Critics say it’s a ‘nonstarter’\nFebruary 25, 2026 12:34 PM\nGovernment & Politics\nHow a Kansas City lawmaker renewed interest in sister’s cold case\nFebruary 26, 2026 5:30 AM\nKacen Bayless\nThe Kansas City Star\n(816) 234-4207\nKacen Bayless is the Democracy Insider for The Kansas City Star, a position that uncovers how politics and government affect communities across the sprawling Kansas City area. Prior to this role, he covered Missouri politics for The Star. A graduate of the University of Missouri, he previously was an investigative reporter in coastal South Carolina.","content_cn":"政府与政治\n堪萨斯城官员回应FBI调查报道：‘令人震惊’\n作者：Kacen Bayless\n2026年2月26日下午6:06\n\n堪萨斯城市长临时代理Ryana Parks-Shaw周四回应了一则报道称，她和担任市政府主管的丈夫正受到联邦调查局调查。\n\nKacen Bayless\nkbayless@kcstar.com\n\n堪萨斯城市长临时代理Ryana Parks-Shaw周四猛烈抨击了一则报道称，她和担任市政府主管的丈夫正受到联邦调查局调查。Parks-Shaw在市政厅的堪萨斯市议会会议厅内发言时表示，联邦调查人员尚未与她联系，但没有直接否认调查的存在。\n\n“昨天，我得知近期一些标题中包含令人震惊且具有误导性的指控，这些指控旨在博取关注，而非告知公众，”她说。“没有任何联邦官员就任何调查与我联系。如果他们联系我，我将全面配合。”\n\nParks-Shaw的言论发表前一天，FOX 4援引匿名消息人士报道称，FBI正在调查Parks-Shaw及其丈夫、该市公共工程主管Michael Shaw。该报道没有详述调查情况，但称FBI向消息人士询问Parks-Shaw及其丈夫是否利用职权为自己谋利。\n\n这些指控出现之际，Parks-Shaw已启动2027年市长竞选活动，可能颠覆市长选举。FBI调查的存在也在周四的市政厅引起震动，Parks-Shaw称其为“房间里的大象”。\n\n堪萨斯城市长Quinton Lucas的一名发言人在周四的声明中承认，他知悉媒体报道，但未提供更多信息。\n\n发言人Megan Strickland说：“市长办公室知悉有关正在进行的联邦调查的报道。我们仍专注于为堪萨斯市居民提供服务，并继续致力于市政府的透明度。”\n\nParks-Shaw周四向同僚讲话时还表示，她将要求开展她自己的伦理调查，以了解更多信息。她的伦理调查将聚焦什么内容当时尚不明确。\n\n《堪萨斯城星报》相关报道\n\n政府与政治\nPort KC希望获得更多权力——以及武装警察力量。批评者称这“不可接受”\n2026年2月25日下午12:34\n\n政府与政治\n一名堪萨斯城议员如何重新唤起对其姐妹悬案的关注\n2026年2月26日上午5:30\n\nKacen Bayless\n《堪萨斯城星报》\n(816) 234-4207\n\nKacen Bayless是《堪萨斯城星报》的“民主内幕”记者，该职位揭示政治与政府如何影响广阔堪萨斯城地区的社区。在此职位之前，他为《星报》报道密苏里州政治。他毕业于密苏里大学，此前曾在南卡罗来纳州沿海地区担任调查记者。","publish_source":"kansascity.com","publish_time":"2026-02-26T18:06:47-06:00"}},{"id":"news-925","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"堪萨斯城官员在FBI调查其与妻子（代理市长）期间宣布退休","title_en":"KC official retiring amid FBI investigation into him and his wife, the Mayor pro tem","summary_cn":"堪萨斯城公共工程主管迈克尔·肖宣布将于5月29日退休，结束近三十年公职生涯。此前他与妻子、代理市长瑞安娜·帕克斯-肖成为美国联邦调查局调查对象，调查聚焦二人是否利用职权谋取财务和职业利益。多名前市政雇员接受FBI问询，涉及政府合同与竞选捐款。目前尚无逮捕或起诉，FBI通常不公开确认调查存在。","summary_en":"Michael Shaw, Kansas City's public works director, is retiring on May 29 after nearly three decades with the city, amid a federal criminal investigation. He and his wife, Mayor pro tem Ryana Parks-Shaw, were subjects of an FBI probe examining whether the couple used their authority for financial and professional gain. Former city employees interviewed by the FBI described questions about government contracts and campaign donations. No arrests or charges have been filed, and the FBI typically declines to confirm or deny investigations.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T10:47:05.835290+00:00","url":"https://www.kansascity.com/news/politics-government/article315830716.html","content":"Government & Politics\nKC official retiring amid FBI investigation into him and his wife, the Mayor pro tem\nBy Dylan Lysen and\nKacen Bayless\nMay 20, 2026 3:13 PM\nMichael Shaw, Kansas City’s public works director, speaks during an inclement weather press conference on Jan. 23, 2025.\nEmily Curiel\necuriel@kcstar.com\nA Kansas City official is retiring from his position in local government amid a federal criminal investigation.City officials confirmed Michael Shaw, the city’s public works director, is retiring on May 29 after a nearly three-decade career with the city.Earlier this year, Shaw and his wife Mayor pro tem Ryana Parks-Shaw were subjects of a Federal Bureau of Investigation probe focusing on whether the couple used their authority for financial and professional gain.Sherae Honeycutt, a spokesperson for the city, declined to answer The Star’s questions on whether Shaw’s decision to leave city government was related to the FBI probe.“This is a time to congratulate and thank Director Michael Shaw (for) his 28 years of service to the City,” Honeycutt said in an email to The Star. “His retirement is well earned.”It’s unclear where the federal probe stands. The FBI typically conducts its investigations in secret and the federal agency has previously declined to confirm or deny the existence of an investigation. There have been no arrests or charges as of Wednesday.Honeycutt declined to provide any further comment.City employees interviewed by the FBIIn March, The Star spoke with three former city employees who were interviewed by the FBI. Those employees, who spoke on condition of anonymity due to fear of retribution, described being asked a wide range of questions about government contracts and campaign donations.One focus of the questions centered on Shaw and Parks-Shaw. But the sources who spoke with The Star also detailed a host of other questions from the FBI, a sign that the exact target of the investigation is unclear.The federal probe also thrust into the spotlight a local nonprofit leader who worked with the city to combat homelessness. Anton Washington, the head of Creative Innovative, was named in a subpoena sent to City Hall last year, The Star previously revealed.Washington has several ties to Parks-Shaw, including court filings that describe him as a “champion” for her mayoral campaign and $203 in campaign donations. Shaw, the public works director, also approved a majority of the city’s contracts with Washington’s organization.\nRelated Stories from Kansas City Star\nGovernment & Politics\nKC proposes ‘no-tax’ bond votes for things like water and housing. What’s next?\nMay 19, 2026 3:41 PM\nGovernment & Politics\nKC councilmembers slam Nathan Willett for promoting Vance visit via city email list\nMay 19, 2026 10:36 AM\nDylan Lysen\nThe Kansas City Star","content_cn":"政府与政治\n堪萨斯城官员在联邦调查局调查其本人及其妻子、代理市长期间退休\n作者：Dylan Lysen、Kacen Bayless\n2026年5月20日下午3:13\n堪萨斯城公共工程主任Michael Shaw于2025年1月23日在恶劣天气新闻发布会上发言。\nEmily Curiel\necuriel@kcstar.com\n一名堪萨斯城官员正在接受联邦刑事调查之际从地方政府职位上退休。市政府官员确认，堪萨斯城公共工程主任Michael Shaw将在5月29日退休，此前他已为该市工作近30年。今年早些时候，Shaw及其妻子、代理市长Ryana Parks-Shaw成为联邦调查局调查对象，调查重点是这对夫妇是否利用职权谋取经济和职业利益。市政府发言人Sherae Honeycutt拒绝回答《星报》关于Shaw离开市政府的决定是否与联邦调查局调查有关的问题。Honeycutt在发给《星报》的电子邮件中说：“这是一个祝贺并感谢Michael Shaw主任为本市服务28年的时刻。他的退休当之无愧。”目前尚不清楚联邦调查进展到哪一步。联邦调查局通常秘密开展调查，该联邦机构此前也拒绝确认或否认调查是否存在。截至周三，尚无逮捕或指控。Honeycutt拒绝进一步置评。\n联邦调查局采访了市政府员工\n3月，《星报》采访了三名前市政府员工，他们曾接受联邦调查局询问。这些员工因担心遭到报复而要求匿名，他们描述了调查人员就政府合同和竞选捐款提出的大量问题。问题的一个重点围绕Shaw和Parks-Shaw展开。但接受《星报》采访的消息人士还详细介绍了联邦调查局提出的许多其他问题，这表明调查的确切目标尚不明确。联邦调查还使一名与市政府合作打击无家可归问题的当地非营利组织负责人受到关注。《星报》此前披露，Creative Innovative负责人Anton Washington曾出现在去年发给市政厅的一份传票中。Washington与Parks-Shaw有多项联系，包括法庭文件称他是其市长竞选的“支持者”，以及203美元的竞选捐款。公共工程主任Shaw还批准了该市与Washington组织签订的大部分合同。\n《堪萨斯城星报》相关文章\n政府与政治\n堪萨斯城提议就水务和住房等事项进行“无税”债券投票。下一步是什么？\n2026年5月19日下午3:41\n政府与政治\n堪萨斯城议员抨击Nathan Willett通过市政府电子邮件列表宣传Vance访问\n2026年5月19日上午10:36\nDylan Lysen\n《堪萨斯城星报》","publish_source":"kansascity.com","publish_time":"2026-05-20T15:13:14-05:00"}},{"id":"news-921","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"诉讼再度聚焦堪萨斯城FBI调查，目前已知情况汇总","title_en":"Lawsuit renews focus on Kansas City FBI probe. Here’s what we know","summary_cn":"一份新的举报人诉讼和一名高官退休，令围绕堪萨斯城市政厅的美国联邦调查局调查再度受到关注。FBI已问询多名市政雇员并发出大陪审团传票，调查至少可追溯至2025年1月，聚焦政府合同、竞选捐款及潜在腐败。代理市长帕克斯-肖及其丈夫迈克尔·肖被问及是否利用职权谋取私利。前助理城市经理科扎凯维奇称在配合FBI问询后数日遭解雇。目前尚无逮捕或起诉。","summary_en":"A new whistleblower lawsuit and a high-profile retirement have renewed focus on the FBI's sweeping investigation tied to Kansas City Hall. The FBI has interviewed several city employees and issued a grand jury subpoena; the probe dates back to at least January 2025 and appears to focus on government contracts, campaign donations and potential corruption. Mayor Pro Tem Ryana Parks-Shaw and her husband Michael Shaw were asked about whether they used their authority for personal gain. Former assistant city manager Melissa Kozakiewicz says she was fired days after speaking with federal authorities. No arrests or charges have been filed.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T10:47:02.763063+00:00","url":"https://www.kansascity.com/news/politics-government/article315845466.html","content":"Government & Politics\nLawsuit renews focus on Kansas City FBI probe. Here’s what we know\nBy Jack Harvel\nMay 21, 2026 3:00 PM\nThe Federal Bureau of Investigation has interviewed several city employees and issued a subpoena for documents. Months into the investigation, the scope and exact focus remains unclear.\nEmily Curiel\necuriel@kcstar.com\nKey TakeawaysAI-generated summary reviewed by our newsroom.Read our AI Policy.A whistleblower lawsuit and a high-profile retirement renewed interest in the FBI probe.City Manager Mario Vasquez has said the investigation dates back to at least January 2024.Melissa Kozakiewicz says she was fired days after an interview with federal authorities.A new whistleblower lawsuit and a high-profile retirement have renewed interest in a sweeping Federal Bureau of Investigation probe tied to City Hall that has plunged Kansas City politics into disarray.While the exact focus of the investigation remains unclear, the revelations have thrust the criminal probe back into the spotlight.City employees have said that federal investigators posed questions focused on top elected officials, contracts with outside vendors and potential instances of favoritism and corruption.Despite the lack of details, pieces of information have slowly trickled out in the months since the probe was revealed.Here’s what we know:Probe dates back monthsCity Manager Mario Vasquez has said that the investigation dates back to at least January 2025. Meanwhile, City Hall received a federal grand jury subpoena tied to the investigation last summer. The FBI typically conducts investigations in secret and there have been no arrests or charges filed as of Thursday.In that time, the FBI has conducted interviews with a handful of city employees, issued at least one subpoena demanding records from the city and obtained copies of Facebook messages tied to a local nonprofit leader, various sources said.The investigation appears to focus on government contracts and campaign donations and could be examining potential instances of corruption.In public corruption investigations, it can be hard to determine the direction of a probe based on a single grand jury subpoena, Pat McInerney, a prominent attorney and former federal prosecutor, previously said. Investigators, he said, typically cast a wide net.“They really kind of cover the gamut,” McInerney said in March. “They cover a whole lot of turf.”Mayoral raceAt least one local politician has been tied to the investigation. Mayor Pro Tem Ryana Parks-Shaw, who is currently running to replace term-limited Mayor Quinton Lucas, was the subject of some questions FBI agents posed during interviews with city employees, according to sources.Parks-Shaw’s husband, the city’s director of public works, Michael Shaw, announced his retirement on Wednesday. His last day of work is May 29.Agents posed questions to city employees about whether the couple used their authority for financial and professional gain.However, the sources detailed a series of other questions, signaling that the exact target of the investigation is unclear.Parks-Shaw has publicly stated that she has not been contacted by federal officials and that she would fully cooperate with an investigation.McInerney, the former federal prosecutor, said that individuals who are contacted by federal investigators typically fall into three categories: target, subject and witness. If a person is considered a target, that means their conduct is the focus of the investigation.If an individual is a subject, that means their conduct has “come within the scope” of the investigation. And witnesses are people who may have relevant information related to the investigation, he said.Parks-Shaw is facing two fellow city council members in the mayoral race: Crispin Rea, who represents the 4th District at Large and Wes Rogers of the Northland.City spendingA federal subpoena sent to City Hall in August sought records between the city and Anton Washington, who runs a nonprofit designed to connect homeless people to resources.Washington denied any wrongdoing tied to the subpoena. However, a pair of emails has alleged inappropriate behavior by Washington. The FBI has obtained a copy of one of those emails, according to a source.In total, Washington’s organization received roughly $287,000 from the city between 2021 and 2024, according to city financial records. Most of the contracts were approved by Michael Shaw, the public works director.Former employee alleges retaliationOn Wednesday, former Assistant City Manager Melissa Kozakiewicz filed a lawsuit against the city, alleging that city leaders retaliated and discriminated against her.The lawsuit alleges that Kozakiewicz was fired just days after she was interviewed by federal authorities about racial hiring decisions. Kozakiewicz said that she was disciplined for disclosing city issues to the FBI.\nRelated Stories from Kansas City Star\nLocal\nAI data center breaks ground in Independence. Who’s on the community advisory board?\nMay 20, 2026 5:03 PM\nGovernment & Politics\nLawmaker could become Kansas’ first Black statewide official since the 1880s\nMay 21, 2026 1:44 PM\nJack Harvel\nThe Kansas City Star\nJack Harvel is the Missouri Politics Insider for The Kansas City Star, where he covers how state politics and government impact people in Kansas City. Before joining the star, he covered state politics in Kansas and reported on communities in Colorado and Oregon. He was born in Kansas City, raised in Lee’s Summit and graduated from Mizzou in 2019.","content_cn":"政府与政治\n诉讼让人们再次关注堪萨斯城联邦调查局调查。以下是我们所知道的\n杰克·哈维尔 撰写\n2026年5月21日下午3:00\n联邦调查局已经询问了几名市政府雇员，并发出传票要求提供文件。调查进行数月后，其范围和确切重点仍不清楚。\n艾米莉·库里尔\necuriel@kcstar.com\n关键要点AI生成的摘要已由本报编辑部审阅。阅读我们的AI政策。一宗举报人诉讼和一名备受关注的退休事件，让人们重新关注联邦调查局的调查。市经理马里奥·巴斯克斯表示，调查至少可以追溯到2024年1月。梅丽莎·科扎凯维奇称，她在接受联邦当局询问几天后被解雇。一宗新的举报人诉讼和一名备受关注的退休事件，让人们重新关注一项与市政厅有关、范围广泛的联邦调查局调查；这项调查已使堪萨斯城政坛陷入混乱。尽管调查的确切重点仍不清楚，但这些披露的信息已让这项刑事调查重新成为焦点。市政府雇员表示，联邦调查人员提出的问题集中在最高层民选官员、与外部供应商签订的合同，以及可能存在的偏袒和腐败行为上。尽管细节匮乏，但自调查曝光以来的数月中，信息片段一直缓慢流出。以下是我们所知道的：调查可追溯至数月前市经理马里奥·巴斯克斯表示，调查至少可以追溯到2025年1月。与此同时，市政厅去年夏天收到了一份与调查有关的联邦大陪审团传票。联邦调查局通常秘密进行调查，截至周四，尚未有人被逮捕或受到指控。据多名消息人士称，在此期间，联邦调查局询问了少数几名市政府雇员，至少发出过一份传票，要求市政府提供记录，并取得了与一名当地非营利组织负责人有关的Facebook消息副本。调查似乎集中在政府合同和竞选捐款上，也可能在审查潜在的腐败行为。知名律师、前联邦检察官帕特·麦金纳尼此前表示，在公共腐败调查中，很难仅凭一份大陪审团传票判断调查方向。他说，调查人员通常会广泛撒网。“他们基本上什么都覆盖，”麦金纳尼在3月说。“他们涉及的范围非常广。”市长竞选至少有一名当地政界人士与调查有关。据消息人士称，现正竞选接替任期届满的市长昆顿·卢卡斯的临时市长赖安娜·帕克斯-肖，成为联邦调查局特工在询问市政府雇员时提出部分问题的对象。帕克斯-肖的丈夫、该市公共工程主任迈克尔·肖于周三宣布退休。他的最后工作日是5月29日。特工向市政府雇员提问，这对夫妇是否利用职权谋取经济和职业利益。然而，消息人士还详细说明了一系列其他问题，表明调查的确切目标尚不清楚。帕克斯-肖公开表示，她没有受到联邦官员联系，并将充分配合调查。前联邦检察官麦金纳尼说，受到联邦调查人员联系的人通常分为三类：目标、涉案对象和证人。如果一个人被视为目标，这意味着其行为是调查的重点\n调查。如果某人是调查对象，这意味着其行为“已进入”调查范围。他说，证人则是可能掌握与调查相关信息的人。\n\nParks-Shaw在市长竞选中面对两名同为市议员的对手：代表第四全市选区的Crispin Rea，以及来自Northland的Wes Rogers。\n\n城市支出\n\n8月发往市政厅的一份联邦传票要求提供该市与Anton Washington之间的记录。Washington经营一家旨在帮助无家可归者对接资源的非营利组织。\n\nWashington否认与该传票有关的任何不当行为。然而，两封电子邮件指控Washington存在不当行为。据一名消息人士称，FBI已获得其中一封电子邮件的副本。\n\n根据市财政记录，2021年至2024年间，Washington的组织共从该市获得约287,000美元。大多数合同由公共工程主管Michael Shaw批准。\n\n前雇员指控报复\n\n周三，前助理城市经理Melissa Kozakiewicz对该市提起诉讼，指控市领导层对她进行报复和歧视。\n\n诉讼称，Kozakiewicz在因种族因素作出的招聘决定接受联邦当局采访后仅数天便被解雇。Kozakiewicz表示，她因向FBI披露城市问题而受到处分。\n\n《Kansas City Star》相关报道\n\n本地\n\nAI数据中心在Independence破土动工。社区咨询委员会有哪些成员？\n\n2026年5月20日 下午5:03\n\n政府与政治\n\n议员或将成为自19世纪80年代以来Kansas首位全州范围的黑人官员\n\n2026年5月21日 下午1:44\n\nJack Harvel\n\n《The Kansas City Star》\n\nJack Harvel是《The Kansas City Star》的Missouri Politics Insider，报道州政治和政府如何影响Kansas City的人们。加入该报前，他报道过Kansas的州政治，并在Colorado和Oregon报道社区新闻。他出生于Kansas City，在Lee’s Summit长大，并于2019年毕业于Mizzou。","publish_source":"kansascity.com","publish_time":"2026-05-21T15:00:04-05:00"}},{"id":"news-3585","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike与达美航空就航班取消责任归属争执","title_en":"CrowdStrike and Delta fight over who’s to blame for the airline canceling thousands of flights","summary_cn":"网络安全公司CrowdStrike与达美航空就7月19日全球技术故障后数千航班取消的责任归属发生争执。达美航空CEO表示损失约5亿美元并威胁起诉，而CrowdStrike律师称其责任应低于1000万美元，并质疑为何其他航空公司恢复更快。美国交通部正在调查达美航空恢复缓慢的原因及客户服务投诉。","summary_en":"CrowdStrike and Delta Air Lines are disputing blame for thousands of canceled flights after a July 19 global technology outage. Delta's CEO threatened to sue over $500 million in losses, while a CrowdStrike lawyer said its liability should be under $10 million and questioned why other airlines recovered faster. The U.S. Department of Transportation is investigating Delta's slower recovery and customer service complaints.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:54:28.928857+00:00","url":"https://www.kbtx.com/2024/08/05/crowdstrike-delta-fight-over-whos-blame-airline-canceling-thousands-flights","content":"CrowdStrike and Delta fight over who’s to blame for the airline canceling thousands of flightsFILE - A Delta Air Lines jet leaves the gate, July 19, 2024, at Logan International Airport in Boston. Delta CEO Ed Bastian says the airline is facing $500 million in costs for the global technology breakdown that happened earlier this month. (AP Photo/Michael Dwyer, File)(AP)By The Associated PressPublished: Aug. 5, 2024 at 5:49 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on Google(AP) - Cybersecurity software company CrowdStrike is disputing Delta Air Lines over who is to blame for damage that the airline suffered after a global technology outage.Delta’s CEO has threatened to sue CrowdStrike for what he said was $500 million in lost revenue and extra costs related to thousands of canceled flights.A lawyer for CrowdStrike says, however, that the company’s liability should be less than $10 million.Michael Carlinsky said in a letter Sunday to Delta lawyer David Boies that the airline’s threatened lawsuit “has contributed to a misleading narrative that CrowdStrike is responsible for Delta’s IT decisions and response to the outage.”The CrowdStrike lawyer questioned why other airlines recovered from the outage much more quickly. He said the software company took responsibility for its actions “while Delta did not.”A faulty software update from CrowdStrike to more than 8 million computers using Microsoft Windows disrupted airlines, banks, retailers and other businesses on July 19.Delta CEO Ed Bastian raised the threat of a lawsuit last week on CNBC. He said Delta was more dependent on Microsoft Windows than other airlines. The Atlanta-based airline hired Boies’ law firm to handle the matter.Bastian said CrowdStrike did not offer to help Delta beyond offering free consulting advice. CrowdStrike said its CEO, George Kurtz, personally contacted Bastian to offer help, but got no response.The U.S. Department of Transportation is investigating why Delta took longer to recover than other airlines. Transportation Secretary Pete Buttigieg said his department would also look into complaints about Delta’s customer service, including long waits for help and reports that unaccompanied minors were stranded at airports.Copyright 2024 The Associated Press. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"CrowdStrike与达美航空争论谁应为该航空公司取消数千航班负责\n文件照——2024年7月19日，达美航空一架飞机离开登机口，地点为波士顿洛根国际机场。达美航空首席执行官埃德·巴斯蒂安表示，该航空公司正面临因本月早些时候发生的全球技术故障而产生的5亿美元成本。（美联社照片/迈克尔·德怀尔，文件照）（美联社）\n美联社\n发布时间：2024年8月5日下午5:49（美国中部时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n（美联社）——网络安全软件公司CrowdStrike正与达美航空争论，该航空公司在全球技术中断后遭受的损失应由谁负责。\n达美航空首席执行官威胁要起诉CrowdStrike，称与数千个航班取消有关的收入损失和额外成本达5亿美元。\n然而，CrowdStrike的一名律师表示，该公司的责任应低于1000万美元。\nCrowdStrike律师迈克尔·卡林斯基周日致信达美航空律师大卫·博伊斯称，航空公司威胁提起的诉讼“助长了一种误导性叙事，即CrowdStrike应为达美航空的IT决策以及对这次中断的响应负责”。\n这名CrowdStrike律师质疑，为什么其他航空公司从此次中断中恢复得快得多。他说，这家软件公司“承担了自身行为的责任，而达美航空没有”。\n7月19日，CrowdStrike向800多万台使用微软Windows的电脑推送了一次有缺陷的软件更新，导致航空公司、银行、零售商和其他企业运营中断。\n达美航空首席执行官埃德·巴斯蒂安上周在CNBC上提出起诉威胁。他说，与其他航空公司相比，达美航空更加依赖微软Windows。这家总部位于亚特兰大的航空公司聘请了博伊斯的律师事务所处理此事。\n巴斯蒂安说，CrowdStrike除了提供免费的咨询建议外，没有提出进一步帮助达美航空。CrowdStrike表示，其首席执行官乔治·库尔茨曾亲自联系巴斯蒂安提供帮助，但没有得到回应。\n美国交通部正在调查达美航空为何比其他航空公司花费更长时间恢复。交通部长皮特·布蒂吉格表示，该部门还将调查有关达美航空客户服务的投诉，包括长时间等待帮助，以及无人陪伴的未成年人被滞留在机场的报告。\n版权所有2024年美联社。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kbtx.com","publish_time":"2024-08-05T22:49:46.017000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2987","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI称一名与委内瑞拉帮派有关联的男子在布莱恩附近被捕","title_en":"FBI says man with ties to Venezuelan gang arrested near Bryan","summary_cn":"据KBTX报道，一名据称与“阿拉瓜火车”帮派有关联的委内瑞拉籍男子于4月9日在得克萨斯州布莱恩附近被联邦调查局、移民和海关执法局及得州公共安全部联合行动逮捕。ICE称47岁的埃斯卡洛纳-穆希卡斯非法入境，2023年在布朗斯维尔附近被边境巡逻人员拘留，移民法官于去年3月下令将其驱逐，但他在驱逐前逃脱。FBI称此次行动体现联邦、州和地方执法合作打击暴力犯罪。","summary_en":"A Venezuelan national with alleged ties to the Tren de Aragua gang was arrested April 9 near Bryan, Texas, during a joint operation by the FBI, ICE and the Texas Department of Public Safety, KBTX reported. ICE said 47-year-old Jesus Alberto Escalona-Mujicas entered the country illegally and was taken into custody near Brownsville in 2023; an immigration judge ordered his removal in March last year, but he escaped before authorities could remove him. The FBI said the operation exemplified federal, state and local law enforcement partnerships targeting violent criminals.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:15:48.896551+00:00","url":"https://www.kbtx.com/2025/04/10/fbi-says-man-with-ties-venezuelan-gang-arrested-bryan","content":"FBI says man with ties to Venezuelan gang arrested near BryanBy Delaney WolovlekPublished: Apr. 10, 2025 at 11:30 AM CDT|Updated: Apr. 10, 2025 at 3:59 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleBRYAN, Texas (KBTX) - A Venezuelan national with alleged ties to the Tren de Aragua gang was arrested April 9 during a joint operation by the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) near Bryan, U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE), and the Texas Department of Public Safety (DPS). A statement from ICE said 47-year-old Jesus Alberto Escalona-Mujicas entered the country illegally at an unknown time, but U.S. Border Patrol agents took him into custody near Brownsville back in 2023. He was then placed into immigration proceedings and a judge from the Justice Department’s Executive Office for Immigration Review ordered Escalona-Mujicas removed in March of last year. According to the FBI, he escaped authorities before they could remove him.Jesus Alberto Escalona-Mujicas, 47. Documented Tren de Aragua gang member(KBTX)ICE officials said Escalona-Mujicas is a documented Tren de Aragua gang member but did not expand on his history. Escalona-Mujicas was taken into ICE custody and transported to the Montgomery Processing Center in Conroe, pending his removal from the country.“Another example of the FBI’s partnerships with federal, state and local law enforcement to strategically target violent criminals within our communities,” a statement from the FBI said.Jesus Alberto Escalona-Mujicas, 47.(KBTX)ICE @EROHouston, @FBI and @TxDPS arrested a Tren de Aragua gang member April 9 who was illegally residing in the Houston area. Details: 👇https://t.co/PkDmyUC5CI— ERO Houston (@EROHouston) April 10, 2025\nCopyright 2025 KBTX. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI称一名与委内瑞拉帮派有关联的男子在布赖恩附近被捕\n作者：Delaney Wolovlek\n发布时间：2025年4月10日 CDT 上午11:30｜更新时间：2025年4月10日 CDT 下午3:59\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n添加为 Google 首选来源\n\n德克萨斯州布赖恩（KBTX）——联邦调查局（FBI）、美国移民和海关执法局（ICE）以及德克萨斯州公共安全部（DPS）于4月9日在布赖恩附近开展联合行动，逮捕了一名据称与阿拉瓜列车帮派有关联的委内瑞拉籍男子。\n\nICE的一份声明称，47岁的Jesus Alberto Escalona-Mujicas在不明时间非法入境，但美国边境巡逻人员于2023年在布朗斯维尔附近将其拘押。随后，他被纳入移民程序，司法部移民审查执行办公室的一名法官于去年3月下令将Escalona-Mujicas遣返。\n\n据FBI称，在当局能够将他遣返前，他逃脱了。\n\nJesus Alberto Escalona-Mujicas，47岁。已被记录的阿拉瓜列车帮派成员\n（KBTX）\n\nICE官员称，Escalona-Mujicas是有记录的阿拉瓜列车帮派成员，但未进一步说明其过往情况。Escalona-Mujicas已被ICE拘押，并被送往康罗的蒙哥马利处理中心，等待被遣返出境。\n\nFBI的一份声明称：“这再次体现了FBI与联邦、州及地方执法机构的合作伙伴关系，战略性地锁定我们社区内的暴力犯罪分子。”\n\nJesus Alberto Escalona-Mujicas，47岁。\n（KBTX）\n\nICE @EROHouston、@FBI和@TxDPS于4月9日逮捕了一名非法居住在休斯敦地区的阿拉瓜列车帮派成员。详情：👇\nhttps://t.co/PkDmyUC5CI\n—— ERO Houston（@EROHouston），2025年4月10日\n\n版权所有 2025 KBTX。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kbtx.com","publish_time":"2025-04-10T16:30:21.303000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1905","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI局长通报明尼苏达州欺诈案调查进展","title_en":"FBI Director provides update on Minnesota fraud investigations","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局（FBI）局长卡什·帕特尔在社交媒体发文称，FBI持续调查明尼苏达州涉及联邦项目的欺诈案。他表示，在舆论升温前FBI已增派人员和调查资源。已查明的“喂养我们的未来”网络案涉2.5亿美元儿童食品援助欺诈，共78人被起诉、57人定罪，部分被告曾以12万美元现金贿赂陪审员并获刑。帕特尔称调查仍在进行，此案只是冰山一角。","summary_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel said in a social media post that the FBI continues investigating fraud schemes involving federal programs in Minnesota, noting the bureau had surged personnel and resources before public discussion escalated. He cited a $250 million COVID-era child food aid fraud tied to the Feeding Our Future network, resulting in 78 indictments and 57 convictions. Some defendants bribed a juror with $120,000 in cash and received prison terms and restitution. Patel said the investigation remains ongoing and is just the tip of a large iceberg.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:21:18.496345+00:00","url":"https://www.kbtx.com/2025/12/28/fbi-director-provides-update-minnesota-fraud-investigations","content":"FBI Director provides update on Minnesota fraud investigationsPatel says agency continues work on federal program fraud schemesFBI director Kash Patel speaks at a press conference announcing the arrests of Portland Trail Blazers head coach Chauncey Billups and Miami Heat guard Terry Rozier in connection with a federal investigation into sports betting and illegal gambling, Thursday, Oct. 23, 2025, in New York. (AP Photo/Angelina Katsanis)(Angelina Katsanis | AP)By Ethan KramerPublished: Dec. 28, 2025 at 3:06 PM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleMINNESOTA (Valley News Live) - FBI Director Kash Patel said Sunday in a social media post that the FBI continues its work investigating fraud schemes involving federal programs in Minnesota.The FBI is aware of recent social media reports in Minnesota, Patel said. The FBI had surged personnel and investigative resources to Minnesota to investigate large-scale fraud schemes involving federal programs before the public conversation escalated online, he said.CASE UPDATE: MINNESOTA FRAUD SCHEME The FBI is aware of recent social media reports in Minnesota. However, even before the public conversation escalated online, the FBI had surged personnel and investigative resources to Minnesota to dismantle large-scale fraud schemes…— FBI Director Kash Patel (@FBIDirectorKash) December 28, 2025\nThe FBI has investigated a $250 million fraud scheme involving federal food aid meant for children during COVID, Patel said. The investigation found sham vendors, shell companies and large-scale money laundering tied to the Feeding Our Future network.The case has resulted in 78 indictments and 57 convictions, Patel said. Defendants included Abdiwahab Ahmed Mohamud, Ahmed Ali, Hussein Farah, Abdilahe Nur Jesow, Asha Farhan Hassan, Ousman Camara and Abdirashid Bixi Dool, each charged for roles ranging from wire fraud to money laundering and conspiracy.Some individuals attempted to bribe a juror with $120,000 in cash, Patel said. Those individuals pleaded guilty and were sentenced, including 10-year prison terms and nearly $48 million in restitution in related cases.“The FBI believes this is just the tip of a very large iceberg,” Patel said. The investigation remains ongoing.Copyright 2025 KVLY. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI局长通报明尼苏达州欺诈调查进展\n帕特尔称该机构继续调查涉及联邦项目的欺诈计划\n2025年10月23日，星期四，纽约，FBI局长卡什·帕特尔在新闻发布会上讲话。此次发布会宣布逮捕波特兰开拓者队主教练昌西·比卢普斯和迈阿密热火队后卫特里·罗齐尔，他们涉嫌卷入一项关于体育博彩和非法赌博的联邦调查。（美联社照片/安吉丽娜·卡萨尼斯）（安吉丽娜·卡萨尼斯 | 美联社）\n作者：伊桑·克莱默\n发布于：2025年12月28日下午3:06（美国中部标准时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n明尼苏达州（Valley News Live）——FBI局长卡什·帕特尔周日在社交媒体发文称，FBI继续调查明尼苏达州涉及联邦项目的欺诈计划。\n帕特尔说，FBI注意到近期明尼苏达州社交媒体上的相关报道。他说，在网上公众讨论升温之前，FBI就已向明尼苏达州增派人员和调查资源，以调查涉及联邦项目的大规模欺诈计划。\n案件进展：明尼苏达州欺诈计划\nFBI注意到近期明尼苏达州社交媒体上的相关报道。然而，甚至在网上公众讨论升温之前，FBI就已向明尼苏达州增派人员和调查资源，以瓦解大规模欺诈计划……——FBI局长卡什·帕特尔（@FBIDirectorKash），2025年12月28日\n帕特尔说，FBI调查了一起涉及2.5亿美元联邦食品援助资金的欺诈计划，这些资金原本用于新冠疫情期间的儿童。调查发现了与“喂养我们的未来”网络有关的虚假供应商、空壳公司和大规模洗钱活动。\n帕特尔说，该案件已导致78项起诉和57项定罪。被告包括阿卜迪瓦哈卜·艾哈迈德·穆罕默德、艾哈迈德·阿里、侯赛因·法拉、阿卜迪拉希德·努尔·杰索、阿莎·法尔汉·哈桑、奥斯曼·卡马拉和阿卜迪拉希德·比希·杜尔；他们分别被控电信诈骗、洗钱和共谋等不同罪名。\n帕特尔说，一些人曾试图用12万美元现金贿赂一名陪审员。这些人认罪并被判刑，其中包括10年监禁，以及在相关案件中近4800万美元的赔偿金。\n“FBI认为，这只是一个非常庞大冰山的尖端，”帕特尔说。调查仍在进行中。\n版权所有2025年KVLY。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kbtx.com","publish_time":"2025-12-28T21:06:07.854000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-762","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI查封13个被指用于中国招募美国工作人员的网站","title_en":"FBI seizes 13 websites that officials say were used by China to target and recruit US workers","summary_cn":"美国司法部称，FBI查封了13个网站，官员指其属于中国针对可接触机密或敏感政府信息的美国工作人员的行动。这些网站冒充咨询公司发布虚假职位，利用伪造身份和AI生成照片增加可信度，并通过加密货币支付以隐藏真实身份。FBI称信息来自主动举报的可疑接触对象，并认为还有类似网站存在。中国驻美使馆发言人称相关间谍指控“纯属捏造”。","summary_en":"The Justice Department said the FBI seized 13 websites that officials say were part of a Chinese effort to target American workers with access to classified or sensitive government information. The sites posed as consulting firms posting sham jobs, using fraudulent identities and AI-generated photos, and paying via cryptocurrency to hide identities. The FBI said tips came from targets who reported suspicious contacts and believes other similar sites exist. A Chinese embassy spokesperson called the espionage allegations entirely fabricated.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:30:30.759554+00:00","url":"https://www.kbtx.com/2026/06/11/fbi-seizes-13-websites-that-officials-say-were-used-by-china-target-recruit-us-workers","content":"FBI seizes 13 websites that officials say were used by China to target and recruit US workersFILE - The seal of the Federal Bureau of Investigation is displayed at its headquarters in Washington, Nov. 18, 2024. (AP Photo/Jose Luis Magana, File)(Jose Luis Magana | AP)By The Associated Press and ERIC TUCKER Published: Jun. 11, 2026 at 3:34 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleWASHINGTON (AP) — The FBI has seized more than a dozen websites that officials say were part of a Chinese effort to target American workers who have access to classified or sensitive government information, the Justice Department said Wednesday.The 13 websites purported to be affiliated with consulting companies that advertised job openings for current and former holders of security clearances. But the companies were all fakes and the job postings were a sham, officials said.The internet domain seizure is part of a broader effort by Western law enforcement and intelligence agencies to sound the alarm about alleged Chinese government plots to recruit workers who can be duped into disclosing sensitive information.Last week, for instance, the English-speaking Five Eyes intelligence-sharing alliance — Australia, Canada, New Zealand, the U.K. and the U.S. — issued a bulletin warning that China is targeting personnel from those countries on job websites to get access to classified or sensitive information.The bulletin said spies for Chinese military intelligence have been posing as workers acting on behalf of private businesses or think tanks, advertising for bogus jobs such as foreign policy or defense analysts and pressuring candidates to provide “non-public” information.According to an FBI affidavit filed in connection with the website seizure, the fake websites relied on fraudulent or stolen identities and AI-generated photographs to give them the appearance of legitimacy, and advertised generic “consulting” jobs geared toward current or former U.S. government employees.“These websites are often linked or referenced within the entities’ job postings on LinkedIn and other hiring platforms,” the affidavit said.Applicants and recruits were offered money for reports related to their work and for sensitive information, the Justice Department said. The operators of the plot, who officials allege to be tied to Chinese intelligence services, used cryptocurrency and online payment systems to hide their real identities, officials said.Law enforcement officials identified the websites through information from targets who came forward to report what they believed to be suspicious interactions.“A lot of this information came from doing interviews, interviews with people who came forward that something didn’t seem right,” Dan Wierzbicki, the special agent in charge of the counterintelligence and cyber division of the FBI’s Washington field office, said in an interview.“They provided information and said, ‘Hey, this is kind of weird, we’re kind of getting paid by a cryptocurrency or an online payment system that’s not typical,’” he added.He said the FBI believes there are other websites serving a similar purpose and is seeking the public’s help in identifying them.A spokesperson for the Chinese embassy in Washington called allegations of Chinese espionage “entirely fabricated” and “malicious slander.”___Associated Press writer Didi Tang in Washington contributed to this report.Copyright 2026 The Associated Press. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI 查封13个网站，官员称这些网站被中国用于锁定和招募美国工作人员\n\n文件——2024年11月18日，美国联邦调查局印章展示于其位于华盛顿的总部。（美联社照片/Jose Luis Magana，资料图）（Jose Luis Magana | 美联社）\n\n作者：美联社和 ERIC TUCKER\n发布时间：2026年6月11日 下午3:34（CDT）\n\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上将其添加为首选来源\n\n华盛顿（美联社）——司法部周三表示，FBI 已查封十多个网站，官员称这些网站是中国为锁定可接触机密或敏感政府信息的美国工作人员而开展行动的一部分。\n\n这13个网站声称与咨询公司有关联，并刊登面向现任和前任持有安全许可人员的职位空缺广告。但官员表示，这些公司全是假的，招聘信息也是骗局。\n\n对互联网域名的查封是西方执法和情报机构更广泛行动的一部分，旨在就涉嫌中国政府招募可能被诱骗泄露敏感信息的工作人员的计划发出警报。\n\n例如，上周，英语国家“五眼”情报共享联盟——澳大利亚、加拿大、新西兰、英国和美国——发布公告警告，中国正在招聘网站上锁定这些国家的人员，以获取机密或敏感信息。\n\n该公告称，中国军事情报机构的间谍一直假扮代表私营企业或智库行事的工作人员，为外交政策或国防分析师等虚假职位刊登招聘广告，并向候选人施压，要求其提供“非公开”信息。\n\n根据 FBI 为查封这些网站而提交的一份宣誓书，这些虚假网站依赖欺诈或被盗身份以及 AI 生成的照片来营造合法外观，并刊登面向现任或前任美国政府雇员的通用“咨询”职位广告。\n\n宣誓书称：“这些网站常常在相关实体于 LinkedIn 和其他招聘平台发布的职位信息中被链接或提及。”\n\n司法部称，申请者和被招募者因提供与其工作有关的报告及敏感信息而获得报酬。官员称，该计划的操作者被指与中国情报部门有关，他们使用加密货币和在线支付系统来隐藏真实身份。\n\n执法官员通过那些主动报告他们认为可疑互动的目标人士所提供的信息，识别出了这些网站。\n\nFBI 华盛顿办事处反情报和网络部门主管特工 Dan Wierzbicki 在采访中说：“这些信息中有很多来自进行访谈，访谈那些主动反映某些事情似乎不太对劲的人。”\n\n他补充说：“他们提供了信息，并说，‘嘿，这有点奇怪，我们似乎是通过加密货币或一种不常见的在线支付系统获得报酬。’”\n\n他说，FBI 相信还有其他网站在发挥类似作用，并正寻求公众协助识别这些网站。\n\n中国驻华盛顿大使馆的一名发言人称，有关中国从事间谍活动的指控“完全是捏造的”，是“恶意诽谤”。\n\n___\n美联社驻华盛顿记者 Didi Tang 对本报道亦有贡献。\n\n版权所有 2026 美联社。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kbtx.com","publish_time":"2026-06-11T20:34:37.605000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-365","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI：美国暴力犯罪历史性下降，谋杀率创70年新低","title_en":"FBI: U.S. experiences historic drop in violent crime, lowest murder rate in 70 years","summary_cn":"FBI最新发布的统一犯罪报告数据显示，2025年美国暴力犯罪率较2024年下降9.3%，为1936年有全国估算以来最大年度降幅。全国谋杀率降至每10万人4.1起，与1955年和1956年并列历史最低。谋杀与非过失杀人下降约18.1%，抢劫下降18.5%，强奸下降7.6%，严重伤害下降7.2%。仇恨犯罪事件从2024年的11404起降至2025年的10606起，下降7.0%。","summary_en":"Newly released FBI Uniform Crime Reporting data show U.S. violent crime fell 9.3% from 2024 to 2025, the sharpest annual drop since national estimates began in 1936. The national murder rate fell to 4.1 per 100,000 inhabitants, tying 1955 and 1956 for the lowest on record. Murder and non-negligent manslaughter fell an estimated 18.1%, robbery 18.5%, rape 7.6% and aggravated assault 7.2%. Reported hate crime incidents dropped 7.0%, from 11,404 in 2024 to 10,606 in 2025.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:50:58.391119+00:00","url":"https://www.kbtx.com/2026/08/16/fbi-us-experiences-historic-drop-violent-crime-lowest-murder-rate-70-years","content":"FBI: U.S. experiences historic drop in violent crime, lowest murder rate in 70 yearsBy Sophia RidleyPublished: Aug. 16, 2026 at 3:37 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleWASHINGTON (KBTX) - The United States experienced its largest year-to-year decline in violent crime rates in nearly a century, according to newly released data from the FBI.Newly published figures from the FBI’s Uniform Crime Reporting (UCR) Program show that violent crime decreased by 9.3% from 2024 to 2025, marking the sharpest annual drop since national estimations began in 1936.The drop brings the national murder rate down to 4.1 per 100,000 inhabitants—tying with 1955 and 1956 for the lowest murder rate in recorded U.S. history.Violent crime by the numbersThe FBI’s detailed report, which analyzed more than 13 million criminal offenses reported by participating law enforcement agencies, highlights significant declines across all major violent crime categories in 2025:Murder and non-negligent manslaughter: Decreased by an estimated 18.1%Robbery: Decreased by an estimated 18.5%Rape: Decreased by an estimated 7.6%Aggravated assault: Decreased by an estimated 7.2%The data was compiled from more than 17,000 federal, state, county, city, tribal, and college law enforcement agencies, covering approximately 96.2% of the U.S. population.source:(Federal Bureau-Investigation)Property and hate crimes also trend downwardIn addition to violent crime, both property crimes and hate crimes saw measurable decreases in 2025.According to the FBI dataset, reported hate crime incidents decreased by 7.0%, falling from 11,404 incidents in 2024 to 10,606 in 2025. Nearly 17,000 agencies participated in the hate crime data collection effort, representing 95.3% of the population.Bias motivations reported in the 13,026 offenses included race, ethnicity, ancestry, religion, sexual orientation, disability, gender, and gender identity.Modernizing crime data accessThe complete 2025 analysis is available on the FBI’s Crime Data Explorer. Alongside the traditional downloadable tables, the agency has launched “RCN Online”—a series of interactive dashboards designed to modernize annual reporting and make high-interest crime data more accessible to the public.Copyright 2026 KBTX. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI：美国暴力犯罪出现历史性下降，谋杀率为70年来最低\n作者：Sophia Ridley\n发布时间：2026年8月16日下午3:37（中部夏令时间）\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上添加为首选来源\n\n华盛顿（KBTX）——根据联邦调查局（FBI）新发布的数据，美国经历了近一个世纪以来暴力犯罪率最大幅度的年度下降。\n\nFBI统一犯罪报告（UCR）项目最新公布的数据显示，暴力犯罪率从2024年到2025年下降了9.3%，这是自1936年开始进行全国估算以来最剧烈的年度降幅。\n\n此次下降使全国谋杀率降至每10万人4.1起，与1955年和1956年持平，成为有记录以来美国最低的谋杀率。\n\n暴力犯罪数据\n\nFBI的详细报告分析了参与执法机构报告的超过1300万起刑事犯罪，显示2025年各主要暴力犯罪类别均大幅下降：\n\n谋杀和非过失杀人：估计下降18.1%\n抢劫：估计下降18.5%\n强奸：估计下降7.6%\n加重袭击：估计下降7.2%\n\n这些数据汇总自超过17,000个联邦、州、县、市、部落和高校执法机构，覆盖约96.2%的美国人口。\n来源：（联邦调查局）\n\n财产犯罪和仇恨犯罪也呈下降趋势\n\n除暴力犯罪外，2025年财产犯罪和仇恨犯罪也出现了可测量的下降。\n\n根据FBI数据集，报告的仇恨犯罪事件下降了7.0%，从2024年的11,404起降至2025年的10,606起。近17,000个机构参与了仇恨犯罪数据收集工作，覆盖95.3%的人口。\n\n在报告的13,026起犯罪中，偏见动机包括种族、族裔、血统、宗教、性取向、残疾、性别和性别认同。\n\n现代化犯罪数据访问\n\n完整的2025年分析可在FBI犯罪数据探索器上查看。除传统的可下载表格外，该机构还推出了“RCN Online”——一系列互动式仪表板，旨在使年度报告现代化，并让公众更容易获取高关注度的犯罪数据。\n\n版权2026 KBTX。版权所有。","publish_source":"kbtx.com","publish_time":"2026-08-16T20:37:04.868000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1673","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI搜查令在拉斯维加斯民宅发现疑似“生物实验室”","title_en":"FBI search warrant leads to possible ‘biological lab’ discovery at Las Vegas home","summary_cn":"拉斯维加斯警方称，一项涉及FBI的调查在拉斯维加斯一处民宅发现疑似“生物实验室”。警方在冰箱内发现“生物材料”和装有不明液体的药瓶，ARMOR小组与FBI、消防等部门共同回收物品。房产记录显示现住户与加州一处类似实验室的发现有关。报道称该加州设施曾被指从中国公司进口新冠检测试剂盒并虚假标注产地，还发现多种病原体样本。调查仍在进行。","summary_en":"Las Vegas police said an investigation involving the FBI uncovered what officials called a biological lab at a Las Vegas home. Officers found biological material in refrigerators and vials containing unknown liquids; the ARMOR team worked with the FBI and fire departments to recover items. Property records link the resident to a similar lab found in California, which was accused of importing COVID-19 test kits from a Chinese company while falsely claiming U.S. origin, and reportedly contained pathogens. The investigation is ongoing.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:12:56.720608+00:00","url":"https://www.kcrg.com/2026/02/02/fbi-search-warrant-leads-possible-biological-lab-discovery-las-vegas-home","content":"FBI search warrant leads to possible ‘biological lab’ discovery at Las Vegas homeA joint investigation involving LVMPD and the FBI unveiled what police are calling a “biological lab” in the east valley. (SOURCE: KVVU)By Cody Lee, Arianna Schmidt, Rachel Zalucki and Gray News staffPublished: Feb. 2, 2026 at 5:45 PM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleLAS VEGAS (KVVU/Gray News) — An investigation involving the Federal Bureau of Investigation has unveiled what officials are calling a “biological lab” in Las Vegas early Saturday morning.According to a release from the Las Vegas Metro Police Department, police discovered the lab during the search of a home on Sugar Springs Drive near Hollywood and Washington Avenue.There, investigators found evidence of “biological material” inside refrigerators with “vials containing unknown liquids.”The release said the police department’s ARMOR team worked with the FBI, local fire departments and other agencies to recover the items found.Clark County property records show the current resident of the home is tied to the discovery of a similar lab in California.The Department of Justice said the California lab was accused of importing hundreds of COVID-19 test kits from a Chinese company but falsely told buyers they were made in the United States and were FDA and CDC-approved. The Justice Department said the suspects are believed to have operated from August 2020 to March 2023 and made $1.7 million from the operation.According to a report from the U.S. Congressional Select Committee on the Chinese Communist Party, the facility contained thousands of vials that included pathogens like HIV, tuberculosis, malaria and hepatitis. A vial labeled “Ebola” was also found during cleanup.The report also noted that thousands of mice were kept in inhumane conditions and genetically modified to simulate human immune systems.Las Vegas police have not yet identified the suspects involved in Saturday’s discovery.An investigation into the lab remains ongoing.Copyright 2026 KVVU via Gray Local Media, Inc. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI搜查令引发拉斯维加斯住宅可能发现“生物实验室”\nLVMPD与FBI联合调查在东部山谷发现警方所称的“生物实验室”。（来源：KVVU）\n作者：Cody Lee、Arianna Schmidt、Rachel Zalucki及Gray News工作人员\n发布时间：2026年2月2日下午5:45（中部标准时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上设为首选来源\n拉斯维加斯（KVVU/Gray News）——周六清晨，一项涉及联邦调查局的调查在拉斯维加斯发现了官员所称的“生物实验室”。\n据拉斯维加斯大都会警察局发布的消息，警方在搜查Sugar Springs Drive、靠近Hollywood和Washington Avenue的一处住宅时发现了该实验室。\n调查人员在那里发现了“生物材料”证据，冰箱内有“装有未知液体的试管”。\n消息称，警察局ARMOR小组与FBI、当地消防部门及其他机构合作，回收了发现的物品。\n克拉克县房产记录显示，该住宅现住户与加州发现类似实验室的案件有关。\n司法部称，加州实验室被指从一家中国公司进口数百套新冠病毒检测试剂盒，却向买家虚假声称这些试剂盒在美国制造，并获得FDA和CDC批准。司法部表示，嫌疑人据信于2020年8月至2023年3月期间运营该项目，并从中获利170万美元。\n根据美国国会中国共产党问题特别委员会的一份报告，该设施内有数千个试管，包含艾滋病毒、结核病、疟疾和肝炎等病原体。清理期间还发现了一个贴有“埃博拉”标签的试管。\n报告还指出，数千只老鼠被关在不人道的条件下，并经过基因改造以模拟人体免疫系统。\n拉斯维加斯警方尚未确认周六发现事件涉及的嫌疑人身份。\n对该实验室的调查仍在进行中。\n版权所有2026 KVVU（经Gray Local Media, Inc.提供）。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kcrg.com","publish_time":"2026-02-02T23:45:57.021000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1107","ktid":1002550,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1002550","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿肯色州立大学发生枪击致多人受伤，调查正在进行","title_en":"Multiple injured in Arkansas State University shooting, investigation underway","summary_cn":"阿肯色州立大学发生夜间枪击事件，造成四人受伤，其中三人为该校学生。校方称午夜后接到枪击报警，事发地点为Unity Park，一人腿部中弹但无生命危险，其他人多为轻伤。校方表示不存在持续威胁，枪击为孤立事件，并向公众表达慰问。目前调查仍在进行中。","summary_en":"An overnight shooting at Arkansas State University left four people injured, including three students. The university said a 911 call about shots fired came just after midnight, and the incident occurred at Unity Park. One woman had a non-life-threatening gunshot wound to her lower leg, while others had minor injuries. Officials said there was no active threat and the shooting was isolated. The investigation is ongoing.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:52:07.208191+00:00","url":"https://www.kcrg.com/2026/04/26/multiple-injured-arkansas-state-university-shooting-investigation-underway/","content":"Multiple injured in Arkansas State University shooting, investigation underwayBy K8 Newsdesk and Brandy BeardPublished: Apr. 26, 2026 at 1:41 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleJONESBORO, Ark. (KAIT/Gray News) - An overnight shooting at Arkansas State University left four people injured.In a statement, the university said a 911 call was received just after midnight Sunday regarding shots fired in the area.Four people were injured, including three Arkansas State students. One student was treated at the scene, and three other people were taken to local hospitals with mostly minor conditions and are currently stable.Todd Clark, the university’s chief marketing and communications officer, said a gathering was underway at Unity Park. An email alert later notified the campus community of an “active shooter” incident.One woman was confirmed to have a non-life-threatening gunshot wound to her lower leg. Other reports indicated minor injuries, including scrapes and scratches, as the crowd dispersed.Clark said there was no active threat and that the shooting was isolated to Unity Park.The university also provided the following message to the public:We are grateful that no lives were lost in this incident. Our thoughts are with those who were injured and their families.Our strength as a university lies in our close-knit campus and the way we care for one another. We encourage everyone to stay connected and support each other in the days ahead.The investigation is ongoing.Copyright 2026 KAIT via Gray Local Media, Inc. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"阿肯色州立大学发生枪击事件，多人受伤，调查正在进行\n\nK8新闻编辑部和布兰迪·比尔德\n发布：2026年4月26日中部时间下午1:41\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n\n阿肯色州琼斯伯勒（KAIT/Gray News）——阿肯色州立大学发生的夜间枪击事件造成4人受伤。\n\n该大学在一份声明中说，周日午夜刚过，警方接到关于该区域发生枪击的911报警电话。\n\n4人受伤，其中包括3名阿肯色州立大学学生。一名学生在现场接受治疗，另外3人被送往当地医院，伤势大多轻微，目前情况稳定。\n\n该大学首席营销与传播官托德·克拉克说，Unity公园当时正在举行聚会。随后发给校园社区的一封电子邮件警报通知称发生了“活跃枪手”事件。\n\n经确认，一名女子小腿中弹，但伤势没有生命危险。其他报道显示还有轻微伤，包括人群疏散时造成的擦伤和划伤。\n\n克拉克说，目前没有持续的威胁，枪击事件仅发生在Unity公园。\n\n该大学还向公众发布了以下信息：\n\n我们很庆幸这起事件没有造成任何人员死亡。我们向伤者及其家人表示慰问。\n\n作为一所大学，我们的力量在于紧密团结的校园以及彼此关怀的方式。我们鼓励每个人保持联系，并在未来几天相互支持。\n\n调查仍在进行中。\n\n版权所有2026 KAIT，隶属Gray Local Media公司。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kcrg.com","publish_time":"2026-04-26T18:41:44.120000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-983","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"爱荷华州一名无家可归的怀孕寻求庇护者起诉国土安全部","title_en":"Homeless, pregnant asylum-seeker in Iowa sues Homeland Security","summary_cn":"据爱荷华资本快讯报道，得梅因一名怀孕且无家可归的寻求庇护者Dania Abdulrahman向美国爱荷华南区联邦地区法院起诉国土安全部及美国公民与移民服务局，指其未在法定30天内处理其庇护工作许可申请，已等待逾750天。诉状称她2016年自叙利亚合法入境，2024年离开寄养系统后申请工作许可，因无收入陷入住房与医疗困境，并援引行政程序法。被告尚未回应。","summary_en":"According to the Iowa Capital Dispatch, Dania Abdulrahman, a pregnant and homeless asylum-seeker in Des Moines, sued the U.S. Department of Homeland Security and U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services in the Southern District of Iowa, alleging they failed to decide her asylum-based work permit application within the statutory 30 days, leaving her waiting over 750 days. The suit says she entered legally from Syria in 2016, aged out of foster care in 2024, and lacks income, housing and medical care. The defendants have not yet responded.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:25:11.197254+00:00","url":"https://www.kcrg.com/2026/05/08/homeless-pregnant-asylum-seeker-iowa-sues-homeland-security","content":"Homeless, pregnant asylum-seeker in Iowa sues Homeland SecurityLawsuit: Woman has waited 750 days for permission to workA pregnant, homeless asylum-seeker in Des Moines is suing the U.S. Department of Homeland Security over its alleged failure to grant her authorization to work in the United States.(Pexels | MGN Image (Credit))By Clark KauffmanPublished: May 8, 2026 at 5:22 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleDES MOINES, Iowa (IOWA CAPITAL DISPATCH) - A pregnant, homeless asylum-seeker in Des Moines is suing the U.S. Department of Homeland Security over its alleged failure to grant her authorization to work in the United States.The lawsuit was filed by Dania Abdulrahman in U.S. District Court for the Southern District of Iowa against DHS and U.S. Customs and Immigration Services.Also named as defendants are Carrie M. Selby, the acting associate director for Service Center Operations within the customs and immigration office, and Markwayne Mullin, head of the Department of Homeland Security.According to the lawsuit, Abdulrahman entered the United States legally from Syria in 2016.  At the time, Abdulrahman was 10 years old and was accompanied by her family, which was seeking asylum in the United States.The lawsuit states Abdulrahman was placed in foster care in 2020 and then, in 2024, aged out of the foster care system at age 18. In April 2024, she applied for asylum-based work authorization, which would enable her to legally work for a living in the United States.The lawsuit alleges that although federal law requires U.S. Customs and Immigration Services to rule on such applications within 30 days, more than 750 days have now passed, and Abdulrahman is still waiting on a decision.“As a result, Ms. Abdulrahman is not legally allowed to accept employment,” her attorney, Katherine Melloy Goettel, told the court recently. “Without income, she has faced housing insecurity and has been unable to receive necessary medical care for herself and her unborn child.”“If she was lucky, she would find food somewhere in the streets of Des Moines. When she was unlucky, she would go hungry.”– Attorney Katherine Melloy GoettelSince aging out of foster care two years ago, Goettel said in court filings, Abdulrahman has been homeless. “If she was lucky, she would find food somewhere in the streets of Des Moines,” Goettel told the court. “When she was unlucky, she would go hungry.”Abdulrahman has not been to a dentist in years, Goettel said, and during her first 15 weeks of pregnancy saw a doctor only once, and that was during a visit to a hospital emergency room.The lawsuit claims Abdulrahman has contacted U.S. Customs and Immigration Services several times to inquire as to the status of her application but no action in the matter has been taken. Abdulrahman has also sought assistance from U.S. Sen. Charles Grassley of Iowa, although, the lawsuit claims, Grassley’s office has indicated that U.S. Customs and Immigration Services was of “no help whatsoever” in resolving the issue.The lawsuit alleges U.S. Customs and Immigration Services is in violation of the federal Administrative Procedures Act by failing to meet its statutory deadline for decisions on such matters and for forcing Abdulrahman to wait at least 25 times longer for a decision than what the law allows.Abdulrahman’s lawyer is asking the court to assume jurisdiction in the case, immediately grant the sought-after work authorization, and order the federal government to pay her attorney’s fees in the case.The defendants have yet to file a response to the lawsuit’s allegations.Copyright 2026 IOWA CAPITAL DISPATCH. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"爱荷华州无家可归的怀孕寻求庇护者起诉国土安全部\n诉讼：女子已等待750天，仍未获准工作\n得梅因一名怀孕、无家可归的寻求庇护者，因美国国土安全部被指未向她授予在美国工作的许可而起诉该部门。\n（Pexels | MGN Image（图片来源））\n作者：Clark Kauffman\n发布时间：2026年5月8日中部夏令时间下午5:22\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n爱荷华州得梅因（IOWA CAPITAL DISPATCH）——得梅因一名怀孕、无家可归的寻求庇护者，因美国国土安全部被指未向她授予在美国工作的许可而起诉该部门。\n该诉讼由Dania Abdulrahman在爱荷华州南区联邦地区法院提起，被告为国土安全部和美国海关与移民服务局。\n被列为被告的还有海关与移民办公室服务中心运营代理副主任Carrie M. Selby，以及国土安全部负责人Markwayne Mullin。\n根据诉讼，Abdulrahman于2016年从叙利亚合法进入美国。当时Abdulrahman年仅10岁，随其家人同行；其家人正在美国寻求庇护。\n诉讼称，Abdulrahman于2020年被安置进寄养家庭，随后于2024年在18岁时因年龄原因退出寄养制度。2024年4月，她申请了基于庇护身份的工作许可，这将使她能够合法在美国工作谋生。\n诉讼指称，尽管联邦法律要求美国海关与移民服务局在30天内就此类申请作出决定，如今已过去750多天，Abdulrahman仍在等待决定。\n“因此，Abdulrahman女士在法律上不得接受工作，”她的律师Katherine Melloy Goettel近日对法院表示。“由于没有收入，她面临住房不稳定，且无法为自己和未出生的孩子获得必要的医疗服务。”\n“如果幸运，她能在得梅因的街头某处找到食物。若不幸运，她就会挨饿。”\n——律师Katherine Melloy Goettel\nGoettel在法庭文件中称，自两年前因年龄原因退出寄养制度以来，Abdulrahman一直无家可归。“如果幸运，她能在得梅因的街头某处找到食物，”Goettel对法院表示。“若不幸运，她就会挨饿。”\nGoettel称，Abdulrahman已有多年未看牙医；在怀孕的头15周里，她只看过一次医生，还是在医院急诊室就诊期间。\n诉讼称，Abdulrahman曾多次联系美国海关与移民服务局，询问其申请的状态，但该事项未采取任何行动。Abdulrahman还寻求了爱荷华州联邦参议员Charles Grassley的协助，不过诉讼称，Grassley办公室表示，美国海关与移民服务局在解决该问题上“毫无帮助”。\n诉讼指称，美国海关与移民服务局未能遵守对这类事项作出决定的法定期限，且迫使Abdulrahman等待决定的时间至少是法律允许时间的25倍，因此违反了联邦《行政程序法》。\nAbdulrahman的律师请求法院受理该案，立即授予所寻求的工作许可，并命令联邦政府支付她在本案中的律师费。\n被告尚未就诉讼指控提交答复。\n版权所有2026 IOWA CAPITAL DISPATCH。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kcrg.com","publish_time":"2026-05-08T22:22:50.172000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-815","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI调查爱荷华汽车集团网络攻击事件","title_en":"FBI investigating cyberattack of Iowa Auto Group","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局正在调查针对Karl Auto Group的网络攻击。该集团是Karl Chevrolet的母公司，今年复活节前后遭攻击，客户的社会安全号码、姓名、金融账户信息和护照可能被泄露。公司已在网站发布通知并向受影响客户发送邮件，目前未发现客户信息被滥用的证据，建议客户开启金融机构通知等自我保护措施。","summary_en":"The FBI is investigating a cyberattack on Karl Auto Group, parent company of Karl Chevrolet, which occurred around Easter this year. Social security numbers, names, financial account information and passports of thousands of customers may have been compromised. The company posted notices on its website and emailed impacted customers, reporting no evidence of misuse so far, and recommends customers take protective steps such as enabling financial institution notifications.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:31:33.452074+00:00","url":"https://www.kcrg.com/2026/06/05/fbi-investigating-cyberattack-iowa-auto-group","content":"FBI investigating cyberattack of Iowa Auto GroupThe FBI is investigating a cyberattack on Karl Auto Group that may have compromised sensitive information for thousands of customers.(wafb)By KCCIPublished: Jun. 4, 2026 at 10:08 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleANKENY, Iowa (KCCI) - The FBI is investigating a cyberattack on Karl Auto Group that may have compromised sensitive information for thousands of customers, KCCI reports.Karl Auto Group, the parent company of Karl Chevrolet, experienced the cyberattack around Easter this year. The company said social security numbers, names, financial account information and passports may have been compromised.Karl Auto Group posted notices on its website and sent emails to impacted customers.The company has not reported any evidence of misuse of customer information. Karl Auto Group recommends customers take steps to protect themselves and their data, such as turning on notifications for their financial institutions.Copyright 2026 KCCI. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"联邦调查局调查爱荷华州汽车集团遭受的网络攻击。联邦调查局正在调查针对卡尔汽车集团的一起网络攻击，该攻击可能已泄露数千名客户的敏感信息。（wafb）\n作者：KCCI\n发布时间：2026年6月4日晚上10:08（中部夏令时）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上将我们添加为首选来源\n爱荷华州安克尼（KCCI）——KCCI报道，联邦调查局正在调查针对卡尔汽车集团的一起网络攻击，该攻击可能已泄露数千名客户的敏感信息。\n卡尔汽车集团是卡尔雪佛兰的母公司，今年复活节前后遭遇了这起网络攻击。该公司表示，社会保障号码、姓名、金融账户信息和护照信息可能已被泄露。\n卡尔汽车集团在其网站上发布了通知，并向受影响客户发送了电子邮件。\n该公司尚未报告任何客户信息遭滥用的证据。卡尔汽车集团建议客户采取措施保护自身及其数据，例如开启金融机构的通知。\n版权所有 © 2026 KCCI。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kcrg.com","publish_time":"2026-06-05T03:08:47.222000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-676","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI局长卡什·帕特尔会见爱荷华州执法部门","title_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel meets with Iowa law enforcement","summary_cn":"据爱荷华州总检察长办公室消息，FBI局长卡什·帕特尔周一上午在得梅因会见爱荷华州执法部门，与总检察长布伦娜·伯德进行炉边谈话，并与100多名地方和州执法人员及县检察官问答。会议不对公众和媒体开放。伯德称帕特尔讨论了国际欺诈和人口贩运等议题，FBI计划扩大对爱荷华州警员的培训机会。爱荷华州民主党主席批评此次会面。","summary_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel met with Iowa law enforcement Monday morning in Des Moines, according to the Iowa Attorney General's office. Patel and Attorney General Brenna Bird held a fireside chat and Q&A with over 100 local and state law enforcement officials and county attorneys. The meeting was closed to the public and media. Bird said Patel discussed international fraud and human trafficking, and the FBI plans to expand training opportunities for Iowa officers. The Iowa Democratic Party chair criticized the event.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:27:05.316948+00:00","url":"https://www.kcrg.com/2026/06/29/fbi-director-kash-patel-meets-with-iowa-law-enforcement","content":"FBI Director Kash Patel meets with Iowa law enforcementBy KCRG Staff and Isabella WarrenPublished: Jun. 29, 2026 at 1:44 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleDES MOINES, Iowa (Gray Media Iowa State Capitol Bureau) — FBI Director Kash Patel met with Iowa law enforcement Monday morning, according to a news release from the office of Iowa Attorney General Brenna Bird.The release stated that Patel and Bird had a “fireside chat” followed by a Q&A with more than 100 local and state law enforcement and county attorneys.The meeting was closed to the public and the media and Patel did not meet with reporters after the event. Patel shared on X after the event: “Iowa is ground zero for our work with partners in the most successful run of crime reduction in U.S. history - with major crime reductions across the state including a 30%+ drop in Des Moines homicides last year alone.”“I want to say thank you to Director Kash Patel for his partnership and work to support law enforcement and fight fraud, scams, human trafficking, and violent crime at the federal level,” Bird said in a statement. “Law enforcement continues to set records crushing violent crime, wiping out drug trafficking networks, and defending the homeland from threats abroad – and those victories are only possible with the men and women on the front lines working 24/7 in Iowa and beyond,\" Patel said in a statement. “I’m honored to join Attorney General Bird and our great partners in Iowa as we work together on our shared priorities and continue making America the safest we’ve been in generations.” Bird said Patel discussed several issues the FBI is working on with local law enforcement across the country, including international fraud and human trafficking. She said the FBI plans to expand training opportunities for Iowa officers to help investigate and stop both.“The FBI has opened up a number of training opportunities for officers, other ways that folks can be detailed out to the office for a few months so that the FBI can learn from local law enforcement what the needs are and build a partnership there,” Bird said. “They also have a national academy that many of our law enforcement leaders have graduated from.”The FBI already partners with Iowa law enforcement on cases that cross state lines. Bird said those partnerships have helped dismantle drug trafficking and human trafficking operations. She said Monday’s meeting focused on finding additional ways for federal, state, and local agencies to work together.“So we’re already working with our federal partners. But I think this meeting today showed us all some ways that we can continue to grow, train, and find more ways to work together,” Bird said.Bird, a Republican, is running for re-election in 2026. Nate Willems, an attorney from Mount Vernan, is the Democrats’ nominee for attorney general.In a response, Iowa Democratic Party Chair Rita Hart said the event was Bird “cozying up to the Trump administration.”“Patel has grossly mismanaged the FBI as its director, including using government resources for lavish personal trips, demanding political loyalty from staff, and prematurely revealing sensitive information on national security investigations,” she said in a statement. “Like Patel, Brenna Bird has been more focused on using her position and taxpayer dollars to push her own extreme political agenda instead of protecting Iowans.”Copyright 2026 KCRG. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI局长Kash Patel会见爱荷华州执法部门人员\n作者：KCRG Staff和Isabella Warren\n发布：2026年6月29日，中部夏令时间下午1:44\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n爱荷华州得梅因（Gray Media爱荷华州议会大厦新闻局）——根据爱荷华州总检察长Brenna Bird办公室发布的新闻稿，FBI局长Kash Patel于周一上午会见了爱荷华州执法部门人员。\n新闻稿称，Patel和Bird进行了“炉边谈话”，随后与100多名地方和州执法人员及县检察官进行了问答。\n此次会议不对公众和媒体开放，活动结束后Patel没有会见记者。Patel活动结束后在X上发文称：“爱荷华州是我们与合作伙伴开展工作的核心地带；在美国历史上最成功的一轮犯罪率下降期间，全州重大犯罪显著减少，仅得梅因去年凶杀案就下降了30%以上。”\nBird在一份声明中表示：“我要感谢FBI局长Kash Patel的合作，以及他在联邦层面支持执法部门、打击欺诈、骗局、人口贩运和暴力犯罪所做的工作。”\nPatel在一份声明中表示：“执法部门持续创下纪录，在打击暴力犯罪、摧毁毒品贩运网络以及保卫国土免受境外威胁方面取得成果——而这些胜利只有依靠爱荷华州及其他地区昼夜奋战在一线的男男女女才有可能实现。能与Bird总检察长及我们在爱荷华州出色的合作伙伴一道，围绕共同优先事项开展工作，并继续让美国成为几代人以来最安全的国家，我深感荣幸。”\nBird表示，Patel讨论了FBI正在与全国各地地方执法部门合作处理的若干问题，包括国际欺诈和人口贩运。她说，FBI计划扩大面向爱荷华州警员的培训机会，帮助调查和制止这两类犯罪。\nBird说：“FBI已经为警员开放了多种培训机会，也提供了其他途径，让相关人员可以被派往该办公室数月，以便FBI能从地方执法部门了解其需求，并在此基础上建立合作关系。他们还设有一所国家学院，我们许多执法部门领导人都从那里毕业。”\nFBI已经在跨州案件中与爱荷华州执法部门合作。Bird表示，这些合作关系帮助捣毁了毒品贩运和人口贩运行动。她说，周一的会议重点是寻找更多让联邦、州和地方机构协作的方式。\nBird说：“因此，我们已经在与联邦合作伙伴开展合作。但我认为，今天的会议向我们所有人展示了一些方式，让我们能够继续发展、培训，并找到更多协同工作的办法。”\n共和党人Bird正在竞选2026年连任。来自Mount Vernan的律师Nate Willems是民主党总检察长候选人。\n作为回应，爱荷华州民主党主席Rita Hart表示，该活动是Bird“与特朗普政府套近乎”。\n她在一份声明中说：“Patel作为FBI局长严重管理不善，包括将政府资源用于奢华的私人旅行、要求员工政治忠诚，以及过早披露有关国家安全调查的敏感信息。和Patel一样，Brenna Bird更专注于利用自己的职位和纳税人的钱来推动她自己的极端政治议程，而非保护爱荷华州民众。”\n版权所有2026 KCRG。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kcrg.com","publish_time":"2026-06-29T18:44:20.837000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-442","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"倡导组织称3人在锡达拉皮兹国土安全部办公室的ICE报到时被拘留","title_en":"3 detained at ICE check-ins at Cedar Rapids DHS office, advocacy group says","summary_cn":"据KCRG报道，倡导组织Escucha Mi Voz称，8月4日上午有3人在锡达拉皮兹国土安全部办公室进行移民报到时被拘留，其中包括来自萨尔瓦多、居住于西利伯蒂的Adela Margarita Angel Melendez，据称她等待其美国公民姐姐提交的居留申请聆讯已七年。报道称办公室外新设围栏限制无预约者靠近，ICE称此举因破坏行为，组织者则称安保日益军事化。此前一段警方将一名女性示威者摔倒在地的视频引发关注，警方内部审查认定使用武力符合培训。","summary_en":"KCRG reports that advocacy group Escucha Mi Voz said three people were detained at their immigration check-ins at the Cedar Rapids Department of Homeland Security office on Aug. 4, including Adela Margarita Angel Melendez, an immigrant from El Salvador living in West Liberty who had reportedly waited seven years for a residency petition filed by her U.S. citizen sister. A newly installed fence now blocks those without appointments; ICE cited vandalism, while organizers described increasingly military-style security. The report also notes a viral video of police taking a female demonstrator to the ground, which an internal review found consistent with training.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:56:24.539805+00:00","url":"https://www.kcrg.com/2026/08/04/2-detained-ice-check-ins-cedar-rapids-dhs-office-advocacy-group-says","content":"3 detained at ICE check-ins at Cedar Rapids DHS office, advocacy group saysBy Conner Woodruff and KCRG StaffPublished: Aug. 4, 2026 at 11:49 AM CDT|Updated: Aug. 4, 2026 at 1:30 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleCEDAR RAPIDS, Iowa (KCRG) - Advocacy group Escucha Mi Voz says three people were detained at their immigration check-ins at the Cedar Rapids Department of Homeland Security office Tuesday morning.One of those people was Adela Margarita Angel Melendez, an immigrant from El Salvador living in West Liberty. According to Escucha Mi Voz, she had been waiting seven years for the office to hear her residency petition filed by her sister, who is a U.S. citizen. The group was outside the office to support immigrants at their regular meetings with the department and said the three were detained after the crowd left. This was the first demonstration since a viral video showed Cedar Rapids Police slamming a woman to the ground outside of the DHS office. Police later released video showing that woman and another person blocking and appearing to spit on DHS vehicles before officers arrived.Changing Conditions and Physical BarriersThe atmosphere outside the office has shifted significantly over the past year. Most notably, a newly installed fence now blocks anyone without an appointment from approaching the entrance.“Certainly this fence that’s here is a new addition to the space,” said Reverend Jonathan Heifner, one of the lead organizers for the accompaniments.As recently as last year, advocates could walk directly into the building alongside those checking in. In a statement regarding the new security measures, ICE cited vandalism, stating, “If everyone respected the law and our property, measures like this wouldn’t be necessary.”However, Heifner noted that the security presence has felt increasingly military. “In the course of the last year, though, we’ve seen standing right over here, 5 or 6 ICE agents in tactical military gear,” he said.Escalating ConfrontationsTensions escalated dramatically last month during a confrontation captured in a viral social media video, which showed Cedar Rapids police officers taking a female demonstrator to the ground.Police body camera footage later showed a small group of protesters blocking, spitting on, and hitting DHS vehicles prior to the arrest. A demonstrator involved stated the group was only there to document vehicles.Following an internal review, the Cedar Rapids Police Department stated the officers’ use of force was consistent with department training.Heifner maintained that the core group of organizers remains committed to peaceful advocacy. “I don’t think that anybody that was body slammed or arrested out here was being violent. But we are intentionally focused—we’re disciplined around non-violence,” Heifner said. He added that while different groups may use different tactics, he believes they come from “a loving approach as well.”A Worthwhile EffortDespite the fences, tactical gear, and arrests, demonstrators say their presence is still vital to helping immigrants navigate a stressful process.For Lagunas and his brother, that support was realized Tuesday when they were finally able to reunite outside the office with a hug.“Every time someone walks out of that building, the crowd cheers,” Heifner said.This story has been updated with an additional reported detainment. Copyright 2026 KCRG. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"倡议团体称，3人在锡达拉皮兹国土安全部办公室进行ICE报到时被拘留\n作者：Conner Woodruff 和 KCRG Staff\n发布：2026年8月4日美国中部夏令时间上午11:49｜更新：2026年8月4日美国中部夏令时间下午1:30\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n将我们添加为Google上的首选来源\n爱荷华州锡达拉皮兹（KCRG）——倡议团体Escucha Mi Voz称，周二上午有3人在锡达拉皮兹国土安全部办公室进行移民报到时被拘留。\n其中一人是Adela Margarita Angel Melendez，她是一名居住在西自由市、来自萨尔瓦多的移民。根据Escucha Mi Voz的说法，她一直等待该办公室审理其由身为美国公民的姐姐提交的居留申请，至今已有7年。该团体在办公室外支持那些定期与该部门会面的移民，并表示这3人在群众离开后被拘留。这是自一段疯传视频显示锡达拉皮兹警察在国土安全部办公室外将一名女子猛摔在地后，举行的首次示威。警方后来发布的视频显示，在警员到达前，该女子和另一人曾阻挡国土安全部车辆，并似乎向车辆吐口水。\n变化的条件与物理障碍\n过去一年中，办公室外的氛围发生了显著变化。最明显的是，新安装的围栏如今阻止没有预约的人靠近入口。\n“当然，这里的围栏是这个空间新增的设施，”陪同活动的主要组织者之一Jonathan Heifner牧师说。\n就在去年，倡议人士还能与前来报到的人一起直接走进大楼。针对新的安全措施，ICE在一份声明中援引破坏行为，称：“如果每个人都尊重法律和我们的财产，就不会需要采取这样的措施。”\n不过，Heifner指出，安保力量越来越带有军事化色彩。“在过去一年里，我们看到就在这边站着5或6名身穿战术军事装备的ICE特工，”他说。\n不断升级的对峙\n上个月，一场被社交媒体疯传视频记录下来的对峙中，紧张局势急剧升级；视频显示锡达拉皮兹警察将一名女性示威者按倒在地。\n警方随后公布的随身摄像机画面显示，在逮捕发生前，一小群抗议者曾阻挡、吐向并击打国土安全部车辆。一名涉事示威者表示，该团体只是在那里记录车辆。\n经过内部审查后，锡达拉皮兹警察局表示，警员使用武力符合部门训练要求。\nHeifner坚持认为，核心组织者群体仍致力于和平倡议。“我不认为任何在这里被猛摔在地或被逮捕的人有暴力行为。但我们是有意聚焦于此——我们在非暴力方面有纪律，”Heifner说。他补充说，尽管不同团体可能采用不同策略，但他相信它们同样出自“充满关爱的方式”。\n一项值得的努力\n尽管有围栏、战术装备和逮捕，示威者表示，他们的存在对于帮助移民应对这一令人压力重重的程序仍然至关重要。\n对Lagunas和他的兄弟而言，这种支持在周二得以实现：他们终于能在办公室外拥抱重聚。\n“每当有人走出那栋大楼，人群都会欢呼，”Heifner说。\n本报道已更新，加入了另一起被报告的拘留事件。版权所有2026 KCRG。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kcrg.com","publish_time":"2026-08-04T16:49:07.972000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2435","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI搜寻据信在堪萨斯城的帮派打手","title_en":"FBI searches for wanted gang enforcer","summary_cn":"FBI正在搜寻一名可能藏身堪萨斯城的在逃暴力帮派打手。FBI斯普林菲尔德（伊利诺伊州）办事处发布公告，通缉22岁的Dontay R. Moore Jr.，据信他是伊利诺伊州南部Lundy Mob帮派的高层暴力打手，与暴力袭击、武器贩运和毒品分销有关。联邦逮捕令已于5月21日签发，FBI悬赏最高1.5万美元征集线索，并警告其可能持械且危险。","summary_en":"The FBI is searching for a wanted violent gang enforcer who may be in Kansas City. The FBI's Springfield, Illinois office issued a bulletin for Dontay R. Moore Jr., 22, believed to be a high-ranking violent enforcer for the Lundy Mob gang in southern Illinois, linked to violent attacks, weapons trafficking and narcotics distribution. A federal warrant was issued May 21. The FBI is offering up to $15,000 for information leading to his arrest and conviction, warning he should be considered armed and dangerous.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:48:05.835408+00:00","url":"https://www.kctv5.com/2025/09/05/fbi-searches-wanted-gang-enforcer-believed-be-kansas-city","content":"FBI searches for wanted gang enforcer believed to be in Kansas CityThe FBI is searching for a wanted and violent gang enforcer who may or may not be in Kansas City.By Sarah MotterPublished: Sep. 5, 2025 at 6:23 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleKANSAS CITY, Mo. (KCTV) - The FBI is searching for a wanted and violent gang enforcer who may or may not be in Kansas City. The Federal Bureau of Investigation says agents are hunting for a wanted fugitive who may or may not be in Kansas City. The FBI is seeking information about the whereabouts of Dontay R. Moore.(Federal Bureau of Investigation)A bulletin was posted by the FBI’s Office in Springfield, Illinois, for law enforcement officials to keep an eye out for Dontay R. Moore Jr., 22.Investigators said they believe Moore to be a high-ranking violent enforcer for the Lundy Mob - a gang with a presence in southern Illinois. The FBI is seeking information about the whereabouts of Dontay R. Moore.(Federal Bureau of Investigation)Law enforcement officials noted that Moore has been linked to violent attacks, weapons trafficking and narcotics distribution. A federal warrant was issued for his arrest on May 21. Detectives have described Moore as a Black man who stands at 5-foot-6, weighs 140 lbs., has black hair and brown eyes. He also has multiple tattoos, including a broken heart on the front of his neck and tattoos on both his left and right forearms. The FBI is seeking information about the whereabouts of Dontay R. Moore.(Federal Bureau of Investigation)Moore is known to go by several aliases - Dontay Remon Moore, Dontay R. Moore, Dontay Remon Moore, Jr., Deonta L. Cooper, Deonte L. Cooper. The FBI noted that a reward of up to $15,000 has been offered for information that leads to Moore’s arrest and conviction. He should be considered armed and dangerous.ALSO READ: Pair of bookkeepers federally charged after $900K stolen from Court’s accountAnyone with information about Moore’s whereabouts has been asked to report it ot to the FBI’s toll-free tipline at 1-800-CALL-FBI. No further information has been released. Copyright 2025 KCTV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI搜寻被通缉的帮派执法者，据信在堪萨斯城\nFBI正在搜寻一名被通缉且暴力的帮派执法者，此人可能在堪萨斯城，也可能不在。\n作者：Sarah Motter\n发布：2025年9月5日 CDT下午6:23\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n密苏里州堪萨斯城（KCTV）——FBI正在搜寻一名被通缉且暴力的帮派执法者，此人可能在堪萨斯城，也可能不在。联邦调查局表示，特工正在追捕一名被通缉的逃犯，此人可能在堪萨斯城，也可能不在。FBI正在寻求有关Dontay R. Moore下落的信息。\n（联邦调查局）\nFBI驻伊利诺伊州斯普林菲尔德办公室发布了一份通告，提醒执法官员留意22岁的Dontay R. Moore Jr.。\n调查人员表示，他们认为Moore是Lundy Mob的高层暴力执法者；该帮派在伊利诺伊州南部活动。FBI正在寻求有关Dontay R. Moore下落的信息。\n（联邦调查局）\n执法官员指出，Moore与暴力袭击、武器贩运和毒品分销有关。联邦法院于5月21日签发了逮捕令。侦探描述Moore为一名身高5英尺6英寸、体重140磅的黑人男子，黑发棕眼。他还有多处纹身，包括颈部正面的破碎心形纹身，以及左右前臂上的纹身。FBI正在寻求有关Dontay R. Moore下落的信息。\n（联邦调查局）\nMoore有多个别名——Dontay Remon Moore、Dontay R. Moore、Dontay Remon Moore, Jr.、Deonta L. Cooper、Deonte L. Cooper。FBI指出，提供能促成Moore被捕并定罪的信息，最高可获15,000美元奖励。他应被视为携带武器且具有危险性。\n另请阅读：两名簿记员因从法院账户盗取90万美元而被联邦起诉\n任何知晓Moore下落的人，都被要求向FBI免费举报热线1-800-CALL-FBI报告。没有发布更多信息。版权所有2025 KCTV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kctv5.com","publish_time":"2025-09-05T23:23:14.872000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2045","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"参议员邀请FBI局长访问堪萨斯城以遏制犯罪","title_en":"Kansas City crime concerns could see attention from FBI","summary_cn":"美国参议员埃里克·施密特致信联邦调查局（FBI）局长卡什·帕特尔，邀请其访问堪萨斯城，商讨减少该地区暴力犯罪的策略。此前两人曾访问圣路易斯，FBI在该市增派了全职探员和情报人员。帕特尔已于5月批准将33个FBI岗位从华盛顿迁至堪萨斯城办事处。施密特还提到明年在堪萨斯城举办的FIFA世界杯及当地逾200万人口，呼吁加强联邦人员配置与协调行动。","summary_en":"U.S. Senator Eric Schmitt invited FBI Director Kash Patel to visit Kansas City to develop strategies to reduce violent crime in the region. The invitation follows their earlier trip to St. Louis, where the FBI added full-time agents and intelligence personnel. Patel had already approved relocating 33 FBI positions from Washington, D.C., to the Kansas City Field Office in May. Schmitt cited next year's FIFA World Cup in Kansas City and the metro area's population of over 2 million, calling for increased federal staffing and coordinated operations.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:28:22.055222+00:00","url":"https://www.kctv5.com/2025/11/26/senator-asks-fbi-director-visit-kansas-city-curb-crime","content":"Senator asks FBI director to visit Kansas City to curb crimeSen. Schmitt invites FBI Director to Kansas CityBy Heidi SchmidtPublished: Nov. 26, 2025 at 1:51 PM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleKANSAS CITY, Mo. (KCTV) - U.S. Senator Eric Schmitt invited FBI Director Kash Patel to visit Kansas City in hopes of creating strategies to reduce crime in the region.It comes after Patel and Schmitt made a trip to St. Louis earlier this month. The stop highlighted the number of full-time agents added to the FBI’s St. Louis field office. Schmitt also said the hirings have the office at its highest number of employees in years. “The FBI’s permanent infusion of full-time agents and intelligence personnel to the St. Louis Field Office, one of the largest per-capita increases in the nation, will be instrumental in promoting law and order in the area,” Schmitt wrote in a letter to Patel. He went on to write that St. Louis is already seeing violent crime drop in the city.ALSO READ: Mediation ends in Jackson County class action lawsuit, filing says county still defies STC orderSchmitt asked Patel to bring the same effort to Kansas City.Patel already approved relocating 33 FBI jobs from Washington, D.C., to the FBI’s Kansas City Field Office in May. Schmitt’s invitation includes a tour of the Kansas City field office and meetings with regional partners to address concerns and next steps to make Kansas City safer.Schmitt pointed to next year’s FIFA World Cup in Kansas City and the fact that the metro is home to more than 2 million people.“They deserve to live in a community free from the blight of unchecked violent crime,” Schmitt wrote.ALSO READ: 'Nothing like it': Plaza lights ceremony returns for century-old Kansas City holiday traditionSchmitt included ideas about future collaborative efforts including:Multilateral crime-fighting effortsBuild on recent momentumSchmitt wrote that be believes increased federal staffing and coordinated operations are necessary to drive down violent crime in Missouri’s largest cities, including Kansas City. ALSO READ: Court records: Woman stomped unconscious victim before fatal downtown shootingThe senator and FBI officials are expected to continue joint outreach to local law enforcement leaders as policing strategies are refined ahead of major events like the World Cup and in response to ongoing community safety concerns.Copyright 2025 KCTV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"参议员要求联邦调查局局长访问堪萨斯城，以遏制犯罪\n施密特参议员邀请联邦调查局局长访问堪萨斯城\n作者：海蒂·施密特\n发布时间：2025年11月26日下午1:51（中部标准时间）\n分享\n将我们添加到 Google\n在 Google 上添加为首选来源\n密苏里州堪萨斯城（KCTV）——美国参议员埃里克·施密特邀请联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔访问堪萨斯城，希望制定减少该地区犯罪的策略。\n此前，本月早些时候帕特尔和施密特曾前往圣路易斯。此行重点介绍了联邦调查局圣路易斯外勤办公室新增的全职特工人数。施密特还表示，此次招聘使该办公室的员工人数达到多年来的最高水平。施密特在给帕特尔的信中写道：“联邦调查局向圣路易斯外勤办公室永久增派全职特工和情报人员，这是全美人均增幅最大的地区之一，将在促进该地区法律与秩序方面发挥重要作用。”他还写道，圣路易斯市的暴力犯罪已经开始下降。\n另请阅读：调解结束杰克逊县集体诉讼，文件称该县仍无视 STC 命令\n施密特要求帕特尔将同样的努力带到堪萨斯城。\n帕特尔已于5月批准将联邦调查局在华盛顿特区的33个职位迁至联邦调查局堪萨斯城外勤办公室。施密特的邀请包括参观堪萨斯城外勤办公室，并与地区合作伙伴会面，以解决相关担忧并讨论让堪萨斯城更加安全的后续措施。\n施密特指出，明年国际足联世界杯将在堪萨斯城举行，而且该都会区有超过200万人口。\n施密特写道：“他们理应生活在一个不受失控暴力犯罪祸害的社区中。”\n另请阅读：“无与伦比”：广场灯光仪式回归，延续有百年历史的堪萨斯城节日传统\n施密特提出了未来开展合作的想法，包括：\n多边打击犯罪行动\n巩固近期势头\n施密特写道，他认为，增加联邦人员配置并开展协调行动，对于降低密苏里州最大城市（包括堪萨斯城）的暴力犯罪是必要的。\n另请阅读：法院记录：女子将受害者踩踏至昏迷，随后发生市中心致命枪击事件\n随着警方策略不断完善，以应对世界杯等重大活动以及持续存在的社区安全担忧，预计这位参议员和联邦调查局官员将继续共同联系当地执法部门领导人。\n版权所有 2025 KCTV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kctv5.com","publish_time":"2025-11-26T19:51:07.585000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1188","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI、堪萨斯城警方与检察官通报在逃嫌犯案进展","title_en":"FBI, KCPD, prosecutor to announce update in active fugitive case","summary_cn":"据KCTV5报道，联邦调查人员与地方检察官4月14日宣布，堪萨斯城女子KaShawn Nicola Roper因2020年8月23日枪杀23岁Jazmyn Henrion被列入FBI十大通缉犯名单，悬赏100万美元。警方称Roper向一辆载人车辆开枪致一死一伤，2020年9月被控二级谋杀、非法使用武器及两项持械犯罪，2021年联邦逮捕令签发。FBI称案件仍是优先事项，检方表示一旦抓获即起诉。","summary_en":"KCTV5 reports that federal investigators and local prosecutors announced on April 14 that KaShawn Nicola Roper, a Kansas City woman wanted in the Aug. 23, 2020 shooting death of 23-year-old Jazmyn Henrion, has been added to the FBI's Ten Most Wanted list with a $1 million reward. Police say Roper fired into an occupied vehicle, killing one and wounding another; she was charged in September 2020 with second-degree murder, unlawful use of a weapon and two counts of armed criminal action, and a federal arrest warrant was issued in 2021. The FBI says the case remains a priority, and prosecutors say they will pursue charges once she is apprehended.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:33:03.076723+00:00","url":"https://www.kctv5.com/2026/04/14/fbi-kcpd-prosecutor-announce-update-active-fugitive-case","content":"Kansas City murder suspect added to FBI’s 10 Most Wanted - $1M reward offeredA Kansas City woman wanted in a 2020 murder is now on the FBI’s 10 Most Wanted list, with a $1 million reward offered.By Sarah Motter and Grace Smith (KCTV5)Published: Apr. 14, 2026 at 9:26 AM CDT|Updated: Apr. 14, 2026 at 10:00 AM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleKANSAS CITY, Mo. (KCTV) - A Kansas City woman wanted in a 2020 murder is now on the FBI’s 10 Most Wanted list, with a $1 million reward offered. Federal investigators and local prosecutors made the announcement on Tuesday morning, April 14, naming KaShawn Nicola Roper, 50, as the fugitive.The CrimeThe Kansas City Police Department says Roper is wanted in connection with the shooting death of 23-year-old Jazmyn Henrion near 68th and Cleveland Ave. on Aug. 23, 2020. ALSO READ: Man charged after shooting Kansas City tow truck driverPolice Chief Stacy Graves notes that officers were called to a local hospital around 3:35 a.m. that morning, after two gunshot victims arrived. Investigators say they believe Roper fired a gun into an occupied vehicle, striking both victims. Henrion died as a result. A second victim survived the incident. Eighteen days later, on Sept. 10, 2020, Graves indicates that the Jackson County Prosecutor’s Office charged Roper with: Second-degree murderUnlawful use of a weaponTwo counts of armed criminal action KaShawn N. Roper, 50(Federal Bureau of Investigation)The FugitiveInvestigators say Roper fled immediately after the shooting and has actively evaded law enforcement ever since - fully aware that she is wanted. In 2021, FBI special agent Jeff Berkebile notes that a federal arrest warrant was issued for unlawful flight to avoid prosecution. Roper is described as: Black female, 50 years old5-foot-5, approximately 120 lbs. Brown hair, brown eyesMultiple tattoos on her arms, calves, neck and abdomenREAD MORE: Man charged with murder after admitting to downtown Kansas City stabbingFederal investigators say Roper previously lived in Kansas City and has ties to Kansas, Nebraska, Texas, Colorado, Georgia and South Dakota. What Authorities Are SayingThe FBI says the case remains a top priority. “The FBI never forgets,” Berkebile adds. “We will leave no stone unturned in our pursuit of justice for victims of violent crime.”KaShawn N. Roper, 50(Federal Bureau of Investigation)Graves says officers have never stopped working the case. “Today, here in 2026, we are still actively pursuing the arrest of KaShawn Nicola Roper and remain committed to bringing her into custody,” Graves adds. Graves notes that KCPD conducts weekly reviews with local partners on cases like this and will continue to pursue justice regardless of how much time has passed.Jackson County Prosecutor Melesa Johnson says the victims deserved better. “Her life had value, and it was taken from her in an instant of senseless violence,” Johnson adds. Since the Ten Most Wanted program began in 1950, 541 fugitives have appeared on the list. Of those, 501 have been apprehended or located, a success rate of 93%. In 163 cases, a tip from a member of the public made the difference.Jackson County Prosecutor Melesa Johnson(KCTV5)Johnson said her office stands ready to prosecute Roper the moment she is apprehended.“Running is a choice, and that choice has consequences,” Johnson said.How to HelpIf you have information about Roper’s whereabouts, call the FBI at 1-800-CALL-FBI. Jeff Berkebile, acting special agent in charge of the FBI's Kansas City Field Office(KCTV5)A $1 million reward is being offered for information leading to her arrest and conviction. Copyright 2026 KCTV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"堪萨斯城谋杀案嫌疑人被列入联邦调查局十大通缉名单——悬赏100万美元\n一名因涉嫌2020年谋杀案而被通缉的堪萨斯城女子现已被列入联邦调查局十大通缉名单，悬赏100万美元。\nSarah Motter和Grace Smith（KCTV5）\n发布：2026年4月14日，美国中部时间上午9:26｜更新：2026年4月14日，美国中部时间上午10:00\n分享\n在Google上关注我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n密苏里州堪萨斯城（KCTV）——一名因涉嫌2020年谋杀案而被通缉的堪萨斯城女子现已被列入联邦调查局十大通缉名单，悬赏100万美元。联邦调查人员和当地检察官于4月14日星期二上午宣布，50岁的KaShawn Nicola Roper为逃犯。\n案件\n堪萨斯城警察局表示，Roper因涉嫌在2020年8月23日于68街和Cleveland大道附近枪杀23岁的Jazmyn Henrion而被通缉。\n另请阅读：男子在枪击堪萨斯城拖车司机后被起诉\n警察局长Stacy Graves说，当天凌晨3:35左右，警方接到通知，两名枪伤受害者被送到当地医院。调查人员称，他们认为Roper向一辆载有人员的车辆开枪，击中两名受害者。Henrion因此死亡。第二名受害者在事件中幸存。\nGraves表示，18天后的2020年9月10日，杰克逊县检察官办公室以以下罪名起诉Roper：\n二级谋杀\n非法使用武器\n两项持械犯罪行为\nKaShawn N. Roper，50岁\n（联邦调查局）\n逃犯\n调查人员称，Roper在枪击案发生后立即逃跑，此后一直积极躲避执法部门，并且完全知道自己已被通缉。联邦调查局特工Jeff Berkebile表示，2021年曾针对她签发一份因非法逃逸以逃避起诉的联邦逮捕令。\nRoper的描述如下：\n黑人女性，50岁\n身高5英尺5英寸，体重约120磅\n棕色头发，棕色眼睛\n手臂、小腿、颈部和腹部有多处纹身\n阅读更多：男子承认在堪萨斯城市中心持刀伤人后被控谋杀\n联邦调查人员称，Roper此前居住在堪萨斯城，并与堪萨斯州、内布拉斯加州、得克萨斯州、科罗拉多州、佐治亚州和南达科他州有联系。\n当局说法\n联邦调查局表示，此案仍是首要任务。“联邦调查局永远不会忘记，”Berkebile补充说。“为了给暴力犯罪受害者伸张正义，我们不会放过任何线索。”\nKaShawn N. Roper，50岁\n（联邦调查局）\nGraves说，警员从未停止办理此案。“今天，在2026年，我们仍在积极追捕KaShawn Nicola Roper，并继续致力于将她缉拿归案，”Graves补充说。Graves指出，KCPD每周都会与当地合作伙伴复查此类案件，无论过去多久，都将继续追求正义。\n杰克逊县检察官Melesa Johnson说，受害者本应得到更好的结果。“她的生命有价值，却在一场毫无意义的暴力中瞬间被夺走，”Johnson补充说。\n自十大通缉计划于1950年启动以来，共有541名逃犯上榜。其中501人已被逮捕或找到，成功率为93%。在163起案件中，公众提供的线索发挥了关键作用。\n杰克逊县检察官Melesa Johnson\n（KCTV5）\nJohnson表示，她的办公室已准备好在Roper被捕后立即起诉她。\n“逃跑是一个选择，而这个选择会带来后果，”Johnson说。\n如何提供帮助\n如果你知道Roper的下落，请致电联邦调查局：1-800-CALL-FBI。\nJeff Berkebile，联邦调查局堪萨斯城外勤办事处代理负责人\n（KCTV5）\n现悬赏100万美元，征集能够促成她被捕并定罪的信息。\n版权所有2026年KCTV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kctv5.com","publish_time":"2026-04-14T14:26:37.995000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-980","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部长马林批评克利弗并呼吁增加ICE和CBP拨款","title_en":"DHS Secretary Mullin calls out Cleaver while urging more ICE, CBP funding","summary_cn":"据KCTV5报道，美国国土安全部长马林5月9日在堪萨斯城国际机场与密苏里州共和党众议员马克·阿尔福德共同发声，推动国会为海关与边境保护局及移民和海关执法局提供多年期充足拨款。两人将协议未达成归咎于民主党。马林在记者会上点名密苏里州众议员伊曼纽尔·克利弗，称其“丧失了道德指南针”。克利弗此前批评本届政府的大规模驱逐议程鲁莽且极端。","summary_en":"DHS Secretary Mullin was in Kansas City on May 9 to push for more funding for the Department of Homeland Security, speaking with Republican U.S. Rep. Mark Alford at Kansas City International Airport, KCTV5 reported. Both urged Congress to fully fund Customs and Border Protection and Immigration and Customs Enforcement on a multi-year basis, blaming Democrats for the lack of a deal. Mullin called out Missouri Congressman Emanuel Cleaver, saying he had \"lost his moral compass.\" Cleaver has called the administration's mass deportation agenda reckless and extreme.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:01:55.804200+00:00","url":"https://www.kctv5.com/2026/05/10/dhs-secretary-mullin-calls-out-cleaver-while-urging-more-ice-cbp-funding","content":"DHS Secretary Mullin calls out Cleaver while urging more ICE, CBP fundingDHS Secretary Mullin calls out Cleaver while urging more ICE, CBP fundingBy KCTV5 StaffPublished: May 9, 2026 at 10:18 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleKANSAS CITY, Mo. (KCTV) - DHS Secretary Mullin was in Kansas City on Saturday to push to bring more funding to the Department of Homeland Security.Mullin and U.S. Rep. Mark Alford spoke (R-Missouri) at Kansas City International Airport.. They are both pushing for Congress to fully fund U.S. Customs and Border Protections along with Immigration and Customs Enforcement.They want the plan to before the next three years. The two pushed blame toward Democrats for the deal not being made.“So now is the time for the House and Senate Republicans to unite with the Trump Administration to pass a multi-year funding through reconciliation and give ICE, give CBP the certainty, the resources that they need to protect our nation, to protect everyone in this room, and to protect everyone watching this,” Rep. Alford said.Secretary Mullins called out Missouri Congressman Emanuel Cleaver during Saturday’s press conference, saying he has, quote, “lost his moral compass.”Cleaver has called this administration’s mass deportation agenda reckless and extreme.Copyright 2026 KCTV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"国土安全部部长Mullin呼吁增加ICE、CBP拨款时点名Cleaver\n国土安全部部长Mullin呼吁增加ICE、CBP拨款时点名Cleaver\nKCTV5工作人员\n发布时间：2026年5月9日中部夏令时间晚上10:18\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n密苏里州堪萨斯城（KCTV）——国土安全部部长Mullin周六来到堪萨斯城，推动为国土安全部争取更多资金。\nMullin和美国众议员Mark Alford（共和党—密苏里州）在堪萨斯城国际机场发表讲话。他们都在推动国会为美国海关与边境保护局以及移民及海关执法局提供全额资金。\n他们希望该计划持续未来三年。两人将未能达成协议归咎于民主党人。\n“所以现在正是众议院和参议院共和党人与特朗普政府团结起来，通过预算协调程序批准多年期拨款的时候了，让ICE、让CBP获得保护我们国家、保护在座每个人以及保护每一位观看者所需的确定性和资源，”Alford议员说。\nMullins部长在周六的新闻发布会上点名密苏里州国会议员Emanuel Cleaver，称他“已经失去了道德指南针”。\nCleaver曾称本届政府的大规模驱逐议程鲁莽且极端。\n版权2026 KCTV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kctv5.com","publish_time":"2026-05-10T03:18:35.438000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3024","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI表彰在肯特协助阻止绑架案的三名少女","title_en":"FBI honors teen girls who helped stop abduction in Kent | Kent Reporter","summary_cn":"据Kent Reporter报道，FBI西雅图分局暴力侵害儿童犯罪小组于3月17日当周向三名少女颁发FBI局长证书，表彰她们2024年7月在肯特一处公寓楼停车场阻止一名6岁女孩被绑架的勇敢行为。西雅图FBI主管特工维耶诺称，三人观察敏锐、反应迅速，不仅救下女孩，还协助警方锁定嫌疑人并促成定罪。嫌疑人阿尔布-穆罕默德于2024年12月认罪，被判缓刑及24个月监管等。","summary_en":"FBI Seattle's Violent Crimes Against Children squad recognized three teen girls the week of March 17 with certificates from the FBI director for preventing the July 2024 abduction of a 6-year-old girl at a Kent apartment complex, the Kent Reporter said. Supervisory Special Agent Steve Vienneau said their keen observation and quick action saved the girl and helped convict the offender. Hayder Hasan Albu-Mohammed pleaded guilty to attempted luring in December 2024 and received a suspended sentence, 24 months of probation and other conditions.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:17:28.738842+00:00","url":"https://www.kentreporter.com/2025/03/26/fbi-honors-teen-girls-who-helped-stop-abduction-in-kent","content":"FBI honors teen girls who helped stop abduction in Kent\nPublished 3:18 pm Wednesday, March 26, 2025\nBy Steve Hunter shunter@soundpublishing.com\n1/2\nSwipe or click to see more\n2/2\nSwipe or click to see more\nSteve Vienneau, a Seattle FBI supervisory special agent, prepares to give out certificates to three girls who helped stopped the abduction of a 6-year-old girl in July 2024 at a Kent apartment complex. SCREENSHOT/FBI video\nGetting your Trinity Audio player ready...\nThe honors and recognition continue for three teen girls who helped prevent an abduction of a 6-year-old girl in July 2024 at a Kent apartment complex.\nFBI Seattle’s Violent Crimes Against Children squad recognized the three girls the week of March 17 with certificates from the FBI director for their bravery in preventing the abduction, according to a FBI Seattle video post on X, formerly known as Twitter.\nBentley Hendrickson, Esme Munguia and Kylie Love received the certificates from Steve Vienneau, a Seattle FBI supervisory special agent. The girls received the Kent Police Chief’s Award for Citizen Commendation at a Sept. 17, 2024 City Council meeting. 0\n“As a result of their keen observation, quick thinking and decisive action, they prevented the abduction of a 6-year-old girl and aided in the conviction of the offender,” Vienneau said as he read a letter he wrote to the FBI director for the certificates. “Their bravery and selflessness bring honor to each of them, to their families and to their community.”\nChildren had gathered in the parking lot July 16, 2024 of the Meridian Glen Apartments, 11305 SE Kent-Kangley Road, as an ice cream truck arrived. The three girls were in the parking lot.\n“They saw something that didn’t look right,” Vienneau said. “They saw a man holding the wrist of their 6-year-old neighbor who appeared frightened and trying to break free. Without hesitation they took action walking toward the man. They challenged him as to whether he was related to the girl.”\nVienneau said the girls, thinking quickly, recorded some of the interaction on video, which they later provided to Kent Police.\n“The man said he was related to the girl, but the girl shook her head,” Vienneau said. “They took the girl by the hand and led her away. After getting the girl home safely, they flagged down responding officers and led them to the suspect.”\nHayder Hasan Albu-Mohammed, 40 at the time of the crime, pleaded guilty to attempted luring on Dec. 16, 2024, according to King County Superior Court documents. Prosecutors initially charged him July 19, 2024 with second-degree attempted kidnapping. He pleaded not guilty Aug. 1, 2024 to the kidnapping charge.\n“I attempted to lure a minor under the age of 16 into an area of the parking lot that was obscured from public without consent of the parent and I was unknown to the minor,” Albu-Mohammed wrote in his plea of guilty court documents. “My actions of taking the minor by the hand and later picking her up constituted a substantial step toward the crime of luring.”\nKing County Superior Court Judge Mark Larrañaga on Dec. 20, 2024 gave Albu-Mohammed credit for 158 days in jail and a 364-day suspended sentence, according to the King County Prosecuting Attorney’s Office. He was released Dec. 20, 2024 from the county jail, according to jail records.\nThe judge ordered 24 months of probation, no contact with the victim, and that Albu-Mohammed get evaluations for substance abuse and alcohol abuse and that he successfully complete programs for substance and alcohol abuse.\nThe judge also ordered him to have no contact with minors “except under supervision of (a) responsible adult aware of this order, and with permission of CCO [state Department of Corrections community corrections officer] and treatment provider and comply with all conditions required by the judgement and sentence.”\nThe judge ordered Albu-Mohammed not to live at the Meridian Green Apartments in Kent.\nYou Might Like\nNews\nProposed bill to honor Covington’s Savino; crew killed in Iraq\nSports\nKent Reporter Athletes of the Week: Kentwood\nNews\nSouthbound I-405 closures with Renton detour| Sept. 25-28\nNews\nYou’re never too late for school: GRC celebrates 30 years in Enumclaw\nSections\nNews\nBusiness\nSports\nLife\nObituaries\nOpinion\nWeather\nServices\neEditions\nNewsletters\nClassifieds\nSubmission Forms\nOur Company\nAbout Us\nContact Us\nOur Partners\n© 2026 Kent Reporter.\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms of Service","content_cn":"FBI表彰帮助阻止肯特市绑架案的少女\n发布于2025年3月26日星期三下午3:18\n作者：Steve Hunter shunter@soundpublishing.com\n1/2\n滑动或点击查看更多\n2/2\n滑动或点击查看更多\n西雅图FBI监督特别探员Steve Vienneau准备向三名女孩颁发证书，她们曾于2024年7月在肯特一处公寓楼帮助阻止一名6岁女孩被绑架。截图/FBI视频\n正在准备您的Trinity Audio播放器……\n三名少女帮助阻止一名6岁女孩于2024年7月在肯特一处公寓楼遭绑架，她们持续获得表彰和认可。\n据西雅图FBI在X（原名Twitter）发布的视频，西雅图FBI“针对儿童的暴力犯罪”小组在3月17日当周向三名女孩颁发了FBI局长签署的证书，以表彰她们阻止绑架行为的英勇表现。\nBentley Hendrickson、Esme Munguia和Kylie Love从西雅图FBI监督特别探员Steve Vienneau手中接过证书。2024年9月17日的市议会会议上，三名女孩获得了肯特警察局长公民嘉奖奖。 0\n“由于她们敏锐的观察、快速的思考和果断的行动，她们阻止了一名6岁女孩被绑架，并协助将犯罪者定罪，”Vienneau在宣读他写给FBI局长、用于申请颁发证书的一封信时说。“她们的勇敢和无私为她们每个人、她们的家人以及她们的社区带来了荣誉。”\n2024年7月16日，冰淇淋车抵达Meridian Glen公寓（地址为11305 SE Kent-Kangley Road）时，孩子们聚集在停车场。三名女孩当时就在停车场。\n“她们看到了一些不对劲的事情，”Vienneau说。“她们看到一名男子抓着邻家6岁女孩的手腕，那名女孩看起来很害怕，正试图挣脱。她们毫不犹豫地采取行动，朝那名男子走去。她们质问他是否与女孩有亲属关系。”\nVienneau说，女孩们迅速作出反应，用视频记录了部分互动，之后将视频交给了肯特警方。\n“那名男子说他与女孩有亲属关系，但女孩摇了摇头，”Vienneau说。“她们牵起女孩的手，把她带走。将女孩安全送回家后，她们拦下赶到现场的警员，并带他们找到嫌疑人。”\n据金县高等法院文件，案发时40岁的Hayder Hasan Albu-Mohammed于2024年12月16日对企图诱骗罪认罪。检方最初于2024年7月19日以二级绑架未遂罪起诉他。2024年8月1日，他对绑架指控不认罪。\n“未经家长同意，我试图诱骗一名未满16岁的未成年人进入停车场一个被公众视线遮挡的区域，而我对该未成年人来说是陌生人，”Albu-Mohammed在认罪法庭文件中写道。“我牵住未成年人的手，后来又把她抱起来，这些行为构成了实施诱骗犯罪的实质性步骤。”\n据金县检察官办公室称，金县高等法院法官Mark Larrañaga于2024年12月20日判处Albu-Mohammed折抵158天监禁，并处以364天缓刑。他于2024年12月20日从县监狱获释，据监狱记录显示。\n法官下令对其进行24个月的缓刑监督，不得与受害者接触，并要求Albu-Mohammed接受药物滥用和酒精滥用评估，并成功完成相关项目\n因药物和酒精滥用。\n法官还命令他不得与未成年人接触，“除非在知悉该命令的负责任成年人的监督下，并获得CCO［州惩教部社区矫正官］和治疗提供者的许可，且遵守判决和量刑所要求的所有条件。”\n法官命令Albu-Mohammed不得居住在肯特的Meridian Green公寓。\n你可能喜欢\n新闻\n拟议法案拟纪念科温顿的萨维诺；在伊拉克遇难的机组人员\n体育\n《肯特报道》本周最佳运动员：Kentwood\n新闻\nI-405州际公路南行封闭，伦顿绕行｜9月25日至28日\n新闻\n上学永远不会太晚：GRC庆祝在Enumclaw成立30周年\n栏目\n新闻\n商业\n体育\n生活\n讣告\n观点\n天气\n服务\n电子版\n新闻通讯\n分类信息\n投稿表格\n关于本公司\n关于我们\n联系我们\n我们的合作伙伴\n© 2026 Kent Reporter。\n隐私政策\n服务条款","publish_source":"kentreporter.com","publish_time":"2025-03-26T22:18:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1910","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"曼凯托市称国土安全部特工正在该市活动","title_en":"City of Mankato says Department of Homeland Security agents working in city","summary_cn":"明尼苏达州曼凯托市公共安全部门表示，已接到通知称美国国土安全部（DHS）特工正在曼凯托市内活动，这些特工出示了有效的执法证件。该市公共安全部门称不了解其活动性质、调查范围及停留时间，也未参与或协助任何行动，并建议民众如有疑问可拨打911核实自称执法人员者的身份。","summary_en":"Mankato Public Safety in Minnesota said it was notified that U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) agents are operating in Mankato and have presented valid law enforcement credentials. The city said it is unaware of the nature of their activities, the scope of any potential investigation, or how long DHS will remain, and is not participating in or assisting with any operation. Residents with questions about individuals claiming to be law enforcement are encouraged to call 911 to verify their identity.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:51:25.754465+00:00","url":"https://www.keyc.com/2025/12/26/city-mankato-says-department-homeland-security-agents-working-city","content":"City of Mankato says Department of Homeland Security agents working in cityBy KEYC News Now StaffPublished: Dec. 26, 2025 at 5:55 PM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleMANKATO, Minn. (KEYC) - Agents with the Department of Homeland Security are now operating in Mankato.Mankato Public Safety has been notified that agents with the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) are working in Mankato. The agents have presented valid law enforcement credentials.Mankato Public Safety is not aware of the specific nature of their activities and is not participating in or assisting with any operation. The city said Public Safety is also not aware of the scope of any potential investigation or how long DHS will be in Mankato. Mankato Public Safety says if you have questions regarding the authority of individuals claiming to be law enforcement, you are encouraged to contact 911 to verify their identity. Click here to download the KEYC News Now app or our KEYC First Alert weather app.Copyright 2025 KEYC. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"曼凯托市称国土安全部特工正在市内开展工作\nKEYC News Now工作人员\n发布时间：2025年12月26日，中部标准时间下午5:55\n分享\n将我们添加到Google\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n明尼苏达州曼凯托（KEYC）——国土安全部特工目前正在曼凯托开展行动。\n曼凯托公共安全部门已获悉，美国国土安全部（DHS）的特工正在曼凯托工作。这些特工出示了有效的执法证件。\n曼凯托公共安全部门不了解其活动的具体性质，也未参与或协助任何行动。该市表示，公共安全部门也不知道任何潜在调查的范围或国土安全部将在曼凯托停留多久。曼凯托公共安全部门表示，如果你对自称执法人员的个人的权限有疑问，建议拨打911核实其身份。点击此处下载KEYC News Now应用或KEYC First Alert天气应用。\n版权所有2025 KEYC。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"keyc.com","publish_time":"2025-12-26T23:55:29.867000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1138","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"代理司法部长在场，FBI局长帕特尔公开回应有关其行为的指控","title_en":"With acting AG at his side, FBI Director Patel publicly addresses allegations about his conduct","summary_cn":"据CNN报道，FBI局长Kash Patel在代理司法部长Todd Blanche陪同下于4月21日记者会上公开回应《大西洋月刊》有关其过度饮酒及无故缺勤的报道，称自己从未在工作中醉酒，并已对该杂志提起2.5亿美元诽谤诉讼。Blanche称报道基于匿名消息源且内容“明显虚假”。《大西洋月刊》表示支持记者Sarah Fitzpatrick的报道并将应诉。记者会主题为宣布起诉南方贫困法律中心。","summary_en":"CNN reports that FBI Director Kash Patel, appearing beside acting Attorney General Todd Blanche at an April 21 press conference, publicly addressed a recent Atlantic article alleging excessive drinking and unexplained absences, saying he has never been intoxicated on the job and that he filed a $250 million defamation lawsuit against the magazine. Blanche called the story based on anonymous sources and 'blatantly false.' The Atlantic said it stands by reporter Sarah Fitzpatrick's work and will defend against the lawsuit. The press conference was held to announce an indictment of the Southern Poverty Law Center.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:31:27.763724+00:00","url":"https://www.kezi.com/news/national/with-acting-ag-at-his-side-fbi-director-patel-publicly-addresses-allegations-about-his-conduct/article_192490a9-1e31-5076-949a-2f53e8b200bb.html","content":"With acting AG at his side, FBI Director Patel publicly addresses allegations about his conduct\nBy Holmes Lybrand, CNN\nApr 21, 2026\nApr 21, 2026\nUpdated\nApr 22, 2026\nFacebook\nTwitter\nWhatsApp\nSMS\nEmail\nFBI Director Kash Patel speaks during a press conference at the Department of Justice in Washington, DC on Tuesday.\nMandel Ngan/AFP/Getty Images via CNN Newsource\nFacebook\nTwitter\nWhatsApp\nSMS\nEmail\nPrint\nCopy article link\nSave\n(CNN) — FBI Director Kash Patel, standing at a lectern beside his boss Tuesday, publicly addressed recent allegations that he has drank to excess, interfering with his duties.“I’ve never been intoxicated on the job,” Patel told a room full of reporters Tuesday, after highlighting what he considers to be a string of law enforcement successes since the start of his tenure.“This FBI director has been on the job twice as many days as every director before me,” Patel said.Standing beside him, acting Attorney General Todd Blanche — whom Patel now reports to — also ridiculed recent reporting in The Atlantic, which said people had previously raised concerns with senior leaders about the FBI director.Blanche told reporters he didn’t read the story, but that it included “blatantly false” information.Patel has previously denied the allegations made in The Atlantic’s story and filed a $250 million defamation lawsuit against the magazine.On Tuesday, though, he and Blanche were probed on the claims by a room full of reporters at an unrelated press conference.The story, published last week, alleged Patel “alarmed colleagues with episodes of excessive drinking and unexplained absences.”Patel said Tuesday he never listens “to the fake news mafia.”“My concerns are completely around the anonymous reporting that comes forth constantly,” Blanche said about the article, adding that it was “based on anonymous sources.”The Atlantic has defended the work of reporter Sarah Fitzpatrick, who wrote the story.“We stand by our reporting on Kash Patel, and we will vigorously defend The Atlantic and our journalists against this meritless lawsuit,” a spokesperson said Monday when the lawsuit was filed.Fitzpatrick responded to the legal threats in an interview with MS NOW on Friday night, saying she stood “by every word of this reporting. We have excellent attorneys.”The press conference Tuesday was held to tout the indictment of the Southern Poverty Law Center over its alleged use of paid informants in extremist groups.This story has been updated with additional details.The-CNN-Wire™ & © 2026 Cable News Network, Inc., a Warner Bros. Discovery Company. All rights reserved.\nFacebook\nTwitter\nWhatsApp\nSMS\nEmail\nPrint\nCopy article link\nSave\nTags\nFederal Bureau Of Investigation\nKash Patel\nAttorney General Todd Blanche\nDefamation Litigation\nMore From KEZI 9 News\nNational\nKennedy tells anti-vaccine activists they have a friend in Trump's White House\nUpdated\n16 hrs ago\nNational\nMan who sprayed Minnesota Rep. Omar with vinegar sentenced to 14 months in prison\nUpdated\n19 hrs ago\nNational\nNorth Korea’s nuclear tests may have reactivated seismic faults\nUpdated\n18 hrs ago\nNational\nWhite House pulls ICE director nominee\nUpdated\n18 hrs ago\nNational\nHouthis release video claiming to show downed Saudi F-15 fighter as both sides continue to trade strikes\nUpdated\n13 hrs ago\nNational\nHouse holds billionaire investor Leon Black in contempt over Epstein probe\nUpdated\nSep 16, 2026\nRecommended for you","content_cn":"代理司法部长在旁，FBI局长帕特尔公开回应有关其行为的指控\n作者：霍姆斯·莱布兰德，CNN\n2026年4月21日\n2026年4月21日\n更新\n2026年4月22日\nFacebook\nTwitter\nWhatsApp\n短信\n电子邮件\n联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔周二在华盛顿特区司法部举行的新闻发布会上发言。\nMandel Ngan/AFP/Getty Images，经由CNN Newsource\nFacebook\nTwitter\nWhatsApp\n短信\n电子邮件\n打印\n复制文章链接\n保存\n（CNN）——周二，联邦调查局（FBI）局长卡什·帕特尔站在讲台前，身旁是他的上司，公开回应了近期有关他酗酒、妨碍履职的指控。“我从未在工作时醉酒，”帕特尔周二对满屋记者表示，此前他强调了自任期开始以来他认为的一系列执法成果。“这位FBI局长在岗天数是我之前每一位局长的两倍，”帕特尔说。\n站在他身旁的代理司法部长托德·布兰奇——帕特尔现向其汇报——也嘲讽了《大西洋月刊》近期的报道。该报道称，人们此前曾向高级领导人提出对这位FBI局长的担忧。\n布兰奇告诉记者，他没有读过这篇报道，但其中包含“公然虚假”的信息。\n帕特尔此前已否认《大西洋月刊》报道中的指控，并对该杂志提起2.5亿美元诽谤诉讼。\n不过周二，他和布兰奇在一场无关的新闻发布会上遭到满屋记者就这些说法的追问。\n该报道于上周发布，称帕特尔“因过度饮酒和原因不明的缺席事件令同事感到担忧”。\n帕特尔周二表示，他从不听“假新闻黑手党”的话。\n“我完全担忧的是不断出现的匿名报道，”布兰奇谈及该文章时说，并补充称其“基于匿名消息来源”。\n《大西洋月刊》为撰写该报道的记者莎拉·菲茨帕特里克的工作辩护。\n该诉讼于周一提起时，一名发言人表示：“我们支持关于卡什·帕特尔的报道，并将积极为《大西洋月刊》和我们的记者抵御这起毫无根据的诉讼。”\n菲茨帕特里克周五晚间在接受MS NOW采访时回应法律威胁，表示她“支持这篇报道中的每一个字。我们有出色的律师。”\n周二的新闻发布会旨在宣传对南方贫困法律中心的起诉，该中心被指在极端主义团体中使用付费线人。\n本文已更新，加入更多细节。\nThe-CNN-Wire™及© 2026 Cable News Network, Inc.，华纳兄弟探索公司旗下企业。保留所有权利。\nFacebook\nTwitter\nWhatsApp\n短信\n电子邮件\n打印\n复制文章链接\n保存\n标签\n联邦调查局\n卡什·帕特尔\n司法部长托德·布兰奇\n诽谤诉讼\nKEZI 9新闻更多内容\n全国\n肯尼迪告诉反疫苗活动人士，他们在特朗普白宫有一位朋友\n更新\n16小时前\n全国\n向明尼苏达州众议员奥马尔喷醋的男子被判监禁14个月\n更新\n19小时前\n全国\n朝鲜的核试验可能重新激活了地震断层\n更新\n18小时前\n全国\n白宫撤回ICE局长提名人选\n更新\n18小时前\n全国\n胡塞武装发布视频，声称显示击落一架沙特F-15战斗机，双方继续相互发动袭击\n更新\n13小时前\n全国\n众议院因爱泼斯坦调查而以藐视罪追究亿万富翁投资者莱昂·布莱克\n更新\n2026年9月16日\n为你推荐","publish_source":"kezi.com","publish_time":"2026-04-21T16:36:00-07:00"}},{"id":"news-1222","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI就迈诺特水处理厂勒索软件攻击发表声明","title_en":"FBI releases statement on ransomware attack of Minot’s water treatment plant","summary_cn":"KMOT报道，北达科他州迈诺特水处理厂3月14日遭勒索软件攻击，未影响城市供水，但迫使员工手动操作数小时。市政府将事件通报联邦调查局，FBI表示正与迈诺特市合作调查此次网络攻击，并赞扬该市迅速行动、配合FBI及当地IT人员和执法伙伴。FBI还提到其网络部门今年早些时候启动的“冬季盾牌行动”，列出提升网络入侵韧性的十项措施。","summary_en":"KMOT reports that Minot, North Dakota's water treatment plant suffered a ransomware attack on March 14 that did not compromise the city's water but forced staff to perform some operations manually for several hours. The city informed the FBI, which said it has been working with Minot as it investigates the cyber attack and applauded the city for acting quickly and allowing the FBI to work with its IT professionals and law enforcement partners. The FBI also cited Operation Winter Shield, launched earlier this year by its Cyber Division, which details ten actions organizations can take to improve resilience against cyber intrusions.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T10:51:03.525233+00:00","url":"https://www.kfyrtv.com/2026/04/04/fbi-releases-statement-ransomware-attack-minots-water-treatment-plant","content":"FBI releases statement on ransomware attack of Minot’s water treatment plantMinot Water Plant Ransomware Attack(KMOT-TV)By Kyona RiveraPublished: Apr. 3, 2026 at 7:33 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleMINOT, N.D. (KMOT) – This week, we have reported on the ransomware attack last month on Minot’s Water Treatment Plant.The March 14 incident did not compromise the city’s water, but forced staff to perform some operations manually for several hours.We reached out to the FBI, who was informed by the city about this incident.The FBI provided the following statement to Your News Leader:“The FBI has been working with the City of Minot as they investigate this cyber attack. We applaud the City for acting quickly and allowing the FBI to work with the City’s IT professionals and our law enforcement partners on this investigation. Unfortunately, the most critical threats to infrastructure come from our networks. “Federal, state and local partnerships are crucial in detecting, confronting, and dismantling cyber threats. Earlier this year, FBI Cyber Division launched Operation Winter Shield, which details the ten most impactful actions organizations can take to improve resilience against cyber intrusions. These recommendations were developed with domestic and international partners and draw on recent investigations to reflect adversary behavior and defensive gaps. Additional information can be found at https://www.fbi.gov/investigate/cyber/wintershield.\"Copyright 2026 KFYR. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"联邦调查局就迈诺特水处理厂遭勒索软件攻击发表声明\n迈诺特水厂勒索软件攻击\n（KMOT-TV）\n作者：Kyona Rivera\n发布时间：2026年4月3日美国中部夏令时间晚上7时33分\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n将我们添加为 Google 首选来源\n北达科他州迈诺特（KMOT）——本周，我们报道了迈诺特水处理厂上个月遭到勒索软件攻击一事。\n3月14日发生的事件没有危及该市供水，但迫使工作人员数小时内以人工方式完成部分操作。\n我们联系了联邦调查局，市政府已将此事件告知该机构。\n联邦调查局向“您的新闻领袖”提供了以下声明：\n“联邦调查局一直在与迈诺特市合作，调查这起网络攻击。我们赞赏该市迅速采取行动，并允许联邦调查局与该市的信息技术专业人员及我们的执法合作伙伴共同开展调查。遗憾的是，对基础设施最严重的威胁来自我们的网络。\n“联邦、州和地方之间的合作伙伴关系，对于发现、应对和瓦解网络威胁至关重要。今年早些时候，联邦调查局网络部门启动了‘冬季盾牌行动’，列出了机构可以采取以增强抵御网络入侵能力的十项最具影响力措施。这些建议与国内外合作伙伴共同制定，并借鉴近期调查，以反映对手行为和防御缺口。更多信息请见：https://www.fbi.gov/investigate/cyber/wintershield。”\n版权所有 © 2026 KFYR。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kfyrtv.com","publish_time":"2026-04-04T00:33:17.353000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2475","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI报告：拉雷多跻身全美最安全城市之列","title_en":"Laredo among safest cities in the country, FBI reports","summary_cn":"KGNS报道，美国联邦调查局（FBI）最新发布的暴力犯罪与谋杀数据继续显示边境城镇属全美最安全城市之列。拉雷多市领导8月25日开会讨论该数据，警察局长罗德里格斯称除凶杀案外犯罪率同比下降，抢劫下降51%、吸毒过量下降71%，并称凶杀多与家庭暴力、精神健康及家庭内部情况有关。据FBI统一犯罪报告，拉雷多每10万人约发生2起谋杀和365起暴力犯罪。","summary_en":"KGNS reports that recent Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) data on violent crime and murders continues to show border towns among the safest U.S. cities. Laredo leaders met on August 25 to discuss the figures; Police Chief Rodriguez said crime is down year over year except homicides, with robberies falling 51% and overdoses 71%, attributing homicides largely to domestic violence, mental health and in-home situations. Per the FBI Uniform Crime Report, Laredo recorded about two murders and 365 violent crimes per 100,000 people.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:53:47.373474+00:00","url":"https://www.kgns.tv/2025/08/25/laredo-among-safest-cities-country-fbi-reports","content":"Laredo among safest cities in the country, FBI reportsBy Lisely GarzaPublished: Aug. 25, 2025 at 4:48 PM CDT|Updated: Aug. 25, 2025 at 9:14 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleLAREDO, Tex. (KGNS) - Recent data from the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) continues to show that border towns are among the safest cities in the nation.It’s that time of year when the FBI releases data on violent crimes and murders in cities across the U.S. This data shows that cities like Detroit, Michigan, and Baltimore, Maryland, have some of the highest murder rates in the country. In contrast, Laredo, Texas, continues to have low murder and crime rates.On Monday morning, August 25, Laredo leaders convened to discuss the recent statistics released by the agency. Laredo Police Chief Miguel Rodrigues Jr. reported that crime rates are declining compared to last year, with the exception of homicides. Additionally, Rodrigues mentioned to KGNS that they are still investigating the reasons behind these deaths.“The murder rates this year have to do with relationships, it has to do with domestic violence and it has to do with in-house situations. So, when we look at those numbers, we always try to figure out what can we do to prevent them. This time around, we can say that we need to get aggressive with domestic violence, we have to get very aggressive with mental health and the other thing is that we also need to continue figuring out how we can prevent crime from happening,“ Rodriguez said. He notes that robberies have decreased by 51% compared to last year, and overdoses have dropped by 71% in the same timeframe. According to the FBI’s Uniform Crime Report, Laredo recorded approximately two murders and 365 violent crimes per 100,000 people.Rodriguez is confident that crime numbers will be lower than last year’s.For more headlines, click here.Copyright 2025 KGNS. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"拉雷多跻身全国最安全城市之列，FBI报告\n作者：Lisely Garza\n发表于：2025年8月25日下午4:48（中部夏令时间）|更新：2025年8月25日下午9:14（中部夏令时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n得克萨斯州拉雷多（KGNS）——联邦调查局（FBI）的最新数据显示，边境城镇仍是全国最安全的城市之一。\n每年这个时候，FBI都会发布美国各城市暴力犯罪和谋杀数据。数据显示，密歇根州底特律和马里兰州巴尔的摩等城市的谋杀率位居全国最高之列。相比之下，得克萨斯州拉雷多的谋杀率和犯罪率仍然很低。\n8月25日星期一上午，拉雷多市领导人召开会议，讨论该机构公布的最新统计数据。拉雷多警察局长小米格尔·罗德里格斯报告称，与去年相比，犯罪率正在下降，凶杀案除外。此外，罗德里格斯向KGNS表示，他们仍在调查这些死亡事件背后的原因。\n“今年的谋杀率与人际关系有关，与家庭暴力有关，也与家庭内部情况有关。因此，当我们查看这些数字时，总会试图弄清楚我们能做些什么来预防它们。这一次，我们可以说需要对家庭暴力采取更强硬的措施，必须高度重视心理健康；另一件事是，我们还需要继续弄清楚如何防止犯罪发生，”罗德里格斯说。他指出，与去年相比，抢劫案减少了51%，同期药物过量事件下降了71%。根据FBI的《统一犯罪报告》，拉雷多每10万人约记录2起谋杀案和365起暴力犯罪。\n罗德里格斯相信，犯罪数字将低于去年。\n如需更多头条新闻，请点击这里。\n版权所有2025 KGNS。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"kgns.tv","publish_time":"2025-08-25T21:48:12.433000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2135","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"纽波特官员称国土安全部正考虑在俄勒冈海岸选址设立移民设施","title_en":"Homeland Security considering Oregon coast locations for immigration facility, Newport officials say | kgw.com","summary_cn":"俄勒冈州纽波特市官员表示，美国国土安全部正在评估俄勒冈海岸的多个地点以设立潜在的移民执法设施，纽波特市政机场被列为可能选址。市政府正与地方、州及联邦议员合作核实信息、评估影响并探讨法律选项，但尚未获得国土安全部回应。市长卡普兰表示“深切担忧”，参议员怀登也批评这一可能的ICE拘留设施计划。","summary_en":"Newport, Oregon officials said the U.S. Department of Homeland Security is evaluating locations along the Oregon coast for a potential immigration enforcement facility, with Newport Municipal Airport identified as a possible site. The city is working with local, state and federal legislators to verify the information, assess impacts and explore legal options, but has received no response from DHS. Mayor Jan Kaplan said she is deeply concerned, and Senator Ron Wyden criticized the possible ICE detention facility plan.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:15:30.925141+00:00","url":"https://www.kgw.com/article/news/local/department-of-homeland-security-considering-oregon-coast-locations-immigration-facility-newport/283-a40ff09b-3738-4d38-868e-446d154f1508","content":"Local News\nHomeland Security considering Oregon coast locations for immigration facility, Newport officials say\nThe Newport Municipal Airport has been identified as a possible ICE facility location. City officials are working to verify the information.\nTo stream KGW on your phone, you need the KGW app.\nDownload the KGW app\nMore Videos\nNext up in 5\nExample video title will go here for this video\nNext up in 5\nExample video title will go here for this video\nAuthor: Sabinna Pierre\nPublished: 5:30 PM PST November 10, 2025\nUpdated: 11:31 PM PST November 10, 2025\nNEWPORT, Ore. — Newport city officials said Monday they are aware the U.S. Department of Homeland Security is evaluating locations along the Oregon coast for a potential immigration enforcement facility and that the Newport Municipal Airport has been identified as a possible site.\nCity officials said they are working with local, state and federal legislators to verify the information, assess potential effects on public safety and city resources, and explore available municipal and legal options. Attempts to contact Homeland Security representatives by phone and email have not received a response, according to the city.\nNewport City Council will hold a public meeting Wednesday, Nov. 12 at 6 p.m. at City Hall.\nMayor Jan Kaplan said she is \"deeply concerned\" by reports suggesting Newport may be under consideration for an Immigration and Customs Enforcement detention facility.\n\"The well-being, safety and values of our community are the highest priorities of myself and our City Council,\" Kaplan said in a statement.\nKaplan said any proposal that could affect those principles \"deserves transparency, public input and a thorough review of potential social and economic consequences.\"\nCity Manager Nina Vetter said city officials have been coordinating with local, state and federal representatives to gather more information and understand the city's rights since learning of the potential facility.\n\"I understand that this news will have personal and professional implications for many in our community,\" Vetter said in a statement. \"I urge our community to stay informed through official City of Newport communications, including our social media channels, as we navigate this complex issue with our legislative leaders.\"\nIn an email to KGW on Monday a city spokesperson further clarified the city's involvement:\n\"At this time we do not know what this facility may be. Given the size of our community, we felt it was important to make them aware of what is a VERY fluid situation that has the potential to provide massive impacts here. To our knowledge, so far no one, from us to state and federal reps, have been able to get in touch with DHS. We can confirm that the Coast Guard helicopter, which is normally housed at a Coast Guard facility at the airport (but not their main station) was moved down to Coos Bay just under two weeks ago.\"\nIn a statement to KGW, Oregon Sen. Ron Wyden commented on Newport as a potential site for an ICE facility:\n“Any unilateral decision made 3,000 miles away from Newport about using any part of this coastal community for an ICE detention facility would be both alarming and asinine,” Wyden said. “I will, of course, be teaming up with local and state officials to wrestle more information from the Trump administration about the prospects for such a scheme. I also look forward to holding my annual Lincoln County town hall in the weeks ahead to hear directly from coastal families and small businesses about any such unwelcome and unneeded makeover of Newport.”\nCity officials said they chose to share the information with the community due to the credibility of the information received and the sensitivity of the issue. The city said it will provide updates as further information becomes available.\nClose Ad\nBefore You Leave, Check This Out","content_cn":"本地新闻\n纽波特官员称，国土安全部正考虑俄勒冈海岸地点建设移民设施\n纽波特市政机场已被确定为可能的 ICE 设施选址。市政府官员正在核实该信息。\n要在手机上观看 KGW 流媒体，您需要 KGW 应用程序。\n下载 KGW 应用程序\n更多视频\n5 秒后播放\n此视频的示例视频标题将显示在这里\n5 秒后播放\n此视频的示例视频标题将显示在这里\n作者：Sabinna Pierre\n发布时间：2025 年 11 月 10 日太平洋标准时间下午 5:30\n更新时间：2025 年 11 月 10 日太平洋标准时间晚上 11:31\n俄勒冈州纽波特——纽波特市政府官员周一表示，他们获悉美国国土安全部正在评估俄勒冈海岸沿线地点，以设立一处潜在的移民执法设施，而纽波特市政机场已被确定为可能选址。\n市政府官员表示，他们正与地方、州和联邦立法者合作，以核实该信息、评估其对公共安全和市政资源的潜在影响，并探索可用的市政及法律选项。据市政府称，尝试通过电话和电子邮件联系国土安全部代表均未获回应。\n纽波特市议会将于 11 月 12 日星期三晚上 6 点在市政厅举行公开会议。\n市长 Jan Kaplan 表示，有报道称纽波特可能正被考虑作为移民与海关执法局拘留设施的地点，这令她“深感担忧”。\nKaplan 在一份声明中说：“我本人和市议会最优先考虑的是我们社区的福祉、安全和价值观。”\nKaplan 表示，任何可能影响这些原则的提议都“应当具有透明度、接受公众意见，并对潜在的社会和经济后果进行全面审查”。\n市经理 Nina Vetter 表示，自得知可能建设该设施以来，市政府官员一直在与地方、州和联邦代表协调，以收集更多信息并了解该市的权利。\nVetter 在一份声明中说：“我理解，这则消息将对我们社区许多人的个人和职业生活产生影响。我们在与立法领导人应对这一复杂问题时，我敦促社区通过纽波特市官方通信渠道——包括我们的社交媒体频道——获取最新信息。”\n周一，一位市政府发言人在给 KGW 的电子邮件中进一步澄清了该市的参与情况：\n“目前我们不知道该设施可能是什么。鉴于我们社区的规模，我们认为有必要让大家了解这一仍在快速变化的情况，它有可能在这里造成巨大影响。据我们所知，到目前为止，从我们到州和联邦代表，都未能联系上 DHS。我们可以确认，通常驻扎在机场一处海岸警卫队设施（但不是其主站）的海岸警卫队直升机，在不到两周前被转移到了库斯湾。”\n俄勒冈州参议员 Ron Wyden 在给 KGW 的声明中就纽波特作为 ICE 设施潜在选址发表评论：\nWyden 说：“在距离纽波特 3,000 英里之外，单方面决定将这个沿海社区的任何部分用于 ICE 拘留设施，既令人震惊又愚蠢。当然，我将与地方和州官员合作，迫使特朗普政府就这种计划的可能性提供更多信息。我也期待在未来几周举行我每年一度的林肯县市民大会，直接听取沿海家庭和小企业对于任何这种不受欢迎且无必要地改造纽波特的意见。”\n市政府官员表示，鉴于所收到信息的可信度以及该议题的敏感性，他们选择与社区分享这一信息。市政府表示，随着获得更多信息，将提供更新。\n关闭广告\n离开前，看看这个","publish_source":"kgw.com","publish_time":"2025-11-10T08:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-739","ktid":1055920,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1055920","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国为何将阿里巴巴列为中国军工企业？一家合资公司提供线索","title_en":"Why Did DOD Label Alibaba as a Chinese Military Company? This Joint Venture Offers a Clue. | Kharon","summary_cn":"美国国防部将阿里巴巴集团列入1260H“中国军工企业”名单，指其与国务院国资委“间接关联”并是“军民融合贡献者”。卡隆公司研究指出，阿里巴巴与国企中国兵器工业集团合资成立的上海千寻位置网络公司或为线索：千寻位置致力于推动北斗卫星导航系统大规模部署，其CEO曾接受国资委采访，并与兵器工业集团合作申请无人机相关专利。文章认为，若美国有意针对阿里巴巴，此类关联可支撑其认定依据。","summary_en":"The Pentagon added Alibaba Group to its 1260H list of \"Chinese military companies,\" alleging indirect affiliation with China's state assets commission and status as a military-civil fusion contributor. Kharon research points to Shanghai-based Qianxun Spatial Intelligence, a joint venture between Alibaba and state defense conglomerate Norinco, as a possible clue: Qianxun Spatial works to drive large-scale deployment of the BeiDou navigation system, its CEO was interviewed by SASAC, and it has worked with Norinco on drone-related patents. Such connections could help build the case if the U.S. specifically wanted to target Alibaba.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:28:09.395498+00:00","url":"https://www.kharon.com/brief/alibaba-china-military-companies-1260-list-defense-department","content":"Kharon illustration / Adobe Stock ImagesNational SecurityJun 16, 20263 minutesWhy Did the U.S. Label Alibaba as a Chinese Military Company? This Joint Venture Offers a Clue.By Yu-Jie Liao and Ryan BacicThe Pentagon’s biggest-name addition to its list of “Chinese military companies” last week was one of China’s biggest tech brands: Alibaba Group.\nThat 1260H listing means the Wall Street-traded e-commerce and AI giant will soon be blocked from doing business with the Department of Defense, with further supply-chain restrictions to take effect next year. As explanation, DOD alleged only that Alibaba was “indirectly affiliated” with China’s state assets commission and a “military-civil fusion contributor” because it was “affiliated” with a state tech regulator.Alibaba in a statement denied that it was “a Chinese military-industrial enterprise” and said there was “no basis for designating Alibaba Group as such.”A Pentagon spokesperson declined to provide further details.\nSo, how might the U.S. have decided that the company known as “China’s Amazon” was supporting Beijing’s military?\nWhat our research shows: One Alibaba-associated company traced by Kharon might offer a clue. Its own ties to state defense strategy run deep.\nThe firm\nShanghai-based Qianxun Spatial Intelligence calls itself the “world’s leading” service provider of high-precision satellite positioning, a technology that has both civilian and military uses.\nA Kharon review of corporate records and public statements shows two distinct pathways connecting it to Alibaba.\n1. Ownership: Qianxun Spatial launched, in 2015, as a joint venture between Alibaba and China North Industries (Norinco) Group, the state-owned defense and industrial conglomerate.\nNorinco, which the U.S. separately flagged in 2021 for involvement in China’s military-industrial complex, still holds a 32% stake in the satellite-positioning firm.\nAnd while an Alibaba venture-capital vehicle relinquished its 50% stake in Qianxun Spatial in 2018, the result effectively appears to be a reshuffle. Two executives tied to Alibaba, including President of Public Affairs Wen Jia, still ultimately own around 45% collectively, according to corporate disclosures from March.Kharon users can explore this network in greater detail through the ClearView platform.2. Services: Qianxun Spatial partners with Alibaba Cloud, whose services it leverages to “deliver innovative spatiotemporal intelligence solutions tailored to diverse industries,” as an Alibaba Cloud news release put it last July.\nIn that release, the Alibaba Group subsidiary touted its “high degree of compatibility” with “high-precision positioning services, enabling it to provide robust support to Qianxun Spatial.”\nThe military connections and risks\nQianxun Spatial’s chief executive, Chen Jinpei, was interviewed in 2019 by China’s State-owned Assets Supervision and Administration Commission of the State Council (SASAC), the body that DOD last week named as “indirectly” connected to Alibaba.\nQianxun Spatial was established, Chen said, to help “drive the large-scale deployment” of the BeiDou Navigation Satellite System, a state-developed geolocation infrastructure overseen by Chinese government authorities. A “clear alignment between national strategy and societal needs” drove Alibaba and Norinco to team up, he added.\nSince then, Qianxun Spatial has built out the BeiDou Ground-Based Augmentation System, a national network of high-precision positioning infrastructure critical to the BeiDou apparatus.\nWhy that matters: Chinese military sources have publicly stated that the People’s Liberation Army (PLA) uses the BeiDou system in combat training, airborne operations, navigation, and field exercises.\nTwo more risk routes:\nPatent data shows that Qianxun Spatial has worked with Norinco on two drone-related patents, including one related to high-precision positioning.According to company statements, it also has partnered on BeiDou-related work with Guangzhou Hi-Target Navigation Tech Co., Ltd. and Runjian Co., Ltd., two companies that operate in dual-use technologies and have sold to the PLA.\nThe bottom line\nThe law that authorizes the 1260H list offers wide latitude for the Pentagon to designate a company, and its reasoning remains unclear not only for Alibaba but also for the Chinese search titan Baidu, for which it cited the same alleged “affiliations.”\nBut if the U.S. specifically had wanted to target Alibaba, connections like Qianxun Spatial’s would help build the case.\nRead more from The Brief:\nChina’s Space Mercenaries: How the Commercial Rocket Economy Is Arming Iran and RussiaBIS Draws Red Line on Chip Exports to China with Enforcement SurgeEU Aims to Upend China Dependency with New Supply Chain QuotasBack to The BriefLatest on KharonWho Are the Houthis? How Iran Funds the Militia Group Now Striking Saudi Arabia.Iran’s Attacks on U.S. Water Systems Look Less Like a New Terror Front and More Like a PsyopWhat Will the Latest Trump-Xi Summit Bring? Four Experts Set the Stakes.Kharon ReadbookWeekly insights delivered to your inbox.First Name*Last Name*Email address*Thank you for subscribing.Subscribe","content_cn":"Kharon插图 / Adobe Stock Images\n国家安全\n2026年6月16日\n3分钟\n为什么美国将阿里巴巴列为中国军方公司？这家合资企业提供了一个线索。\n作者：廖玉洁和Ryan Bacic\n上周，五角大楼将中国最大牌的新增企业列入其“中国军方公司”名单，而该企业正是中国最大的科技品牌之一：阿里巴巴集团。\n这项1260H列名意味着，这家在华尔街交易的电商和人工智能巨头很快将被禁止与国防部开展业务，进一步的供应链限制将于明年生效。作为解释，国防部仅声称阿里巴巴因与一家国家科技监管机构“有关联”，而“间接关联”中国国家资产监督管理机构，并且是“军民融合贡献者”。阿里巴巴在一份声明中否认自己是“中国军工企业”，并表示“没有依据将阿里巴巴集团如此认定”。五角大楼发言人拒绝提供更多细节。\n那么，美国可能是如何认定这家被称为“中国亚马逊”的公司正在支持北京军方的呢？\n我们的研究显示：Kharon追踪到的一家与阿里巴巴有关联的公司或许能提供线索。它自身与国家防务战略的联系十分深厚。\n该公司\n总部位于上海的千寻位置智能自称是全球领先的高精度卫星定位服务提供商，这项技术同时具有民用和军事用途。\nKharon对公司记录和公开声明的审查显示，有两条不同路径将其与阿里巴巴连接起来。\n1. 所有权：千寻位置智能于2015年成立，是阿里巴巴与中国北方工业集团（北方工业）的合资企业；后者是国有防务和工业企业集团。\n北方工业曾于2021年因参与中国军工复合体而被美国单独列入名单，目前仍持有这家卫星定位公司的32%股份。\n虽然一家阿里巴巴风险投资实体于2018年放弃了其在千寻位置智能持有的50%股份，但结果实际上似乎只是一次重新洗牌。根据3月的公司披露，包括公共事务总裁温嘉在内的两名与阿里巴巴有关联的高管最终仍合计持有约45%的股份。Kharon用户可以通过ClearView平台进一步详细了解这一网络。\n2. 服务：千寻位置智能与阿里云合作，并利用阿里云的服务“提供针对不同行业量身定制的创新时空智能解决方案”，正如阿里云去年7月一份新闻稿所称。\n在那份新闻稿中，这家阿里巴巴集团子公司宣称其与“高精度定位服务”具有“高度兼容性”，从而能够“为千寻位置智能提供强有力的支持”。\n军事联系与风险\n千寻位置智能首席执行官陈金培于2019年接受了中国国务院国有资产监督管理委员会（国资委）的采访；国资委正是五角大楼上周称与阿里巴巴存在“间接”关联的机构。\n陈金培表示，成立千寻位置智能是为了帮助“推动”北斗卫星导航系统的大规模部署；北斗是由国家开发、由中国政府机构监管的地理定位基础设施。他补充说，“国家战略与社会需求之间的明确契合”促成了阿里巴巴与北方工业的合作。\n此后，千寻位置智能建设了北斗地基增强系统，这是一个全国性的高精度定位基础设施网络，对……至关重要\n至北斗设备。\n为何这很重要：中国军方消息人士曾公开表示，中国人民解放军（PLA）在战斗训练、空降行动、导航和野外演习中使用北斗系统。\n另外两条风险路径：\n专利数据表明，千寻位置曾与北方工业合作申请两项与无人机相关的专利，其中一项涉及高精度定位。根据公司声明，该公司还曾就北斗相关工作与广州海格星航信息科技有限公司和润建股份有限公司开展合作，这两家公司都从事军民两用技术，并曾向解放军销售产品。\n底线\n授权设立1260H名单的法律为五角大楼指定公司提供了很大的裁量空间，而其理由不仅对阿里巴巴不明确，对中国搜索巨头百度也同样不明确；五角大楼以所谓的“关联”为由将百度列入名单。\n但如果美国确实有意针对阿里巴巴，那么像千寻位置这样的关联将有助于构建理由。\n阅读《简报》的更多内容：\n中国的太空雇佣军：商业火箭经济如何武装伊朗和俄罗斯\nBIS通过加强执法，对中国芯片出口划出红线\n欧盟拟通过新的供应链配额打破对中国的依赖\n返回《简报》\nKharon最新内容\n胡塞武装是谁？伊朗如何资助这个如今袭击沙特阿拉伯的民兵组织。\n伊朗对美国供水系统的攻击，与其说像一个新的恐怖战线，不如说更像一场心理战\n最新的特朗普—习近平峰会将带来什么？四位专家界定关键问题。\nKharon Readbook\n每周洞察，直接送达您的收件箱。\n名*姓*电子邮件地址*\n感谢您的订阅。","publish_source":"kharon.com","publish_time":"2026-06-16T11:25:21-07:00"}},{"id":"news-2326","ktid":1055920,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1055920","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"BIS“50%规则”指南：对全球子公司的影响、案例研究等","title_en":"A Guide to the BIS ‘50% Rule’: Its Global Impacts on Subsidiaries, Case Studies and More | Kharon","summary_cn":"卡隆公司简报汇总其关于美国工业与安全局（BIS）“50%规则”的系列报道。该规则要求被实体清单或军事最终用户清单实体持股50%及以上的子公司自动适用同等贸易限制。文章回顾了规则出台背景、前BIS官员的评论、对合规筛查的影响、相关案例研究，以及9月和10月实体清单新增指定情况。","summary_en":"Kharon Brief compiles its coverage of the U.S. Bureau of Industry and Security's 50% ownership rule, which subjects subsidiaries majority-owned by Entity List or Military End-User List parties to the same trade restrictions as their parents. It reviews the rule's background, comments from a former BIS official, compliance screening impacts, case studies, and September-October Entity List additions.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T17:16:39.127610+00:00","url":"https://www.kharon.com/brief/bis-50-percent-rule-faq-entity-list-meu-list","content":"Kharon illustration / Adobe Stock ImagesExport ControlsSep 30, 20252 minutesA Guide to the BIS ‘50% Rule’: Its Global Impacts on Subsidiaries, Case Studies and MoreBy Ryan Bacic[Updated, 10/29/25] The arrival of the U.S. Bureau and Industry’s (BIS) 50% ownership rule stands to be a game-changer for export-control enforcement and compliance screening.\nThe rule mandates that subsidiaries that are owned 50% or more by entities on the BIS Entity List or Military End-User list will be subjected to the same trade restrictions as those parents.\nThroughout this year, the Kharon Brief had chronicled the potential for such a policy from a number of angles, from the news developments to case studies to the impacts on subsidiaries in China and around the world.\nWant to get fully up to speed on the new 50% rule? Explore our best related coverage below.\nThe news, scale and impacts\nMatt Axelrod, the former assistant secretary for export enforcement at BIS, told Kharon in a May webinar that the possibility of a 50% ownership rule had “been a debate internally for a while.”\nWithout one, Axelrod explained, it was “easy” for “an Entity-Listed company to set up a different subsidiary, and that’s not caught by the Entity List.” With such a rule, the responsibilities of compliance screening now grow:\nUS Expands Export Controls with Long-Awaited ‘50% Rule’ — Here’s What To KnowThe New BIS 50% Rule: Answers to 9 Frequently Asked QuestionsKharon Data: A BIS 50% Rule Would Pull Thousands of Hidden Subsidiaries into Export-Control Crosshairs\nCase studies\nAs BIS outlined in its interim final rule, its 50% ownership threshold will apply in the aggregate, and it will count direct and indirect ownership by one or more U.S.-listed foreign parties. But even minority ownership by listed actors is a red flag, BIS said.\nThat all can make the tricky math of risk assessment trickier. Prepare with the examples in the three pieces below:How the New BIS 50% Rule Could Ensnare a Tech Firm’s Subsidiaries, in China and the West\nWeeks After BIS Listed These Chinese Tech Companies, They Spun Up Unrestricted SubsidiariesA BIS 50% Rule Case Study: Three High-Tech Subsidiaries of a Restricted Chinese Institute\nThe latest designations\nThe Entity List also got longer in September and October, adding more parties that the 50% rule will now sweep up. Both rollouts zeroed in on Chinese suppliers of sensitive, U.S.-origin electronic components.\nOctober: BIS Targets Iran Drone Networks in First Entity List Additions Since 50% Rule\nSeptember: New US Entity List Designations Target Chinese Tech, Diversion to Russia, Iran\nMore from the Kharon Brief:\nThe Biggest Client No One Names: How Huawei Lurks Behind China’s Chip IPOsThe US Sanctioned Ships Named for Disney Characters. Right Away, Their Network Reshuffled.‘The Robot Dog’s Time to Kill’: At China’s Star Robotics Firm, the Military Ties Keep MountingLearn more about Kharon's industry-leading BIS 50% Rule (\"Affiliates Rule\") SolutionsBack to The BriefLatest on KharonWho Are the Houthis? How Iran Funds the Militia Group Now Striking Saudi Arabia.Iran’s Attacks on U.S. Water Systems Look Less Like a New Terror Front and More Like a PsyopWhat Will the Latest Trump-Xi Summit Bring? Four Experts Set the Stakes.Kharon ReadbookWeekly insights delivered to your inbox.First Name*Last Name*Email address*Thank you for subscribing.Subscribe","content_cn":"Kharon 插图 / Adobe Stock Images\n出口管制\n2025年9月30日\n2分钟\nBIS“50%规则”指南：其全球影响、案例研究及更多内容\n作者：Ryan Bacic\n[更新于2025年10月29日]\n\n美国商务部工业与安全局（BIS）50%所有权规则的出台，有望成为出口管制执法和合规筛查领域的游戏规则改变者。\n\n该规则规定，由BIS实体清单或军事最终用户清单上的实体持有50%或以上股权的子公司，将受到与其母公司相同的贸易限制。\n\n今年以来，《Kharon Brief》从多个角度记录了这一政策的可能性，包括新闻进展、案例研究，以及对中国和世界各地子公司的影响。\n\n想全面了解新的“50%规则”？请浏览以下我们精选的相关文章。\n\n新闻、规模与影响\n\nBIS前出口执法助理部长Matt Axelrod在5月的一场网络研讨会上告诉Kharon，50%所有权规则的可能性“在内部已经争论了一段时间”。\n\nAxelrod解释说，如果没有这项规则，“实体清单上的公司很容易设立另一家子公司，而这家子公司不会被实体清单涵盖”。有了这项规则，合规筛查的责任范围如今扩大了：\n\n美国扩大出口管制，姗姗来迟的“50%规则”——你需要了解的内容\n新的BIS“50%规则”：9个常见问题解答\nKharon数据：BIS“50%规则”将把数千家隐性子公司置于出口管制的打击范围\n\n案例研究\n\n正如BIS在其临时最终规则中所阐述的，其50%所有权门槛将按合计计算，并将计算一个或多个列入美国清单的外国方的直接和间接持股。但BIS表示，即使清单所列实体持有少数股权，也属于危险信号。\n\n所有这些都会让风险评估中本已棘手的计算变得更加复杂。请通过以下三篇文章中的示例做好准备：\n\n新的BIS“50%规则”如何可能牵连一家科技公司的子公司，涉及中国和西方\nBIS列入这些中国科技公司数周后，它们成立了不受限制的子公司\nBIS“50%规则”案例研究：一家受限制的中国研究机构的三家高科技子公司\n\n最新列入名单的实体\n\n9月和10月，实体清单进一步延长，增加了更多将被“50%规则”纳入范围的实体。两轮新增名单都集中于中国敏感的美国原产电子元件供应商。\n\n10月：BIS针对伊朗无人机网络采取行动，这是“50%规则”以来首次新增实体清单\n9月：美国新的实体清单指定针对中国科技企业，以及转运至俄罗斯、伊朗的行为\n\n《Kharon Brief》更多内容：\n\n没有人点名的最大客户：中国芯片IPO背后的华为身影\n美国制裁了以迪士尼角色命名的船只。它们的网络立即重新洗牌。\n“机器狗的杀戮时刻”：在中国明星机器人公司，军事关联仍在不断增加\n\n了解更多Kharon业内领先的BIS“50%规则”（“关联公司规则”）解决方案\n返回《Brief》\nKharon最新消息\n\n胡塞武装是谁？伊朗如何资助这个如今正在袭击沙特阿拉伯的民兵组织。\n\n伊朗对美国供水系统的攻击，与其说像新的恐怖主义战线，不如说更像一场心理战\n\n最新的特朗普—习近平峰会将带来什么？四位专家阐明关键问题。\n\nKharon读本\n每周洞察，送达您的收件箱。\n\n名*姓*电子邮件地址*\n\n感谢订阅。\n订阅","publish_source":"kharon.com","publish_time":"2025-09-30T12:19:11-07:00"}},{"id":"news-467","ktid":1055920,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1055920","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国最大规模扩大强迫劳动黑名单，新增43家中国企业","title_en":"U.S. Makes Largest-Ever Expansion of Forced-Labor Blacklist, Adding 43 Chinese Companies | Kharon","summary_cn":"美国国土安全部将43家中国企业列入《维吾尔强迫劳动预防法》实体清单，被称为该清单史上最大规模扩容，也是特朗普第二任期首次更新。新增企业涉及金属矿业、工业材料、纺织、农业和食品加工，包括山东黄金、白银有色、福建七匹狼和洽洽食品。卡隆研究指出洽洽食品存在与新疆相关的强迫劳动风险信号。","summary_en":"The Department of Homeland Security added 43 Chinese companies to the Uyghur Forced Labor Prevention Act Entity List, its largest-ever expansion and the first update under the second Trump administration. Additions span metals, mining, industrial materials, textiles, agriculture and food processing, including Shandong Gold, Baiyin Nonferrous, Fujian Septwolves and Chacha Food. Kharon research flagged Chacha Food for Xinjiang-linked forced-labor risk indicators.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:10:41.646565+00:00","url":"https://www.kharon.com/brief/china-uyghur-forced-labor-us-list","content":"Adobe StockForced LaborJul 31, 20262 minutesU.S. Makes Largest-Ever Expansion of Forced-Labor Blacklist, Adding 43 Chinese CompaniesBy Jane TangThe Department of Homeland Security on Friday added 43 Chinese companies to the Uyghur Forced Labor Prevention Act (UFLPA) Entity List, in what the agency called the list’s “single largest-ever expansion.”\nThe additions, scheduled to take effect Monday, mark the first update to the UFLPA Entity List under the second Trump administration.\n“The Trump Administration remains steadfast in its commitment to remove forced labor from U.S. supply chains and to holding foreign companies accountable for their exploitation,” said DHS Undersecretary Rob Law, chair of the Forced Labor Enforcement Task Force. He said the expansion would help prevent unfair practices that undermine American businesses while protecting U.S. economic and national security interests.\nAnalysis: After an 18-month wait, the additions offer “a meaningful signal that [forced-labor] enforcement remains active,” said LeRoy Potts, a former DHS official who worked on UFLPA enforcement and now leads his own consultancy.\nThe designations are the latest in a string of recent Trump administration listings targeting Chinese entities. They also follow the imposition last week of tariffs against 60 top U.S. trading partners for allegedly taking insufficient steps to root out forced labor.\nThe UFLPA update, Potts said, reinforces a message that Washington is prepared to back its forced-labor agenda with enforcement actions.Among the new names: companies involved in metals and mining, industrial materials, textiles, agriculture, and food processing, including publicly traded companies and consumer brands.\nThe additions include:\none of China’s largest gold producers, the Shanghai- and Hong Kong-listed state-owned enterprise Shandong Gold Mining Co.;the state-owned mining and metals processor Baiyin Nonferrous Group Co.;the menswear maker Fujian Septwolves Industry Co.;and the snack producer Chacha Food Co., known for its packaged sunflower seeds and nuts.\nFrom Kharon research: Chacha Food, which touted large U.S. retailers among its primary “direct offline clients” in its 2025 annual report, had demonstrated ongoing red flags for forced labor risks linked to the Xinjiang region.\nChinese state media has highlighted as recently as January that Chacha, which was introduced to Xinjiang by a branch of forced-labor-linked Xinjiang Aid, had “enabled local farmers to secure stable employment right on their doorsteps.”\nAs of May, it maintained and sourced from at least five subsidiaries in Xinjiang. One is located at an industrial park that in 2020 received “registered impoverished laborers” for employment from the Xinjiang government.\nBy the numbers: CBP has denied entry to more than 24,300 shipments, valued at nearly $1 billion, under the UFLPA since its enactment, DHS said in its press release Friday.\nThat’s about 14,000 more shipments than it said CBP had denied as of an update last August.\nThis story has been updated.\nRead more from The Brief on forced labor risk:\nHow UFLPA Risks from Xinjiang Flow into Major Automakers’ Car Seats\nThe EU’s New Forced Labor Guidelines Are Sweeping. Here’s How To Comply.\nInside a Top Chinese Apple Juice Concentrate, Red Flags for Forced Labor\nBack to The BriefLatest on KharonWho Are the Houthis? How Iran Funds the Militia Group Now Striking Saudi Arabia.Iran’s Attacks on U.S. Water Systems Look Less Like a New Terror Front and More Like a PsyopWhat Will the Latest Trump-Xi Summit Bring? Four Experts Set the Stakes.Kharon ReadbookWeekly insights delivered to your inbox.First Name*Last Name*Email address*Thank you for subscribing.Subscribe","content_cn":"Adobe Stock\n强迫劳动\n2026年7月31日\n2分钟\n美国史上最大规模扩大强迫劳动黑名单，新增43家中国企业\n作者：Jane Tang\n美国国土安全部周五将43家中国企业加入《维吾尔强迫劳动预防法》（UFLPA）实体清单，此举被该机构称为该清单“史上最大规模的单次扩展”。\n这些新增企业定于周一生效，标志着第二届特朗普政府上任以来首次更新UFLPA实体清单。\n“特朗普政府坚定不移地致力于清除美国供应链中的强迫劳动，并追究外国企业剥削行为的责任，”国土安全部副部长、强迫劳动执法工作组主席Rob Law说。他表示，此次扩展将有助于防止损害美国企业的不公平做法，同时保护美国的经济和国家安全利益。\n分析：曾参与UFLPA执法、现负责自己咨询公司的前国土安全部官员LeRoy Potts说，在等待18个月后，这些新增企业“发出了一个有意义的信号，表明（强迫劳动）执法仍在进行”。\n这些列入清单的企业是特朗普政府近期针对中国实体的一连串行动中的最新一批。它们还紧随上周对60个美国主要贸易伙伴征收关税的措施，此举指责这些贸易伙伴在根除强迫劳动方面采取的措施不足。\nPotts说，UFLPA的更新强化了这样一个信息：华盛顿准备通过执法行动支持其强迫劳动议程。\n新名单中的企业包括涉及金属和采矿、工业材料、纺织品、农业和食品加工的公司，其中包括上市公司和消费品牌。\n新增企业包括：\n中国最大的黄金生产商之一、在上海和香港上市的国有企业山东黄金矿业股份有限公司；国有采矿和金属加工企业白银有色集团股份有限公司；男装制造商福建七匹狼实业股份有限公司；以及以包装葵花籽和坚果闻名的零食生产商洽洽食品股份有限公司。\n来自Kharon的研究：洽洽食品在其2025年年度报告中将大型美国零售商列为主要“线下直接客户”，并已显示出与新疆地区相关的持续强迫劳动风险警示信号。\n中国官方媒体最近在1月还强调，洽洽是由与强迫劳动有关联的新疆援助机构的一个分支引入新疆的，并且“让当地农民能够在家门口获得稳定就业”。\n截至5月，该公司在新疆至少维持并从至少五家子公司采购。其中一家位于一个工业园区；2020年，新疆政府曾向该园区安排“登记在册的贫困劳动者”就业。\n数据：国土安全部在周五的新闻稿中表示，自UFLPA颁布以来，美国海关与边境保护局（CBP）已拒绝超过24,300批货物入境，这些货物价值近10亿美元。\n这比该部门所称CBP截至去年8月一次更新时拒绝入境的货物多约14,000批。\n本文已更新。\n阅读《The Brief》更多关于强迫劳动风险的内容：\n《新疆UFLPA风险如何流入主要汽车制造商的汽车座椅》\n《欧盟新的强迫劳动指南覆盖面广，如何遵守？》\n《一家中国大型苹果汁浓缩汁企业内部：强迫劳动风险警示信号》\n返回《The Brief》\nKharon最新内容\n胡塞武装是谁？伊朗如何资助这个如今正在袭击沙特阿拉伯的民兵组织。\n伊朗对美国供水系统的袭击，与其说像新的恐怖战线，不如说更像一场心理战。\n最新特朗普—习近平峰会将带来什么？四位专家评估关键问题。\nKharon读本\n每周洞察送达您的收件箱。\n名*姓*电子邮箱*\n感谢订阅。","publish_source":"kharon.com","publish_time":"2026-07-31T10:58:15-07:00"}},{"id":"news-1616","ktid":1055920,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1055920","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"五角大楼正重建供应链以对抗中国，愿意接受部分“风险”","title_en":"The Pentagon Is Rebuilding Supply Chains To Counter China. It’s Willing To Accept Some ‘Risk.’ | Kharon","summary_cn":"美国国防部工业基础政策助理部长Michael Cadenazzi在哈德逊研究所表示，五角大楼正通过多年期大额合同重塑武器采购，以修复受劳动力短缺、工厂老化和中国制造业主导地位冲击的国防供应链。他称中国占全球制造业产出约30%，造船能力约为美国200倍，并强调将加强对外国投资和1260H清单相关实体的审查。","summary_en":"Michael Cadenazzi, assistant secretary of defense for industrial base policy, said at the Hudson Institute that the Pentagon is reshaping weapons procurement through larger multiyear contracts to repair defense supply chains strained by labor shortages, aging factories and China's manufacturing dominance. He noted China accounts for about 30% of global manufacturing output and roughly 200 times U.S. shipbuilding capacity, and stressed intensified scrutiny of foreign investment and 1260H-listed entities.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:54:07.144958+00:00","url":"https://www.kharon.com/brief/defense-department-us-manufacturing-michael-cadenazzi-china-news","content":"Courtesy of the Hudson InstituteSupply ChainsFeb 12, 20263 minutesThe Pentagon Is Rebuilding Supply Chains To Counter China. It’s Willing To Accept Some ‘Risk.’By Jane TangThe Pentagon is reshaping how it buys weapons in an effort to repair fragile defense supply chains strained by labor shortages, aging factories and China's dominance in global manufacturing, a senior official said at an event in Washington this week.\nRather than spreading funding across short-term contracts, the Defense Department plans to make larger multiyear bets on critical production lines, from missile systems to hypersonic weapons, to stabilize demand and unlock private investment, said Michael Cadenazzi, assistant secretary of defense for industrial base policy.\n“We’re accepting acquisition risk to lessen operational risk,” Cadenazzi said, speaking Tuesday at the Hudson Institute.\nCadenazzi, who joined the Pentagon in September after two decades in the private sector, delivered his remarks as the department implements its Acquisition Reform strategy, announced in November, as well as the 2026 National Defense Authorization Act (NDAA), the $901 billion bill that granted the Pentagon sweeping new authorities to rebuild the U.S. defense-industrial base.\nCritical U.S. Manufacturing Gaps\nGovernment Accountability Office reports reflect some of that base’s yearslong shortfalls: how Army vehicles have consistently missed readiness targets, Army ammunition has gone untracked and F-35 fighter jets have been delivered on average 238 days late.\n“We spent billions on the DIB [defense industrial base] over the past decade,” Cadenazzi said. “The problems that existed 10, 15 years ago are sometimes worse. That’s a terrible investment.”\nBig picture: China accounts for roughly 30% of global manufacturing output, compared with the United States’ 17%, and its shipbuilding capacity is roughly 200 times greater, Cadenazzi noted. The gap underscores the Trump administration’s push to reshore or “near-shore” manufacturing, including most prominently through tariffs, as it noted in December in its new National Security Strategy.\nBut that U.S. urgency comes as the defense industry’s workforce remains under pressure. Keith DeVries, then the managing director of manufacturing technology for the Office of the Secretary of Defense, said in September 2023 that there were more than 800,000 open jobs in U.S. manufacturing, with projections of a four-million-job shortfall over the next decade. Cadenazzi cited both numbers again Tuesday.\nThe problem, as he later cast it in conversation with Hudson Institute senior fellow Nadia Schadlow, isn’t just recruitment—it’s challenging cultural expectations.\n“Twenty-five years ago, they said, ‘You got to go to college,’” Cadenazzi said. “What we need to do is convince those parents that they need to go ahead and convince that kid that [a manufacturing career] is a good thing for them.”\nIt would take, he said, “an all-American effort to go ahead and drive a fundamental transformation in how we view defense production.”\nWhy it matters: China’s manufacturing output “allows them to go ahead and scale production and delivery, not just in the naval domain but across multiple domains,” Cadenazzi said.\n“We need some radically different outcomes, and that means we need some radically different approaches.”\nMultiyear Contracts, More Targeted Bets\nOne such approach is rethinking how the Pentagon buys weapons, by accepting greater upfront commitments to secure faster, more reliable deliveries. Central to the strategy, Cadenazzi said, is stabilizing defense supply chains by inking contracts that last five to seven years, designed to reduce the unpredictability that can discourage private investment.\n“The key element here is the demand signal,” he said. “Why would anyone bet on this if funding goes up one year and down the next?”\nZoom in: That’s a strategy the new NDAA empowers, as the White House touted before its passage.\nSection 804, for example, authorizes multi-year contracts beginning in fiscal 2026 for major weapons systems and munitions. That approach supplants traditional annual contracting cycles, “providing the certainty needed to expand industrial capacity and delivering cost savings for the taxpayer,” the White House said in December.Michael Cadenazzi, assistant secretary of defense for industrial base policy, speaks Tuesday with Nadia Schadlow, a senior fellow at the Hudson Institute. (Courtesy of the Hudson Institute)Focal points: Rather than spreading limited funds across many projects—a practice that Cadenazzi said produced little lasting impact—the Defense Department will concentrate on larger, longer-term investments in priority supply chains, including solid rocket motors, critical minerals and batteries. It also is aiming, he said, to fix the “fragility” of the energetics industrial base, which produces, among others, the chemicals used in explosives and propellants.\n“We used to put five million dollars down when we really needed 55,” Cadenazzi said. “We’re peanut-butter-spreading less and focusing on fewer, bigger wins.”\nScreening Foreign Investment\nBeyond production capacity, he said his office is closely monitoring foreign capital flows into the defense sector, particularly from China.\nFor context: The new NDAA codified a Trump-backed expansion of the U.S. outbound investment rule, adding additional “countries of concern” and broadening the list of national-security-related transactions it covers.\nCadenazzi’s team supports the Committee on Foreign Investment in the United States, the interagency panel that reviews foreign acquisitions of U.S. companies for national security risks. It also maintains the so-called 1260H list of Chinese-military-affiliated companies operating in the U.S.\n“This year, we are intensifying our analysis under our Section 805 authorities, targeting companies that do business with 1260H-listed entities,” Cadenazzi said. “We urge all defense firms to assess these relationships internally and get ahead of potential risks.”\nRead more from The Brief:\n2026 NDAA Fortifies Outbound Investment Rule, Fentanyl Enforcement, China ListsWhite House’s 2025 National Security Strategy Puts Supply Chains on the Front LinesHypersonic Secret: ‘China’s MIT’ Worked with U.S. while Developing Weapons to Use Against It‘The Robot Dog’s Time to Kill’: At China’s Star Robotics Firm, the Military Ties Keep MountingBack to The BriefLatest on KharonWho Are the Houthis? How Iran Funds the Militia Group Now Striking Saudi Arabia.Iran’s Attacks on U.S. Water Systems Look Less Like a New Terror Front and More Like a PsyopWhat Will the Latest Trump-Xi Summit Bring? Four Experts Set the Stakes.Kharon ReadbookWeekly insights delivered to your inbox.First Name*Last Name*Email address*Thank you for subscribing.Subscribe","content_cn":"由哈德逊研究所提供\n供应链\n2026年2月12日\n3分钟\n五角大楼正在重建供应链以对抗中国。它愿意承担一些“风险”。\n作者：Jane Tang\n一名高级官员本周在华盛顿的一场活动上表示，五角大楼正在调整武器采购方式，努力修复因劳动力短缺、工厂老化以及中国在全球制造业中的主导地位而承受压力的脆弱国防供应链。\n国防部负责工业基础政策的助理部长迈克尔·卡德纳齐表示，国防部不再把资金分散到短期合同上，而是计划对从导弹系统到高超音速武器等关键生产线进行更大规模的多年期投资，以稳定需求并释放私人投资。\n“我们正在接受采购风险，以降低作战风险。”卡德纳齐周二在哈德逊研究所发表讲话时说。\n卡德纳齐在私营部门工作了20年后于9月加入五角大楼。他发表上述讲话之际，国防部正在实施11月宣布的《采购改革》战略，以及《2026年国防授权法案》（NDAA）。这项规模达9010亿美元的法案授予五角大楼广泛的新权限，以重建美国国防工业基础。\n美国制造业的关键缺口\n政府问责局的报告反映出该工业基础多年来的一些不足：陆军车辆一直未能达到战备目标，陆军弹药去向长期未被追踪，而F-35战斗机平均延迟238天交付。\n“过去十年，我们在国防工业基础（DIB）上投入了数十亿美元。”卡德纳齐说，“10年、15年前存在的问题有时反而更严重了。这是一项糟糕的投资。”\n总体而言：卡德纳齐指出，中国约占全球制造业产出的30%，而美国为17%；中国的造船能力约为美国的200倍。这一差距凸显了特朗普政府推动制造业回流或“近岸化”的努力，其中最突出的是通过关税实现这一目标，正如政府在12月发布的新《国家安全战略》中所指出的那样。\n但美国的紧迫感出现之际，国防工业的劳动力仍承受压力。时任国防部长办公室制造技术主管的基思·德弗里斯于2023年9月表示，美国制造业有超过80万个职位空缺，预计未来十年将短缺400万个职位。卡德纳齐周二再次引用了这两个数字。\n正如他后来在与哈德逊研究所高级研究员娜迪娅·沙德洛的交谈中所说，问题不仅在于招聘，还在于改变文化观念。\n“25年前，他们会说：‘你得上大学。’”卡德纳齐说，“我们需要做的是说服那些家长，让他们进一步说服自己的孩子，相信（从事制造业职业）对他们来说是一件好事。”\n他说，这需要“全美国共同努力，推动我们看待国防生产方式发生根本性转变”。\n为何重要：中国的制造业产出“使他们能够扩大生产和交付规模，不仅是在海军领域，而且覆盖多个领域”，卡德纳齐说。\n“我们需要截然不同的结果，这意味着我们需要截然不同的方法。”\n多年期合同，更有针对性的投资\n其中一种方法是重新思考五角大楼采购武器的方式，通过接受更大的前期承诺来确保\n更快、更可靠的交付。Cadenazzi说，战略的核心是通过签订为期五至七年的合同来稳定国防供应链，旨在减少可能打击私人投资积极性的不确定性。\n“这里的关键要素是需求信号，”他说。“如果资金今年增加、明年又减少，谁会愿意押注于此？”\n聚焦：正如白宫在新NDAA通过前所宣传的那样，这正是该法案赋予权力的一项战略。\n例如，第804条授权从2026财年开始，为主要武器系统和弹药签订多年期合同。白宫在12月表示，这种做法取代了传统的年度合同周期，“提供扩大工业产能所需的确定性，并为纳税人节省成本”。国防部工业基础政策助理部长Michael Cadenazzi周二与Hudson研究所高级研究员Nadia Schadlow交谈。（Hudson研究所提供）重点：Cadenazzi说，与其把有限资金分散到许多项目上——这种做法几乎没有产生持久影响——国防部将把重点放在优先供应链中更大规模、更长期的投资上，包括固体火箭发动机、关键矿产和电池。他说，国防部还旨在修复能源材料工业基础的“脆弱性”，该行业生产包括炸药和推进剂所用化学品在内的产品。\n“我们过去在真正需要5500万美元时，只投入500万美元，”Cadenazzi说。“我们正在减少像涂花生酱一样摊薄资金的做法，专注于更少、更大的成功。”\n审查外国投资\n他说，除生产能力外，他的办公室还在密切监测流入国防领域的外国资本，尤其是来自中国的资本。\n背景：新NDAA将特朗普支持的美国对外投资规则扩展编入法典，增加了其他“受关注国家”，并扩大了其涵盖的涉国家安全交易清单。\nCadenazzi的团队支持美国外国投资委员会，该跨部门机构负责审查外国收购美国企业是否带来国家安全风险。该团队还维护所谓的1260H名单，其中列有在美国运营的中国军方关联企业。\n“今年，我们正根据第805条授权加强分析，重点关注与列入1260H名单实体开展业务的公司，”Cadenazzi说。“我们敦促所有国防企业在内部评估这些关系，并提前防范潜在风险。”\n阅读《简报》的更多内容：\n2026年NDAA强化对外投资规则、芬太尼执法和中国名单白宫2025年国家安全战略将供应链置于前线高超音速机密：“中国的MIT”在开发用于对付美国的武器时曾与美国合作“机器狗的击杀时刻”：在中国星际机器人公司，其军事联系持续增加返回《简报》Kharon最新消息胡塞武装是谁？伊朗如何资助这个如今正在袭击沙特阿拉伯的民兵组织。伊朗对美国供水系统的袭击，与其说像新的恐怖战线，不如说更像一场心理战。特朗普—习近平最新峰会将带来什么？四位专家设定议题。Kharon读本每周洞察，直达您的收件箱。名*姓*电子邮箱*感谢订阅。","publish_source":"kharon.com","publish_time":"2026-02-12T11:27:35-08:00"}},{"id":"news-480","ktid":1055920,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1055920","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"五角大楼将中国精英高校列入“问题”名单，扩大资助禁令","title_en":"Pentagon Names Elite Chinese Universities to ‘Problematic’ List, Broadening Funding Bans | Kharon","summary_cn":"美国国防部上周将复旦大学、上海交通大学和山东大学三所中国知名民用研究型大学列入第1286条“问题活动”外国机构名单，该名单已扩展至中俄伊130家机构。自2026财年起，五角大楼禁止资助涉及名单实体的基础研究，涵盖拨款、合同及联邦援助。文章援引卡隆公司研究，分析三所高校与中国军事现代化及军民融合的联系，并讨论美中“黑名单之战”的监管策略。","summary_en":"The U.S. Department of Defense last week added Fudan University, Shanghai Jiao Tong University and Shandong University to its Section 1286 list of foreign institutions tied to \"problematic activity,\" which now covers 130 entities across China, Russia and Iran. Since fiscal year 2026, the Pentagon is barred from funding fundamental research involving listed entities, covering grants, contracts and federal assistance. Drawing on Kharon research, the article examines the three universities' ties to China's military modernization and military-civil fusion, and discusses the U.S.-China \"war of blacklists.\"","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:12:33.891139+00:00","url":"https://www.kharon.com/brief/dod-china-universities-1286-list","content":"Kharon illustration / Adobe StockResearch SecurityJul 29, 20264 minutesPentagon Names Elite Chinese Universities to ‘Problematic’ List, Broadening Funding BansBy Jane TangThe Department of Defense last week added three of China’s most prominent civilian research universities — Fudan University, Shanghai Jiao Tong University, and Shandong University — to its list of foreign institutions tied to “problematic activity” that could threaten U.S. national security.\nThat Section 1286 list, which has grown to include 130 institutions across China, Russia, and Iran, coincides with a growing focus in Washington on the breadth of China’s military-civil fusion ecosystem.\nAnd the list’s designations now carry tangible consequences for U.S. research institutions.\nWhat it means: Since the start of fiscal year 2026, the Pentagon is barred from funding fundamental research involving any entity on the expanding 1286 list.\nThat ban covers grants, contracts, and other federal assistance to universities, prohibits the use of equipment from listed entities, and applies to all employees at recipient institutions. DOD has warned researchers, too, that collaborating with anyone affiliated with a listed entity “constitutes a compliance risk and may negatively impact their eligibility for federal funding.”\n“The Department of War is strengthening its commitment to protect taxpayer-funded research and preserving the integrity of the American scientific enterprise,” Undersecretary for Research and Engineering Emil Michael said in announcing the update, using the Trump administration’s preferred name for the department.\nChina’s Ministry of Commerce criticized the U.S. for “generalizing the concept of national security” and “politicizing, weaponizing and instrumentalizing scientific cooperation.”\nWhat Kharon’s research shows: The three newly listed civilian universities all connect to China’s military-modernization efforts, from hypersonic weapons to advanced semiconductors.\nRedefining Research Security Risks\nThe 1286 list initially focused heavily on institutions tied to China’s defense-industrial base, including its state-backed “Seven Sons of National Defense” and a small number of academies run by the People’s Liberation Army (PLA), in addition to a handful of Russian and Iranian institutions.\nSubsequent updates added dozens of service academies and defense laboratories, before the list expanded to cover Chinese civilian universities starting last year.\n“The new listings show that the Department of War recognizes the depth of cooperation between Chinese civilian academies and the military,” said Timothy Heath, founder of the research firm Perceptum, who served for years as a China analyst for RAND and the U.S. military. “As that collaboration deepens, civilian universities and research institutes increasingly become research-security concerns for Washington.”Fudan University and Shanghai Fudan Microelectronics Group hold a strategic-cooperation signing ceremony in July 2025. The U.S. named the latter to the Entity List two months later, for procuring U.S. components in support of China's “military modernization.” (Shanghai Fudan Microelectronics Group)It’s also reflective of Washington’s typical regulatory approach, said Nazak Nikakhtar, chair of the national security practice at the D.C. law firm Wiley and a former Commerce Department undersecretary.\n“When the government first exercises this [type of] legal authority, it tends to use it narrowly with easily defensible targets, in order to understand the litigation risks and the industry reactions, and then gradually the restrictions become more expansive,” Nikakhtar said. “The government tends to go after the low-hanging fruit first, and then it broadens restrictions to have greater impact.”\nTop Universities, Military Ties\nTwo of the newly listed schools best illustrate how Chinese civilian institutions and the military can intersect.\nShanghai Jiao Tong University (SJTU), China’s self-styled MIT, was one of the first nine schools in “Project 985,” a state initiative to build a Chinese Ivy League capable of competing with the West.\nLast year, Kharon reported that a national laboratory inside SJTU’s School of Materials Science and Engineering was involved in hypersonic weapons research, including for components of anti-ship missiles that state-run CCTV dubbed the “carrier killer.” At the same time, SJTU and the lab maintained joint institutes and research ties with American universities and companies.\nIn all, at least five SJTU schools hold licenses that specifically recognize their contributions to “military quality” research and products.Fudan University, a fellow Project 985 school, drives chip research at state-funded labs and forms partnerships that then funnel breakthroughs into commercial production. It’s based in Shanghai, in the heart of the industrial cluster that China is counting on to build a self-sufficient chip industry and blunt the effects of U.S. export controls.\nZoom in: The university’s School of Microelectronics cites “military-civil fusion” and “major national strategic needs” as guiding goals.\nIn 1998, Fudan’s laboratory dedicated to integrated circuits spun off a company called Shanghai Fudan Microelectronics Group, which has maintained ties to the university since. Last July, they signed a strategic cooperation agreement they said would “raise the country’s competitiveness in core chip technology and safeguard the security of the nation’s supply chains in strategic core fields.”\nMeanwhile, according to corporate disclosures and reports from Chinese banks, the company’s downstream customers include the PLA and Entity-Listed vendors, among them the state chip foundry SMIC. In September, the U.S. Commerce Department added Fudan Microelectronics to the Entity List itself, for “acquiring and attempting to acquire U.S.-origin items in support of China’s military modernization” and for supplying its military, government, and security apparatus directly.\nThe designation said the company also had supplied technology to Russian military end-users.Analysis: “While neither university is a military academy, under China’s military-civil fusion strategy, both play important roles in generating the research, technologies, and technical talent that can support the modernization of the PLA alongside civilian economic and scientific development,” said Richard Fisher, a senior fellow at the International Assessment and Strategy Center and the author of “China’s Military Modernization: Building for Regional and Global Reach.”\nThe Bigger U.S.-China Picture\nThe Section 1286 update came just weeks after the Pentagon had expanded another list, its Section 1260H designations of “Chinese military companies.” China had sanctioned U.S. companies in response, marking another round of tit-for-tat measures.\nThe two U.S. lists, Nikakhtar said, reflect the same strategy: using “name and shame” designations to signal risks, while imposing narrower compliance requirements than tools such as the Commerce Department’s Entity List.\nBy framing the measures as security-related actions rather than trade restrictions, she added, U.S. officials also can more easily defend them in legal and diplomatic settings, while preserving regulatory flexibility.\n“This is very much a war of blacklists between China and the U.S.,” Nikakhtar said, “with both sides still exercising some restraint.”\nYu-Jie Liao contributed research to this report.\nRead more from The Brief:\nWhy Did the U.S. Label Alibaba as a Chinese Military Company? This Joint Venture Offers a Clue.China’s New Sanctions Arsenal Is Challenging the U.S. — and Creating a Business ‘Nightmare’A Chinese Firm Sidestepped U.S. Sanctions by Getting a New Owner (with the Same Surname)Back to The BriefLatest on KharonWho Are the Houthis? How Iran Funds the Militia Group Now Striking Saudi Arabia.Iran’s Attacks on U.S. Water Systems Look Less Like a New Terror Front and More Like a PsyopWhat Will the Latest Trump-Xi Summit Bring? Four Experts Set the Stakes.Kharon ReadbookWeekly insights delivered to your inbox.First Name*Last Name*Email address*Thank you for subscribing.Subscribe","content_cn":"Kharon 插图 / Adobe Stock研究安全2026年7月29日4分钟五角大楼将中国顶尖高校列入“有问题”名单，扩大资金禁令作者：Jane Tang美国国防部上周将中国三所最知名的民用研究型大学——复旦大学、上海交通大学和山东大学——列入其与可能威胁美国国家安全的“有问题活动”有关联的外国机构名单。\n这份第1286条名单已扩大至涵盖中国、俄罗斯和伊朗的130家机构，同时华盛顿日益关注中国军民融合生态系统的广泛程度。\n而该名单的认定如今对美国研究机构带来了实质性后果。\n这意味着什么：自2026财年开始以来，五角大楼被禁止资助涉及不断扩大的1286名单中任何实体的基础研究。\n该禁令涵盖向大学提供的拨款、合同和其他联邦援助，禁止使用名单所列实体的设备，并适用于受资助机构的所有员工。国防部还警告研究人员，与任何隶属于所列实体的人合作“构成合规风险，并可能对其获得联邦资金的资格产生负面影响”。\n“战争部正在加强其保护纳税人资助研究、维护美国科学事业完整性的承诺，”负责研究与工程的副部长Emil Michael在宣布更新时表示，并使用了特朗普政府对该部门偏好的名称。\n中国商务部批评美国“泛化国家安全概念”以及“将科学合作政治化、武器化和工具化”。\nKharon的研究显示：这三所新列入名单的民用大学均与中国的军事现代化努力有关联，涉及从高超音速武器到先进半导体等领域。\n重新界定研究安全风险\n1286名单最初主要聚焦于与中国国防工业基础相关联的机构，包括获得国家支持的“国防七子”和少数由中国人民解放军（PLA）运营的学院，以及少数俄罗斯和伊朗机构。\n后续更新增加了数十所军种院校和国防实验室，此后该名单自去年开始扩大至涵盖中国民用大学。\n“新的列名表明，战争部认识到中国民用院校与军方之间合作的深度，”研究公司Perceptum创始人Timothy Heath表示；他曾多年担任兰德公司和美国军方的中国问题分析师。“随着这种合作不断深化，民用大学和研究机构日益成为华盛顿的研究安全关切。”复旦大学与上海复旦微电子集团于2025年7月举行战略合作签约仪式。两个月后，美国将后者列入实体清单，理由是其采购美国零部件以支持中国“军事现代化”。（上海复旦微电子集团）\n这也反映了华盛顿典型的监管方式，华盛顿特区律师事务所Wiley国家安全业务负责人、前商务部副部长Nazak Nikakhtar表示。\n“当政府首次行使这种[类型的]法律权力时，它往往会以狭窄的方式使用，并以容易\n可辩护的目标，以便了解诉讼风险和行业反应，然后限制措施才逐步变得更加广泛，”Nikakhtar说。“政府往往先针对容易下手的目标，然后再扩大限制范围，以产生更大影响。”\n顶尖大学、军事联系\n两所新列入名单的学校最能说明中国民用机构与军方如何可能交织在一起。\n上海交通大学（SJTU），这所中国自称的麻省理工学院，是“985工程”最初九所学校之一；这是一项旨在建设能够与西方竞争的中国常春藤盟校的国家倡议。\n去年，Kharon报道称，上海交大材料科学与工程学院内的一家国家实验室参与了高超音速武器研究，包括用于反舰导弹部件的研究；国营央视曾将这类导弹称为“航母杀手”。与此同时，上海交大及该实验室与美国大学和企业保持着联合研究院及研究联系。\n总体而言，上海交大至少有五个学院持有明确认可其对“军工质量”研究和产品所作贡献的许可证。复旦大学是另一所“985工程”高校，在国家资助的实验室推动芯片研究，并建立合作关系，继而将突破性成果导入商业生产。它位于上海——中国正指望该市核心工业集群建设自给自足的芯片产业，并削弱美国出口管制影响的中心地带。\n聚焦：该大学微电子学院将“军民融合”和“国家重大战略需求”列为指导目标。\n1998年，复旦大学专注于集成电路的实验室孵化出一家名为上海复旦微电子集团的公司，此后该公司一直与大学保持联系。去年7月，双方签署了一项战略合作协议，称这将“提升国家在核心芯片技术领域的竞争力，并维护战略核心领域国家供应链安全”。\n与此同时，根据公司披露和中国银行的报告，该公司的下游客户包括中国人民解放军（PLA）和被列入实体清单的供应商，其中包括国有芯片代工厂中芯国际（SMIC）。9月，美国商务部将复旦微电子本身列入实体清单，理由是其“为支持中国军事现代化而获取并试图获取美国原产物项”，并直接向其军方、政府和安全机构供货。\n该认定还称，该公司曾向俄罗斯军事最终用户供应技术。分析：“尽管两所大学都不是军事院校，但在中国军民融合战略之下，两者都在产生可支持解放军现代化的研究、技术和技术人才方面发挥重要作用，同时也服务于民用经济与科学发展，”国际评估与战略中心高级研究员、著有《中国军事现代化：建设区域和全球投射能力》的Richard Fisher说。\n更广泛的美中图景\n第1286条更新出台仅数周前，五角大楼刚刚扩展了另一份名单，即其根据第1260H条作出的“中国军工企业”认定。中国随后制裁了美国企业，标志着又一轮针锋相对的措施。\nNikakhtar说，这两份美国名单反映了同一策略：利用“点名批评”认定来传递风险信号，同时施加更狭窄的\n比商务部的实体清单等工具更严格的合规要求。\n她补充说，通过将这些措施界定为与安全相关的行动，而非贸易限制，美国官员也能更容易地在法律和外交场合为其辩护，同时保留监管灵活性。\nNikakhtar说：“这在很大程度上是中国与美国之间的一场黑名单战争，双方仍都在保持一定克制。”\nYu-Jie Liao为本报道提供了研究支持。\n阅读更多《The Brief》报道：\n美国为何将阿里巴巴列为中国军工企业？这家合资企业提供了一个线索。中国的新制裁武器库正在挑战美国——并制造一场商业“噩梦”一家中国公司通过更换新所有者（姓氏却相同）规避了美国制裁返回《The Brief》Kharon最新报道胡塞武装是谁？伊朗如何资助如今正袭击沙特阿拉伯的这一民兵组织。伊朗对美国供水系统的攻击，看起来不像新的恐怖主义战线，更像一场心理战。最新的特朗普—习近平峰会将带来什么？四位专家评估其利害关系。Kharon Readbook每周洞见，发送至您的收件箱。名字*姓氏*电子邮箱地址*感谢您的订阅。订阅","publish_source":"kharon.com","publish_time":"2026-07-29T11:29:57-07:00"}},{"id":"news-642","ktid":1055920,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1055920","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"欧盟强迫劳动法规指南范围广泛，企业应如何合规","title_en":"The EU’s Forced Labour Regulation Guidelines Are Sweeping. Here’s How To Comply. | Kharon","summary_cn":"欧盟委员会发布《强迫劳动法规》指南，规定在欧盟运营的企业须确保产品不涉及强迫劳动，自2027年12月起对不合规行为实施处罚，包括将“受污染”产品撤出欧盟市场。文章介绍法规运作机制、市场禁令与罚款后果，并详述基于OECD框架的六步尽职调查最佳实践，以及私营、国家实施和强迫童工三类风险的不同应对要求。","summary_en":"The European Commission published guidelines on its Forced Labour Regulation, requiring businesses operating in the EU to ensure products are free from forced labor, with penalties starting December 2027 including removal of \"tainted\" products from the EU market. The article explains how the regulation works, market bans and fines, and details a six-step OECD-based due diligence framework, plus differing responses for privately imposed, state-imposed and forced child labor risks.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:19:03.577319+00:00","url":"https://www.kharon.com/brief/eu-forced-labour-regulation-compliance","content":"Kharon illustration / Adobe StockForced LaborJul 07, 20264 minutesThe EU’s New Forced Labor Guidelines Are Sweeping. Here’s How To Comply.By Alberto BallesterosThe European Commission published long-awaited guidelines last week on its forthcoming Forced Labour Regulation (FLR), putting substantial meat on the bones of one of the bloc’s most consequential trade rules in years.\nThe rule mandates that businesses operating in the EU ensure their products are free from forced labor. It then establishes penalties, starting in December 2027, for those that don’t comply, starting with the removal of any “tainted” products from the EU market.\nThe new FLR guidelines give companies a roadmap for how to avoid supply-chain disruptions — or worse.\nHow it will work: The FLR will apply to all products exported from or placed on the EU market, including through online retailers, regardless of where in the world they were made.\nThe regulations empower the EU Commission and national authorities to initiate investigations if they suspect a product is made using forced labor.\nBusinesses will have to be ready to provide all information authorities require, such as details on their supply chains, their due-diligence efforts, any relevant transactions, and working conditions at the site where the suspected forced labor took place. If a company fails to cooperate, the guidelines say that can contribute toward establishing a violation.\nIn other words: Companies with EU operations can’t afford to wait for a knock on the door before taking these regulations seriously.\nThe Consequences: Market Bans and Fines\nWhen forced labor is identified in a product on the market, the EU says, authorities will issue a ban-violation decision, which will involve:\na prohibition on selling that product in the EU market or exporting it elsewhere.an order to withdraw any such product from the EU market.an order to dispose of those products or any specific, replaceable parts that are tainted with forced labor.\nSellers beware: Crucially, the EU market bans will apply to the product itself, not just to the companies under investigation.\nThat means any operator placing the product in question on the EU market, even one uninvolved in the original probe, can be affected by the same ruling. That broad scope is designed to prevent circumvention.\nFurther penalties: Failure to comply with a ban-violation decision can trigger fines.\nEach member state has “discretion” to decide how those penalties will be calculated, the EU says, but the “gravity and duration” of non-compliance with a ban are the main factors that will be used. The company’s revenue, the total value of the products, and any previous instances of non-compliance can influence the final amount as well.Best Practices to Address Forced Labor Risks\nThe EU guidelines detail a due-diligence framework, originally designed by the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD), to help businesses assess and address risks. It consists of six complementary steps:\n“Integrate forced labour due diligence into company policies and risk management systems.”“Identify and assess forced labour risks in the company’s operations, supply chains and business relationships.”“Prevent, mitigate and bring to an end forced labour risks.”“Monitor and assess implementation and results.”“Communicate [publicly] how risks are addressed.”“Provide or cooperate in remediation” when necessary.\nZoom out: Following that exact framework isn’t required. But the potential commercial disruption of products’ withdrawal from the market means robust due diligence will be the most practical insurance policy available.\nZoom in: The third step above includes developing corrective action plans and adjusting business practices to prevent or mitigate identified forced labor risks.\nOne example: building “due diligence expectations” into contracts with suppliers.\nBut the right response under the FLR can depend on the type of forced labor risk that’s involved.\nWhat the Three Categories of Forced Labor Require\nThe EU guidelines segment forced labor into:\nprivately imposed forced labor, which the EU called the most common type, spanning industry, services, agriculture, and domestic work;state-imposed forced labor;and forced child labor.\nWhy it matters: When forced labor is imposed by private actors, the EU expects businesses to use their commercial “leverage” to push suppliers or partners toward corrective action. Disengaging from the relationship should be “a last resort.”\nThat guidance applies in cases of state-imposed forced labor (SIFL), too. But SIFL cases can leave companies with little to no corrective leverage, since the coercion originates from a government rather than a supplier, and the usual mechanics of corporate due diligence tend to break down.\nAudits in high-risk countries are unlikely to provide impartial evidence that a product or supply chain is free of forced labor, the EU notes. In their place, it recommends that companies and authorities scrutinize possible SIFL risks by relying on independent sourcing: “desktop research, reporting from international organisations, expert risk analysis, and credible civil society data.”\nRemediation also becomes harder to achieve in areas where SIFL is present. The EU guidelines suggest that suspending or terminating a contract may be the only realistic response.The EU is not alone in scrutinizing state-linked forced labor risk. In the U.S., the Uyghur Forced Labor Prevention Act (UFLPA) specifically blocks the import of goods produced wholly or in part in Xinjiang, China — where forced labor risk stems from state-run programs — unless a company provides clear and convincing evidence that they were not made using forced labor. The Brief has previously detailed red flags for forced labor risks from Xinjiang-based companies, such as references to “poverty alleviation” or “economic revitalization” programs, connections to sanctioned entities like Xinjiang Aid, or the use of language promoting ethnic assimilation.The Bottom Line\nWith the EU regulation coming online in December 2027, companies have less than 18 months left to prepare. Those that get ahead of their forced labor exposure now will be far better positioned to demonstrate compliance than those waiting to see how enforcement unfolds.\nRead more on forced labor:\nEU Aims to Upend China Dependency with New Supply Chain QuotasTracking Shifts in China’s Rhetoric Around Xinjiang Forced Labor Red FlagsHow UFLPA Risks from Xinjiang Flow into Major Automakers’ Car SeatsBack to The BriefLatest on KharonWho Are the Houthis? How Iran Funds the Militia Group Now Striking Saudi Arabia.Iran’s Attacks on U.S. Water Systems Look Less Like a New Terror Front and More Like a PsyopWhat Will the Latest Trump-Xi Summit Bring? Four Experts Set the Stakes.Kharon ReadbookWeekly insights delivered to your inbox.First Name*Last Name*Email address*Thank you for subscribing.Subscribe","content_cn":"Kharon 插图 / Adobe Stock\n强迫劳动\n2026年7月7日\n4分钟\n欧盟新的强迫劳动指南涵盖广泛领域。以下是合规方法。\n作者：Alberto Ballesteros\n\n欧洲委员会上周发布了备受期待的、针对即将出台的《强迫劳动条例》（FLR）的指南，为这一欧盟多年来最具影响力的贸易规则之一提供了实质性细节。\n\n该规则要求在欧盟运营的企业确保其产品不涉及强迫劳动。该规则还规定，从2027年12月开始，对不合规者实施处罚，首先是将任何“受污染”的产品从欧盟市场撤下。\n\n新的FLR指南为企业提供了路线图，帮助其避免供应链中断，或更糟糕的后果。\n\n运作方式：FLR将适用于所有出口到欧盟市场或投放到欧盟市场的产品，包括通过在线零售商销售的产品，无论这些产品在世界何地制造。\n\n如果怀疑某产品使用了强迫劳动，欧盟委员会和各国主管机关有权启动调查。\n\n企业必须准备好提供主管机关要求的所有信息，例如供应链详情、尽职调查工作、任何相关交易，以及疑似发生强迫劳动地点的工作条件。指南称，如果企业未能合作，这可能会促成违规行为的认定。\n\n换句话说：在欧盟开展业务的企业不能等到监管部门找上门时，才开始认真对待这些规定。\n\n后果：市场禁令与罚款\n\n欧盟表示，当发现市场上的某件产品涉及强迫劳动时，主管机关将发布禁令违规决定，其中包括：\n\n禁止在欧盟市场销售该产品或将其出口到其他地方。\n\n命令将任何此类产品从欧盟市场撤回。\n\n命令处置这些产品，或处置任何受到强迫劳动污染的特定可替换部件。\n\n销售者注意：至关重要的是，欧盟市场禁令将针对产品本身，而不仅仅是接受调查的企业。\n\n这意味着，任何将相关产品投放到欧盟市场的经营者，即使未参与最初的调查，也可能受到同一裁决的影响。这一广泛适用范围旨在防止规避。\n\n进一步处罚：不遵守禁令违规决定可能触发罚款。\n\n欧盟表示，各成员国可“酌情”决定这些处罚的计算方式，但不遵守禁令的“严重程度和持续时间”将是主要考量因素。企业收入、产品总价值以及以往不合规的情况，也可能影响最终金额。\n\n应对强迫劳动风险的最佳实践\n\n欧盟指南详细介绍了一个最初由经济合作与发展组织（OECD）设计的尽职调查框架，帮助企业评估和应对风险。该框架由六个相互补充的步骤组成：\n\n“将强迫劳动尽职调查纳入公司政策和风险管理体系。”\n\n“识别并评估公司运营、供应链和商业关系中的强迫劳动风险。”\n\n“预防、减轻并终止强迫劳动风险。”\n\n“监测并评估实施情况和结果。”\n\n“公开说明如何应对风险。”\n\n必要时“提供补救措施或参与补救”。\n\n概括而言：并不要求严格遵循这一框架。\n但产品退出市场可能造成的商业冲击意味着，稳健的尽职调查将是现有最切实可行的保险政策。\n放大来看：上述第三步包括制定纠正行动计划，并调整商业做法，以防止或减轻已识别的强迫劳动风险。\n一个例子是：将“尽职调查要求”纳入与供应商签订的合同。\n但根据《强迫劳动条例》（FLR），正确的应对措施可能取决于所涉及的强迫劳动风险类型。\n强迫劳动三大类别的要求\n欧盟指南将强迫劳动分为：\n私人施加的强迫劳动，欧盟称其为最常见的类型，涵盖工业、服务业、农业和家政工作；国家施加的强迫劳动；以及童工强迫劳动。\n为何重要：当强迫劳动由私人行为者施加时，欧盟希望企业利用其商业“影响力”，推动供应商或合作伙伴采取纠正行动。退出这种关系应当是“最后手段”。\n该指导同样适用于国家施加的强迫劳动（SIFL）案件。但SIFL案件可能使企业几乎没有纠正影响力，因为胁迫源自政府而非供应商，而企业尽职调查的通常机制往往会失灵。\n欧盟指出，在高风险国家开展的审计不太可能提供产品或供应链不存在强迫劳动的公正证据。作为替代方案，欧盟建议企业和主管部门依靠独立来源来审查可能存在的SIFL风险：“案头研究、国际组织的报告、专家风险分析以及可信的公民社会数据。”\n在存在SIFL的地区，实现补救也会变得更加困难。欧盟指南建议，暂停或终止合同可能是唯一现实的应对措施。欧盟并非唯一一个审查与国家有关联的强迫劳动风险的机构。在美国，《维吾尔强迫劳动预防法》（UFLPA）明确禁止进口全部或部分在中国新疆生产的商品——强迫劳动风险源自国家运营的项目——除非企业提供清晰且令人信服的证据，证明这些商品并非使用强迫劳动制造。《简报》此前已详细介绍了新疆企业强迫劳动风险的警示信号，例如提及“扶贫”或“经济振兴”项目、与新疆援助等受制裁实体存在联系，或使用推动民族同化的语言。\n底线\n随着欧盟法规将于2027年12月生效，企业准备的时间已不足18个月。现在就掌握自身强迫劳动风险敞口的企业，将比那些等待观察执法如何展开的企业更有能力证明合规。\n进一步阅读强迫劳动相关内容：\n欧盟拟通过新的供应链配额打破对中国的依赖\n追踪中国围绕新疆强迫劳动警示信号的措辞变化\nUFLPA对新疆风险如何传导至主要汽车制造商的汽车座椅\n返回《简报》\nKharon最新动态\n谁是胡塞武装？伊朗如何资助这个如今袭击沙特阿拉伯的民兵组织。\n伊朗对美国水务系统的攻击看起来不像新的恐怖战线，更像是一场心理战\n最新的特朗普—习近平峰会将带来什么？四位专家列出关键问题。\nKharon读本\n每周洞察直达您的收件箱。\n名*姓*电子邮箱\n感谢您的订阅。\n订阅","publish_source":"kharon.com","publish_time":"2026-07-06T13:56:17-07:00"}},{"id":"news-519","ktid":1055920,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1055920","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"欧盟第21轮制裁方案冻结石油价格上限，对俄实施四年来最多列名","title_en":"EU’s 21st Sanctions Package Freezes Oil Price Cap, Hits Russia with Most Listings in 4 Years | Kharon","summary_cn":"欧盟通过第21轮对俄制裁方案，共列名218个实体与个人，为四年来规模最大，重点针对俄金融与能源领域。方案将俄石油价格上限冻结在每桶44.10美元一年，并首次制裁协助俄“影子船队”的船舶。此外制裁94家俄银行和4家与A7网络相关的加密平台，对33家俄银行及4家外国银行实施交易禁令。因希腊反对，全面禁止运输俄液化天然气的条款被删除。","summary_en":"The EU approved its 21st sanctions package against Russia, designating 218 entities and individuals—its largest round in four years—targeting Russia's financial and energy sectors. The package freezes the Russian oil price cap at $44.10 per barrel for another year and, for the first time, sanctions vessels assisting Moscow's oil-shipping shadow fleet. It also sanctions 94 Russian banks and four crypto platforms linked to the A7 network, and imposes transaction bans on 33 Russian and four foreign banks. A full ban on transporting Russian LNG was dropped under Greek pressure.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:15:43.657926+00:00","url":"https://www.kharon.com/brief/eu-russia-21st-sanctions-package-oil-price-cap","content":"Kharon illustration / Adobe StockSanctionsJul 23, 20263 minutesEU’s 21st Sanctions Package Freezes Oil Price Cap, Hits Russia with Most Listings in 4 YearsBy Alberto BallesterosThe EU approved its 21st package of sanctions against Russia on Thursday, overcoming its latest infighting to land its largest number of blacklistings in four years, with Russia’s financial and energy sectors the primary targets.\nBesides the package’s 218 designations, the bloc agreed to freeze the Russian oil price cap at its current level for another year, a measure intended to blunt Moscow’s revenues as the Iran war sends oil prices surging again.\nFor the first time, the EU also sanctioned vessels assisting Moscow’s oil-shipping shadow fleet, expanding beyond targeting the fleet itself.\n“At a time when Ukraine has built military momentum, our sanctions continue to weaken the economic foundations of Russia’s war effort,” EU Commission President Ursula von der Leyen posted on social media.\nOther elements, however, were stripped out from the package — the first under Ireland’s EU leadership — under pressure from various member states. Most prominent: Greece’s holdup around providing services for Russian liquefied natural gas.\nHere’s what to know.\nTargeting Russian Banks and Cryptocurrency\nThe new EU package sanctions 94 Russian banks and 4 cryptocurrency platforms linked to the A7 network, which had already been targeted in previous sanctions designations by the EU, U.K., and U.S.\nIt also placed 33 Russian and four foreign banks under a transaction ban and prohibited transactions with 14 cryptocurrency platforms in the UAE, Georgia, Panama, the UAE, Marshall Islands, Kyrgyzstan, and Belarus. That means these entities will not be able to send or receive funds to the EU.\nKaja Kallas, the EU’s foreign affairs chief, said it was “hitting [Vladimir] Putin where it hurts most: cutting off the financial lifelines he relies on to sustain his war.”\nMeanwhile, a new authority included in the package will allow the EU to impose a full “third-country ban for crypto asset-services,” which could cut off countries deemed to be helping Russia evade sanctions through cryptocurrencies. Von der Leyen said the measure would “act as a strong deterrent.”Dive deeper: The Brief last month reported on an international network of crypto platforms openly offering ways to circumvent Western sanctions on Russia. The Oil Price Cap, LNG, and the Shadow Fleet\nBut the star of the 21st package — and the reason it could not be delayed any longer — is the freezing of the oil price cap at its current level of $44.10 per barrel for another 12 months.\nMired in debate over the package, the EU had already had to extend the most recent deadline to lock in the price cap from last week to Thursday. If that deadline had been allowed to lapse, the Russian oil price cap automatically would have updated to 15% below the average market price, which would have meant a significant wartime increase.\nOriginally, the price-cap freeze was due to last just six months. But the EU reached a compromise with the Greek government after agreeing to drop a full ban on companies’ transporting Russian LNG to third countries. Greece operates the largest merchant fleet in the world, and it argued the ban would harm its maritime services industry.\nAdditional energy-related measures include:\nsanctions against 41 more shadow fleet vessels, along with eight entities and one individual for their involvement in shadow fleet activities.the introduction of legal language to allow for sanctions on vessels providing refueling services to Russia’s shadow fleet. designations of 18 entities, including a Belarusian refinery, and one individual for supporting Russia’s oil industry. a ban on transactions with a Georgian refinery it accused of “trading and processing” Russian oil, under another new EU authority.\nRussia’s Military-Industrial Complex ... but Not Its Soldiers\nThe package also sanctioned 56 actors involved in Russia’s military-industrial complex. The majority of those (37), the EU Commission said, were directly linked to the production of long-range drones.\nExport restrictions factored in, too. The EU subjected 51 new entities — including some in China, Hong Kong, India, Kyrgyzstan, and the UAE — to heightened controls over their “support” for Russia’s military production and expanded its export ban to cover drone-related tech, certain metals, and other items that Russia’s military industry relies on.Update: China’s Commerce Ministry announced Friday that it was banning the export of dual-use items to 14 EU companies, in response to its listing of 14 mainland Chinese and Hong Kong entities. The move marks Beijing’s latest sanctions retaliation against the West.\nBut a buzzy proposal to ban current and former Russian soldiers from Europe was among the pieces that was weakened in the package’s final version, after reported objections by France and Italy. The package instead only “introduce[d] the basis for a comprehensive visa ban,” with the EU Council to decide when it will “enter into force.”\nCritical Infrastructure, Metals, and Two Names Left Out\nBulgaria again reportedly vetoed sanctions against Patriarch Kirill, a Putin ally who leads Russia’s Orthodox Church, as well as against Vagit Alekperov, the founder of sanctioned Lukoil.\nBut other assorted measures sailed through, including:\ntrade restrictions on key Russian revenue drivers, including copper and nickel ores, alkaline earth metals, and car parts.sanctioning “major actors” in Russia’s gold sector, plus more in diamonds and mining.transaction bans on two additional Russian ports and four airports. designating eight individuals for spreading Moscow’s war propaganda.\nRyan Bacic contributed to this report, which has been updated.\nRead more from The Brief:\nThe U.K. Fined Bank of Scotland for Violating Russia Sanctions. Here’s What Went Wrong.Amid Ukraine War, Europeans Power a Russian Drone Project That Looks Like a Pyramid SchemeU.K. Drops Anonymity for Sanctions Settlements in a Broader Transparency PushBack to The BriefLatest on KharonWho Are the Houthis? How Iran Funds the Militia Group Now Striking Saudi Arabia.Iran’s Attacks on U.S. Water Systems Look Less Like a New Terror Front and More Like a PsyopWhat Will the Latest Trump-Xi Summit Bring? Four Experts Set the Stakes.Kharon ReadbookWeekly insights delivered to your inbox.First Name*Last Name*Email address*Thank you for subscribing.Subscribe","content_cn":"Kharon 插图 / Adobe Stock\n制裁\n2026年7月23日\n3分钟\n欧盟第21轮制裁冻结石油价格上限，4年来以最多列名打击俄罗斯\n作者：Alberto Ballesteros\n欧盟周四批准了针对俄罗斯的第21轮制裁方案，克服了最近的内部分歧，以四年来最大规模的列入黑名单行动落地，俄罗斯的金融和能源部门成为主要目标。\n除该方案列出的218个对象外，欧盟成员国还同意将俄罗斯石油价格上限维持在当前水平，再延长一年；此举旨在遏制莫斯科的收入，因为伊朗战争再次推高了油价。\n欧盟还首次制裁协助莫斯科运营石油运输“影子船队”的船只，将打击范围扩大到船队本身之外。\n“在乌克兰已经取得军事势头之际，我们的制裁继续削弱俄罗斯战争努力的经济基础，”欧盟委员会主席乌尔苏拉·冯德莱恩在社交媒体上发文称。\n然而，在多个成员国施压下，该方案的其他内容被删去——这是爱尔兰领导欧盟期间推出的首个方案。其中最突出的是：希腊阻挠向俄罗斯液化天然气提供服务。\n以下是需要了解的内容。\n针对俄罗斯银行和加密货币\n欧盟新的制裁方案制裁了94家俄罗斯银行和4家与A7网络有关联的加密货币平台；欧盟、英国和美国此前已在制裁名单中针对该网络采取措施。\n该方案还将33家俄罗斯银行和4家外国银行列入交易禁令，并禁止与位于阿联酋、格鲁吉亚、巴拿马、阿联酋、马绍尔群岛、吉尔吉斯斯坦和白俄罗斯的14家加密货币平台进行交易。这意味着这些实体将无法向欧盟发送或接收资金。\n欧盟外交事务负责人卡娅·卡拉斯表示，此举是在“打击[弗拉基米尔]·普京最痛处：切断他赖以维持战争的金融生命线”。\n与此同时，方案中纳入的一项新授权将允许欧盟实施全面的“针对第三国的加密资产服务禁令”，这可能切断被认定为通过加密货币帮助俄罗斯规避制裁的国家。冯德莱恩表示，该措施将“发挥强有力的威慑作用”。深入了解：《简报》上月报道了一个国际加密货币平台网络，该网络公开提供规避西方对俄制裁的方法。\n石油价格上限、液化天然气与影子船队\n但第21轮方案的核心——也是不能再推迟的原因——是将石油价格上限按当前每桶44.10美元的水平冻结，再延长12个月。\n由于围绕该方案陷入争论，欧盟已经不得不将锁定价格上限的最近期限从上周延长至周四。如果任由该期限到期，俄罗斯石油价格上限将自动更新为低于市场平均价格15%的水平，这将意味着战时价格大幅上升。\n最初，价格上限冻结原定只持续六个月。但欧盟在同意放弃全面禁止企业向第三国运输俄罗斯液化天然气后，与希腊政府达成妥协。希腊拥有世界上最大的商船队，并认为该禁令会损害其海事服务业。\n其他与能源有关的措施包括：\n因参与影子船队活动，再制裁41艘影子船队船只、8个实体和1名个人\n活动：引入法律语言，以允许对向俄罗斯“影子舰队”提供加油服务的船只实施制裁。指定18个实体（包括一家白俄罗斯炼油厂）以及一名支持俄罗斯石油行业的个人为制裁对象。根据另一项新的欧盟授权，禁止与一家被指控“交易和加工”俄罗斯石油的格鲁吉亚炼油厂进行交易。\n\n俄罗斯军工复合体……但不是其士兵\n该一揽子措施还制裁了56名参与俄罗斯军工复合体的行为者。欧盟委员会表示，其中大多数（37个）与远程无人机的生产直接相关。\n\n出口限制也被纳入其中。欧盟对51个新实体（包括一些位于中国、香港、印度、吉尔吉斯斯坦和阿联酋的实体）实施更严格的管控，理由是它们“支持”俄罗斯的军事生产；同时扩大出口禁令范围，涵盖无人机相关技术、某些金属以及俄罗斯军工所依赖的其他物品。更新： 中国商务部周五宣布，作为对欧盟将中国大陆和香港的14个实体列入名单的回应，禁止向14家欧盟公司出口两用物项。此举标志着北京针对西方的最新制裁反制措施。\n\n但一项颇受关注的提议——禁止现役和前俄罗斯士兵进入欧洲——在据报道遭到法国和意大利反对后，成为该一揽子措施最终版本中被削弱的内容之一。该一揽子措施最终仅“提出全面签证禁令的依据”，由欧盟理事会决定其何时“生效”。\n\n关键基础设施、金属以及被遗漏的两个名字\n据报道，保加利亚再次否决了对普京盟友、领导俄罗斯东正教会的基里尔大牧首，以及受制裁的卢克石油创始人瓦吉特·阿列克佩罗夫实施制裁的提案。\n\n但其他各种措施均顺利通过，包括：\n\n限制对俄罗斯主要收入来源的贸易，包括铜矿和镍矿、碱土金属以及汽车零部件。制裁俄罗斯黄金行业的“主要行为者”，并扩大至钻石和采矿领域的更多对象。禁止与另外两个俄罗斯港口和四座机场进行交易。指定8名传播莫斯科战争宣传的个人为制裁对象。\n\nRyan Bacic参与了本报道，本报道已经更新。\n\n阅读《简报》的更多内容：\n\n英国因违反俄罗斯制裁规定对苏格兰银行处以罚款。问题究竟出在哪里？\n乌克兰战争期间，欧洲人为一个看似传销骗局的俄罗斯无人机项目提供动力\n英国取消制裁和解协议中的匿名性，推动更广泛的透明化\n返回《简报》\n\nKharon最新消息\n\n胡塞武装是谁？伊朗如何资助这个如今袭击沙特阿拉伯的民兵组织。\n伊朗对美国供水系统的攻击，与其说像新的恐怖战线，不如说更像一场心理战\n最新的特朗普—习近平峰会将带来什么？四位专家阐明关键问题。\n\nKharon读本\n\n每周洞察，送达您的收件箱。\n名字*姓氏*电子邮件地址*\n感谢您的订阅。\n订阅","publish_source":"kharon.com","publish_time":"2026-07-23T11:23:19-07:00"}},{"id":"news-157","ktid":1055920,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1055920","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"胡塞武装是谁？伊朗如何资助这支正打击沙特的民兵组织","title_en":"Who Are the Houthis? How Iran Funds the Militia Group Now Striking Saudi Arabia. | Kharon","summary_cn":"伊朗支持的胡塞武装近期升级对也门及沙特阿拉伯的袭击，威胁红海航运与能源市场。美国去年将其列为外国恐怖组织。卡隆公司研究显示，伊朗通过迪拜关联公司每月向胡塞提供石油，胡塞则经萨那兑换机构向阿联酋汇款支付；武器采购多通过受制裁的Al-Ridhwan兑换公司。Coin Cash等数字平台为相关资金流动提供国际通道。","summary_en":"The Iran-backed Houthis have escalated attacks in Yemen and on Saudi Arabia, threatening Red Sea shipping and energy markets. Kharon research shows Iran supplies the group with monthly oil shipments via Dubai-based firms, while the Houthis send payments through Sanaa exchange houses to UAE-based exchanges. Weapons are procured largely via the sanctioned Al-Ridhwan Exchange. Digital platforms such as Coin Cash give these funding efforts international reach.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T15:58:31.306209+00:00","url":"https://www.kharon.com/brief/houthis-saudi-arabia-strikes-iran-war","content":"Houthi Media Center/Handout via XinhuaTerrorismSep 17, 20263 minutesWho Are the Houthis? How Iran Funds the Militia Group Now Striking Saudi Arabia.By Ryan BacicThe Iran-backed Houthi militia has escalated both its campaign in Yemen and strikes on neighboring Saudi Arabia in recent days, seizing strategic locations around the Red Sea and threatening further turmoil for global shipping and energy markets.\nIsolated Iran has made militias like the Houthis, Hizballah, and others in Iraq a core piece of its security for decades. The U.S. designated the Houthis, like the others, as a foreign terrorist organization in March of last year, as the group continued to attack ships passing through the Red Sea.\nBut while Hizballah jumped to Iran’s defense quickly when the war with the U.S. and Israel began, the Houthis had mostly stuck to their insurgency in Yemen — until this month’s regional escalation.A satellite image shows a large smoke plume rising from fires Sept. 8 in Jazan City, Saudi Arabia, after Houthi drone and missile strikes tore through a Saudi Aramco tank farm along the southern Red Sea. (Gallo Images/Orbital Horizon/Copernicus Sentinel Data 2026)Big picture: The Houthi movement now controls much of Yemen’s coast along the Red Sea, a critical shipping lane for global commerce that connects the Indian Ocean and Middle East to Europe through the Suez Canal. The group’s stronghold is in Sanaa, which had been the Yemeni capital.\nHouthi missile strikes on hundreds of vessels starting in 2023, including on U.S. cargo ships, turned the Red Sea into a gauntlet, leading some major international shipping companies to reroute an extra 4,000 miles around Africa rather than risk it. Iran then adopted a similar strategy with a different Middle Eastern chokepoint: the Strait of Hormuz.\nFor months, Saudi Arabia’s East-West pipeline had allowed it to circumvent the strait and push its oil instead to ports along the Red Sea. But a drone strike on that pipeline last week, which Saudi authorities blamed on an Iran-backed militia in Iraq, has now forced the kingdom to close it for repairs.\nSaudi Arabia, a longtime regional adversary of Iran, separately claimed this week that it intercepted a Houthi drone near the holy city of Mecca, a charge the group denies.Iran’s role: supplying the Houthis with training, arms and oil.\n“U.S. officials have described Iran’s efforts to supply the Houthis with weaponry, targeting information, and military advice,” the Congressional Research Service wrote in a Feb. 20 report on the Houthis. In one representative case, the Treasury Department sanctioned five Iranian individuals “with links to Iran’s ballistic missile program” in 2018 for providing the Houthis with missiles and “related technical expertise.”\nThen, in a January designation, Treasury claimed that Tehran “both sells and provides a free monthly shipment of oil to the Houthis using Iranian-owned or affiliated companies based in Dubai.” That would probably make up a sizable chunk of the more than $2 billion in annual oil revenue, by U.S. estimates, that underpins the Houthis’ operations.\nHow the money flows: through exchanges and front companies based both in Yemen and abroad. The Houthis pay for their Iranian oil, Treasury said, “by sending money to UAE-based exchanges … via exchange companies in Sana’a.” They then sell that oil to Yemenis at “exorbitant rates.”\nThe group reportedly pays for weapons, meanwhile, through Yemeni outfits, most prominently the Houthi-affiliated (and now U.S.-sanctioned) Al-Ridhwan Exchange and Transfer Company, in Sanaa. The U.S. said Houthi leaders have used Al-Ridhwan to facilitate “numerous payments to Houthi-owned accounts outside Yemen for missile components, advanced weapon systems, and other military-grade materials.”A truck carrying Houthi-aligned former detainees arrives in a supporter-lined street in Sanaa, after they were among the more than 200 the Houthis released from prisons this month in the port city of Mokha. (Mohammed Hamoud/Getty Images)From Kharon’s research: Digital platforms give these Houthi-affiliated exchanges — and, by extension, the Houthis’ funding efforts — international reach.\nCoin Cash, for instance, is a Yemen-based entity offering crypto-fiat and fiat-crypto conversion, as well as money transfer services to get funds into and out of Yemen. According to its website, its “most common” cryptocurrency “partners” are Binance, the world’s largest crypto exchange, and Dubai-based Bybit.\nAn archived 2023 version of its website reviewed by Kharon had listed another notable partner: the Sana’a-based Al Hazmi Exchange Company, which the U.S. sanctioned in December 2024 for facilitating money laundering on the Houthis’ behalf.\nCoin Cash advertises its services on an Instagram page, where it calls itself an “Internet Marketing Service.” It also operates a website that directs prospective users to initiate transactions by contacting it through WhatsApp or Telegram.\nJane Tang and Kharon Research contributed to this report, which was adapted from a piece first published in February.\nRead more from The Brief on Iran and terrorist groups:\nTreasury Launches Sanctions ‘Operation’ Against Iran’s Trade Partners: What To Know\n‘A Very Convenient Cover’: Nearly $200M in Gold Entered Iran Through a Network Selling VegetablesFor Years Before a Charity Leader’s Arrest, Its Hamas Links Had MountedBack to The BriefLatest on KharonIran’s Attacks on U.S. Water Systems Look Less Like a New Terror Front and More Like a PsyopWhat Will the Latest Trump-Xi Summit Bring? Four Experts Set the Stakes.‘A Very Convenient Cover’: Nearly $200M in Gold Entered Iran Through a Network Selling VegetablesKharon ReadbookWeekly insights delivered to your inbox.First Name*Last Name*Email address*Thank you for subscribing.Subscribe","content_cn":"胡塞媒体中心/新华社通过X提供的资料\n恐怖主义\n2026年9月17日\n3分钟\n\n谁是胡塞武装？伊朗如何资助这个如今袭击沙特阿拉伯的民兵组织\n作者：Ryan Bacic\n\n近几日，伊朗支持的胡塞民兵组织升级了其在也门的行动以及对邻国沙特阿拉伯的袭击，占领红海周边的战略要地，并威胁全球航运和能源市场将进一步动荡。\n\n数十年来，与世隔绝的伊朗一直将胡塞武装、真主党以及伊拉克其他民兵组织作为其安全体系的核心。去年3月，美国将胡塞武装与其他组织一样列为外国恐怖组织，当时该组织仍在持续袭击通过红海的船只。\n\n但在与美国和以色列的战争开始后，真主党迅速出手为伊朗辩护；胡塞武装却基本上一直专注于其在也门的叛乱活动——直到本月地区局势升级。\n\n一张卫星图像显示，9月8日，沙特阿拉伯吉赞市上空升起一大片烟柱。此前，胡塞武装的无人机和导弹袭击撕裂了沙特阿美位于红海南部的一处储油罐区。（Gallo Images/Orbital Horizon/Copernicus Sentinel Data 2026）\n\n大局：胡塞运动目前控制着也门沿红海的大部分海岸线。红海是全球商业的重要航道，经苏伊士运河连接印度洋和中东与欧洲。该组织的大本营位于萨那，那里曾是也门首都。\n\n自2023年开始，胡塞武装袭击了数百艘船只，其中包括美国货船，使红海变成一条险象环生的通道，导致一些大型国际航运公司为避免风险，改道绕行非洲，额外增加4000英里的航程。随后，伊朗在另一个中东咽喉要道——霍尔木兹海峡——采取了类似策略。\n\n数月来，沙特阿拉伯的东西管道使其能够绕过该海峡，将石油转运至红海沿岸港口。但上周，这条管道遭到无人机袭击；沙特当局指责伊朗支持的伊拉克民兵组织发动袭击，如今沙特王国被迫关闭管道进行维修。\n\n沙特阿拉伯是伊朗长期的地区对手。本周，沙特另行声称在圣城麦加附近拦截了一架胡塞无人机，但该组织否认了这一说法。\n\n伊朗的作用：为胡塞武装提供培训、武器和石油。\n\n美国国会研究处在2月20日发布的一份有关胡塞武装的报告中写道：“美国官员曾描述伊朗为胡塞武装提供武器、目标信息和军事建议的努力。”一个具有代表性的案例是，财政部于2018年制裁了5名“与伊朗弹道导弹项目有关联”的伊朗个人，理由是他们向胡塞武装提供导弹及“相关技术专长”。\n\n随后，在1月的一项认定中，财政部声称，德黑兰“利用总部设在迪拜的伊朗所有或关联公司，既向胡塞武装出售石油，也每月免费提供一批石油”。按美国估算，这可能构成胡塞武装每年超过20亿美元石油收入中的很大一部分，而这些收入支撑着该组织的运作。\n\n资金如何流动：通过设在也门境内外的兑换机构和空壳公司。财政部称，胡塞武装“通过萨那的兑换公司向设在阿联酋的兑换机构汇款……以支付伊朗石油”。随后，他们以“高得离谱的价格”将这些石油卖给也门人。\n\n与此同时，据报道，该组织通过也门的实体支付武器费用，其中最主要的是\n与胡塞武装有关联（现已受到美国制裁）的萨那 Al-Ridhwan Exchange and Transfer Company。美国称，胡塞领导人利用 Al-Ridhwan“向也门境外由胡塞拥有的账户进行多笔付款，以购买导弹部件、先进武器系统及其他军用级材料”。一辆载有与胡塞武装结盟的前被拘留者的卡车抵达萨那一条挤满支持者的街道，此前他们是胡塞武装本月在港口城市摩卡从监狱释放的200多人中的一部分。（Mohammed Hamoud/Getty Images）\n\n摘自 Kharon 的研究：数字平台赋予这些与胡塞武装有关联的交易所——进而也赋予胡塞武装的筹资活动——国际触达能力。\n\n例如，Coin Cash 是一家总部位于也门的实体，提供加密货币与法定货币之间的兑换，以及资金进出也门的转账服务。根据其网站介绍，其“最常见”的加密货币“合作伙伴”是全球最大的加密货币交易所 Binance，以及总部位于迪拜的 Bybit。\n\nKharon 审阅的该网站2023年存档版本还列出了另一家知名合作伙伴：总部位于萨那的 Al Hazmi Exchange Company。美国于2024年12月制裁了该公司，理由是其代表胡塞武装协助洗钱。\n\nCoin Cash 在一个 Instagram 页面上宣传其服务，并自称为“互联网营销服务”。它还运营着一个网站，引导潜在用户通过 WhatsApp 或 Telegram 联系该公司来发起交易。\n\nJane Tang 和 Kharon Research 为本报告作出贡献；本报告改编自一篇最初于2月发表的文章。\n\n阅读《The Brief》关于伊朗和恐怖组织的更多内容：\n\n财政部针对伊朗贸易伙伴启动制裁“行动”：须知事项\n\n“非常方便的掩护”：在一家销售蔬菜的网络中，近2亿美元黄金进入伊朗\n\n在一家慈善机构领导人被捕前多年，其与哈马斯的联系不断加深\n\n返回《The Brief》\n\nKharon 最新动态\n\n伊朗袭击美国供水系统，与其说像新的恐怖战线，不如说更像一场心理战\n\n最新的特朗普—习近平峰会将带来什么？四位专家阐明关键看点。\n\n“非常方便的掩护”：在一家销售蔬菜的网络中，近2亿美元黄金进入伊朗\n\nKharon Readbook\n\n每周洞见直达你的收件箱。\n\n名字*\n\n姓氏*\n\n电子邮箱*\n\n感谢订阅。","publish_source":"kharon.com","publish_time":"2026-09-16T12:21:51-07:00"}},{"id":"news-1812","ktid":1055920,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1055920","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"伊朗镇压抗议沿用中国剧本，原因何在","title_en":"Iran’s Protest Crackdown Followed a China Playbook. There’s a Reason for That. | Kharon","summary_cn":"卡隆公司（Kharon）文章分析伊朗对抗议的镇压与中国安全合作的关系。伊朗警察总长拉丹主导镇压，曾于2024年访华签署执法合作备忘录。中国公安大学自2015年起为伊朗警官提供培训。文章还追踪中国监控企业天地伟业在伊朗的销售网络，其产品被指用于监控抗议和追踪异见人士，美国2022年将其列入实体清单。中国外交部呼吁伊朗保持稳定，反对外部干涉。","summary_en":"A Kharon article examines how Iran's protest crackdown draws on security cooperation with China. Police chief Radan, who leads the crackdown, signed a law enforcement cooperation memorandum in Beijing in 2024, and China's People's Public Security University has run training programs for Iranian officers since 2015. Kharon traces Chinese surveillance firm Tiandy Technologies' Iran sales network, whose products are reportedly used to monitor protests and track dissidents; the U.S. added Tiandy to the Entity List in 2022. China's foreign ministry urged stability and opposed external interference.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:58:14.363020+00:00","url":"https://www.kharon.com/brief/iran-protests-news-china-irgc-tiandy-technologies","content":"Protesters gather Jan. 8 in Tehran. (Getty Images)SurveillanceJan 16, 20265 minutesIran’s Protest Crackdown Followed a China Playbook. There’s a Reason for That.By Jane Tang and Yu-Jie LiaoWestern countries have condemned what rights groups and U.N. officials describe as a brutal crackdown on protesters in Iran, where tens of thousands of people took to the streets and security forces responded with lethal force. The U.S. this week imposed new sanctions on Iranian officials tied to the suppression, while the United Nations has expressed “horror” at the scale of the violence, urging that “the killing of peaceful demonstrators must stop.”\nAs death-toll estimates stretch into the thousands, Iran's leadership has sought to justify its actions by labeling demonstrators as “terrorists” and blaming foreign powers for fomenting unrest. The government has cut internet access for more than a week, marking one of the country’s longest-ever blackouts, according to the cybersecurity watchdog NetBlocks.\nInternational support appears to have played a role. Tehran's longstanding security relationship with Beijing—spanning police training, “counterterrorism” cooperation and surveillance technology—offers insight into how Iranian authorities both prepared their aggressive approach to dissent internally and how they have characterized it publicly.\nThe Police ChiefIranian Police Chief Ahmad-Reza Radan, left, meets with Chinese Minister of Public Security Wang Xiaohong in Beijing in January 2024. (Xinhua)  Ahmad-Reza Radan, Iran’s police chief and a vocal supporter of employing force against protesters, is leading the current state clampdown. His roles in previous ones led to Western sanctions.\nThe U.S. sanctioned Radan for human rights abuses in 2010, when he was deputy chief of the National Police, calling him “responsible for beatings, murder, and arbitrary arrests and detentions against protestors that were committed by the police forces.” It then sanctioned him again in 2011 for his role in repressing dissent in neighboring Syria.The EU sanctioned Radan in 2020, citing the same repressive actions the U.S. cited in 2010.\nWhile under Western restrictions, Radan has pursued closer security coordination with China. In 2024, he visited China and signed a “memorandum on law enforcement cooperation” with China’s minister of public security, Wang Xiaohong, pledging to “upgrade law enforcement and security cooperation” and “strengthen practical collaboration in areas such as counterterrorism” to contribute to regional stability, according to China’s Xinhua state news agency. Neither Xinhua nor IRNA, Iran’s own state news agency, released the memorandum’s full text.\nThe agreement with China followed a similar public security pact between Tehran and Moscow, signed in 2023. According to IRNA, that agreement called for “the expansion of security and law enforcement cooperation and the exchange of experiences in dealing with factors that foment insecurity.”\nThe Training Pipeline\nThe People’s Public Security University of China, the country’s top police academy, has run “Advanced Iranian Police Officers Training Programs” since 2015, organized by China’s Ministry of Public Security, according to Chinese school materials and state media reports reviewed by Kharon. Such Iranian cooperation appears to have deepened since, and in 2018, Iran’s National Police University signed a formal agreement institutionalizing more exchange and training programs.\nThe relationship remains active. On December 25, 2025, just days before Iran’s protests erupted, its ambassador to China visited the People’s Public Security University, pledging to continue “pragmatic cooperation in law enforcement and security,” according to a school press release.Iran’s ambassador to China, Abdolreza Rahmani Fazli, visits the People’s Public Security University of China. (People’s Public Security University of China)What China teaches carries influence. The Carnegie Endowment for International Peace, a think tank based in Washington, D.C., reported in November that China uses such police trainings to export its domestic “stability maintenance” expertise, which it has most prominently applied in Xinjiang, also in the name of “counterterrorism.” The trainings, the Carnegie Endowment said, often come bundled with business opportunities for Chinese surveillance firms.\nThe China-Exported Surveillance Network\nTiandy Technologies, a Chinese provider of video surveillance tech, has built deep roots in Iran—and in China’s security establishment.\nIts equipment, which flows through sales agents into a country where surveillance technology has reportedly been used to monitor the protests and track dissidents, offers one link between China’s security industry and Tehran’s monitoring capabilities.\nBackground: Tiandy Technologies says on its website that it has worked in China's public security sector for more than 20 years, serving clients including the Ministry of Public Security, which awarded it a first-class science and technology award in 2018.\nThe U.S. added Tiandy to the Entity List in 2022, citing its roles both in surveilling Muslim minorities in Xinjiang and in “enabling the procurement of U.S.-origin items for use by the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps.” In 2023, the Wall Street Journal reported that U.S. officials were considering additional sanctions on Chinese surveillance companies, including Tiandy, as Tehran increasingly relied on monitoring technology to suppress protests. Tiandy's products had been sold to IRGC units, the Journal said.Connecting the dots: Kharon research traced Tiandy’s Iran-facing sales network through Iranian entities tied to the brand:\nTiandy Center is a subsidiary of Iran-based Ati Negar Basir Elektronik Company and a self-described “distributor of Tiandy Products.” An archived version of its website from July 2025 listed 18 offices across Iran and advertised that if a company becomes a Tiandy representative in Iran, it can also represent other Chinese video-surveillance brands, including Hangzhou Hikvision Digital Technology Co., Ltd. and Zhejiang Dahua Technology Co., Ltd. The U.S. added both those companies to the Entity List in 2019, citing their roles in China’s repression and “high-technology surveillance” of minorities, and it later designated both as companies in China’s military industrial complex. Elm va Sanat Hafez Gostar Company is another distributor of Tiandy products in Iran. According to an archived version of its website from last month, the company listed Iranian government entities as its customers, including the Iran Ministry of Culture and Islamic Guidance and the national traffic police. In addition to Tiandy products, Elm va Sanat Hafez Gostar also said it was a representative for Hangzhou Hikvision and Zhejiang Dahua.\nA public pushback: The scope of Tiandy’s Iran operations drew scrutiny in spring 2024, when four Tehran City Council members complained about what they called a “secret” surveillance contract. In a letter to the council chairman, the members protested a deal between Tehran Municipality and several Chinese companies for facial recognition cameras, vans and security equipment, according to Persian-language media reports.\nThe letter, published by the news site Roydad24, said that Tehran Mayor Alireza Zakani had planned contracts, including a €400 million purchase of smart cameras, with “unnamed” Chinese companies that had no internet presence. According to the Independent, municipality documents identified one vendor as “Tidndy”—a name that yielded no search results but appeared to be a misspelling of Tiandy.\nThe Messaging\nIn response to Iran’s protests and crackdown, China has staked out a clear public position: for its security and trading partner’s “stability” and against U.S. intervention.\n“We hope the Iranian government and people will overcome the current difficulties and uphold stability in the country,” a Ministry of Foreign Affairs spokeswoman said at a press briefing Wednesday. China opposes, she added, “external interference in other countries’ internal affairs.”\nJohn Krzyzaniak contributed research to this report.\nRead more from the Kharon Brief:\nHypersonic Secret: ‘China’s MIT’ Worked with U.S. while Developing Weapons to Use Against ItThe Brief’s Top Iran Stories from a Year of Renewed ‘Maximum Pressure’Timeline: How U.S. Sanctions on Venezuela Escalated for Years Before Maduro’s CaptureBack to The BriefLatest on KharonWho Are the Houthis? How Iran Funds the Militia Group Now Striking Saudi Arabia.Iran’s Attacks on U.S. Water Systems Look Less Like a New Terror Front and More Like a PsyopWhat Will the Latest Trump-Xi Summit Bring? Four Experts Set the Stakes.Kharon ReadbookWeekly insights delivered to your inbox.First Name*Last Name*Email address*Thank you for subscribing.Subscribe","content_cn":"抗议者于1月8日在德黑兰聚集。（盖蒂图片社）监控\n2026年1月16日\n5分钟\n伊朗镇压抗议活动遵循了中国模式。原因就在于此\n作者：简·唐和廖玉洁\n西方国家谴责了伊朗对抗议者的残酷镇压，人权组织和联合国官员对此有这样的描述。在伊朗，数万人走上街头，安全部队以致命武力回应。本周，美国对与镇压行动有关的伊朗官员实施了新制裁；联合国则对暴力的规模表示“震惊”，敦促“必须停止杀害和平示威者”。\n随着死亡人数估计达到数千，伊朗领导层试图通过将示威者称为“恐怖分子”并指责外国势力煽动动乱，为其行动辩护。据网络安全观察机构NetBlocks称，政府已切断互联网接入超过一周，创下该国有史以来持续时间最长的断网之一。\n国际支持似乎发挥了作用。德黑兰与北京长期存在的安全关系——涵盖警务培训、“反恐”合作和监控技术——有助于了解伊朗当局如何在内部为其对异议采取强硬手段做好准备，以及如何在公开场合描述这一做法。\n警察首长\n2024年1月，伊朗警察总长艾哈迈德-礼萨·拉丹（左）在北京会见中国公安部部长王小洪。（新华社）艾哈迈德-礼萨·拉丹是伊朗警察总长，也是公开支持对抗议者使用武力的人，目前正领导这场国家镇压行动。他在此前镇压行动中担任的职务，曾导致西方对他实施制裁。\n2010年，拉丹担任国家警察副总长期间，美国以侵犯人权为由制裁了他，称他“应对警察部队实施的殴打、谋杀以及任意逮捕和拘留抗议者行为负责”。2011年，美国又因他参与镇压邻国叙利亚的异议而再次制裁他。欧盟于2020年制裁拉丹，理由是他实施了与美国2010年所指控相同的镇压行动。\n在受到西方限制期间，拉丹寻求加强与中国的安全协调。2024年，他访问中国，并与中国公安部部长王小洪签署了一份“执法合作谅解备忘录”。据中国官方媒体新华社报道，备忘录承诺“提升执法和安全合作”，并“加强反恐等领域的务实协作”，以促进地区稳定。新华社和伊朗官方通讯社伊斯兰共和国通讯社（IRNA）均未公布该备忘录全文。\n这项与中国达成的协议，此前已有德黑兰与莫斯科之间类似的公共安全协定，该协定于2023年签署。据伊斯兰共和国通讯社报道，该协议要求“扩大安全和执法合作，并交流应对煽动不安全因素的经验”。\n培训渠道\n据Kharon查阅的中国学校资料和官方媒体报道，中国人民公安大学是该国最高警察学院，自2015年起开设“伊朗警官高级培训项目”，由中国公安部组织。此类伊朗合作似乎自那以后进一步深化；2018年，伊朗国家警察大学签署了一项正式协议，将更多交流和培训项目制度化。\n这种关系\n仍然活跃。2025年12月25日，就在伊朗抗议爆发前几天，其驻华大使访问了人民公安大学，并承诺继续开展“执法和安全领域的务实合作”，人民公安大学在一份新闻稿中称。伊朗驻华大使Abdolreza Rahmani Fazli访问中国人民公安大学。（中国人民公安大学）\n\n中国所传授的内容具有影响力。总部位于华盛顿特区的智库卡内基国际和平基金会在11月报告称，中国利用此类警务培训输出其国内的“维稳”专业知识，而这套知识最突出地应用于新疆，同样以“反恐”为名。卡内基国际和平基金会表示，这些培训往往与中国监控企业的商业机会捆绑在一起。\n\n中国输出的监控网络\n\n中国视频监控技术供应商Tiandy Technologies已在伊朗——以及中国的安全体系——扎下深厚根基。\n\n其设备通过销售代理流入伊朗；据报道，伊朗曾利用监控技术监视抗议活动并追踪异议人士，这些设备成为中国安全产业与德黑兰监控能力之间的一个连接点。\n\n背景：Tiandy Technologies在其网站上表示，公司在中国公共安全领域运营了20多年，客户包括公安部；公安部曾于2018年授予其一等科学技术奖。\n\n美国于2022年将Tiandy列入实体清单，理由是该公司既参与监视新疆的穆斯林少数群体，也“帮助采购供伊斯兰革命卫队使用的美国原产物项”。2023年，《华尔街日报》报道称，随着德黑兰越来越依赖监控技术镇压抗议活动，美国官员正考虑对包括Tiandy在内的中国监控公司实施额外制裁。《华尔街日报》称，Tiandy的产品已售给伊斯兰革命卫队部队。\n\n串联线索：Kharon的研究通过与该品牌有关联的伊朗实体，追踪了Tiandy面向伊朗的销售网络：\n\nTiandy Center是总部位于伊朗的Ati Negar Basir Elektronik Company的子公司，自称“Tiandy产品的分销商”。其网站2025年7月的存档版本列出了遍布伊朗的18个办事处，并宣传称，如果一家公司成为Tiandy在伊朗的代表，还可以代理其他中国视频监控品牌，包括杭州海康威视数字技术股份有限公司和浙江大华技术股份有限公司。美国于2019年将这两家公司列入实体清单，理由是它们参与了中国对少数群体的镇压和“高科技监控”；之后，美国又将两家公司列为中国军工复合体企业。Elm va Sanat Hafez Gostar Company是Tiandy在伊朗的另一家产品分销商。根据其上月网站的存档版本，该公司将伊朗政府实体列为客户，包括伊朗文化和伊斯兰指导部以及国家交通警察。除Tiandy产品外，Elm va Sanat Hafez Gostar还表示自己是杭州海康威视和浙江大华的代理商。\n\n公开反弹：2024年春季，Tiandy在伊朗的运营规模受到审查，当时四名德黑兰市议会成员抱怨他们所谓的一个\n“秘密”监控合同。据波斯语媒体报道，在致市议会主席的一封信中，这些成员抗议德黑兰市政府与数家中国公司达成的一项交易，内容涉及面部识别摄像头、厢式车和安保设备。\n\n据新闻网站Roydad24刊登的这封信称，德黑兰市长阿里雷扎·扎卡尼曾计划与没有互联网信息的“未具名”中国公司签订合同，其中包括购买价值4亿欧元的智能摄像头。据《独立报》报道，市政府文件将一家供应商标为“Tidndy”——这一名称搜索不到任何结果，但看起来像是对天迪（Tiandy）的拼写错误。\n\n信息传递\n\n面对伊朗的抗议和镇压，中国明确表明了公开立场：支持其安全和贸易伙伴的“稳定”，反对美国干预。\n\n外交部一名女发言人在周三的新闻发布会上说：“我们希望伊朗政府和人民能够克服当前困难，维护国家稳定。”她补充说，中国反对“外部干涉别国内政”。\n\nJohn Krzyzaniak为本报道提供了研究支持。\n\n阅读更多《卡隆简报》内容：\n\n高超音速秘密：“中国的麻省理工”在研发用于对付美国的武器期间曾与美国合作《简报》伊朗年度头条：新一轮“极限施压”Timeline：美国制裁委内瑞拉多年升级，最终导致马杜罗被捕返回《简报》卡隆最新消息胡塞武装是谁？伊朗如何资助这个如今袭击沙特阿拉伯的民兵组织。伊朗对美国供水系统的攻击，与其说像一条新的恐怖战线，不如说更像一场心理战最新特朗普—习近平峰会将带来什么？四位专家设定关键议题。卡隆读本每周将洞见发送到您的收件箱。名*姓*电子邮箱*感谢订阅。订阅","publish_source":"kharon.com","publish_time":"2026-01-16T12:53:17-08:00"}},{"id":"news-137","ktid":1055920,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1055920","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"伊朗对美国供水系统的攻击更像心理战而非新恐怖战线","title_en":"Iran’s Attacks on U.S. Water Systems Look Less Like a New Terror Front and More Like a Psyop | Kharon","summary_cn":"今年针对美国水处理设施的一系列协同黑客攻击波及12个州和100个市镇，引发恐慌。但网络安全分析人士认为，这更像伊朗的心理战，旨在影响美国国内政治辩论，而非新的恐怖战线。文章梳理了与伊朗革命卫队网络电子指挥部相关的CyberAv3ngers组织、其指挥结构及美国制裁与悬赏措施。","summary_en":"A wave of coordinated hacks against U.S. water treatment facilities this year hit 12 states and 100 municipalities, sparking alarm. But cybersecurity analysts say the campaign looks more like an Iranian psyop to shape U.S. political debate than a new terror front. The article examines the CyberAv3ngers group, its links to the IRGC Cyber Electronic Command, its command structure, and U.S. sanctions and bounties.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T15:56:15.251508+00:00","url":"https://www.kharon.com/brief/iran-war-cyberattacks-water-systems-cyberav3ngers","content":"Kharon illustration / Adobe Stock ImagesTransnational CrimeSep 17, 20264 minutesIran’s Attacks on U.S. Water Systems Look Less Like a New Terror Front and More Like a PsyopBy Ian TalleyThe wave of coordinated hacks this year against U.S. water treatment facilities — striking 12 states and 100 municipalities since the Trump administration launched its war against Iran — sparked alarm that Tehran was escalating the conflict by targeting civilians on U.S. soil.\nBut cybersecurity analysts who track the groups implicated in the cyberattacks say that’s likely only what Iran wanted Americans to fear. The hacks, they say, look less to be a new terror front than an ongoing psyops campaign designed to shape American political debate on the war.\n“They’re doing things that are quick and easy, and they’re doing it for that information value,” said Nikita Shah, a senior analyst at the Center for Strategic and International Studies, calling the cyberattacks a way “to signal and to project power” to a U.S. audience. “They want to wear down regular citizens and businesses by applying pressure this way.”\nMore tailored and destructive cyberattacks, Shah said, would likely take far longer to plan than this year’s barrage, which has caused minimal damage and no reported casualties, though some authorities have reported isolated flooding or loss of water pressure and issued boil-water advisories.An aerial view of a wastewater treatment plant in San Rafael, Calif., in 2024, seen shortly after the Biden administration warned of previous cyberattacks on water systems by the CyberAv3ngers and other Iran-linked groups. (Justin Sullivan/Getty Images)U.S. officials and cybersecurity analysts have connected the campaign to an Iranian elite military unit, and authorities have targeted its leadership and affiliated officials with sanctions and $10 million bounties, including a new reward issued just last week.\nTheir cyber campaign against the U.S. didn’t just start. It’s been running for nearly three years.\nA New Wave of Attacks with IRGC Links\nAnalysts trace the attacks on critical infrastructure back to a broader campaign that began in late 2023, after Hamas’s Oct. 7 attacks, that hit a number of U.S. states along with Israel. U.S. authorities say “Iran-affiliated cyber actors” have mounted a coordinated new wave since March, infiltrating water, waste, energy, and government facilities.\nAmong the recent hacks was one operation in July that targeted more than 30 water systems in Minnesota, the most of any state. Intruders now, authorities said, are exploiting a security flaw in internet-exposed “programmable logic controllers,” unsophisticated computers that monitor and activate mechanical systems like water pumps, valves and switches.\nIn a joint advisory issued by the Federal Bureau of Investigation and six other agencies in late July, officials did not identify a suspected culprit, but they said the activity was similar to opportunistic disruptions perpetrated by the CyberAv3ngers, which they called “a cyber threat actor” affiliated with Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC).\nSince then, several private cybersecurity firms in blog posts and corporate briefs have corroborated that assessment, saying the U.S. hacks bore the patterns of the group.\nWho they are: The CyberAv3ngers maintain various social media accounts that occasionally communicate publicly, including to claim responsibility for some past water-facility hacks in the U.S. and abroad and to threaten others.\nIn the 2023 hack of a Pennsylvania city’s municipal water authority, for instance, the touchscreens of its industrial control systems displayed the message: “You have been hacked, down with Israel. Every equipment ‘made in Israel’ is CyberAv3ngers legal target.”The State Department said the Anonymous-inspired online persona “Mr. Soul” — seen here on Telegram — was “associated with” CyberAv3ngers when it issued a $10 million bounty for information about the group.According to the threat analytics firm Claroty, one of the group’s digital fingerprints in hacks that targeted fuel systems and gas stations was a malware tool designed to establish persistent, covert access to industrial control systems.\nAccounts associated with the CyberAv3ngers present them as a hacktivist group, a non-state collective that uses digital attacks to advance political and social agendas. But the State Department says the group’s true mastermind is the IRGC’s Cyber Electronic Command.\nIran’s strategy: The IRGC-CEC sits within a broader command structure whose policy is set by the Supreme Council of Cyberspace, established in 2012 by the Supreme Leader. Besides the commander of the IRGC, that body includes the ministers of intelligence, defense, judiciary and communications.\nCybersecurity analysts say that command structure marks the CEC and its subordinate cyber divisions not only as military units but as tools for information warfare, both within the country and without.\nU.S. officials and human rights groups accuse the Ministry of Communications and Information Technology, for example, of enabling the regime’s repression of dissent within Iran, overseeing country-wide internet outages and censorship and integrating telecommunications data with security forces to track and arrest dissidents.Information warfare is central to the IRGC’s martial doctrine, analysts say, a principle developed as a practical response to its limited military power — similar to the IRGC’s early focus on low-cost drone warfare.Kharon users can explore networks like this one through the ClearView platform.Although little is publicly known about CyberAv3ngers’ internal organizational structure, some analysts say its operational history points to a unit created in-house, not commandeered or contracted by the state.\n“CyberAv3ngers represents the latest evolution in Iran’s long-standing tradition of blending cyber operations with ideological messaging,” the cybersecurity firm DomainTools wrote in a June blog post on hacks against U.S. water infrastructure announced in April. “CyberAv3ngers has refined the model into a fully realized propaganda apparatus.”\nTo the U.S. government, Shah said, the critical-infrastructure hacks this year send a message about capability: We can reach your homeland. To the American public, she said, the message is that this war isn’t happening somewhere else — it’s in your water supply, your infrastructure, your backyard.\nInside Iran’s Cyber Command\nIsrael’s military said in early March it struck Iran’s cyber command center, but U.S. intelligence made public earlier this month suggests the unit is still active. Shah said the cyber command’s priority since the war has likely been on identifying targets for missiles and drones and intelligence collection amid peace negotiations.\nBut its cyberattacks on critical infrastructure continue to be used to justify sanctions and substantial U.S. bounties for the suspected leaders behind them.\nA few months after the late-2023 attacks, the U.S. Treasury Department levied sanctions against the leadership of the IRGC-CEC, including against its head, Hamid Reza Lashgarian, a commander in the IRGC’s Qods Force. Just last week, the State Department’s Rewards for Justice program issued a $10 million bounty for information on the whereabouts of Amir Yaryab, who it says leads the IRGC-CEC’s Cyber Operations Command. In that role, State said, Yaryab “oversees and controls operations conducted by IRGC-CEC-affiliated groups such as CyberAv3ngers.”(State Department)(State Department)A key operational arm: the Shahid Kaveh Cyber Unit, an IRGC-CEC unit that U.S. officials say uses a roster of aliases, including CyberAv3ngers, depending on the target and the audience.\nWithin Shahid Kaveh sits Intelligence Group 13, a sub-unit that analysts say is tasked with building a “target bank” — identifying weakly defended infrastructure in advance for CEC’s teams to attack.\nA key figure: Among the half-dozen other IRGC-CEC officials sanctioned by the U.S. Treasury and sought by the State Department is Mohammad Bagher Shirinkar. Revealing the breadth of the IRGC’s information-warfare operations, Treasury has said Shirinkar manages Iranian firms used in cyber campaigns intended to influence the 2020 presidential election and the surveillance of counterintelligence agents.\nLooking Ahead\nU.S. officials have urgently warned regulators and companies to update and modernize equipment prone to Iranian attacks, expecting an ongoing campaign on American infrastructure.\nIn the meantime, the threats have continued. In one August post, a “Mr. Soul” account on Telegram warned hackers were primed to “detonate within their systems and the systems of their allies–a powerful and large-scale attack unlike anything the world has ever seen in cyberspace…”\nNo such attack has materialized. But Tehran may have found a new attack vector: U.S. officials said this week they were probing whether Iran was involved in cyberattacks against two Texas-bound tankers on the other side of the Atlantic.\nRead more from The Brief on Iran and cyber:\n‘A Very Convenient Cover’: Nearly $200M in Gold Entered Iran Through a Network Selling VegetablesInside the Low-Profile Chinese Companies Named in the ‘Salt Typhoon’ HackThe Network That’s Kept Foreign Cash Flowing into Iran, Through Sanctions and WarBack to The BriefLatest on KharonWho Are the Houthis? How Iran Funds the Militia Group Now Striking Saudi Arabia.What Will the Latest Trump-Xi Summit Bring? Four Experts Set the Stakes.‘A Very Convenient Cover’: Nearly $200M in Gold Entered Iran Through a Network Selling VegetablesKharon ReadbookWeekly insights delivered to your inbox.First Name*Last Name*Email address*Thank you for subscribing.Subscribe","content_cn":"Kharon插图 / Adobe Stock Images\n跨国犯罪\n2026年9月17日\n4分钟\n\n伊朗对美国供水系统的攻击，与其说像新的恐怖战线，不如说更像一场心理战\n伊恩·塔利\n\n今年以来，美国供水处理设施遭到一波协调一致的黑客攻击——自特朗普政府对伊朗发动战争以来，已波及12个州和100个市镇——这引发了人们的警觉，担心德黑兰正通过在美国本土针对平民来升级冲突。\n\n但追踪涉案网络攻击团伙的网络安全分析师表示，这很可能只是伊朗希望美国人担心的事情。他们说，这些黑客攻击与其说是新的恐怖战线，不如说是一场持续进行的心理战行动，旨在塑造美国国内围绕战争的政治辩论。\n\n战略与国际问题研究中心高级分析师尼基塔·沙阿说：“他们做的事情快速而简单，而这样做是为了获取信息价值。”她称网络攻击是一种面向美国受众“发出信号并展示力量”的方式。“他们希望通过这种施压方式让普通民众和企业疲于应对。”\n\n沙阿说，更具针对性、破坏性更强的网络攻击可能需要远比今年这轮攻势更长的策划时间；这轮攻势造成的损害很小，也没有人员伤亡报告，不过一些当局报告了局部洪水或水压下降，并发布了煮沸饮用水建议。\n\n2024年，加利福尼亚州圣拉斐尔一座污水处理厂的航拍图；此前不久，拜登政府曾警告称，CyberAv3ngers及其他与伊朗有关联的团体曾对供水系统发动网络攻击。（贾斯汀·沙利文/Getty Images）\n\n美国官员和网络安全分析师已将这场行动与伊朗一支精锐军事部队联系起来，当局已对其领导层及关联官员实施制裁，并悬赏1000万美元缉拿相关人员，其中包括上周刚刚发布的一项新悬赏。\n\n他们针对美国的网络行动并不是刚刚开始的，而是已经持续了近三年。\n\n与革命卫队有关联的新一轮攻击\n\n分析师将针对关键基础设施的攻击追溯到一场更广泛的行动。该行动始于2023年末、哈马斯于10月7日发动袭击之后，袭击目标包括美国多个州以及以色列。美国当局表示，自3月以来，“与伊朗有关联的网络行为者”已发起协调一致的新一轮行动，入侵供水、废弃物处理、能源和政府设施。\n\n近期的黑客攻击中，有一次行动于7月针对明尼苏达州30多个供水系统，数量为全美各州之最。当局称，入侵者目前正利用暴露在互联网中的“可编程逻辑控制器”安全漏洞；这类简陋的计算机负责监控并启动水泵、阀门和开关等机械系统。\n\n联邦调查局和另外六个机构于7月底联合发布的一份公告中，官员没有指明涉嫌实施者，但表示，这些活动与CyberAv3ngers实施的机会主义破坏行为相似，并称该组织是一个与伊朗伊斯兰革命卫队（IRGC）有关联的“网络威胁行为者”。\n\n此后，几家私营网络安全公司在博客文章和企业简报中证实了这一评估，称美国遭受的黑客攻击呈现出该团伙的作案模式。\n\n他们是谁：CyberAv3ngers维护着多个社交媒体账号，偶尔公开发声，包括声称对过去在美国及海外发生的一些供水设施黑客攻击负责，并且\n威胁他人。\n例如，在2023年对宾夕法尼亚州一座城市的市政供水机构发动的黑客攻击中，其工业控制系统的触摸屏上显示着这样的信息：“你们已经被黑客入侵，打倒以色列。每一件‘以色列制造’的设备都是 CyberAv3ngers 的合法目标。”国务院表示，受“匿名者”启发的网络化身“Mr. Soul”——此处可见其在 Telegram 上的身影——在国务院悬赏1000万美元征集有关该组织的信息时，被称为“与” CyberAv3ngers “有关联”。据威胁分析公司 Claroty 称，该组织在针对燃料系统和加油站的黑客攻击中留下的数字指纹之一，是一种旨在建立对工业控制系统持续、隐蔽访问权限的恶意软件工具。\n与 CyberAv3ngers 有关联的账号将其描述为一个黑客行动主义组织，即利用数字攻击来推进政治和社会议程的非国家团体。但国务院表示，该组织真正的幕后主使是伊朗伊斯兰革命卫队的网络电子司令部。\n伊朗的战略：伊斯兰革命卫队网络电子司令部隶属于一个更广泛的指挥体系，其政策由最高领袖于2012年设立的最高网络空间委员会制定。除伊斯兰革命卫队司令外，该机构还包括情报、国防、司法和通信部长。\n网络安全分析人士表示，这一指挥体系表明，网络电子司令部及其下属网络部门不仅是军事单位，也是信息战工具，既用于国内，也用于国外。\n例如，美国官员和人权组织指责通信与信息技术部助长政权在伊朗境内对异议的镇压，负责监督全国范围的互联网中断和审查，并将电信数据与安全部队整合，以追踪和逮捕异议人士。分析人士称，信息战是伊斯兰革命卫队军事 doctrine 的核心，这一原则是在其军事力量有限的情况下作为实际应对方案发展起来的——类似于伊斯兰革命卫队早期对低成本无人机战的重视。Kharon 用户可以通过 ClearView 平台探索这样的网络。尽管公众对 CyberAv3ngers 的内部组织结构知之甚少，但一些分析人士表示，其行动历史表明这是一个内部组建的单位，而不是由国家接管或承包的组织。\n网络安全公司 DomainTools 在6月一篇关于4月公布的针对美国供水基础设施黑客攻击的博客文章中写道：“CyberAv3ngers 代表了伊朗长期以来将网络行动与意识形态宣传相结合传统的最新演变。CyberAv3ngers 已将这一模式完善为一个完全成形的宣传机器。”\nShah 说，对美国政府而言，今年针对关键基础设施的黑客攻击传达的是能力信息：我们可以触及你的国土。她说，对美国公众而言，传达的信息是，这场战争并非发生在别的地方——它就在你的供水系统、你的基础设施、你的后院。\n伊朗网络司令部内部\n以色列军方在3月初表示，其袭击了伊朗网络司令部中心，但美国情报部门本月早些时候公开的信息表明，该部门仍在活动。Shah 说，自战争开始以来，网络司令部的重点很可能一直是确定导弹和无人机的目标，并在和平谈判期间开展情报收集。\n但其对关键基础设施发动的网络攻击仍被用于为制裁以及针对这些攻击背后涉嫌领导人的巨额美国悬赏提供理由。\n几个月\n在2023年末的袭击之后，美国财政部对伊斯兰革命卫队网络电子战司令部（IRGC-CEC）的领导层实施制裁，其中包括其负责人Hamid Reza Lashgarian——伊斯兰革命卫队圣城部队的一名指挥官。就在上周，国务院“正义奖励”计划悬赏1000万美元，征集有关Amir Yaryab下落的信息。国务院称，他领导着IRGC-CEC的网络行动司令部。国务院表示，在这一职务上，Yaryab“监督并控制由CyberAv3ngers等隶属于IRGC-CEC的团体开展的行动”。(国务院)(国务院)\n一个关键行动部门：Shahid Kaveh网络部队，这是IRGC-CEC的一个单位。美国官员称，该单位使用一系列别名，包括CyberAv3ngers，具体取决于目标和受众。\nShahid Kaveh内部设有第13情报组，这是一个子单位。分析人士称，该小组负责建立“目标库”——提前识别防护薄弱的基础设施，供CEC团队发动攻击。\n一个关键人物：在美国财政部制裁、并被国务院追捕的另外六名左右IRGC-CEC官员中，有Mohammad Bagher Shirinkar。财政部表示，Shirinkar管理着一些伊朗企业，这些企业被用于旨在影响2020年总统大选以及监视反情报人员的网络行动，揭示了伊斯兰革命卫队信息战行动的广度。\n\n展望未来\n\n美国官员紧急警告监管机构和企业更新并现代化容易遭受伊朗攻击的设备，并预计针对美国基础设施的行动将持续下去。\n\n与此同时，威胁仍在继续。在8月的一篇帖子中，Telegram上的“Mr. Soul”账号警告称，黑客已经准备好“在他们的系统及其盟友的系统中引爆——这将是网络空间有史以来前所未见的强大而大规模的攻击……”\n\n这样的攻击尚未发生。但德黑兰可能找到了新的攻击途径：美国官员本周表示，他们正在调查伊朗是否参与了针对大西洋彼岸两艘驶往得克萨斯州的油轮的网络攻击。\n\n阅读《简报》中更多关于伊朗和网络空间的内容：\n“一个非常方便的掩护”：近2亿美元黄金通过一个销售蔬菜的网络进入伊朗深入了解“盐台风”黑客攻击中被点名的低调中国公司维持外国现金流入伊朗的网络：穿越制裁与战争返回《简报》Kharon最新消息谁是胡塞武装？伊朗如何资助这个如今袭击沙特阿拉伯的民兵组织。最新的特朗普-习近平峰会将带来什么？四位专家阐述关键问题。“一个非常方便的掩护”：近2亿美元黄金通过一个销售蔬菜的网络进入伊朗Kharon Readbook每周洞察，送达您的收件箱。名*姓*电子邮箱*感谢您的订阅。","publish_source":"kharon.com","publish_time":"2026-09-17T08:49:31-07:00"}},{"id":"news-1925","ktid":1055920,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1055920","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"BIS关联方规则与人才流失将持续影响美国出口管制","title_en":"BIS Affiliates Rule and Brain Drain Will Continue To Impact U.S. Export Controls | Kharon","summary_cn":"两位BakerHostetler律师回顾2025年美国出口管制两大主线：BIS于9月29日发布并实施“50%关联方规则”，将实体清单等限制延伸至被列名方持股50%以上的非美国实体，但该规则自11月10日起暂停一年；同时BIS出口管理局出现大量资深人员离职。文章展望2026年规则可能恢复，并预计先进计算芯片出口管制将带来更多波动。","summary_en":"Two BakerHostetler attorneys review two defining 2025 storylines in U.S. export controls: BIS published and implemented its long-anticipated Affiliates Rule on Sept. 29, extending Entity List and related restrictions to non-U.S. entities 50% or more owned by listed parties, before suspending it for a year effective Nov. 10; and BIS saw dozens of experienced personnel departures. They expect the rule's likely reinstatement in 2026 and continued volatility over advanced computing chip controls.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T17:02:20.466601+00:00","url":"https://www.kharon.com/brief/kharon-debrief-2025-bis-affiliates-rule-us-export-controls-china-melissa-mannino-james-perry","content":"Kharon illustrationThe 2025 DebriefDec 30, 20252 minutesBIS Affiliates Rule and Brain Drain Will Continue To Impact U.S. Export ControlsBy Melissa Mannino and James PerryAs the year came to a close, the Kharon Brief asked a range of industry leaders to assess 2025’s biggest storylines and what’s coming in 2026 in sanctions, risk and compliance.\nMelissa Mannino is a partner at BakerHostetler and former chief of the Enforcement and Litigation Division at the U.S. Commerce Department’s Office of Chief Counsel for Industry and Security.\nJames Perry is an associate at BakerHostetler.\nLooking back: The Bureau of Industry and Security’s Affiliates Rule and organizational brain drain were two defining storylines for U.S. export controls in 2025.\nBIS published and implemented that long-anticipated “50% rule” on Sept. 29; it was then suspended for a year effective Nov. 10, as part of U.S.-China trade negotiations. The Affiliates Rule extended the Entity List, Military End-User (MEU) List and select Specially Designated Nationals restrictions to any non-U.S. entity owned 50% or more—directly or indirectly, individually or in the aggregate—by listed parties, and the most restrictive license requirement of the entity’s parents applied. That meant the BIS regulations exceeded OFAC’s own 50% rule.\nThe rule’s pause gave businesses extra time to prepare before its likely reinstatement, whether by BIS or Congress, in 2026.\nBIS this year also saw the departures of dozens of knowledgeable and experienced personnel, notably from its Export Administration unit, in the first year of the new Trump administration. This tremendous loss and the apparent review of license applications, proposed charging letters and settlements at the highest level of BIS signal delays and uncertainty for 2026 and beyond.\nLooking ahead: We believe that 2026 will mirror much of 2025’s volatility.\nSome good news for businesses: We believe the reinstated version of the Affiliates Rule will be limited to entities owned by parties just on the Entity List, not the MEU or SDN lists. But it will be important for companies to design their compliance programs and, arguably, their business models, to be able to adapt quickly to statutory timelines, evolving covered parties, agency delays and increased due-diligence requirements, while remaining competitive in today’s globalized market. That’s not an easy balance to implement quickly.\nIn addition to the Affiliates Rule, we expect to see significant government activity on export-controls policies and requirements relating to advanced computing integrated circuits for AI language modeling. More volatility and uncertainty are likely as the U.S. balances competing priorities of its own: national security versus maintaining leadership in AI.Read more from the 2025 Kharon Debrief:Tariffs Showed Companies ‘the Underlying Structure of Risk Itself Had Changed’Robust White House Action Broadened the Net for National Security EnforcementA Year When the U.S. Expanded Terrorism Sanctions Targets Like Never BeforeLukoil and Rosneft Sanctions Underscored the Need for Agility in the Face of UnpredictabilityBack to The BriefLatest on KharonWho Are the Houthis? How Iran Funds the Militia Group Now Striking Saudi Arabia.Iran’s Attacks on U.S. Water Systems Look Less Like a New Terror Front and More Like a PsyopWhat Will the Latest Trump-Xi Summit Bring? Four Experts Set the Stakes.Kharon ReadbookWeekly insights delivered to your inbox.First Name*Last Name*Email address*Thank you for subscribing.Subscribe","content_cn":"Kharon插图\n2025年回顾\n2025年12月30日\n2分钟\nBIS关联方规则和人才流失将继续影响美国出口管制\n作者：Melissa Mannino和James Perry\n年末之际，《Kharon简报》邀请多位行业领导者评估2025年的最大热点，并展望2026年制裁、风险与合规领域的发展。\nMelissa Mannino是BakerHostetler律师事务所合伙人，曾任美国商务部工业与安全局首席法律顾问办公室执法与诉讼部门负责人。\nJames Perry是BakerHostetler律师事务所律师。\n回顾：美国工业与安全局的关联方规则和组织人才流失，是2025年美国出口管制领域的两大决定性热点。\nBIS于9月29日发布并实施了期待已久的“50%规则”；随后，作为美中贸易谈判的一部分，该规则自11月10日起暂停一年。关联方规则将实体清单、军事最终用户（MEU）清单以及部分特别指定国民限制，扩展适用于任何由清单所列主体直接或间接单独或合计持有50%或以上的非美国实体，并适用其母公司的最严格许可要求。这意味着BIS的规定超出了OFAC自身的50%规则。\n该规则的暂停为企业争取了额外准备时间，预计2026年无论由BIS还是国会推动，该规则都可能恢复实施。\n今年，BIS还经历了数十名知识丰富、经验老到的人员离职，尤其是出口管理部门人员的离开；这发生在特朗普新政府执政的第一年。这一巨大损失，以及BIS最高层似乎正在审查许可证申请、拟议指控函和和解协议，预示着2026年及以后将出现延误和不确定性。\n展望：我们认为，2026年将延续2025年的大部分波动性。\n对企业而言有一些好消息：我们认为，恢复后的关联方规则将仅限于由实体清单所列主体拥有的实体，而不包括MEU清单或SDN清单所列主体拥有的实体。但企业必须设计合规计划，并且可以说还要设计其商业模式，以便在适应法定时限、受管辖主体不断变化、机构延误和更高的尽职调查要求的同时，保持在当今全球化市场中的竞争力。这种平衡并不容易迅速实现。\n除关联方规则外，我们预计政府还将大力推动与用于人工智能语言建模的先进计算集成电路有关的出口管制政策和要求。随着美国在自身相互竞争的优先事项之间寻求平衡——国家安全与保持人工智能领域的领导地位——未来可能会有更多波动和不确定性。\n阅读更多2025年《Kharon回顾》内容：\n关税让企业看到“风险本身的底层结构已经改变”\n白宫采取强有力行动，扩大国家安全执法的覆盖范围\n美国前所未有地扩大恐怖主义制裁目标的一年\n卢克石油和俄罗斯石油公司制裁凸显了在不可预测性面前保持敏捷的必要性\n返回《简报》\nKharon最新内容\n胡塞武装是谁？伊朗如何资助如今正在袭击沙特阿拉伯的民兵组织。\n伊朗对美国供水系统的袭击，与其说像新的恐怖战线，不如说更像一场心理战\n最新特朗普—习近平峰会将带来什么？四位专家设定观察重点。\nKharon读本\n每周洞见直达您的收件箱。\n名*姓*电子邮件地址*\n感谢订阅。","publish_source":"kharon.com","publish_time":"2025-12-23T12:53:22-08:00"}}];
